    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Technical-Specialist--Mathematics---Mathematics-Education-Department---NIE-_R00025170": {
      "title": "Senior Technical Specialist (Mathematics & Mathematics Education Department) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nABOUT THE NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF EDUCATION (NIE) The National Institute of Education (NIE) , Singapore, is Singapore’s national teacher education institute and we are proud to be an integral part of the nation’s education service. We play a key role in the preparation of teachers and in the provision of teacher professional and school leadership development programmes. We are committed to our vision of being An Institute of Distinction: Leading the Future of Education and our mission to Inspire Learning, Transform Teaching and Advance Research . Read more about NIE here . NIE invites applications for the position of Senior Technical Specialist in the Mathematics & Mathematics Education Department. Responsibilities Managing the MME Outreach events to the Singapore schools, Ministry of Education and the academic faculties. The key events for MME include (1) the annual Mathematics Teachers Conference; (2) the bi-annual MME colloquium; (3) NIE / MME Mathematics challenge; (4) developing and maintaining social media outreach for MME. Provide IT/AV support for MME Department in the following areas: (a) coding and programming lessons; (b) cert in Primary Math Education course; (c) MME E- learning system; (d) manage MME labs for the IT/AV and facilities; (e) loaning of MME teaching manipulative, IT equipments and accessories; (f) MME representative for registering the removable storage media (RSM) in CAMs; (g) support MME lecturer with technical problem on the new laptop; (h) stamping of MME calculator for students before end-of-term examination. MME Website, social media and MME server management. Website management includes (1) School Mathematics Mastery Test; and (2) MME Math Qualify Test (MQT) system. Social media includes Facebook, X and Xiaohongshu. Video recording and video editing of MME events. Provide support roles in (a) assist Head MME for the NIE workload system; (b) MME facilities lab Booking Administrator; (c) manage and maintain Computer Labs and Math Labs; (d) MME Staff Welfare Committee (SWC) member. Provide Finance support in (a) Economy Drive Saving; (b) collating purchase requests for computer hardware and software; (c) supporting Good Receipt Officer; (d) keeping track of MME software and maintenance fund usage; (e) annual Software License Renewal; (f) managing MME fixed assets and records of inventories. Any other tasks assigned. Requirements A Bachelor’s Degree in any discipline, preferably related to Computer and Technologies. At least one year of experience as a technical support staff. Strong technical support and administrative skills, with experience in website/social media management, video recording and video editing, will be an added advantage. Ability to multi-task, work independently and effectively in a team. Strong interpersonal and communication skills, both written and oral.   Hard working, self-discipline, responsible, committed.  Closing Date The closing date of the advertisement is 2 Sep 2026. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Other Information NIE staff can take chartered buses at their own expense from or near their homes to NIE campus.  This is subject to the availability of seats. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Unit-Head--Research-Support-and-Grants-Management--RSGM---Office-for-Research--NIE-_R00024794-1": {
      "title": "Unit Head, Research Support and Grants Management (RSGM), Office for Research [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-07\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nABOUT THE NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF EDUCATION (NIE) The National Institute of Education (NIE), Singapore, is Singapore’s national teacher education institute, and we are proud to be an integral part of the nation’s education service. We play a key role in the preparation of teachers and in the provision of teacher professional and school leadership development programmes. We are committed to our vision of being An Institute of Distinction: Leading the Future of Education, and our mission to Inspire Learning, Transform Teaching and Advance Research. Read more about NIE here . NIE invites suitable applications for the position of Unit Head, Research Support and Grants Management , Office for Research. The Research Support and Grants Management Unit manages pre and post award administration of internal and external research grants, enabling NIE faculty to secure research funding and administer grants effectively in compliance with funding and institutional requirements.  The unit also oversees all Research Support functions in capacity building faculty staff.   As the Unit Head of RSGM, you will lead a team overseeing research support, grants management and administration and play a key leadership role in providing strategic oversight and direction in strengthening institutional research capabilities and drive NIE’s strategic research agenda. Responsibilities Provide strategic leadership and oversight of the Research Support and Grants Management Unit within the Office for Research. Work closely with the Dean, Associate Deans and Assistant Deans in strategic planning and implementation of research support and grants management initiatives. Ensure alignment of unit activities, processes and initiatives with NIE’s institutional priorities and research agenda. Bridge and integrate research support and grants management functions to ensure coherent and effective operations. Provide guidance and advisory support to team members on research support, grants administration and related operational matters. Liaise with academic departments, research centres, administrative units and external parties on grants-related matters. Oversee grants management compliance, audit readiness and adherence to funder and institutional guidelines. Prepare and present reports on grants matters, research funding and research support initiatives to senior management and stakeholders. Lead the planning, coordination and implementation of research support initiatives and capacity-building programmes. Represent the unit in roadshows, presentations and engagement sessions on research support initiatives. Work with academic departments to promote and implement research support programmes and related activities. Oversee the administration of Education Research Funding Programme (ERFP) and non-ERFP grant programmes. Coordinate research data management and governance matters where relevant. Drive process reviews and improvements, including the adoption of AI initiatives, to strengthen governance, operational efficiency and service delivery. Oversee and maintain standard operating procedures, ensuring workflows remain current and effective. Supervise, mentor and support the team to ensure operational excellence and strategic alignment. Plan team workload, support capacity building and promote continuous professional development. Support in any other duties, as assigned by the reporting officer. Requirements A University Degree. Minimum 5 to 8 years of relevant experience in research administration, grants management, research support, policy coordination, or a similar administrative leadership role. Knowledge of audit, risk, and compliance frameworks related to grants and research administration. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to review processes and implement improvements. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to prepare reports, briefs, presentations, and updates for senior management. A strong team lead who is highly motivated and also able to collaborate within and across teams. Strong interpersonal and relationship management skills. Integrity and discretion when handling confidential information. Proficient in using Microsoft Office applications and administrative systems relevant to grants or research operations. Closing Date   14 September 2026. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Other Information NIE staff can take chartered buses at their own expense from or near their home to the NIE campus. This is subject to the availability of seats. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Assessment_R00025473": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Assessment",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Student and Academic Services Department (SASD) is a dedicated team committed to delivering comprehensive support across the entire student life cycle—from admission and matriculation to graduation and beyond the classroom. SASD works collaboratively with schools, colleges, and autonomous institutes to ensure a seamless and enriching academic journey for all students. This position sits with the Office of Academic Services (OAS), which plays a key role in advancing the University's educational goals through implementing and administering the academic policies and services within the University.  Being part of a team that manages students’ assessment, progression and award, the key responsibilities of the role are as follows: Processing of academic results: creation of exam records, course withdrawal, handle dissertation results related matters, marks processing, release and review of results. Maintain and update academic records for students on Leave of Absence, credit transfer, exemptions, programme withdrawal and change of programme. Post release of results activities: support administration of Medals and Prizes, compile and filing of mark lists and reports, and provide the relevant student academic information to stakeholders within the NTU community. Support the degree conferment process and regular data provision to MOE. Manage queries received from role-based mailbox and maintain access for secured folders. Attend to queries from stakeholders (e.g. students and Schools) on areas related to academic records. Support senior officers implementing policies and guidelines for proper governance, and to assist in advising Schools on procedures and guidelines. Support business process streamlining, designing of workflow, process automation and system enhancements. Requirements:  Degree/ Diploma holders with at least 3 years of working experience in administration functions. Entry-level candidates are welcome. Candidates with prior experience in administrative roles will have an added advantage. Proficient in office IT applications and Microsoft Office suite of application. Possess working knowledge of database and process management. Familiar with the Personal Data Protection Act, in relation to collection, use and disclosure of student personal data. Working knowledge of VQL will be an added advantage. Experience and exposure to Robotic Process Automation (RPA) or AI tools will be an added advantage. Meticulous and organised. Proactive, efficient and able to multi-task. Able to work independently and be a good team player. Good communication skills, able to express ideas clearly and concisely (written and oral). Good interpersonal skills and able to collaborate with people at different levels of the organization. Service-oriented mindset. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Housekeeping-Manager--Nanyang-Executive-Centre--Hospitality-_R00025647": {
      "title": "Housekeeping Manager, Nanyang Executive Centre (Hospitality)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe NTU Office of Commercial and Auxiliary Services (OCAS) is responsible for the strategic planning, management, and marketing of commercial real estate, hospitality (including Nanyang Executive Centre) and auxiliary services (car parks and shuttle bus services) in NTU main campus and NTU@one-north. The Nanyang Executive Centre (NEC) is located at the NTU Main Campus. NEC features 150 refurbished guestrooms and refreshed event spaces that aims to offer a premier venue for high-level conferences, workshops, executive programmes, and industry engagements.    We are looking for an experienced person to join us as the Housekeeping Manager. The Housekeeping Manager will be responsible for establishing and maintaining high standards of cleanliness and organization throughout the NEC, including guest rooms, public areas, and back-of-house spaces. This role involves leading and training the housekeeping team, managing inventory, and collaborating with other departments to ensure a positive guest experience. Pre-opening duties will include setting up the housekeeping department, developing procedures, and preparing the team for the NEC’s launch. You will be responsible for executing Pre-Opening Tasks, assisting with the setup and organization of the housekeeping operations, participating in the development of operational procedures, standards & training staff on all aspects of service standards. KEY RESPONSIBILITES Create and implement housekeeping procedures and standards to ensure a clean, safe, and comfortable environment for guests and staff. Manage the daily activities of the housekeeping staff, including scheduling, training, and performance management. Ensure that all rooms and public spaces are cleaned and maintained to the highest standards. Accountable for departmental budgeting and P&L. Monitor the inventory of housekeeping supplies and equipment and make recommendations for purchases. Ensure compliance with all safety and health regulations and standards. Work with other departments to ensure the overall guest experience is positive and consistent. Participate in the recruitment and hiring process of new housekeeping staff. Essential Skills: Leadership and Team Management:  The ability to motivate, guide, and manage a team of housekeepers.  Communication:  Effective communication skills to interact with staff, guests, and other departments.  Organizational Skills:  The ability to plan, prioritize, and manage multiple tasks and responsibilities.  Attention to Detail:  The ability to notice and correct even minor imperfections in cleanliness and maintenance.  Knowledge of Cleaning Products and Techniques:  Understanding the appropriate use of cleaning supplies and equipment.  Problem-Solving:  The ability to identify and resolve issues related to housekeeping operations and guest requests.  Financial Management:  Understanding budgeting and cost control principles.  Customer Centric:  Service oriented style with professional presentations skills. REQUIREMENT Bachelor’s degree in Sales & Marketing, Hotel Management or relevant discipline. Diploma holders with extensive experience may be considered. Minimum 3-5 years of experience in housekeeping management within a hotel. Experience with accommodation/hotel pre-opening would be highly advantageous. Strong organizational and leadership skills. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Knowledge of safety and health regulations and standards. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager---Assistant-Manager--Faculty-Affairs_R00025648": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager / Assistant Manager, Faculty Affairs",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Materials Science and Engineering at Nanyang Technological University, Singapore offers a dynamic environment for education, research and innovation in materials science and engineering. The Senior Assistant Manager/Assistant Manager, Faculty Affairs provides strategic and operational leadership for the School’s faculty affairs portfolio, covering recruitment and appointments, faculty lifecycle administration, engagement and recognition, space and infrastructure matters, academic events, reporting and related operations. Working within the governance framework and directions of the College of Engineering and the University, the role translates College and University requirements into effective School-level plans and processes. The role works closely with School leadership, faculty committees, the College, HR and relevant University offices to deliver accurate, timely and professional outcomes. Key Responsibilities: 1. Faculty Recruitment, Appointment and Reappointment Lead and manage the end-to-end faculty recruitment lifecycle, including recruitment, appointments, onboarding, appraisal, promotion, and reappointment. Develop and implement recruitment strategies to attract and retain high-calibre academic talent. Ensure all faculty appointment processes are accurate, efficient, and compliant with University policies, governance requirements, and timelines. Drive continuous process improvements to deliver a seamless and positive experience for faculty and stakeholders. 2. Faculty Development, Culture & Engagement Drive initiatives to foster a collaborative, inclusive, and high-performing faculty culture. Lead the annual faculty performance appraisal process from planning to completion, ensuring timely completion, data integrity, data confidentiality, fairness and compliance with institutional policies.  Support faculty career development, leadership development and succession planning initiatives. Manage faculty welfare and case matters, including well-being, peer-to-peer issues, and student-faculty matters. 3. Space & Infrastructure Planning Lead the planning and management of faculty offices, researcher workspaces, research-focused laboratories, and shared facilities to optimize space utilization and support the School’s academic and research priorities.  Support policy development, strategic planning, data analysis, and documentation related to space and infrastructure management.  4. Stakeholder Management & Governance Serve as the primary liaison for faculty affairs-related queries from the Chair and senior leadership. Coordinate with College of Engineering to ensure consistent implementation of faculty-related policies, procedures and strategic initiatives. Engage with HR, finance, and administrative teams to align faculty affairs with broader institutional goals. 5. Strategic Planning, Data Management & Operations     Maintain accurate and up-to-date faculty records and databases to support budgeting, reporting, and strategic decision-making. Analyse faculty-related data and prepare management reports, dashboards, presentations, and briefing materials for senior leadership. Identify opportunities for continuous process improvement through data analysis and operational review. Provide operational guidance and support to team members, contributing to an effective, collaborative, and service-oriented work environment. Qualifications: A recognised Bachelor's, Master's, or PhD degree (or equivalent) with at least 5 years of relevant experience in people management, faculty administration, human resources, or a related field. Strong organisational, planning, and project management skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities effectively. Excellent stakeholder management and interpersonal skills, with the ability to build trusted relationships across all levels. Ability to balance strategic thinking with hands-on operational execution. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with a data-driven approach to decision-making. High level of integrity, professionalism, and discretion in managing confidential and sensitive information. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive---Executive--Finance-Department---NIE-_R00023103": {
      "title": "Senior Executive / Executive (Finance Department) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nABOUT THE NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF EDUCATION (NIE) The National Institute of Education (NIE), Singapore, is Singapore’s national teacher education institute and we are proud to be an integral part of the nation’s education service. We play a key role in the preparation of teachers and in the provision of teacher professional and school leadership development programmes. We are committed to our vision of being An Institute of Distinction: Leading the Future of Education and our mission to Inspire Learning, Transform Teaching and Advance Research. Read more about NIE here . NIE invites applicants for a Senior Executive / Executive position in the Finance Department . The Senior Executive / Executive plays a critical role in providing payroll and claims administration support for the Institute and ensuring accurate and timely payroll posting and claim processing for all employees within the organization. He/She oversees the payroll posting and claims administration, ensures compliance with statutory requirements, government legislation and group policies and standards, supports reporting needs and attends to queries from staff and stakeholders.  Responsibilities Manage payroll administration support including the monthly payroll postings for both full-time and part-time staff, statutory contributions and period end closing activities. Process payroll-related payments including but not limited to education allowances, passage claims and other miscellaneous payments. Perform finance related activities including but not limited to journal entries, reclassifications, and general ledger (GL) postings. Ensure employee claims submissions are accurate and in compliance with group policies and standards. Support budget submission and evaluation. Prepare and maintain regular and ad hoc requests of management reports/data by staff. Provide payroll posting related information for internal and external audits. Address employee inquiries and concerns related to payroll and claim posting. Educate employees on payroll and claim-related policies and procedures. Ensure the confidentiality of payroll data. Ensure service levels and targets are consistent with standards and timeliness, and service is delivered to customers in accordance with pre-defined Service Level Agreement. Support in various payroll and claim related projects and initiatives. Requirements A Polytechnic Diploma or Degree preferably in Accountancy, Business or its equivalent. Preferably 2 or more years of working experience in handling payroll or claims. Some experience in finance matters, with accounting knowledge, will be an advantage. Organized, meticulous in handling data and a service-oriented mind-set. A positive attitude and willingness to learn and adapt, with problem-solving skills. An effective team player with the ability to work independently is preferred. Ability to prioritize and plan work activities in an organized manner, able to multi-task, track and deliver assignments on schedule. Proficient in Microsoft Office applications, especially Excel is a must. Experience in SAP and Ariba would be an added advantage. Closing Date The closing date of the advertisement is 7 September 2026 . We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Other Information NIE staff can take chartered buses at their own expense from or near their homes to NIE campus.  This is subject to the availability of seats. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Project-Officer--Clinical-Trials---Translational-Research-_R00025393": {
      "title": "Project Officer (Clinical Trials & Translational Research)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJoin Our Team at the School of Biological Sciences, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore The School of Biological Sciences (SBS), part of the College of Science, was established in 2002 with a mission to advance biological and biomedical sciences. At SBS, our research spans various areas, including infectious diseases, immunology, neurodegenerative diseases, telomere biology, and genome function. Over the years, SBS has attracted talented individuals from around the world and Singapore to join as scientific leaders and researchers. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/sbs. We are looking for a Project Officer with a background and strong interest in integrative oncology, traditional Chinese medicine, Tai Chi and exercise therapy, massage therapy, or music therapy, to join the Yang Lab at NTU (https://www.ntu.edu.sg/sbs/Research/lab-pages/yang-mingxiao-lab). The successful candidate will contribute to an interdisciplinary project evaluating the clinical efficacy and biological mechanisms of traditional, complementary, and integrative medicine (TCIM) interventions for symptom management in cancer populations. The role will focus on coordinating clinical trials and supporting laboratory operations, bridging patient-centered trial activities with bench-based biospecimen handling and multiomics investigations. Through this work, the candidate will be well-positioned to grow at the interface of clinical and laboratory science, while shaping a distinctive academic and professional trajectory. Key Responsibilities: Coordinate randomized clinical trials, including ethics/IRB application and regulatory compliance Manage trial logistics, patient recruitment, scheduling, and follow-up Provide and/or coordinate integrative medicine treatments to study participants Oversee collection, processing, and management of clinical data and biospecimens Conduct data entry, curation, quality control, and preliminary analyses Oversee laboratory operations, ensuring compliance with institutional and local safety regulations and good laboratory practices Manage procurement of equipment, reagents, and consumables Train and onboard new research staff and students Liaise with clinical collaborators, institutional partners, and external stakeholders Support project reporting and documentation for funding and administrative purposes Engage in and contribute to other research activities the Lab is focusing on Job Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in life sciences, biomedical sciences, public health, social sciences, or related field A practitioner license issued by a foreign or international authority (i.e., traditional Chinese medicine, massage therapy, physical therapy, exercise therapy, etc.) registerable in Singapore Training or experience in complementary and integrative medicine practice or research from a reputable university At least 1-2 years of relevant experiences in clinical trial coordination, IRB submissions, or patient-facing research (entry-level candidates with strong interest are welcome to apply) Familiarity with biospecimen collection and handling, molecular biology, or omics techniques Good written and oral communication skills Proficiency in data management, statistical analysis, or clinical research software Strong organizational and project management skills Excellent interpersonal skills to work both independently and collaboratively within a multidisciplinary team Demonstrated interest in integrative medicine, oncology, or translational research The College of Science seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive---Assistant-Manager--Student-Care---Pastoral-Support_R00025643": {
      "title": "Senior Executive / Assistant Manager, Student Care & Pastoral Support",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Undergraduate Office is seeking a Senior Executive/Assistant Manager to support the Lead, Student Care & Development in providing timely and caring support to undergraduate students who may be experiencing academic, personal, social or adjustment difficulties. This is a developmental role with structured exposure, coaching and on-the-job learning to build capability in student care and pastoral support. Key Responsibilities: Provide first-line support, information and regular follow-up to students, and escalate concerns requiring further assessment or professional intervention. Coordinate student case follow-up, appointments, referrals and administrative support, including relevant academic support processes. Maintain accurate, timely and confidential case records, trackers, summaries and reports. Support academic intervention and outreach for students experiencing academic or attendance difficulties, including faculty mentoring referrals. Support student wellbeing, transition, adjustment and integration programmes, including logistics, communications, participation tracking and feedback. Maintain student-care data, assist with reporting and simple analysis, and support process improvement, digitalisation and student-facing resources. Work collaboratively across the Undergraduate Office and with relevant faculty and University support units. Role Boundary: The incumbent is not expected to independently manage high-risk or complex cases, provide professional counselling, or make crisis-intervention decisions. Such matters are escalated to the Lead and/or appropriate University professional services. Requirements: Diploma or Degree in Education, Psychology, Social Sciences, Social Work, Counselling, Community Services or a related discipline; candidates from other disciplines with a strong interest in student development and pastoral care may also be considered. 1–3 years of relevant working experience would be advantageous. Relevant education, youth work, student services, social services, community engagement, internship, volunteering, mentoring or student-development experience is useful. Empathy, patience, good listening and interpersonal skills, strong follow-up and organisation, appropriate judgement and escalation, confidentiality and discretion, and good written and verbal communication. Proficiency in Microsoft Office; familiarity with databases, Microsoft Forms, SharePoint or similar digital tools would be advantageous. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTUOne-North-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Director--Legal_R00025646": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Director, Legal",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe NTU Investment Office which manages the University’s multi-billion-dollar global investment fund, is seeking to add an experienced Fund Counsel to join its team. The successful candidate will work on complex investments across a broad range of asset classes, transaction structures and geographies. Reporting to the Chief Investment Officer, the Fund Counsel will work closely with investment professionals and key stakeholders, providing legal support throughout the investment lifecycle and helping to identify and manage legal, regulatory and contractual risks. Responsibilities: Review and advise on fund and investment structures, transaction terms and related legal documentation. Negotiate investment terms and transaction documentation with counterparties and external counsel. Advise investment teams on key legal, contractual, governance and regulatory considerations. Provide commercially focused legal advice that balances investment objectives with appropriate risk management. Requirements: Degree in Law from a reputable institution. Minimum 10 years of post-qualification legal experience. Strong experience in investment transactions, fund structures, corporate transactions, private markets and/or financial investments. Ability to work independently and manage multiple matters in a fast-paced investment environment. Strong communication, negotiation and stakeholder management skills. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Student-Experience-and-Vibrancy_R00025385": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Student Experience and Vibrancy",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Student and Academic Services Department (SASD) provides comprehensive support across the student life cycle—from admission and matriculation to graduation and beyond. SASD works closely with schools, colleges, and autonomous institutes to ensure a seamless and enriching academic journey. Within SASD, the Student Affairs Office (SAO) plays a central role in shaping student life through leadership development, student-led activities, residential life, integration efforts, community engagement, arts, and sports. The successful candidate will support in the planning and execution of two flagship initiatives – the NTU Varsity Arts Programme and the inaugural NTU Arts Festival, while extending NTU’s Cultural presence into the western precinct and enriching arts and cultural life across the Halls of Residence. Key Responsibilities NTU Varsity Arts Programme Support year-round planning and delivery – coordinating performances, showcases and development opportunities for student artists. Work with Varsity Arts groups, coaches, and venues to keep programme on schedule and within budget, and establish the routines (calendars, booking, logistics). Inaugural NTU Arts Festival Assist in programme development, stakeholder engagement and partnership coordination. Manage festival project timelines, logistics, procurement and budget tracking. Coordinate marketing and publicity effors with internal and external stakeholders. Support onsite festival operations and ensure smooth event execution. Arts & Cultural Vibrancy in Halls of Residence Bring arts and culture into residential life by working with residential experience stakeholders to seed performances, workshops, pop-ups and student-led creative activities within the halls. Connect hall-based arts activity to the wider Varsity Arts Programme and Festival so residential life becomes a feeder and stage for campus arts. Neighbourhood & Stakeholder Engagement  Support the mission in broadening the reach of NTU Arts Festival beyond campus by establishing partnerships with residents, community groups, and public/private organisations. Through community-based arts activations and outreach initiatives, create meaningful opportunities for public participation and engagement, contributing to stronger community connections and elevating NTU's reputation as a vibrant arts and cultural hub. Requirements Degree in any discipline; entry-level candidates are welcome to apply. Candidates with experience in arts/cultural programming, event or festival management and/or related field will have an added advantage.  Strong interpersonal, communication, and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to build positive working relationships and engage effectively with diverse groups of stakeholders. Good organisational and project management capabilities, with the ability to coordinate multiple workstreams, manage timelines, and ensure smooth execution of programmes and events. A collaborative team player with a service-oriented mindset and the ability to work independently when required. Comfortable managing operational, logistical, and administrative aspects of events and programmes, including procurement, budgeting, and stakeholder coordination. Proficient in Microsoft Office applications. Willingness to work occasional evenings and weekends to support programme delivery, performances, festivals, and student engagement activities as required. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive---Assistant-Manager---Lab-Operations-and-Tech-support_R00025642": {
      "title": "Senior Executive / Assistant Manager – Lab Operations and Tech support",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-07\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout NTU Nanyang Technological University (NTU) is one of the world’s top research-intensive universities, committed to nurturing talent and creating knowledge for a better world. Earth Observatory of Singapore (EOS) is a leading research unit within NTU dedicated to advancing understanding of Earth’s systems, environmental change, and natural hazards. As teaching and research in Asian School of the Environment (ASE) is closely tied with EOS; we work closely with each other ensuring that all lab environments meet regulatory standards and are well-equipped to support research and academic activities. About the Role We are looking for a proactive and detail-oriented professional to join the team within ASE/EOS at NTU. In this role, you will play a key part in ensuring our research laboratories and office facilities are safe, compliant, operating efficiently and aligned with NTU’s research and education goals – directly supporting world-class scientific research. The incumbent will also work closely with and influence stakeholders to achieve the team’s operational and strategic objectives. Key Responsibilities Oversee laboratories equipment maintenance/certification, ensuring equipment under the custodian of the laboratory are always in safe working condition, complying with local regulations as well as OEM requirements. Liaise and coordinate with service engineers, vendors and contractors for laboratories maintenance, repairs, site surveys and facilities related works. Oversee the chemical inventory management system and hazardous waste disposal processes, ensuring proper documentation, safe handling practices, and compliance with Singapore regulatory and institutional safety requirements. Ensure chemical inventories are properly maintained, updated, and reconciled by laboratories in compliance with institutional safety policies. Plan, conduct, and support laboratory and office safety inspections, audits, and compliance reviews, ensuring proper documentation, audit readiness, and timely closure of findings. Lead the investigation of safety incidents, accidents, and non-compliance cases, including root cause analysis, and development of corrective and preventive actions to prevent recurrence. Track, monitor, and ensure timely follow-up and closure of all safety-related incidents, breaches, and rectification actions across laboratories and office facilities. Conduct safety induction briefings and training sessions for new staff, students, and research personnel, including fieldwork safety awareness and laboratory safety requirements. Monitor the completion of mandatory Online Safety Modules for staff and students, in accordance with University requirements. Oversee the maintenance and readiness of emergency response equipment, including first aid and fire safety equipment in laboratories and office areas. Support the preparation of fieldwork safety equipment and consumables. Support continuous improvement initiatives in laboratory operations, workplace safety and health, and facilities management to enhance efficiency, compliance, and service quality. Serve as a key operational point of contact for laboratory operations, safety, and facilities matters, ensuring adherence to safety standards and regulatory compliance. Provide backup support to other laboratories and safety personnel as required to ensure continuity of laboratory operations and safety coverage. Provide administrative and operational support to the OPS team, including coordination, documentation, reporting, and other ad-hoc duties as required. Requirements Bachelor’s degree in related field is preferred. At least 1–2 years of relevant experience in laboratory operations, facilities management, or safety administration. Knowledge of local safety regulations and guidelines relevant to typical research and laboratory activities, preferably in an IHL setting. Strong organisational and coordination skills with the ability to effectively manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to engage and collaborate effectively with diverse internal and external stakeholders at all levels. Strong analytical and problem-solving abilities, with the capability to identify issues, determine root causes, and implement appropriate corrective and preventive measures. High attention to detail, particularly in maintaining accurate records, documentation, and compliance-related reporting requirements. A proactive team player who is also able to work independently with minimal supervision and demonstrate initiative when required. We seek a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Artificial-Intelligence--Computer-Science--Data-Science-_R00025623": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Artificial Intelligence, Computer Science, Data Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nEstablished as a partnership between Nanyang Technological University (NTU) and the National Healthcare Group (NHG), the Asian Centre for Health Behavioural Insights & Interventions (HABITS) aims to improve population health through multidisciplinary and translational research to support interventions, policy and programmes; strengthen national capabilities through the integration of translational research into health intervention processes; and increase Singapore’s regional and international profile as a centre of excellence for health behavioural sciences. We are looking for a Research Fellow to work closely with the Centre’s Pillar Leads and Directors to support the management of research projects and the development of competitive research grant applications. The role will focus on project management, research expertise, managing and day-to-day research operations, such as data storage, budgets, expenses, assets, and ethics approvals. Key Responsibilities: Develop, validate, and deploy AI algorithms for digital health and AI-driven research projects. Lead technical innovation by exploring and implementing emerging AI methodologies. Support data platform development and retrospective data collection and analysis. Collaborate with researchers, clinicians, coordinators, and biostatisticians to deliver project outcomes. Publish research findings in high-impact journals and present results to investigators and collaborators. Prepare technical reports and research updates for project leadership. Mentor junior AI researchers and contribute to capability building within the team.   Job Requirements: PhD in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Mathematics, Engineering, or a related field. Entry level candidates with demonstrated expertise in artificial intelligence (AI), machine learning, deep learning, or digital health technologies. Strong expertise in developing and applying AI solutions to real-world healthcare challenges. Good understanding of clinical research and healthcare data. Proficiency in machine learning, deep learning, and advanced AI techniques. Strong analytical, problem-solving, and communication skills. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant--Natural-Hazards-_R00025631-1": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Natural Hazards)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Earth Observatory of Singapore (EOS) is a University Research Institute at Nanyang Technological University Singapore that conducts fundamental research on earthquakes, volcanic eruptions, tsunamis, and climate change in and around Southeast Asia, towards safer and more sustainable societies.  For more details, please view http://www.earthobservatory.sg. EOS are looking for a Research Assistant in the areas of natural hazards. The candidate will work under the supervision of Susanna Jenkins and will collaborate with researchers from the ‘ Integrating Volcano and Earthquake Science and Technology (InVEST) in Southeast Asia’ project, a 5-year project that aims to provide a holistic understanding of regional tectonics, volcanoes, the linkages between the two, and their cascading hazards and impacts in Singapore and Southeast Asia.  Key Responsibilities: Collect and analyse data from natural hazards Support the team in simulating natural hazards and critically evaluating results Write technical reports, with the aim of publishing results in scientific journals Requirements: BSc in relevant area, e.g. geography, computer science, physics, earth/environmental science Experience with coding and GIS preferred An interest in natural hazards and their impacts. A quantitative mindset Good written and oral communication skills We seek a diverse and inclusive workforce and are committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Quantum-Physics-_R00025636": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Quantum Physics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJoin Our Team at the Centre for Quantum Technologies , Nanyang Technological University, Singapore The Centre for Quantum Technologies is a pioneering quantum centre in the world offering a diverse research culture at the intersection of three different fields, namely, theoretical, experimental Physics and computer science. We offer competitive salary and enriching intellectual experience in a city known for its forward outlook. This program also allows strong collaboration with leading academic and industrial groups within and outside the country. We are seeking a Research Fellow to be in charge of an experimental apparatus aiming to develop a quantum processor based on Neutral Atom Arrays. The role will focus on developing the experiment, data acquisition and analysis, and supervision of undergraduate and PhD students. Key Responsibilities Develop numerical twins for digital quantum computer Develop mapping of many-body problems into class of Hamiltonians compatible with our experimental machines Report on at least on a weekly basis to the principal investigator Supervise and train young researchers Job Requirements PhD in Theoretical Physics, with a specialization in Quantum Physics, Optics, or a closely related field Proven knowledge, experience, or exposure to areas such as condensed-matter physics, AMO physics, and Rydberg physics. Ability to work independently and in collaboration with an experimental research team. Experience in supervising or mentoring students or junior researchers would be advantageous. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Director--Administration_R00025640": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Administration",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Air Traffic Management Research Institute (ATMRI) at Nanyang Technological University (NTU), Singapore, was established in 2013 through a collaboration between NTU and the Civil Aviation Authority of Singapore (CAAS). Its mission is to conduct cutting-edge research in air traffic management (ATM) to support Singapore's position as a leading air hub and drive innovation in the Asia-Pacific region. ATMRI focuses on modernizing and harmonizing regional airspace operations to sustain the rapid growth of air transportation in the region. Its strategic research areas include artificial intelligence and data analytics for ATM, urban aerial transport systems, regional ATM modernization, exploratory studies on emerging technologies, and talent development through PhD programs. The institute aims to generate world-class ATM research, find innovative solutions, and catalyze transformation in the field. It plays a pivotal role in advancing the efficiency, safety, and sustainability of air traffic management systems. The Assistant Director, Administration provides strategic and operational leadership for ATMRI’s administrative functions. Reporting to the Director, the job holder oversees governance, finance, human resources, research programme administration, agreements, stakeholder engagement and institutional communications. The role supports the effective operation of the Institute, ensures compliance with University and funding-agency requirements, and facilitates the timely delivery of programme and institutional objectives. Job responsibilities: Lead the development, implementation and review of administrative policies, processes and operational plans. Oversee budget planning, expenditure monitoring, claims, financial reporting and audit readiness in accordance with NTU policies and funding requirements. Coordinate recruitment, onboarding, contract renewal, performance appraisal and other HR matters for research and administrative staff. Supervise and develop the administrative team, allocate responsibilities and ensure effective service delivery. Coordinate Governing Council and Scientific Advisory Panel appointments, meetings, papers, minutes, decisions and follow-up actions. Establish and maintain systems for monitoring research programme budgets, milestones, KPIs, deliverables, risks and contractual obligations. Coordinate programme reviews, claims, audits and submissions to funding agencies and oversight bodies. Manage the administrative coordination of MOAs, Project Agreements, Variation Agreements, MOUs, NDAs and other institutional agreements with NTU corporate offices and external partners. Maintain appropriate registers, records and evidence trails for governance, finance, agreements, programme reporting and compliance. Act as a key liaison with NTU corporate offices, government agencies, funding bodies, academic institutions and industry partners. Coordinate institutional communications, events, website content and outreach activities in accordance with NTU policies. Provide advice and administrative support to the Director and Institute Management Team on operational, governance and programme matters. Education qualifications: Recognised Bachelor’s Degree in Business Administration, Finance, Public Policy, Human Resource Management, or a related field. Postgraduate qualifications (e.g., MBA, MPA) will be advantageous. Relevant experience: Minimum 8 years of relevant working experience is preferred. Proven experience in administrative management, financial oversight, HR management, research programme management, and stakeholder engagement in a research center or university setting. Experience working with senior leadership, managing committees (e.g., Governing Councils, Scientific Advisory Panels), and coordinating large-scale institutional projects. Skills: Financial management skills. Human resource management skills. Corporate communication skills. Administrative skills. Statistical and data analysis. Competencies: Excellent written and oral communication skills. Good planning and organisation skills. Good problem solving and analytical skills. Good public relations, communication and influencing skills. Strong leadership and interpersonal skills. Able to work independently and as a team. Good supervisory skills. Proficiency in financial management tools and marketing platforms. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Finance--Accounts-Receivable-_R00024812": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Finance (Accounts Receivable)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNTU Shared Services (NSS) Finance is responsible for the efficient and effective operation of the finance related transaction services. One of the divisions in Accounts Receivables function is Student Finance. Student Finance oversees the end-to-end process of student billing and collection. Key responsibilities include monitoring accounts receivable, managing outstanding debts, enforcing credit control, and preparing management reports. This position is part of the Student Finance team reporting to Account Receivables Team. The job is required to process timely and accurate billing, collection of revenue, journal posting, prepare management reporting and financial aid disbursement. It ensures completeness in revenue recognition and compliance to University’s standard guideline and policy. This role will support functional process improvement and streamlining to meet university mission and vision. Candidate has an opportunity to learn more than 1 system in billing and collection, involve in system implementation and learn automated tools in process improvement. Qualification: Knowledge and Experience Minimum Degree / Equivalent Qualification in Accounting Minimum 5 years of relevant working experience Key Competency Requirements Able to work in a fast-paced environment and to work under pressure Service oriented, be hands-on, meticulous, analytical and have initiative Good interpersonal & communication skills Proficient in MS Excel and IT savvy, SAP knowledge is preferred Knowledge of Power Query or Power Automate is an advantage Able to work independently and collaboratively within a team We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Research-Fellow--Humanities---Social-Studies-Education-Department---NIE-_R00025639-1": {
      "title": "Senior Research Fellow (Humanities & Social Studies Education Department) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe National Institute of Education invites suitable applications for the position of Senior Research Fellow on an 18-month contract at the Humanities & Social Studies Education Department . Project Title: The characterization, mechanism, predictability, and impacts of the unprecedented 2023 Southeast Asia heatwave Project Introduction: In April and May 2023, Southeast Asia experienced an unprecedented heatwave, with temperatures exceeding 42°C across the region and Thailand recording a historic 49°C. This project examines the event's spatiotemporal evolution, synoptic conditions, driving mechanisms, forecasting performance, return period, and multi‑sectoral impacts using high‑resolution meteorological data, satellite imagery, and climate models. It evaluates both natural drivers (El Niño, monsoon anomalies) and anthropogenic factors (urban heat islands, greenhouse gas emissions). The findings will improve forecasting, inform regional policy, and serve as educational resources for NIE's curriculum. By advancing research, transforming teaching, and inspiring learning, this project strengthens NIE's role in preparing future generations to address climate change challenges. Requirements: Ph.D. in Climate Science, Atmospheric Science, Environmental Science, Computer Science, AI/Data Science, Remote Sensing, Urban Sustainability, or a related field. Experience with Linux-based high-performance computing environments and GPU computing. Proven experience in weather and climate models development and applications. Experience in machine learning, deep learning, or AI applications for atmospheric modeling. Proficiency in Python and experience with AI/ML frameworks such as PyTorch or TensorFlow. Experience handling large geospatial, atmospheric, or remote sensing datasets is preferred. Strong analytical and programming skills. Strong scientific writing skills. Experience in publishing research findings in peer-reviewed journals. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in interdisciplinary research teams. Responsibilities: Develop and apply AI-assisted weather and climate models with high spatial and temporal resolution. Integrate remote sensing, observational, and numerical model datasets for climate and urban sustainability applications. Conduct research on urban climate processes, including urban heat island effects, boundary layer dynamics, air pollution, and building energy consumption. Apply machine learning and statistical approaches for climate risk assessment, prediction, and scenario analysis. Analyze large-scale atmospheric, environmental, and geospatial datasets. Support the development of innovative AI tools and workflows for climate and sustainability research. Collaborate with interdisciplinary research teams and external stakeholders. Prepare scientific manuscripts, technical reports, and conference presentations. Contribute to grant proposals and ongoing research projects. Any other duties as assigned by the Principal Investigator. Application Applicants (external and internal) will apply via Workday. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Closing Date Closing date for advertisements will be set to 14 calendar days from date of posting. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Humanities---Social-Studies-Education-Department---NIE-_R00025638": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Humanities & Social Studies Education Department) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe National Institute of Education invites suitable applications for the position of Research Fellow on a 25-month contract at the Humanities & Social Studies Education Department . Project Title: FastTrackAI: Fast-Tracking AI for Scientific Discovery with Accelerated Networking and Computation on Modern Architectures in Singapore Project Introduction: The advancement of accelerated computation and communication technologies is driving the progression of modern AI. However, current efforts are predominantly concentrated on Large Language Models (LLMs) tailored for industrial applications, leaving AI for Science with inadequate attention and support. This proposal addresses the gap by focusing on the development of optimized implementations for AI for Science workloads. Bespoke communication and computation libraries specific to particular architectures are often difficult-to-use as soon as one deviates from mainstream language models to multi-model AI for Science workloads. The result can be inefficient and slow training and inference, increasing costs and decreasing researcher productivity by orders of magnitude. To overcome these challenges, we propose to design and develop the first performance-portable software optimization and communication stack for AI for Science workloads. The compute acceleration is achieved using dataflow optimization techniques that integrate with scientific simulations to enable efficient use of new capabilities such as combination of simulation and AI models. The communication acceleration will be compatible with both current and next-generation communication infrastructures, such as InfiniBand and Ultra Ethernet. Our project will also deliver a comprehensive set of PyTorch libraries, encompassing various optimized models for scientific applications, including Graph Neural Networks (GNNs), Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs), and Transformers. These resources will be made available to researchers across different scientific domains. Ultimately, this initiative will empower scientists to effectively leverage the computational infrastructure available in Singapore, addressing the most complex and demanding AI for Science problems with enhanced efficiency and efficacy. With Singapore pledging to spend one billion dollars on AI in the near future and possible performance optimizations of more than 10x, the impact of our work could be transformational. Requirements: PhD in Hydrology, Computing, Earth science or a related field Proficiency in remote sensing, geographic information systems, and statistics Proficiency in programming with Python, R, and Google Earth Engine Minimum 3 years of relevant working experience in an academic environment Experience in academic report writing or paper publication Experience with geography fieldwork Able to work independently and possess strong follow-through skills A team player in a multi-cultural environment Strong communication and organization skills Strong analytical, problem-solving and writing skills Responsibilities: Conduct independent and collaborative research work Manage research project Liaise and work with research stakeholders and vendors Prepare literature reviews to synthesize prior studies Propose, design, and implement appropriate research methodologies Remote sensing and field data collection, storage and archival General quantitative data analysis Writing of reports, publications, and presentation materials Planning and executing tasks to achieve key deliverables Any other administrative duties as assigned by Principal Investigators Application Applicants (external and internal) will apply via Workday. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Closing Date Closing date for advertisements will be set to 14 calendar days from date of posting. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate---Research-Fellow--Electrical---Electronics-_R00025242": {
      "title": "Research Associate / Research Fellow (Electronics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Emerging nanoscience Research Institute (EnRI) focuses its research on advanced materials, computational modelling & simulation and development of small-scale testing and materials characterization.  We are looking for a Research Associate / Research Fellow to support micro device research and development work. The role will work closely with the project team on the full spectrum of project activities, including experimental design, device fabrication, testing, and data analysis. Key Responsibilities: Design, develop and fabricate micro devices with desired performance that meet project requirement Provide research support to the project team and laboratory, including equipment maintenance, troubleshooting issues, and managing consumables Document methodologies, results, and findings in technical reports and presentations Job Requirements: Master’s (for Research Associate equivalent) / PhD (for Research Fellow equivalent) qualification degree in Electrical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Materials Science, Applied Physics, or related field Experience in high-reliability microelectronics Familiar with micro-fabrication techniques and semiconductor processing Experience in conducting electrical pulse testing Good written and oral communication skills A collaborative team player with strong interpersonal skills and a proactive and willingness to learn mindset Actual appointment grade will depend on candidate’s qualification and experience We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Construction-Technology-and-Protective-Engineering--CTPE--Laboratory_R00025548": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Construction Technology and Protective Engineering (CTPE) Laboratory",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Senior Executive, Construction Technology and Protective Engineering (CTPE) Laboratory is responsible for overseeing the day-to-day operations of the CTPE Laboratory in the School of Civil and Environmental Engineering (CEE), ensuring the efficient management of facilities, equipment, resources, and safety compliance. This key role drives operational excellence through the optimization of workflows, implementation of process improvements, and adoption of innovative laboratory and workshop practices Key Responsibilities: Serve as the primary person in charge of the workshop, managing laboratory and workshop operations, facilities, equipment, resources and schedules. Provide technical expertise in machining, fabrication and Computer Numerical Control (CNC) operations. Support faculty, researchers and students with fabrication, laboratory and technical requirements. Ensure safety, risk management, compliance and equipment maintenance. Oversee procurement, inventory, asset management and operational budgets. Train and mentor students, researchers and staff in equipment use and safe workshop practices. Drive process improvement, innovation and digital transformation in laboratory operations. Requirements Degree in Civil, Environmental, Mechanical Engineering or a related field, with at least 3 years’ relevant experience in laboratory/workshop operations, preferably in an academic or research environment. A Diploma in Engineering or related field with at least 5 years’ relevant experience may be considered. Proven expertise in machining, fabrication, CNC tools and workshop operations. Knowledge of construction technology, protective engineering equipment, laboratory safety and digital tools. Strong commitment to safety, compliance and operational excellence. Excellent organisation, communication, collaboration and mentoring skills, with strong attention to detail and multitasking ability. Passion for innovation, digital transformation and sustainable solutions. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant--Centre-for-Research-in-Pedagogy-and-Practice---NIE-_R00025635-1": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Centre for Research in Pedagogy and Practice) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe National Institute of Education invites suitable applications for the position of Research Assistant on a 12-month contract, renewable, at the Centre for Research in Pedagogy and Practice . Project Title: Developing and Validating a Comprehensive Multi-Perspective, Accountable, and Explainable System of Standards for Learning Analytics and Artificial Intelligence in Education (CoMPA(I)SS) Project Introduction: This project aims to develop and validate a framework designed to support the trustworthy, accountable, and explainable adoption of Learning Analytics (LA) and Artificial Intelligence in Education (AIEd). The project involves conducting a SWOT analysis of existing LA and AIEd frameworks, consulting international experts, administering stakeholder surveys, and implementing pilot case studies across educational contexts. The final outcome will be a validated framework to guide researchers, developers, educational leaders, teachers, and students in the ethical and effective use of AI and learning analytics technologies. Requirements: Bachelor's degree in Education, Social Sciences, Psychology, Learning Sciences, Data Analytics, Computer Science, Information Studies, Law, Public Policy, or a related discipline. Prior research experience in educational research, learning analytics, artificial intelligence in education, educational technology, technology governance, ethics, or related fields Familiarity with ethics review processes, research protocol development, research governance requirements, and issues related to AI, privacy, data protection, and accountability Knowledge and experience in qualitative and/or quantitative research methods. Experience in literature reviews, framework analysis, SWOT analysis, survey administration, and/or thematic/content analysis Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Ability to work independently and collaboratively within a multidisciplinary research team. Strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and ability to manage project timelines. Preferred Qualifications Experience in research project management and coordination. Proficiency in data management and analysis software (e.g., NVivo, SPSS, R, Python, or equivalent). Responsibilities: Assist with overall project management and coordination of research activities. Assist in developing research protocols, instruments, and study procedures. Conduct comprehensive literature reviews and synthesize findings. Perform SWOT analyses of existing Learning Analytics and AIEd frameworks. Coordinate and support engagement with international expert panel members. Assist with survey development, administration, participant recruitment, and data collection. Manage research databases and ensure proper data storage, documentation, and governance. Conduct quantitative data analysis, including data cleaning, descriptive statistics, inferential statistics, and survey data analysis, with supervision. Conduct qualitative data analysis, including content analysis, thematic analysis, coding of interviews and focus group discussions, and cross-case analysis, with supervision. Support qualitative data collection for pilot case studies, including interviews, focus groups, observations, and collection of reflective artefacts. Assist in the preparation of reports, presentations, conference papers, and journal manuscripts for the dissemination of research findings. Liaise with stakeholders, including researchers, educators, industry partners, and educational institutions. Undertake other duties related to the project as assigned by the Principal Investigator. Application Applicants (external and internal) will apply via Workday. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Closing Date Closing date for advertisements will be set to 14 calendar days from date of posting. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Librarian--Digital-Scholarship---Education_R00025634": {
      "title": "Senior Librarian, Digital Scholarship & Education",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is a leading research-intensive university known for its strong focus on innovation, interdisciplinary learning, and creating meaningful impact through education and research. The Student and Academic Services Department (SASD) plays an important role in supporting students across their academic journey, from admission and matriculation to graduation and beyond the classroom. Working closely with schools, colleges, and other partners across the University, SASD helps to create a seamless, enriching, and student-centred experience at NTU. Within this broader mission, NTU Libraries , under the Office of Information, Knowledge and Library Services (OIKLS) , provide essential learning, research, and collaborative environments that support the University community. We are seeking an experienced Senior Librarian, Digital Scholarship & Education to lead digital scholarship, academic integrity, reference management and library learning services that support the University’s teaching, learning and research needs. Key Responsibilities Lead the planning, delivery and evaluation of digital scholarship programmes, tools and learning resources. Champion responsible reference management and academic integrity practices through training, outreach and expert support. Evaluate and enhance reference management software and related digital scholarship tools based on user needs and service priorities. Develop instructional frameworks, learning programmes and online resources for undergraduate, postgraduate and Continuing Education and Training learners. Build stakeholder partnerships and outreach initiatives to increase awareness, engagement and adoption of library services. Monitor emerging trends in digital scholarship, AI-enabled tools and instructional practices to guide service improvement. Requirements Master’s degree in information studies or equivalent, with a bachelor’s degree in any field. At least seven years of relevant experience in academic, research or special libraries. Strong knowledge of reference and citation management, digital scholarship and information literacy instruction. Good research, communication, collaboration, organisational and stakeholder engagement skills. Proactive, adaptable and committed to continuous learning and service improvement. At NTU, you will join a collaborative and forward-looking university environment committed to continuous learning, innovation, and service excellence. This role offers the opportunity to work across diverse library settings, partner stakeholders across the University, and contribute to improvements that have meaningful and visible impact on the campus community. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Executive--Finance-Department---NIE-_R00022754": {
      "title": "Executive (Finance Department) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nABOUT THE NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF EDUCATION (NIE) The National Institute of Education (NIE), Singapore, is Singapore’s national teacher education institute and we are proud to be an integral part of the nation’s education service. We play a key role in the preparation of teachers and in the provision of teacher professional and school leadership development programmes. We are committed to our vision of being An Institute of Distinction: Leading the Future of Education and our mission to Inspire Learning, Transform Teaching and Advance Research. Read more about NIE here . NIE invites applicants for an Executive position in the Finance Department . This is a 3-year contract position . Responsibilities You will be part of the team which handles undergraduate billing and other student-related financial matters for the institute. Your responsibilities will include: Billing for undergraduate courses, hostels and facilities. Checking that all payment transactions have appropriate certification and approvals before being processed for payments. Responding to enquiries pertaining to facilities and student matters. Assisting in the design, implementation and review of financial processes, policies and guidelines for continuous improvements, through streamlining and automation. Participating in system implementation, enhancements, and user acceptance testing. Handling ad hoc duties as assigned. Requirements A Polytechnic Diploma in Accountancy or its equivalent. At least 2 years of financial administration and accounting work experience. Good organizational and communication skills. A positive attitude and willingness to learn and adapt, with problem-solving skills. An effective team player with the ability to work independently is preferred. Ability to prioritize and plan work activities in an organized manner, able to multi-task, track and deliver assignments on schedule. Self-motivated, energetic and results oriented. Proficient in Microsoft Office applications, especially Microsoft Word and Excel. Experience in SAP and Ariba would be an added advantage. Closing Date The closing date of the advertisement is 1 September 2026 . We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Other Information NIE staff can take chartered buses at their own expense from or near their homes to NIE campus.  This is subject to the availability of seats. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager--EdTech-Solutions_R00025633": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager, EdTech Solutions",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nShape the Future of Learning: Senior Assistant Manager, Educational Technology Solutions About Nanyang Technological University (NTU) Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is a world-class, research-intensive public university dedicated to providing a transformative education, advancing research, and nurturing global leaders. Driven by innovation, excellence, and a commitment to positive global impact, NTU fosters an inclusive and vibrant ecosystem where cutting-edge technology meets education. At InsPIRE - Educational Services, we implements, integrates, and optimises our digital learning ecosystem to deliver a seamless, user-centric and high-impact teaching and learning experience. We lead the deployment, integration, and enhancement of next-generation educational technologies and artificial intelligence (AI) solutions, ensuring world-class learning outcomes for faculty and students alike. The Opportunity We are seeking a dynamic, forward-thinking Senior Assistant Manager, EdTech  Solutions to join our dedicated team. In this pivotal role, you will be at the forefront of educational technology innovation, designing and deploying enterprise AI applications that directly transform teaching and learning across the university. Key Highlights of the Role Drive AI-Powered Innovation: Build and implement modern AI tools, smart agent frameworks, and enterprise educational applications that directly enhance student and faculty engagement. High-Impact Collaboration: Work closely with educators, technologists, and university leaders to solve complex educational challenges and transform digital learning paradigms. Modern Cloud & Systems Architecture: Architect, integrate, and manage scalable cloud applications on leading cloud infrastructure platforms. Role & Responsibilities Department: InsPIRE Educational Services Location: Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (Main Campus) Reporting To: Senior Assistant Director, Educational EdTech Solutions   As a Senior Assistant Manager, you will play a hands-on role in software development, AI tool integration, and stakeholder empowerment. Primary Duties: Solution Delivery & Software Development: Design, test, and deploy enterprise-grade software applications and AI-driven educational tools using Python and Java to improve learning outcomes and engagement metrics. Systems Integration & Scalability: Build secure, reliable integrations between learning management platforms and enterprise databases to enable smooth data flow and seamless user experiences. AI Tool Development & Framework Management: Harness Large Language Model application programming interfaces (APIs) and modern AI agent frameworks to build intelligent educational assistants and workflow automations. Stakeholder Enablement & Engagement: Partner with academic units and operational teams to understand user needs, provide technical guidance, and empower faculty and students to maximize the value of new technologies. Technical Documentation & Support: Maintain standardized, high-quality system architecture documentation to ensure smooth onboarding, efficient troubleshooting, and minimal system downtime. Technology Exploration: Continuously research, evaluate, and prototype emerging technologies in artificial intelligence, automation, and analytics to elevate educational service delivery. Why Join NTU? At NTU, we value our people as our greatest strength. Joining InsPIRE Educational Services means becoming part of an inspiring, supportive, and growth-oriented work environment. Continuous Learning & Professional Growth: Access extensive learning and development opportunities, professional certification programs, and workshops to keep your technical skills sharp in fast-evolving fields like AI and DevOps. Career Progression: Enjoy structured career development opportunities within a leading global university system. Staff Welfare & Hybrid Work Initiatives: Benefit from flexible work arrangements (including Work-From-Home options), comprehensive medical coverage, and regular university-wide employee engagement and team-building activities (CREW initiatives). Vibrant Campus Community: Experience a diverse, inclusive, and collaborative campus atmosphere equipped with world-class facilities. Candidate Qualifications & Requirements Must-Have Qualifications: Education: Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Information Technology, or a relevant technical discipline. Software Engineering Experience: At least 3+ years of hands-on backend software development experience using Python or Java in an enterprise environment. AI & Machine Learning Exposure: Practical experience building applications using Large Language Model (LLM) APIs (e.g., Gemini, OpenAI, Claude) and prompt engineering techniques. AI Agent Frameworks: Hands-on experience working with modern AI agent frameworks (e.g., LangGraph, Google ADK, Bedrock Agents). Cloud & DevOps Skills: Practical experience deploying containerized applications (using Docker) on cloud platforms (AWS or GCP) with standard Continuous Integration / Continuous Deployment (CI/CD) pipelines. Core Competencies: Excellent problem-solving skills, strong stakeholder engagement abilities, adaptable thinking, and high integrity. Good-to-Have Skills (Preferred): Experience with Infrastructure-as-Code (IaC) tools such as Terraform. Familiarity with container orchestration using Kubernetes. Prior experience working within higher education or ed-tech environments. How to Apply If you are passionate about leveraging technology to shape the future of education, we would love to hear from you! Please submit your updated CV and cover letter through the NTU Careers Portal. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager--Student-Discipline_R00025632": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager, Student Discipline",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Office of Student Conduct (OSC), Student Experience Office (SEO) is seeking to hire an independent and experienced Senior Assistant Manager to support the Associate Vice Provost (Student Conduct) and Senior Assistant Director in the running of the Office of Student Conduct which oversees the holistic administration of student discipline matters at NTU.     The incumbent is required to:  Provide secretariat support, including the management of discipline cases, to the Board of Discipline and Appeal Committee. Formulate and review policies and procedures on student discipline. Analyse trends of student misconduct and assist with the formulation of effective policies to foster student character development. Coach and guide Colleges/Schools/Departments on the management of discipline cases. Plan and organise workshops for stakeholders from Colleges/Schools/Departments. Establish a community of practice with partners from other local universities to share best practices. Prepare discipline statistics and reports. Facilitate the bi-annual external audit exercise on academic integrity processes, procedures and management of academic integrity offences by the Colleges/Schools. Oversee the data management of discipline records and provide guidance to Colleges/Schools/Departments on the proper housekeeping of these records. Oversee other matters pertaining to student discipline. Job Requirements: Degree with at least 7 years of work experience. Experience with case management and good knowledge of interview techniques. Experience working in IHL and track record in working with people from diverse background and levels.  Knowledge of Criminal Law, Penal Code, Rules and Legislation would be advantageous.   Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Presentation skills and workshop facilitations skills. Proficient in Microsoft Office applications and the use of IT towards operational productivity. Meticulous and good with data. Self-Motivated and takes initiative. Critical thinker and problem solver. Ability to multi-task, prioritize and meet tight deadlines. Excellent report writing ability would be necessary.  We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Math-Foundation-of-AI-_R00025629": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Math Foundation of AI)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences (SPMS) at NTU Singapore hosts research and education activities in two divisions: Division of Mathematical Sciences (MAS) and Division of Physics and Applied Physics (PAP). MAS covers diverse topics ranging from pure mathematics to the applications of mathematics in cryptography, computing, business, and finance. PAP covers many areas of fundamental and applied physics, including quantum information, condensed matter physics, biophysics, and photonics. Over the years, SPMS has attracted talented individuals from around the world and Singapore to join as scientific leaders and researchers. The group of Wang Zhongjian is looking for postdocs working on scientific computing and machine learning related topics. The funding is currently under a MOE grant entitled: Towards Infinite Dimensional Generative Models. The contract period of the position is up to three years subject to funding availability. Applicants should be familiar with and have track records in at least one of the following fields: approximation of neural networks, convergence of Langevin/MC sampling, analysis and algorithm design of interacting particle systems, operator learning, regularity theories in inverse/scattering problems. Once successful, the candidate is expected to transfer his expertise to machine learning/scientific computing in collaborations with other group members (phd students, exchange graduate students, etc). When projects are required, the group will provide reasonable GPGPU computing resources from the NSCC. The review of candidates will be conducted monthly until all the positions are filled. Once applied on Workday, the candidate may drop an email with application packages for faster screening. Key Responsibilities: Research Paper/proposal writing Teaching assisting Graduate student mentoring Job Requirements: Master’s degree in mathematics or related areas, with focus on numerical analysis or machine learning. Candidates who have submitted their PhD thesis or are awaiting thesis examination and award of the PhD degree are welcome to apply. Experience in computational math. Proficient in coding languages, such as C, C++, Fortran, and Python. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Strong publication record. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager--Research-Grant-Administration_R00023325": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager, Research Grant Administration",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nRoles and Responsibilities: The position will be responsible for the administration of research grants handled by NTU’s Research Support Office. This includes: Submission of research proposals and coordination of review panel meetings and the administration of awarded research grants. Be part of a team to handle the governance aspect of research data management relevant to research grants.  The role will also be involved in ad-hoc initiatives undertaken by the Office. Requirements: Degree in a relevant field with at least 5 years of proven experience in research grant administration. Strong time management, planning, and organisational skills, with the ability to handle multiple assignments. Fast learner who can work independently and adapt quickly. Strong analytical skills with keen attention to detail. Excellent writing, communication, and interpersonal skills. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Manager--Research-Grant-Administration_R00023326": {
      "title": "Manager, Research Grant Administration",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nRoles and Responsibilities: The position will be responsible for the administration of research grants handled by NTU’s Research Support Office. This includes: Submission of research proposals and coordination of review panel meetings and the administration of awarded research grants. Be part of a team to handle the governance aspect of research data management relevant to research grants.  The role will also be involved in ad-hoc initiatives undertaken by the Office. Requirements: Degree in a relevant field with at least 7 years of proven experience in research grant administration. Strong time management, planning, and organisational skills, with the ability to handle multiple assignments. Fast learner who can work independently and adapt quickly. Strong analytical skills with keen attention to detail. Excellent writing, communication, and interpersonal skills. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Grant-Management-_R00024908": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager (Grant Management)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe CyberSG R&D Programme Office (CRPO) is a new national centre at Nanyang Technological University, Singapore. CRPO will focus its efforts on three main thrusts to advance cybersecurity comprehensively: cutting-edge research and development, advancements in technology and translational development, and fostering ecosystem/industry growth and training. CRPO aspires to propel Singapore to the forefront of cybersecurity innovation and implementation, fueled by funding from the Cybersecurity Agency of Singapore (CSA). This financial backing empowers CRPO to finance visionary projects proposed by diverse entities, including research institutes (RIs), institutions of higher learning (IHLs), and industries. The scope of these initiatives spans the entire Technology Readiness Level (TRL) spectrum, from nascent concepts at TRL 1 to advanced, field-tested solutions at TRL 9, all within the dynamic realm of cybersecurity. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/crpo . As Assistant Manager (Grants Management), you will assist Team Lead to oversee the full lifecycle of grant programmes, ensuring robust governance, strategic alignment, and impactful outcomes. Key Responsibilities: Assist Team lead in grant strategy & programme design Co-Lead the design and implementation of grant programmes, including funding frameworks, thematic priorities, and evaluation approaches aligned with national cybersecurity objectives. Governance & Policy Development Enforce and maintain strong policies, procedures, and controls to ensure transparency, compliance, and accountability in grant administration. Evaluation & Funding Decisions Assist Team lead to oversee proposal evaluation processes, working with expert panels to ensure fair, rigorous, and strategic selection of projects with strong innovation and translation potential. Stakeholder Engagement Build and manage partnerships across universities, research institutes, industry, and government agencies to drive collaboration and alignment. Financial Stewardship Manage grant budgets and funding allocation, ensuring effective utilisation of resources and adherence to financial and audit requirements. Project Monitoring & Impact Delivery Oversee project performance, ensuring milestones, deliverables, and outcomes are achieved, with a focus on real-world cybersecurity impact. Programme Improvement Continuously enhance grant frameworks and processes through data-driven insights, stakeholder feedback, and benchmarking against global best practices. Leadership & Team Development Lead and develop a multidisciplinary team, fostering a high-performance culture and strong collaboration across functions. Job Requirements: At least a degree in a relevant field (e.g., business management, project management, cybersecurity, engineering, computer science, public policy, or related disciplines) At least 3 years of relevant experience in grant management, research administration, project or programme management Good understanding of research and innovation ecosystems, preferably in cybersecurity or deep technology domains Proven experience in designing and managing funding programmes or large-scale initiatives Good stakeholder management skills, with experience engaging across academia, industry, and government Demonstrated experience in complex projects Prior experience in coordination of internal review, approval, and submission processes Good analytical, strategic thinking, and decision-making capabilities Good-to-Have: Experience in public sector or national-level R&D programmes Familiarity with research translation, commercialisation, or innovation ecosystems Knowledge of financial governance, audit processes, and compliance frameworks Established network within the cybersecurity or technology community We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager--Data-and-Analytics_R00025570": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager, Data and Analytics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-07\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Office of Data and Analytics (ODA) at Nanyang Technological University is seeking a Senior Assistant Manager, Data and Analytics to support NTU’s strategic decision-making through rigorous data analysis, statistical modelling and evidence-based insights. The role contributes to institutional planning, university rankings and reputation, faculty and student outcomes, research analytics, and continuous improvement of data processes across the University. Job Responsibilities: Generate insights from both external and internal data to facilitate evidence-based decision making at all levels of the University.  Build databases, develop data analytics and implement strategies to optimize statistical efficiency. Refine existing processes and define new processes in data collection to support decision-making at all levels of the University. Work in teams of stakeholders across various units. Job Requirements: PhD in Social Sciences, Science, Technology, Engineering, Mathematics or a related discipline. Strong knowledge of applied statistics, empirical research methods and quantitative analysis. Experience handling, cleaning, validating and analysing complex datasets. Good coding skills; familiarity with Python and R will be advantageous. Ability to develop analytical models and communicate complex findings clearly to diverse stakeholders. Resourceful, resilient and collaborative, with good communication skills; data visualisation skills will be an added advantage. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager--Research-Management_R00025530": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager, Research Management",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Research Office at College of Humanities, Arts and Social Sciences oversees high quality college internal grant initiatives in addressing research funding needs of faculty. The Office provides seed funding to faculty members and commit to bolstering excellence in their external grant applications through grant admin support, high profile grant consultancy, and organisation of workshops that disseminate knowledge on grant writing and foster interdisciplinary research collaboration. This is in line with NTU's aspiration and continued rise as a leading research university, with research evolved to be more collaborative, global and interdisciplinary in nature. The incumbent works closely within CoHASS Research Administration at the College level to mobilise resources with the aim to increase discussions at conferences, symposia and workshops to bring forth interesting and important ideas leading to further research and collaboration, publications, and proposals for external grant applications. The incumbent would also provide secretariat support to Associate Dean (Research). Key Responsibilities: Research Grants Administration Co-lead and oversee the end-to-end administration of research grants , Drive and coordinate grant call launches with CoHASS Research Offices and Research Offices in other NTU colleges and institutions by facilitating review, approval and account creation processes with various parties. Take ownership of internal seed grant funding schemes of the College Research Office (including grants, such as the Startup Grants and MOE Tier 1 Seed grants) and SSHR 2030 Seed Grant scheme, throughout the entire lifecycle of the funding/grant scheme. Review seed grants administrative processes, analyse and recommend areas of process improvements, and follow through with providing consultation to School Research Offices on implementation of process improvements. Proactively engage and build relationships with PIs and research managers across Colleges’ and Institutes’ School Research Offices and obtain grant data, information and grant reports for application and variation/virement processing, and for regular monitoring. Serve as trusted advisor and problem solver , addressing complex faculty queries on research grants matters. Research publicity Co-lead the strategic planning and execution of innovative initiatives to enhance research engagement and participation in CoHASS internal grants, external competitive grants and SSHR 2030. Drive and oversee the activities of the College Research Centres fostering collaboration and multidisciplinary research partnerships among Schools to strengthen research impact and visibility. Co-lead research event publicity planning and execution efforts , proactively coordinate dissemination strategies, liasing with key NTU stakeholders and ensuring high quality content across websites, posters and electronic mailers that effectively showcase the college research office and research Centres, analyse and make recommendations on publicity initiatives that will enhance participation in key college events across schools and research centres. Data Management and Reporting Co-lead the development and implementation of robust processes and tools to enhance data management and reporting for the College Research Office and Centres, and SSHR 2030, ensuring accuracy, efficiency, and strategic alignment. Drive data governance and integrity by co-supervising the collection, management and reporting of research metrics, including research outputs at the College, Schools and Research Centre levels, as well as SSHR 2030 progress. Administrative and Secretarial support Provide high level administrative leadership and strategic support to Associate Dean (Faculty), ensuring seamless coordination of faculty related initiatives and operational efficiency. Drive collaboration and process improvements by working proactively with School Associate Chair (Faculty) Offices to enhance service excellence, make recommendations on streamlining administrative workflows, and ensure timely resolution of complex faculty-related requests. Lead the end-to-end management and delivery of the college driven programmes, working closely with Dean and relevant stakeholders to drive successful implementation and outcomes. Requirements: At least a degree in a relevant field (e.g., business management, project management, finance). Minimum 5 years of relevant experience in research development, grant writing, funding strategy or research management, preferably in a university, research institute, or R&D environment. Familiarity with Singapore research funding landscape (e.g., NRF, MOE, A*STAR) is advantageous. Experience in preparing large competitive research grant proposals or coordinating multi-investigator submissions. Excellent technical writing, analytical, organisational, and stakeholder engagement skills. Relevant experience in administration, research, grants, finance, compliance or stakeholder support would be advantageous. Strong organisational and analytical skills, with the ability to manage multiple deadlines, track deliverables and follow through on outstanding matters. Good communication skills and comfortable working with different stakeholders. Adaptable and willing to learn. Proficient in using digital tools for tracking, documentation and collaboration; familiarity with grant management systems would be an advantage. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Executive--Outreach--Industry-Partnerships-_R00025495": {
      "title": "Executive, Outreach (Industry Partnerships)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering (MAE) in NTU is renowned for its research prowess in advanced manufacturing, aerospace, biomedical, industrial, maritime engineering, and robotics. Aligned with Singapore’s RIE2030 strategy, MAE drives technological innovation, bolstering local manufacturing and engineering sectors. MAE offers comprehensive undergraduate programmes in Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering, ensuring students gain a robust engineering foundation and modern technological expertise. At the graduate level, MAE provides Master of Science programmes and Ph.D. opportunities that emphasize industry-relevant skills and cutting-edge research, preparing students for leadership roles in their fields. The Executive, Outreach (Industry Partnerships) supports the University’s mission by strengthening industry engagement, creating meaningful employment and internship opportunities for MAE graduate students, and enhancing graduate employability through coordinated outreach initiatives and strategic partnerships. Key Responsibilities: 1. Outreach & Stakeholder Engagement Identify target industries, associations, and potential partner organizations. Engage industry partners to identify and secure employment and internship opportunities for students. Event Planning & Coordination with Students and Programme Directors. Manage end-to-end planning for seminars and industry visits (concept, agenda, speakers, venues, logistics). Coordinate with speakers, venues, vendors, and internal teams to ensure seamless execution. Act as a backup or support lead for other organizational events (workshops, seminars) as needed, including planning, logistics, and on-site support. 2. Marketing & Communications Support Collaborate with Marketing to promote events through email campaigns, social media, and industry networks. Maintain accurate contact records, track outreach activities, and monitor attendance and engagement metrics. Requirements: Diploma in Business, Communications, Marketing, Public Relations, Human Resource or a related field. At least 3 years’ experience in partnerships or business development; experience with industry seminars or corporate visits is a plus; demonstrated ability to support other types of events is beneficial. Excellent written and verbal communication; persuasive and professional presentation skills. Project management with the ability to manage multiple events concurrently. Strong networking and relationship-building capabilities. Budgeting, vendor management, and contract negotiation skills. Skills & Competencies: Strategic thinker with a results-oriented mindset. Detail-oriented, organized, and proactive problem-solver. Ability to work collaboratively across departments and with external partners. Comfort with travel for on-site visits and events as required. Other Personal Attributes Team player. High Integrity & Confidentiality. Adaptability & Resilience. Customer-Centric Mindset. Financial Awareness. Collaborative & Team-Oriented. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/AI-Engineer--Data-Infra_R00025373": {
      "title": "AI Engineer, Data Infra",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAI Singapore (AISG) is a national AI programme launched by the National Research Foundation (NRF), Singapore, to build and anchor deep national capabilities in AI.  AISG is supported through a government-wide partnership including the NRF, Ministry of Digital Development and Information (MDDI), Infocomm Media Development Authority (IMDA), Economic Development Board (EDB) and Enterprise Singapore (ESG). We bring together research institutions and the vibrant ecosystem of AI start-ups and companies to support impactful research, develop talent, and power Singapore's AI efforts. This position will be hosted at Nanyang Technological University (NTU) under VP (Artificial Intelligence & Digital Economy)’s office and we welcome you to join our community. We're looking for an AI Engineer to join the Platform team within AI Products at AISG. In this role, you will design, build, and scale the data infrastructure that powers large language model (LLM) training, fine-tuning, evaluation, and retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) across the organisation. Your work will directly contribute to the architecture and reliability of data storage systems, data pipelines, and the compute infrastructure that supports large-scale AI workloads. Responsibilities: Data infrastructure and architecture Develop and maintain the overall data architecture, ensuring it scales to support AI training, fine-tuning, evaluation, and RAG workloads. Define and manage the data technology stack, evaluating and adopting tools that best fit evolving data needs. Build automation for data transfer and backup, and support data cataloging/discovery tools. Design and maintain data pipelines (batch and streaming) using tools like AWS Glue and Amazon EMR. Data governance and management Architect and govern org-level IAM policy across AWS Organizations including SCPs, cross-account roles, and permission boundaries to enforce least-privilege access at scale. Review and enhance data access patterns for performance and cost optimization. Develop and manage data analytics and dashboarding capabilities using tools like Amazon Athena and QuickSight to give stakeholders visibility into platform usage and cost. AI-assisted ops and continuous improvement Use AI tools (e.g. Claude, Copilot, Cursor) appropriately in your daily work responsibilities. Build internal tools leveraging AI to reduce manual effort in day-to-day operations. Requirements: You should be a hands-on engineer who enjoys both building robust infrastructure and designing tools that other engineers and researchers want to use. You should be comfortable balancing platform ownership (architecture, cost, governance) with product thinking (usability, self-service, adoption). A degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or equivalent. At least 2–4 years of data infrastructure, platform or systems engineering experience, with a track record of operating production systems at scale. Strong knowledge of distributed data systems and storage technologies (object storage, data lakes, distributed file systems, vector databases) and data pipelining tools (e.g. Apache Spark, Apache Airflow, Ray, Dagster). Working knowledge of data access control and data orchestration. Familiarity with cloud organisational structures (e.g. AWS Organizations, GCP folder/project hierarchy), including multi-account/multi-project setups, org-level IAM, and billing/cost allocation. Hands-on experience operating workloads on different cloud providers including IaC (e.g. Terraform), containers and orchestration (e.g. Docker, Kubernetes), and managed services for compute, storage, and networking. Demonstrated use of AI tools (e.g. Claude, Copilot, Cursor) in your day-to-day engineering — for code generation, review, debugging, and documentation — with a clear sense of where they help and where they don't. Solid scripting/programming skills (e.g. Python, SQL) and comfortable reading other people's code across the stack. Strong communication skills and a team collaborator. Good to Have: Experience with LLM training dataset (e.g. Common Crawl). C/C++/Rust/Go or other relevant programming languages. Contributions to open-source AI/ML projects. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/AI-Engineer--Platforms_R00025364": {
      "title": "AI Engineer, Platforms",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAI Singapore (AISG) is a national AI programme launched by the National Research Foundation (NRF), Singapore, to build and anchor deep national capabilities in AI. AISG is supported through a government-wide partnership including the NRF, Ministry of Digital Development and Information (MDDI), Infocomm Media Development Authority (IMDA), Economic Development Board (EDB) and Enterprise Singapore (ESG). We bring together research institutions and the vibrant ecosystem of AI start-ups and companies to support impactful research, develop talent, and power Singapore's AI efforts. This position will be hosted at the Nanyang Technological University (NTU) under VP (Artificial Intelligence & Digital Economy)’s office and we welcome you to join our community. We're looking for an AI Engineer to join the Platform team within AI Products at AISG. In this role, you will be collaborating with different internal teams to design and implement optimized inference workflows and support the team to build customized LLM-based solutions. Your work will directly contribute to the deployment, optimisation and management of large language models (LLMs) in production, retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) services, AI agent orchestration platforms and GPU-enabled AI infrastructure. Responsibilities: Platform operations and reliability Own day-to-day operations of SEA-LION API Farm, our multi-cloud LLM inference platform — monitoring environment health, GPU capacity, performance, cost, and security posture. Optimise LLM inference across various modalities to drive business value and support production goals. Diagnose and troubleshoot performance and reliability issues on API Farm. Build new API services such as batch API services, MCP services. Infrastructure, CI/CD, and automation Manage high performance AI clusters and storage systems using infrastructure-as-code (e.g. Terraform) across different cloud providers. Develop and maintain CI/CD pipelines, container build/registry workflows, and deployment automation so teams can ship safely and frequently. Strengthen observability across the stack including logs, metrics, traces, and dashboards, and reduce toil by automating repetitive operational tasks. AI-assisted ops and continuous improvement Use AI tools (e.g. Claude, Copilot, Cursor) appropriately in your daily work responsibilities. Build internal tools leveraging AI to reduce manual effort in day-to-day operations. Requirements: You should be a hands-on engineer who is comfortable operating cloud and GPU infrastructure end-to-end, who understands how to deploy and run large language models reliably in production, and who actively uses AI tools to make platform work faster and more reliable. A degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or equivalent. 1–3 years of DevOps, SRE, or platform engineering experience, with a track record of operating production systems at scale. Hands-on experience operating workloads on different cloud providers including IaC (e.g. Terraform), containers and orchestration (e.g. Docker, Kubernetes), and managed services for compute, storage, and networking. Strong knowledge on Inference frameworks and libraries (e.g., vLLM, SGLang, TensorRT-LLM, Transformers). Hands-on experience deploying and serving LLMs in production — model serving, GPU scheduling, autoscaling, latency/throughput optimisation, and inference cost management. REST API design, model context protocol (MCP), Internet authentication patterns (e.g. OAuth). Strong fundamentals in CI/CD, observability (logs/metrics/traces), and incident response. Demonstrated use of AI tools (e.g. Claude, Copilot, Cursor) in your day-to-day engineering — for code generation, review, debugging, and documentation — with a clear sense of where they help and where they don't. Solid scripting/programming skills (e.g. Python, Bash) and comfortable reading other people's code across the stack. Strong communication skills with the ability to explain technical concepts. Good to Have: Experience with multimodal AI models (e.g. vision language models, audio language models). C/C++/Rust/Go or other relevant programming languages. Contributions to open-source AI/ML projects. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/AI-Engineer--AI-Products-_R00024969": {
      "title": "AI Engineer (AI Products)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAI Singapore (AISG) is a national AI programme launched by the National Research Foundation (NRF), Singapore, to build and anchor deep national capabilities in AI.  AISG is supported through a government-wide partnership including the NRF, Ministry of Digital Development and Information (MDDI), Infocomm Media Development Authority (IMDA), Economic Development Board (EDB) and Enterprise Singapore (ESG). We bring together research institutions and the vibrant ecosystem of AI start-ups and companies to support impactful research, develop talent, and power Singapore's AI efforts. The AI Products Pillar of AI Singapore develops AI-powered products and solutions that benefit Singapore and the region. We are looking for an AI Engineer to contribute to the development, training, evaluation and engineering of state-of-the-art multilingual, multicultural and multimodal foundation Large Language Models (LLMs), with a focus on underrepresented languages and cultures and real-world AI applications. The role involves working at the intersection of frontier LLM research, large-scale data engineering, distributed model training, evaluation, and productisation. This position will be hosted at the Nanyang Technological University (NTU) under VP (Artificial Intelligence & Digital Economy)’s office and we welcome you to join our community. Key Responsibilities: Develop, train, fine-tune and evaluate multilingual, multicultural and multimodal foundation LLMs and related technologies, including continued pre-training, supervised fine-tuning, instruction tuning, preference optimisation and model adaptation. Build and maintain scalable data pipelines for multilingual text ingestion, cleaning, filtering, deduplication, tokenisation, contamination detection and dataset mixture creation. Support large-scale distributed model training workflows, including experiment tracking, checkpointing, training monitoring, debugging, profiling and compute optimisation. Review frontier AI and LLM research papers, reproduce relevant methods, and translate research findings into practical improvements in model training, evaluation and deployment workflows. Contribute to reusable engineering assets such as training scripts, evaluation tools, model artefacts, APIs, documentation and deployment-ready components. Collaborate with internal teams, external research labs, academic institutions, industry partners and ecosystem stakeholders on LLM research, development and knowledge-sharing activities. Support AI Singapore’s community-building efforts through technical sharing, seminars, workshops, publications or other outreach activities where relevant. Requirements: We welcome applicants from all disciplines and qualification pathways, including NITEC, Diploma, Bachelor’s, Master’s or PhD holders, as well as candidates with equivalent practical experience. A formal qualification in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, Data Science, Engineering, Mathematics, Computational Linguistics or a related field would be advantageous but is not mandatory. Candidates should be able to demonstrate the following skills and experience: Strong AI/ML engineering capability:  Proficient in Python with strong software engineering practices, including clean and modular code, Git, testing, documentation and code review. Hands-on experience with PyTorch and modern NLP/LLM frameworks, especially the Hugging Face ecosystem such as Transformers, Datasets, Tokenizers, Accelerate and TRL. LLM development and multilingual NLP expertise:  Experience or strong working knowledge in LLM pre-training, continued pre-training, fine-tuning, instruction tuning, preference optimisation, evaluation and model adaptation. Familiarity with multilingual NLP challenges such as low-resource languages, code-switching, language imbalance, script diversity, tokenisation issues and multilingual benchmark design. Large-scale data and training pipeline development:  Ability to build scalable pipelines for text processing, dataset preparation and model training. Familiarity with distributed training concepts, GPU-based training, checkpointing, experiment tracking, training stability and compute optimisation. MLOps, infrastructure and deployment:  Familiarity with Linux environments, Docker, CI/CD concepts, cloud platforms or GPU/HPC clusters. Experience with reproducible model development workflows, model versioning, evaluation automation and deployment through APIs or serving frameworks such as vLLM, SGLang, TGI or equivalent tools would be advantageous. Research, problem-solving and communication:  Able to read and evaluate research papers, design experiments, conduct ablation studies, analyse results and translate findings into practical model or system improvements. Able to communicate technical concepts, trade-offs and evaluation outcomes clearly to both technical and non-technical stakeholders. Personal attributes:  Self-directed learner with strong curiosity, high ownership and resilience. Collaborative, rigorous and engineering-minded, with a commitment to reproducibility, reliability, documentation and responsible AI development. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Laboratory-Operations_R00024160": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Laboratory Operations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nEstablished in 1981, the School of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering (MAE) at Nanyang Technological University (NTU) is one of the largest mechanical engineering schools globally. With a distinguished faculty and a vibrant community of undergraduate and graduate students, MAE is renowned for its cutting-edge research in advanced manufacturing, aerospace, biomedical, industrial, maritime engineering, and robotics. The Assistant Manager supports business operations within the Thermofluids and Marine cluster, including but not limited to Seatrium New Energy Lab.  The incumbent will support full-time/part-time undergraduate lab sessions, facilitate lab users to achieve their academic and research goals efficiently in areas of safety, security, asset procurement, maintenance and data protection. Responsible for: Support lab teachings throughout the academic year. Supervise undergraduates and postgraduates on conduct of risk assessments, safety training online modules and other SOPs requirements under the workplace, safety and health management system. Perform lab’s requisition via Ariba on behalf of faculty members, researchers for their teachings and research needs. Responsible for lab equipment maintenance/certification, ensuring equipment under the custodian of the laboratory are always in safe working condition, complying to local regulations as well as OEM requirements. Responsible for lab asset management, ensuring assets under the custodian of the laboratory are properly accounted for. Participate in internal/external audit preparation, ensuring lab documents are updated, properly documented and organized for auditing. Requirements: Degree in relevant engineering disciplines. At least 3 years of relevant experience. Familiarity with laboratory equipment and protocol. Knowledge in ISO45001, Risk Management. Knowledge in WSH requirements and other regulatory requirements such as NEA, SCDF. Knowledge in SAP Ariba, IBM Workday, Office 365 suites. Analytical, good observational skills and problem-solving abilities. Resourceful. Able to support part-time classes (after office hours). Operational knowledge of combustion engines and conventional fabrication equipment – lathe, milling, drill and cutting machine. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager--Annual-Giving_R00025547": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager, Annual Giving",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe University Advancement Office (UAO) supports NTU’s giving mission by fostering meaningful relationships and strategic partnerships with philanthropists, alumni, business community partners, corporations that result in goodwill and philanthropy towards education and research that underpin a shared sustainable future. Reporting to the Senior Assistant Director , the Senior Assistant Manager, Annual Giving plays a pivotal role by cultivating a broad-based, sustainable culture of giving across the University community. The role is directly accountable for designing, developing, and executing creative annual giving campaigns targeting students, parents, as new and recurring donors. Beyond the transactional, this role strengthens the pipeline of long-term philanthropic relationships, converting graduating students and engaged stakeholders into lifelong supporters of NTU, thereby sustaining the University's endowment and programme development goals. Main Responsibilities: Engage key stakeholders—including faculty, staff, students, parents and alumni—to foster a culture of giving and support Annual Giving programmes. Conceptualise, develop and execute dynamic and relevant graduation giving campaigns and programmes to drive sustained giving and achieve fundraising targets. Collaborate closely with colleagues to co-promote projects, campaigns and marketing collateral. Ensure integrated and consistent marketing efforts that maximise campaign effectiveness and support the overall objectives of the team. Requirements: A university degree in any discipline. Diploma holders with relevant experience may be considered. Minimum of 4 years’ relevant experience in marketing communications, event management and/or fundraising. Strong interpersonal, communication and relationship-building skills, with the ability to engage, motivate and interact effectively with stakeholders at all levels. Strong project management and organisational skills, with the ability to manage multiple programmes and deliverables concurrently. Creative and resourceful, with the ability to develop engaging campaigns and initiatives that encourage participation and giving. A strong team player who is able to collaborate effectively with colleagues and stakeholders across different functions. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Grant-Support_R00023364": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Grant Support",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Air Traffic Management Research Institute (ATMRI) at Nanyang Technological University (NTU), Singapore, was established in 2013 through a collaboration between NTU and the Civil Aviation Authority of Singapore (CAAS). Its mission is to conduct cutting-edge research in air traffic management (ATM) to support Singapore's position as a leading air hub and drive innovation in the Asia-Pacific region. ATMRI focuses on modernizing and harmonizing regional airspace operations to sustain the rapid growth of air transportation in the region. Its strategic research areas include artificial intelligence and data analytics for ATM, urban aerial transport systems, regional ATM modernization, exploratory studies on emerging technologies, and talent development through PhD programs. The institute aims to generate world-class ATM research, find innovative solutions, and catalyze transformation in the field. It plays a pivotal role in advancing the efficiency, safety, and sustainability of air traffic management systems. Key Responsibilities: Oversee manpower planning and administration through RISE, including approvals, budget checks, expenditure monitoring, and reporting. Lead finance functions and timely reporting. Act as the point of contact for finance and operational matters with research teams, institutional offices, and external partners. Oversee planning and execution of events, meetings, visits and institute-wide activities. Job Requirements: Bachelor’s degree or equivalent in Business, Communications, Public Policy, or related discipline. 6–8 years of relevant experience in project administration and programme coordination. Experience in higher education, research administration, or public-sector programmes preferred. Strong organizational skills, with the ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously. Effective communication and stakeholder management abilities. Familiarity with project management tools and MS Office suite. This is a yearly renewable contract position subject to performance and funding requirements.  We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Director-Senior-Assistant-Director--Gift-Stewardship-and-Reporting--Stewardship_R00024899": {
      "title": "Assistant Director/Senior Assistant Director, Gift Stewardship and Reporting, Stewardship",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe University Advancement Office (UAO) supports NTU’s giving mission by fostering meaningful relationships and strategic partnerships with philanthropists, alumni, business community partners, corporations that result in goodwill and philanthropy towards education and research that underpin a shared sustainable future. Reporting into the Deputy Director, Stewardship, the Senior Assistant Director of Gift Stewardship and Reporting plays a pivotal role in managing the stewardship and reporting functions for major donors at NTU. This role is primarily responsible for developing and executing comprehensive fund stewardship procedures. Working collaboratively with faculties, the position ensures effective donor fund utilisation by aligning donor contributions with institutional needs, while maintaining adherence to donor intentions and organisational priorities. Key responsibilities include Monitoring of Donor Fund Utilisation: Work with Faculties to ensure the allocation and administration of donor funds are used according to donor intentions and organisational priorities. Monitor the effectiveness of fund utilisation and provide transparent reporting on fund impacts. Develop, implement and improve upon processes to aid the accurate monitoring of these funds. Impact Reporting: Supervise the preparation and delivery of detailed impact reports for major donors. Ensure reports accurately reflect the outcomes and achievements resulting from their contributions, and maintain high standards of reporting accuracy and integrity. Data Management and Analysis: Ensure the accuracy and confidentiality of donor records within the CRM system. Track and analyse donor engagement data to inform strategic decisions and maintain compliance with reporting standards. Stewardship and Donor Engagement: Develop and implement strategic plans to recognise and engage major donors. This involves creating tailored recognition programs, managing personalised communications, and fostering strong donor relationships to enhance engagement and retention. Faculty Engagement: Collaborate with faculty members to ensure that donor funds are utilised effectively. Align donor contributions with faculty needs and projects and facilitate communication between faculty and donors to demonstrate the impact of their support. Strategic Alignment: Work closely with leadership to align stewardship initiatives with NTU’s strategic goals. Contribute to long-term planning and goal-setting to support the university’s growth and success. Requirements: A good university Degree, preferably Master’s Degree in Accountancy, Finance, Economics, or Engineering fields. Minimum of 10 - 12 years’ progressive experience, preferably within higher education, philanthropic organisations or a comparably complex organisation. Demonstrated success in achieving strategic outcomes in a large and complex environment. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to think strategically and critically. Proficiency in numerical analysis to derive insights that can improve strategies, polices and processes is essential. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with a track record of engaging stakeholders across all levels. Excellent ability to innovate and deal with ambiguity and organisational sensitivity with tact and diplomacy; to be opportunistic, responsive, resourceful, and resilient. Demonstrate a clear understanding and awareness of ethical considerations pertaining to advancement work, as well as an understanding and appreciation of cultural and intercultural sensitivities. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Admissions-and-Outreach_R00024951": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Admissions and Outreach",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering (MAE) in NTU is renowned for its research prowess in advanced manufacturing, aerospace, biomedical, industrial, maritime engineering, and robotics. Aligned with Singapore’s RIE2030 strategy, MAE drives technological innovation, bolstering local manufacturing and engineering sectors. MAE offers comprehensive undergraduate programmes in Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering, ensuring students gain a robust engineering foundation and modern technological expertise. At the graduate level, MAE provides Master of Science programmes and Ph.D. opportunities that emphasize industry-relevant skills and cutting-edge research, preparing students for leadership roles in their fields. The Senior Executive, Admissions and Outreach strengthens the University’s strategic admissions and outreach efforts for MSc and PhD programmes, with a focus on expanding engagement in China and attracting high-quality global applicants. Through data-informed admissions support, cross-functional coordination, and a positive applicant experience, the role contributes to the University’s mission of advancing academic excellence, internationalisation, and a diverse, high-calibre graduate student community. Key Responsibilities: Support Overall Graduate Admissions, Outreach and Market Development Strategies. Support MSc/PhD admissions and outreach to meet enrolment targets and strengthen the graduate recruitment pipeline. Drive China-market recruitment through market analysis, planning, partnerships, outreach channels, and compliance oversight. Develop dashboards and analyse admissions, outreach, conversion, and market data to guide recruitment actions. Coordinate with school and university stakeholders to ensure consistent messaging and a professional applicant experience. Graduate Admissions – Strategic and Operational Administration. Support admissions target-setting, intake planning, and budgeting, with focus on China recruitment priorities. Coordinate eligibility, compliance, documentation, and audit trail requirements for local and international applicants. Provide Chinese-language applicant support and monitor response times to ensure timely, accurate engagement. Improve admissions processes to enhance conversion, reduce gaps, and support a smoother applicant journey. Manage admissions communications across Chinese digital platforms with accurate, consistent messaging. Outreach – Market Expansion and Engagement. Manage China-focused candidate funnels from awareness to enrolment, with coordinated channels, timelines, and follow-ups. Build partnerships with Chinese agents, universities, alumni, and institutions to expand outreach and referral pipelines. Plan and support recruitment events for China-based applicants with locally tailored content and engagement. Localise recruitment content for China audiences while ensuring accuracy, brand alignment, and regulatory compliance. Track outreach effectiveness, diversity, inclusion, and geographic reach, while supporting consistent campaign messaging. Stay updated on China regulations, digital platform requirements, mobility policies, and market trends to keep outreach relevant and compliant. Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration, Marketing or a related field. Minimum of 3 years of relevant experience in admissions, international recruitment, or related strategic roles, with demonstrated success and strong familiarity with the China market. Strong knowledge of the China market, including student recruitment trends, education landscape, stakeholder networks, and market dynamics. Strong programme or project management skills across complex pipelines and varying stakeholders. Deep understanding of higher education admissions, data privacy and regulatory landscapes. Excellent cross-cultural communication and relationship-building. Data-driven mindset with hands-on analytics experience. Skills & Competencies: Strategic thinking with execution excellence. Clear written and verbal communication. Problem-solving and proactive planning. Familiarity with marketing channels and event workflows. Resilience and adaptability; crisis communication skills. Other Personal Attributes Team player. High Integrity & Confidentiality. Adaptability & Resilience. Customer-Centric Mindset. Financial Awareness. Collaborative & Team-Oriented. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/AI-Engineer--Full-Stack_R00024983": {
      "title": "AI Engineer, Full Stack",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAI Singapore (AISG) is a national AI programme launched by the National Research Foundation (NRF) to anchor deep national capabilities in Artificial Intelligence (AI). Hosted by the Nanyang Technological University (NTU), AISG brings together all Singapore-based research institutions and the vibrant ecosystem of AI start-ups and companies developing AI products to perform use-inspired research, grow the knowledge, create the tools, and develop the talent to power Singapore's AI efforts. We're looking for an AI Engineer, Full Stack to join the Data Platform team within AI Products at AISG. ATLAS Data Platform is a data platform which supports a global effort to collect multimodal language and cultural data. You'll develop modules end-to-end for this platform from UI/UX through to backend services and deploy them on cloud infrastructure. You'll work heavily with AI tools in your day-to-day engineering workflow, and you'll build features that support evaluations, benchmarks, and data annotation across our internal teams and external partner communities. This role calls for solid engineering fundamentals, comfort working across the stack, and an appetite for shipping. This position will be hosted at the Nanyang Technological University (NTU) under VP (Artificial Intelligence & Digital Economy)’s office and we welcome you to join our community. Duties & Responsibilities: Platform development and engineering Design, build, and maintain modules of the data platform across the full stack such as frontend interfaces, backend services, APIs, and data models to support multimodal data collection, curation, and access. Use AI tools (e.g. Claude, Copilot, Cursor) deliberately in your engineering workflow for code generation, refactoring, code review, debugging, and documentation and help the team codify good practices around AI-assisted development. Write clean, well-tested, maintainable code; participate in code reviews and design discussions; and contribute to the platform's technical documentation. Domain workstreams: evaluations, benchmarks, and annotation Build features and tooling that support model and data evaluations, benchmark execution, and result tracking across the platform. Develop interfaces and workflows for data annotation used by internal teams and external community partners including task design, quality control, reviewer workflows, and progress tracking. Integrate with relevant evaluation frameworks, benchmark suites, and annotation tools, and help the team make sound build-vs-adopt decisions. Infrastructure and deployment Deploy and maintain platform UI/UX and backend services on Google Cloud Platform (GCP) and Amazon Web Services (AWS), including configuration, networking, and storage. Set up and maintain CI/CD pipelines, monitoring, logging, and alerting to ensure reliability, performance, and security across environments. Manage cloud resources cost-effectively, and contribute to architecture decisions on scalability, multi-region considerations, and data residency. Collaboration and delivery Work closely with the Project Manager, data engineers, researchers, and external partners to translate requirements into shippable features at a steady cadence. Participate in incident response, post-mortems, and continuous improvement of the platform's operations. Requirements: You should be a hands-on full stack engineer who is comfortable across frontend, backend, and cloud, and who actively uses AI tools to move faster and produce higher-quality work. The ideal candidate would have: A degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or equivalent. Around 2-3 years of full stack development experience, shipping production features in a modern web stack (e.g. TypeScript/React on the frontend; Python or Node.js on the backend; REST/GraphQL APIs; SQL and/or NoSQL data stores). Hands-on experience deploying applications on GCP and AWS, including containerised workloads, managed services, and CI/CD. Demonstrated use of AI tools (e.g. Claude, Copilot, Cursor) in your day-to-day engineering for code generation, review, debugging, and documentation with a clear sense of where they help and where they don't. Familiarity with data platform concepts: pipelines, storage, metadata, catalogues, and access controls. Working knowledge of AI/ML evaluation, benchmarking, and/or data annotation workflows, and the tooling ecosystem around them (e.g. evaluation harnesses, annotation platforms). Strong communication skills and the ability to work with both technical and non-technical stakeholders across cultures and time zones. Bonus: experience with multimodal data systems (text, audio, image, video); contributions to open-source AI/data tooling; experience operating within Singapore public sector or research programmes. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Director--Research_R00023946": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Director, Research",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe are seeking an exceptional strategic leader to serve as Senior Assistant Director, Research within the College of Humanities, Arts and Social Sciences (CoHASS). Working closely with the Dean, Associate Dean (Research), and Director (Operations), you will play a pivotal role in shaping and delivering the College’s research strategy, translating vision into programmes, structures and support systems that enable academic excellence, interdisciplinary collaboration, and global visibility. As the senior professional lead for research, you will oversee the College’s research ecosystem, driving performance, strengthening research impact, and fostering connections across Schools, Research Centres, and external partners. You will lead and enhance research support operations, ensuring high-quality and efficient systems that enable both investigator-led and collaborative research to thrive, while also supporting the development of research centres, major initiatives, and competitive funding opportunities. Working in close partnership with the Director (Operations), you will help ensure alignment between research strategy, operations, and resource planning across the College, translating strategic priorities into coordinated execution. With a strong focus on data-informed decision-making, you will provide strategic insight on research performance and influence, while contributing to a research environment that supports diverse scholarship and intellectual leadership. This is a unique opportunity for a collaborative and forward-looking leader to shape the future of research in a globally ambitious and interdisciplinary environment. Relevant Experience: Bachelor’s degree from a recognized university. At least 10 years of relevant work experience in research administration especially in grant sourcing, grant administration (pre-grant award and post-grand award) in an academic and (or) research institutions.  At least 3 years of people management/ leadership experience. Skills & Competencies: Strong interpersonal skills and ability to work effectively with multiple stakeholders across levels and cultures. Highly proficient in data analysis and reporting of grant information and research output, financial projection and budgeting. Able to handle confidential information sensitively. Strong working knowledge of MS Office applications. Knowledge of quantitative data analysis would be a plus. Proactive, resourceful, adaptable, hands-on, meticulous, organised and motivated to take on new challenges. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/AI-Engineer--Dev-Ops_R00024968": {
      "title": "AI Engineer, Dev Ops",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAI Singapore (AISG) is a national AI programme launched by the National Research Foundation (NRF), Singapore, to build and anchor deep national capabilities in AI.  AISG is supported through a government-wide partnership including the NRF, Ministry of Digital Development and Information (MDDI), Infocomm Media Development Authority (IMDA), Economic Development Board (EDB) and Enterprise Singapore (ESG). We bring together research institutions and the vibrant ecosystem of AI start-ups and companies to support impactful research, develop talent, and power Singapore's AI efforts. We're looking for an AI Engineer, Dev Ops to join the Data Platform team within AI Products at AISG. The role is to keep the Data Platform and the central data management infrastructure that sits beneath it running reliably, securely, and efficiently. You'll own the day-to-day operations of cloud infrastructure across GCP and AWS, the CI/CD and observability stack that the engineering team relies on, and the data pipelines, storage layers, and access controls that move data through the platform. You'll also bring strong AI fluency to the role: we expect the engineer to have knowledge in using AI tools deliberately for ops work such as incident triage, runbook generation, log analysis, IaC drafting, and automation and to help the team raise its operational bar by codifying those practices. This position will be hosted at the Nanyang Technological University (NTU) under VP (Artificial Intelligence & Digital Economy)’s office and we welcome you to join our community. Duties & Responsibilities: Platform operations and reliability Own day-to-day operations of the Data Platform across GCP and AWS which includes environment health, capacity, performance, cost, security posture and define and uphold SLOs, alerting policies, and on-call practices. Lead incident response: triage, mitigate, run blameless post-mortems, and drive preventive actions through to completion. Central data management and data engineering ops Operate the central data management infrastructure which includes data pipelines, storage layers, catalogues, access control, and lineage tooling and partnering with engineering team on reliability, throughput, cost, and data quality. Implement and maintain backup, retention, disaster recovery, and data residency controls aligned to programme and funder requirements. Infrastructure, CI/CD, and automation Manage infrastructure-as-code (e.g. Terraform) across GCP and AWS, and maintain CI/CD pipelines, container build/registry workflows, and deployment automation so teams can ship safely and frequently. Strengthen observability across the stack using logs, metrics, traces, dashboards and reduce toil by automating repetitive operational tasks. AI-assisted ops and continuous improvement Use AI tools (e.g. Claude, Copilot, Cursor) deliberately in your ops workflow for incident triage, log and metric analysis, runbook drafting, IaC generation and review, and on-call support and codify good patterns for the team. Build lightweight internal tooling that leverages AI to reduce operational load (e.g. summarising incidents, suggesting remediations, generating change reports), and contribute to security, compliance, and access reviews (secrets management, IAM hygiene, vulnerability patching, audit-readiness). Requirements: You should be a hands-on Dev Ops engineer who is comfortable operating cloud infrastructure end-to-end, who understands data engineering well enough to keep central data systems healthy, and who actively uses AI tools to make ops work faster and more reliable. The ideal candidate would have: A degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or equivalent. At least 3–5 years of Dev Ops, SRE, or platform engineering experience, with a track record of operating production systems at non-trivial scale. Hands-on experience operating workloads on both GCP and AWS including IaC (e.g. Terraform), containers and orchestration (e.g. Docker, Kubernetes), and managed services for compute, storage, and networking. Strong cybersecurity knowledge and hands-on practice including IAM and least-privilege design, secrets management, network security, vulnerability and patch management, audit logging, and security incident response. Familiarity with relevant standards and frameworks (e.g. ISO 27001, NIST, OWASP) and with data protection requirements (e.g. Singapore PDPA, GDPR where applicable) is expected. Working knowledge of data engineering and central data management including pipelines, storage formats, catalogues, access controls, and data quality/observability concepts. Strong fundamentals in CI/CD, observability (logs/metrics/traces), and incident response. Demonstrated use of AI tools (e.g. Claude, Copilot, Cursor) in your day-to-day engineering for code generation, review, debugging, and documentation with a clear sense of where they help and where they don't. Solid scripting/programming skills (e.g. Python, Bash, Go) and comfort reading other people's code across the stack. Strong communication skills and the ability to work with both technical and non-technical stakeholders across cultures and time zones. Working knowledge of AI/ML evaluation, benchmarking, and/or data annotation workflows, and the tooling ecosystem around them (e.g. evaluation harnesses, annotation platforms). Bonus: experience with multimodal data systems (text, audio, image, video); contributions to open-source AI/data tooling; experience operating within Singapore public sector or research programmes. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Director--Operations_R00024053": {
      "title": "Director, College Strategy & Operations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe College of Humanities, Arts and Social Sciences (CoHASS) at Nanyang Technological University (NTU) invites applications for the position of Director, College Strategy & Operations.   This is one of the most senior professional leadership role within the College and offers a unique opportunity to shape the strategic and organisational effectiveness of one of NTU's largest and most diverse academic colleges. Reporting directly to the Dean and serving as a key member of the College Leadership Team, the Director, College Strategy & Operations, will lead the transformation and delivery of a broad portfolio encompassing academic administration, postgraduate education, research administration, communications, external relations, governance, finance, and operational services.   We are seeking a strategic, forward-thinking leader with a strong track record of driving organisational excellence, leading large and diverse teams, and partnering with senior stakeholders to deliver institutional impact. The successful candidate will play a critical role in advancing the College's strategic priorities, fostering innovation, strengthening operational capabilities, and enabling excellence in teaching, research, and engagement.   Role Impact and Opportunity: As Director, College Strategy & Operations, you will: Serve as a trusted strategic advisor and thought partner to the Dean and College Leadership Team, translating vision into actionable plans and measurable outcomes. Lead and inspire a high-performing team of senior administrators and matrix teams across Schools, Centres, and College functions, fostering a culture of collaboration, accountability, and continuous improvement. Drive organisational transformation by redesigning processes, implementing scalable operating models, and strengthening service delivery across the College. Champion operational excellence, ensuring efficient, effective, and sustainable management of resources, systems, and services. Build strong partnerships across the University to advance interdisciplinary initiatives, institutional priorities, and shared operational goals. Lead complex strategic projects and change initiatives that enhance organisational effectiveness and position the College for future growth and success. Strengthen governance, risk management, and compliance frameworks while ensuring sound stewardship of financial and operational resources.   Key Responsibilities: Strategic Leadership and Institutional Planning Lead the planning, execution, and monitoring of College-wide strategic initiatives and transformation programmes. Partner with the Dean and senior leadership to develop and implement long-term strategies aligned with University priorities. Provide strategic advice on organisational design, policy development, governance, resource planning, and institutional effectiveness. Anticipate emerging challenges and opportunities, recommending innovative solutions to support the College's evolving needs.   Organisational Effectiveness and Service Excellence Oversee the delivery of a comprehensive portfolio of operational and academic services, including academic administration, postgraduate education, research administration, communications, external relations, and related operational functions. Review, redesign, and optimise business processes, service delivery models, and organisational structures to improve effectiveness and efficiency. Lead cross-functional initiatives to harmonise practices, improve stakeholder experience, and enhance operational performance across Schools and Centres. Promote data-informed decision-making and leverage technology to drive innovation and continuous improvement.   Governance, Risk and Compliance Ensure compliance with University policies, regulatory requirements, and governance standards. Strengthen risk management frameworks, internal controls, and operational resilience across the College. Provide expert guidance to College leadership on governance, policy implementation, and risk-related matters.   Financial and Operational Leadership Oversee the College's financial planning, budgeting, resource allocation, procurement, and operational management. Ensure prudent stewardship of financial and physical resources while aligning investments with strategic priorities. Identify opportunities to improve operational efficiency, optimise resource utilisation, and deliver sustainable outcomes.   Stakeholder Engagement and Partnership Building Develop and maintain strong relationships with academic leaders, professional staff, University offices, external partners, and other stakeholders. Facilitate collaboration across organisational boundaries to support strategic initiatives and operational excellence. Represent the College on University committees, taskforces, governance bodies, and institutional projects.   Leadership and Talent Development Lead, mentor, and develop a diverse team of professional staff leaders, fostering engagement, capability building, and succession planning. Build a high-performance culture that encourages innovation, accountability, collaboration, and continuous learning. Champion change management and organisational development initiatives that enhance team effectiveness and employee experience.   Qualifications and Experiences: Bachelor's degree from a recognised university. A postgraduate qualification in Management, Business Administration, Public Administration, Higher Education Leadership, or a related discipline will be advantageous. At least 15 years of progressive leadership experience in higher education, public sector organisations, or other large and complex institutions. Demonstrated success leading broad corporate services, operations, administration, or shared services functions at a senior level. Proven track record in organisational transformation, strategic planning, operational excellence, and change management. Strong experience leading diverse teams and influencing outcomes in complex matrix environments. Sound understanding of governance, compliance, risk management, financial stewardship, and institutional operations.   Key Competencies: Strategic leadership and organisational transformation. Executive stakeholder management and influencing skills. Strong commercial, operational, and financial acumen. Ability to lead through complexity, ambiguity, and change. Excellence in programme and project leadership. Analytical thinking, problem-solving, and sound judgment. Exceptional communication, relationship-building, and collaboration skills. Digital and data literacy with an appreciation of technology-enabled transformation.   Personal Attributes: Visionary yet pragmatic, with the ability to translate strategy into execution. Collaborative, inclusive, and relationship-oriented. Resilient, adaptable, and comfortable operating in a dynamic environment. Highly credible, professional, and trusted in handling complex and sensitive matters. Results-driven with a strong commitment to excellence and continuous improvement. Innovative and future-focused, with a passion for building organisational capability and impact.   Join us in shaping the future of one of Asia's leading universities and contribute to an environment that advances excellence in education, research, and societal impact. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Internship_R00024396": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Internship",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Assistant Manager, Internship serves as both an individual contributor and deputizes for the Team Manager in the administration of designated internship programmes under the NTU Career & Attachment Office’s Internship team.  The Internship team facilitates internships for all NTU undergraduates to enhance their career readiness. It strives to improve internship participation and experiences for both students and host organisations by providing a unified platform for engagement, communication, and support.    The incumbent's role is to take responsibility towards the following areas of work: Programme Operations and Service Management Oversee the end-to-end management of internship programmes, including: Manage the internship operations and work processes. Develop strategies to increase internship opportunities and facilitate students’ participation and placement. Monitoring the internship progress and proactively identify and pre-emptively address potential issues that may arise to support successful effective placement and completion. Provide guidance and advice to students on internship matters. Addressing and resolving common internship-related issues raised by either students or host organisations, including supporting the team on complex case management issues. Account Management and Stakeholders Management Engage with the college and/or schools to collaborate in managing and optimizing internship placement and increase student’s career readiness for internship. Develop & maintain new and existing partners (host internship organisations) to support their requisition and increase their uptake of students in internship. Collaborate with the respective internal stakeholders to ensure the provision of support for students’ internship search journey for an internship placement. Team Management Support team members in performing their assigned roles and responsibilities. Support the Team Manager to ensure continuity of operations and overcome potential changes and challenges. Collaborate across intra-teams to drive optimal operational performance through strong partnerships and coordinated. Performance Reporting Supervision and Management Prepare and work with data and statistics for tracking and reporting. Analyse data and develop data insights for strategic planning. Adhoc Projects and Initiatives Lead and play a key role adhoc projects in areas of operations, data analysis and/or communications. Seek to adopt and use new technology/system to improve overall performance and outcome. Contributes in the solutioning for continuous improvement on workflows and stakeholder management. Job Requirements: Bachelor's degree in any discipline from a recognised university. Candidates with a polytechnic diploma and extensive relevant work experience are also welcome to apply. Relevant work experience preferably in internship management, programme/project management, customer service management and process engineering. Successful track record in the managing of internships and cooperative education is highly advantageous. Minimum 5 years of work experience. Basic understanding about tertiary education landscape, career development and job market. Strong written and verbal communication skills. A collaborative team player who contributes actively to team success. Demonstrated passion for supporting youth in their career journeys. Comfortable with data, systems, managing structured processes and adhering to established policies and administrative frameworks. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Deputy-Director--Administrations_R00024217": {
      "title": "Deputy Director, Administrations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAs the Deputy Director, Administrations (DD) of MAE, the incumbent plays a vital role in supporting the Chair of MAE to provide leadership in various aspects of the school’s administrative initiatives including technical operations to drive organizational excellence to achieve the strategic goals and objectives of MAE. He/She is expected to lead in the development and implementation of organisational strategies, policies, standards, structures, systems and practices to achieve the overall goals of the School. In overseeing business operations, processes, initiatives and resources, the DD will provide integrated efficient and effective administrative services within the school, which is aligned with the School’s strategic goals and objectives and the University’s policies and processes. The DD will also provide foremost support to the School Management on strategizing and setting up of new initiatives, such as Capital Campaigns, Continuing Education, Community Engagement and External Relations. As a member of the School Management Committee, the DD will work closely with Chair and Associate Chairs in the formulation and review of policies to ensure the smooth and efficient operation of the administrative systems and processes throughout the School. This would also include active participation in the evolution of college-school relationship, organization reviews and partnering the central administrative offices in various administrative excellence projects in the university. Your key responsibilities include (but not limited to): Chart the strategic directions and roadmaps of MAE in alignment with University’s goals / new or changes to policies of the school by reviewing, recommending and driving process improvements to MAE’s structure, systems, policies and procedures with the aim of improving productivity, efficiency and effectiveness in operations. Work with the central administrative offices and College to align and coordinate workflow processes between functions and departments within NTU. Provide leadership and guidance to administrative / technical functions of the school and ensure all services are carried out smoothly and efficiently. Plan and review manpower allocation in order to achieve efficient use of resources and adequate support provided to faculty members, students and other stakeholders. Conduct and review performance appraisals for all direct reporting MSOs. Assist and advise Chair in MSO performance appraisal calibration exercise. Proactively develop, review and drive improvements in the School’s structure, systems, policies, processes and procedures with the aim of enhancing organizational effectiveness and creating an effective and conducive work environment. Oversee the overall financial operations of the school including financial reporting and analysis, budget planning and monitoring, as well as asset management, for financial effectiveness. Analyze, provide recommendations and proposals to redesign and reinvent current MAE space to further enhance and optimize usage for admin office, teaching and research facilities. Ensure lab and admin operations are in line with the Statutory requirement and University's safety standards. Ensure operations are in accordance with ISO45001/BizSAFE Star safety standard. Requirements: A recognized university degree, preferably from Mechanical or Aerospace Engineering. Prior experience in an institute of higher learning will be an added advantage. At least 15 years of working experience, with at least 8 years of experience in a senior managerial role with a proven track record. Knowledgeable about MAE industry trends, challenges, and opportunities. Strong verbal and written communication skills, with an excellent command of the English language, as the incumbent will represent MAE and engage with a wide range of stakeholders, including senior management and external partners or sponsors. Excellent collaborative, influencing and leadership skills. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills to build a sense of community within the school. Strong in strategic thinking and has an analytical mind. Confident and proactive with demonstrated dynamism and resourcefulness in problem solving. Highly adaptable and self-motivated with lots of initiative to take on new challenges. Able to redesign processes to achieve better and more efficient work performance. Attention to details. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Director--Communications_R00024051": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Director, Communications",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe College of Humanities, Arts, and Social Sciences (CoHASS) at Nanyang Technological University (NTU) is seeking a forward-thinking and experienced communications professional to lead its newly established College Communications team. As the Senior Assistant Director, Communications, you will play a pivotal role in shaping and executing integrated communications plans that align with NTU’s institutional goals and enhance the College’s visibility and engagement with stakeholders across its schools and research centres. This is an exciting opportunity to build a new function that will drive coherence, storytelling, and stakeholder alignment in a matrix academic environment. Job Responsibilities: Lead the development and implementation of a College-wide communications strategy, branding, and messaging framework that reflects CoHASS’s academic mission and evolving priorities. Drive alignment and coherence across school and centre communications teams through collaborative platforms, joint initiatives, and stakeholder engagement mechanisms. Develop and oversee campaigns that highlight emerging cross-college research themes, interdisciplinary initiatives, and newly established research centres to strengthen CoHASS’s positioning as a thought leader. Lead international communications efforts to build partnerships with global universities and academic networks, with the goal of improving CoHASS’s visibility and contributing to NTU’s standing in global reputation rankings (e.g., QS). Oversee the production of high-impact content that highlights CoHASS’s research, academic strengths, events, and societal contributions. Provide strategic advice to the Dean’s Office on media engagement, reputational matters, and institutional positioning, including responses during sensitive issues or crises. Establish editorial and visual standards for College publications, digital platforms, and campaigns to ensure consistency and brand integrity. Manage vendor relationships and communications budgets to deliver cost-effective, high-quality creative, media, and digital services. Monitor communications performance through analytics and reporting, applying data-driven insights to inform strategy and continuous improvement. Lead and mentor the College Communications team to foster capability development and a culture of collaboration, innovation, and excellence. Job Requirements: At least 10 years of relevant experience, with 3–5 years in a leadership or supervisory role, preferably in higher education, government, or public sector. Strong track record in strategic communications, campaign development, and stakeholder management. Excellent writing, storytelling, and editorial judgement for diverse internal and external audiences. Proven ability to lead through influence and collaboration, particularly in dynamic, matrixed environments. Experience in media relations, digital communications and brand management. Experience in managing vendors, projects, and communications-related budgets. Professional presence, sound judgment, and the ability to balance strategic vision with operational demands. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Faculty-Ops---Support_R00022829": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Faculty Ops & Support",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nEstablished in 1981, the School of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering (MAE) has grown into a leading institution recognized for its academic excellence, cutting-edge research, and innovative spirit. Today, MAE is home to over 90 distinguished faculty members and a vibrant community of more than 3,000 students, shaping the future of engineering through education, research, and industry collaboration. We are seeking highly motivated individuals to join our team as a Senior Executive . Job Description The Senior Executive will support the Head of Faculty Affairs in managing faculty operational and administrative matters, ensuring the Faculty Affairs Office delivers accurate, timely, and efficient services. As a Senior Executive , you will play a key role in driving operational excellence across a range of administrative functions within the School of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering. Based at NTU’s main campus, you will be part of the school’s central administrative team, providing dedicated support to faculty members and contributing to the smooth functioning of academic operations. Key Responsibilities, but not exhaustive: Executive & Secretarial Support : Provide comprehensive administrative support to faculty including procurement, claims, travel arrangements, and document submissions. Provide secretariat support for committees and meetings, including booking of meeting rooms, agenda preparation, minute-taking, and follow-up actions. Maintain confidentiality and handle sensitive documentation with accuracy and discretion. Support digitalisation initiatives and contribute to streamlining workflows and improving service delivery. Maintain up-to-date records and assist in the preparation of reports, presentations, and internal communication materials. Liaise with internal departments (e.g., Finance, HR, Research Office) and external vendors to resolve, compliance, and process-related issues. Perform any other duties as assigned to support the team’s and school’s objectives. Space Management : Provide administrative support to the Head, Faculty Affairs for research focused laboratory spaces, School’s renovation and any other ad-hocs projects. Events & Engagement: Organise and support planning as well as execution events such as school-level and department-level meetings, events, seminars, workshops, retreats and academic visits, including logistics, funding arrangements, and documentation. Faculty Appointment Administration Support: Datamining and profiling of potential international candidates; create database for easy references. Liaise with School’s HR and Shared Services team to advance Faculty appointment, re-appointment, and related processes and ensure smooth execution of administrative process. Maintain up-to-date records and assist in the preparation of reports, presentations, and internal communication materials Perform any other duties as assigned to support the team’s and school’s objectives. Serve as key support to school management for faculty recruitment-related publicity materials. Research Administration Support: Provide support and assist PIs in managing research grant budgets or any other research-related queries. Prepare and consolidate research data and indicators for reporting and submission. Serve as key support to school management for research-related publicity materials. Represent the school in various initiatives as assigned. Qualifications : Degree in Business Administration, Management, Education, or related field. 3–5 years of professional administrative experience, ideally in higher education or faculty-recruitment or research-intensive settings. Proven experience supporting leaders and managing complex workflows (travel, events, scheduling, logistics). Strong organisational and time-management skills with the ability to meet deadlines. Demonstrated adaptability and resilience, with the ability to adjust to evolving priorities. Excellent interpersonal and written communication skills. Proficiency in productivity and collaboration tools; familiarity with Workday and Ariba preferred. You’ll Thrive in This Role if You Are: Calm under pressure and able to juggle competing priorities. Detail-oriented yet adaptable to academic environments. A strong relationship builder who anticipates needs and takes initiative. Reliable, discreet, and responsive in supporting both faculty members and leadership. Willing to learn, with openness to acquiring new skills and knowledge as required. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Platforms-Engineer--MLOps_R00023688": {
      "title": "Platforms Engineer, MLOps",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAI Singapore (AISG) is Singapore's national programme in artificial intelligence, launched by the National Research Foundation (NRF) to anchor deep national capabilities in AI. Hosted at Nanyang Technological University (NTU), AI Singapore brings together Singapore-based research institutions and the vibrant ecosystem of AI start-ups and companies to perform use-inspired research, grow knowledge, create tools, and develop the talent to power Singapore's AI efforts. Since our inception in 2017, we have established a culture of respect, continuous learning, experimentation and curiosity, centred around innovation. The Platforms Engineering Group builds and operates the infrastructure and systems that enable AI practitioners across AISG's programmes to develop, train, and deploy machine learning models at scale. The group comprises four teams: Infrastructure Operations (InfraOps), Data Operations (DataOps), Machine Learning Operations (MLOps), and Experiences (EX). As a Platforms Engineer, MLOps in the Platforms Engineering Group, you will help build and operate modern infrastructure and systems to run large-scale machine learning and deep learning workloads. You will also design, develop, and maintain the AISG platform and tooling stack to enable project teams and partners to build products better and faster. You will serve as a domain expert to nurture AI talents and play a key part in driving the growth of Singapore's AI sector. In this role, you will: Design, build and maintain the platform and tooling stack that empowers AISG engineers to deliver their work effectively. Serve as the liaison between Platforms Engineering and AI project teams, ensuring they have the right ML tooling, infrastructure, and CI/CD processes in place. Develop and implement MLOps practices and processes, including CI/CD pipelines for ML models, automated testing, and model monitoring and versioning. Collaborate with data scientists, data engineers, and other stakeholders to ensure that ML solutions meet AISG's needs and are aligned with operational goals. Build and maintain production infrastructure to be resilient, secure, and high-performing. Implement infrastructure-as-code to automate systems configuration, provisioning, deployment, and monitoring. Document and investigate issues arising from our systems when they occur. Develop tools and software that improve and automate infrastructure. Propose and drive technical decisions to completion. Mentor AISG Apprentices and contribute to the MLOps curriculum for the AI Apprenticeship Programme (AIAP). To succeed in this role, you should have: Must-haves: At least 3 years of experience in an engineering or infrastructure position. Proficiency in at least one programming language such as Python, Go, Rust, or JavaScript/TypeScript (proficiency in Python and TypeScript is highly preferable). Proficiency in administering Linux systems. Proficiency in at least one automation tool (e.g., Ansible, Terraform, Bash). Familiarity with container and container orchestration technologies (e.g., Docker, Kubernetes, Helm). Familiarity with cloud platforms such as AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud Platform. A systematic approach to development and engineering, including debugging, DevOps/MLOps practices, and agile development. Excellent communication skills, including the ability to express complex ideas clearly. Good-to-haves: Basic proficiency in machine learning concepts, including data analysis, predictive modelling, and model evaluation. Experience with ML experiment tracking tools (e.g., MLflow, Weights & Biases). Experience with infrastructure-as-code and GitOps workflows. Familiarity with observability tools (e.g., Prometheus, Grafana). Experience mentoring or training others in a technical capacity. Candidates with relevant professional experience or graduates of the AI Singapore AI Apprenticeship Programme (AIAP) are welcome to apply. We offer a dynamic environment at the forefront of Singapore's national AI efforts, opportunities to work with cutting-edge AI/ML infrastructure, and a culture that values continuous learning and professional development. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Engineer-I--Computer-Science---Artificial-Intelligence---Data-Science---Electrical-Engineering-_R00025627": {
      "title": "Research Engineer I (Computer Science / Artificial Intelligence / Data Science / Electrical Engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Alibaba-NTU Global e-Sustainability CorpLab (ANGEL) represents a key collaboration between Alibaba Group and Nanyang Technological University (NTU). Supported by the Singapore RIE2025 Fund, ANGEL creates and deploys impactful green digital technologies for global sustainability. ANGEL’s mission aligns seamlessly with Singapore’s national objectives, such as the Singapore Green Plan 2030 and the Singapore Smart Nation Initiative. ANGEL’s work in developing sustainable and equitable digital solutions and promoting a sustainable and green lifestyle will contribute to a smaller carbon footprint. Its holistic approach will help to secure a brighter, more sustainable future for humanity.  We are seeking a highly motivated Research Engineer to develop next-generation Green AI technologies that improve the efficiency, sustainability, and scalability of artificial intelligence systems. The successful candidate will contribute to cutting-edge research and engineering in large language models (LLMs), efficient machine learning, and AI systems, translating research innovations into practical solutions for sustainable computing and real-world applications. This role offers opportunities to work at the intersection of AI research, software engineering, and sustainability, collaborating with multidisciplinary teams across academia and industry. Job Description: Support the design, development, and implementation novel machine learning and large language model (LLM) algorithms for Green AI applications. Support the research of efficient AI techniques, including model optimization, parameter-efficient fine-tuning, self-training, retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), prompt engineering, and efficient inference. Conduct experiments, benchmark algorithms, and analyze performance using rigorous scientific methodologies. Contribute to publications in leading AI conferences and journals. Collaborate with cross-functional teams to translate research outcomes into deployable technologies. Keep abreast of the latest developments in Green AI, foundation models, code intelligence, and AI systems. Job Requirements: Bachelor's in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Data Science, Electrical Engineering, or a related discipline. Strong background in machine learning, deep learning, and large language models. Experience working with large-scale datasets and distributed model training. Strong programming skills in Python. Experience with modern deep learning frameworks such as PyTorch or TensorFlow. Strong analytical and problem-solving abilities. Good written and verbal communication skills. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Scientist--Artificial-Intelligence---Computer-Science---Machine-Learning---Natural-Language-Processing---Information-Retrieval---Data-Science-_R00025626": {
      "title": "Research Scientist (Artificial Intelligence / Computer Science / Machine Learning / Natural Language Processing / Information Retrieval / Data Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Alibaba-NTU Global e-Sustainability CorpLab (ANGEL) represents a key collaboration between Alibaba Group and Nanyang Technological University (NTU). Supported by the Singapore RIE2025 Fund, ANGEL creates and deploys impactful green digital technologies for global sustainability. ANGEL’s mission aligns seamlessly with Singapore’s national objectives, such as the Singapore Green Plan 2030 and the Singapore Smart Nation Initiative. ANGEL’s work in developing sustainable and equitable digital solutions and promoting a sustainable and green lifestyle will contribute to a smaller carbon footprint. Its holistic approach will help to secure a brighter, more sustainable future for humanity.  We are seeking an outstanding Research Scientist to join our Green AI research team. You will conduct cutting-edge research on efficient and sustainable artificial intelligence technologies, advancing the development of foundation models that are both high-performing and environmentally responsible. You will work closely with interdisciplinary researchers and engineers to develop novel AI algorithms, publish in top-tier venues, and translate research innovations into real-world sustainability solutions. Job Description: Conduct research in Green AI, with a focus on improving the efficiency, scalability, and sustainability of large AI models. Design and develop novel algorithms for efficient training, inference, retrieval, and deployment of large language models (LLMs) and multimodal foundation models. Develop AI technologies that contribute to sustainability applications. Publish research findings in leading AI conferences and journals Collaborate with internal and external research partners to deliver innovative Green AI solutions. Mentor junior researchers and contribute to research proposal development and strategic initiatives. Job Requirements: Ph.D. in Artificial Intelligence, Computer Science, Machine Learning, Natural Language Processing, Information Retrieval, Data Science, or a closely related discipline. Strong research background in Large Language Models (LLMs), Green AI and efficient machine learning, LLM-based Agents, Distributed AI systems and scalable model serving, etc Strong publication records in reputable journals/conferences Strong programming skills in Python and modern AI frameworks (e.g., PyTorch, Hugging Face). Ability to work independently and collaborate across multidisciplinary teams. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Scientist--Computer-Science---Artificial-Intelligence---Machine-Learning---Natural-Language-Processing-_R00025624": {
      "title": "Research Scientist (Computer Science / Artificial Intelligence / Machine Learning / Natural Language Processing)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Alibaba-NTU Global e-Sustainability CorpLab (ANGEL) represents a key collaboration between Alibaba Group and Nanyang Technological University (NTU). Supported by the Singapore RIE2025 Fund, ANGEL creates and deploys impactful green digital technologies for global sustainability. ANGEL’s mission aligns seamlessly with Singapore’s national objectives, such as the Singapore Green Plan 2030 and the Singapore Smart Nation Initiative. ANGEL’s work in developing sustainable and equitable digital solutions and promoting a sustainable and green lifestyle will contribute to a smaller carbon footprint. Its holistic approach will help to secure a brighter, more sustainable future for humanity.  We are seeking an outstanding Research Scientist – Green AI to conduct cutting-edge research on efficient, sustainable, and scalable artificial intelligence technologies. The successful candidate will develop novel algorithms and system-level innovations that significantly improve the energy efficiency, computational efficiency, and deployment of large AI models while maintaining high model performance. The ideal candidate has a strong research background in large language models (LLMs), efficient deep learning, natural language processing, model optimization, and AI systems, with a proven publication record at top-tier AI conferences and journals. Job Description: Conduct research on Green AI technologies, including efficient training and inference of foundation models and large language models (LLMs). Develop scalable AI systems that enable practical deployment of foundation models on resource-constrained computing platforms. Develop AI technologies that contribute to sustainability applications. Publish research findings in leading AI conferences and journals Collaborate with internal and external research partners to deliver innovative Green AI solutions. Mentor junior researchers and contribute to research proposal development and strategic initiatives. Job Requirements: PhD in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, Natural Language Processing, or a closely related discipline. Demonstrated expertise in Large Language Models (LLMs), Natural Language Processing, Efficient Deep Learning, AI Model Optimization, etc. Research experience in Green AI, sustainable computing, or energy-efficient machine learning. Excellent publication records in reputable journals/conferences Strong programming skills in Python and modern AI frameworks (e.g., PyTorch, Hugging Face). Ability to work independently and collaborate across multidisciplinary teams. Strong publication record in top-tier AI conferences and/or journals. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant--Organic-Chemistry-_R00025625-1": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Organic Chemistry)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Chemistry, Chemical Engineering and Biotechnology (CCEB) is a newly established interdisciplinary joint school under College of Engineering and College of Science at NTU Singapore. Prof Loh Teck Peng's group conducts research in organic synthesis, green chemistry, and the synthesis of complex organic molecules. The Loh’s group is looking for research assistant to facilitate the group’s research and lab housekeeping. We are looking for a Research Assistant, Organic Chemistry, to support the day-to-day operation of Prof Loh Teck Peng's laboratory. The role will focus on laboratory housekeeping, chemical procurement, general administrative support, and facilitate the Loh group’s research. Key Responsibilities: Support day-to-day laboratory operations, records and inventories. Coordinate approved laboratory procurement and purchasing documentation. Provide routine administrative support to the PI and research group. Assist with supervised experimental research, data collection and documentation. Support laboratory housekeeping, safety and procedural compliance. Job Requirements: Bachelor's degree in Chemistry or a related field. Relevant research experience in organic or synthetic chemistry is preferred. Good organisational skills, with the ability to maintain laboratory records, inventories and routine procurement/admin documentation. Basic knowledge of laboratory safety, good research practices and accurate record keeping. Ability to support experimental research under supervision and to collect, organise and perform basic analysis of research data. Good written and oral communication skills, with working proficiency in common office productivity software. Meticulous, responsible and able to work independently while prioritising multiple laboratory, administrative and research tasks. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Manager--Graduate-Career-Development_R00025622": {
      "title": "Manager, Graduate Career Development",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNanyang Business School competes with top business schools worldwide to attract graduate students from diverse backgrounds to join its graduate programmes. The Graduate Studies Career Development (“GSCD”) team is an instrumental part of NBS’s Graduate Studies division, and aims to provide world-class career services to post-graduate students to develop them into career-savvy professionals and in helping NBS’s post-grad students find the ideal job after graduation. The position holder will be part of the GSCD team. The key purpose of the role is to provide world-class career services to NBS’s graduate students, manage employer relationships in key sectors, and source for suitable positions for NBS’s graduate students. The position holder is responsible for employer engagement with companies in Singapore and international markets, to bring jobs for 900+ students. Responsibilities: GSCD strategy & implementation: Engage with the GSCD team in providing multi-faceted career workshops, networking events, company presentations, etc. Identify and support implementation of strategic initiatives for GSCD to lift the level of career services for all GS participants. Support business development and employer engagement to secure full-time jobs and internship opportunities in Singapore and globally: Identify global career opportunities for graduate students, and develop strategies to engage key hiring organisations in identified markets. Develop tiering and engagement of companies in key markets, with a view to securing full-time jobs, internships and industry projects for students. Identify and build strong partnerships with recruiters and hiring managers globally, particularly in key hiring sectors. Work closely with internal NTU/NBS stakeholders such as Associate Deans, Academic Directors, Program and Management Office, NTU Career Office, Alumni Affairs Offices, Development Offices to source for full-time jobs and internship placements from existing and new industry contacts. Maintain a deep understanding of market factors relative to employer organisations in key markets. Cultivate relationships with alumni in key markets, particularly in identified hiring sectors, to help build and provide pipeline of full-time jobs and internships for students. Provide timely and comprehensive administrative support necessary in securing and matching students to jobs and internships Thought Leader for all international roles: Be the key thought partner to GSCD Career Leads in areas of understanding employers and employment trends. Support NBS endeavours in key markets e.g., sourcing for industry projects and managing industry visits. Provide student counselling to give insights into sectors/ countries: Develop a calendar of recruitment activities to ensure pipeline of jobs are availed to all post-graduate students. Place students in their desired roles (full-time jobs and internships). Monitor student performance and growth during internships and propose win-win solutions for students and industry partners. Coach and counsel students interested in relevant sectors / geographies to ensure readiness for career-related interactions with employers. All other tasks assigned to the role. Requirements: Degree from a top-tier global business school is required. An MBA or a Master's degree will be an advantage. Good knowledge of practices and hiring mandates of companies across different sectors in Singapore and in key international markets. At least 7 years' work experience, possessing strong and deep networks with hiring companies. Proven track record of business development including internal and external successful collaborative and leadership experience. Work experience in international markets will be a distinct advantage. Outstanding ability to manage senior stakeholders, and interact effectively with people of varying levels and backgrounds. Excellent interpersonal skills and presentation skills, including the ability to deliver high impact presentations to senior executives. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Takes initiative and is a good team player. Meticulous with a good eye for details. Able to work under tight deadlines. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Manager--External-Relations_R00025045": {
      "title": "Manager, External Relations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe incumbent will drive the School’s external relations and stakeholder engagement strategies, and manage events and initiatives that strengthen partnerships and enhance the School’s visibility as a nexus for innovation, research, and business education locally and internationally. Job Responsibilities: External Relations Engagement and Partnership Development Promote and elevate awareness of College of Business/Nanyang Business School (NBS) Spearhead and execute appropriate strategies to advance the College’s external relations agenda Cultivate partnerships for the College for a wide spectrum of initiatives for teaching and research. Identify new opportunities for partnerships, collaborations and engagements. Formulate action plans and establish relations with industry. Drive integrated and coordinated external relations programmes and activities across units within the College. Support networking at relevant industry/research forums and business meetings. Act as the primary administrative contact for external engagements and corporate partners. Event Management and Operations Develop and implement comprehensive event planning for partner events and collaborative initiatives with industry. Lead and coordinate with internal and external stakeholders to effectively plan and execute partner events and engagement activities Select suitable event venues and negotiate contracts Coordinate with NTU Events Office for events. Manage and host visits to the College by external parties, visitors and guests. Manage the College’s external relations budget which includes budget planning and accounts management Develop and manage event budgets Track expenses, reconcile invoices, and provide regular financial updates to stakeholders. Collaborate with the marketing team to create promotional materials and strategies for events. Conduct post-event evaluations to gather feedback and assess the success of each event, and prepare relevant reports for management where applicable. Streamline work processes and workflows Support to leadership and strategy development Lead consultation with the College Management to strategise, strengthen and establish industry partnerships and engagements.  Support the formulation of the College’s external relations strategies and implementation plans. Support College management in building relationships with local, regional, and international partners. Requirements: Degree from a recognized university At least 8 years of relevant work experience in events management and partnership engagement Able to connect with people at all levels, establish and maintain a network of relationships and partnerships Proficient in IT, experienced in managing in-person, virtual and hybrid events; and engaging online communities Resourceful and driven, with the ability to think strategically, creatively and analytically Excellent presentation and communication skills Able to influence and engage internal and external stakeholders Team player and must be able to work within tight deadlines Highly relationship-oriented while balancing stakeholder needs with institutional priorities We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Finance--AISG-_R00024430": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Finance (AISG)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAI Singapore (AISG) is Singapore's national programme in artificial intelligence, launched by the National Research Foundation (NRF) to anchor deep national capabilities in AI. Hosted at Nanyang Technological University (NTU), AI Singapore brings together Singapore-based research institutions and the vibrant ecosystem of AI start-ups and companies to perform use-inspired research, grow knowledge, create tools, and develop the talent to power Singapore's AI efforts. Since our inception in 2017, we have established a culture of respect, continuous learning, experimentation and curiosity, centred around innovation. We are seeking a Assistant Manager, Finance (AISG) to partner with Office of Finance, NTU Shared Services and other stakeholders such as funding agencies to ensure compliance with the policies, guidelines and procedures, and to align with as well as contribute to the mission, goals and objectives of the University. Key Responsibilities include: Manage non-grant related finance operations for AISG including payments, invoicing, and fixed assets. Work with the AISG team to support financial planning and monitoring of educational collaborations, research collaborations and gifts. Ensure accurate and timely payments. Review and follow-up on outstanding fund receipts. Handle enquiries from collaborators or trainees related to financial issues. Support management in various financial and management reporting and audit issues. Qualification : Degree or diploma in Accounting, Finance, Business, or related discipline. 2-3 years of relevant experience in finance operations, preferably in a university or research environment. Basic understanding of research grant administration and compliance requirements; prior experience in grant claims or research finance is an advantage. Able to liaise confidently with researchers, Schools/Centres, and collaborators on financial matters. Detail‑oriented, organised, and able to manage multiple deadlines and high operational volumes. Team‑oriented, responsive, and able to escalate issues appropriately to senior finance staff. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager---Senior-Executive--Operations-_R00025352": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager / Senior Executive (Operations)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAI Singapore (AISG) is a national AI programme launched by the National Research Foundation (NRF), Singapore, to build and anchor deep national capabilities in AI.  AISG is supported through a government-wide partnership including the NRF, Ministry of Digital Development and Information (MDDI), Infocomm Media Development Authority (IMDA), Economic Development Board (EDB) and Enterprise Singapore (ESG). We bring together research institutions and the vibrant ecosystem of AI start-ups and companies to support impactful research, develop talent, and power Singapore's AI efforts. The candidate will primarily support office operations of AISG. This position will be hosted at the Nanyang Technological University (NTU) under VP (Artificial Intelligence & Digital Economy)’s office and we welcome you to join our community. Key Responsibilities: Working closely with NTU administrative offices and different teams within AISG to support all procurement matters (Small Value Purchase, Simplified Quotation, Invitation to Quote, Direct Contracting & Invitation to Tender), while ensuring adherence to university policies. Support effective office operations of AISG, including tracking AISG’s assets, supporting onboard / offboard of AISG staff, and managing AISG’s office environment. Oversees daily operations to ensure a safe, functional and well maintained workplace. Administer employee access requirements. Support the setup and coordination of training sessions, meetings and corporate events. Provide administrative support for senior management meetings, including coordination of logistics and visitor arrangements. Qualification: Possess a Degree and at least 2 years’ experience in relevant field. Possess time, task, and resource management skills. Detail‑oriented, organised, and able to manage multiple deadlines and high operational volumes. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/AI-Safety-Research-Associate--Computational-Linguistics-Computer-Science-_R00025620": {
      "title": "AI Safety Research Associate (Computational Linguistics/Computer Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAI Singapore (AISG) is a national AI programme launched by the National Research Foundation (NRF), Singapore, to build and anchor deep national capabilities in AI. AISG is supported through a government-wide partnership including the NRF, Ministry of Digital Development and Information (MDDI), Infocomm Media Development Authority (IMDA), Economic Development Board (EDB) and Enterprise Singapore (ESG). We bring together research institutions and the vibrant ecosystem of AI start-ups and companies to support impactful research, develop talent, and power Singapore's AI efforts. ​This position will be hosted at the Nanyang Technological University (NTU) under VP (Artificial Intelligence & Digital Economy)’s office and we welcome you to join our community. Key Responsibilities: Co-designing and co-implementing safety and alignment strategies for LLMs in the medical domain Co-developing guardrails and safeguard models Assist in analysing failure modes specific to Southeast Asian languages and cultural contexts Supporting development of regional language capabilities to extend utility of SEA-LION for the region Assist in identifying culturally grounded safety risks and ensure our safety systems generalise robustly beyond English-centric assumptions for SEA languages and code-mixed text Assist in designing leaderboards and relevant visualisations for auditable reporting of results Co-authoring top-tier publications (e.g., ACL, EMNLP, NeurIPS, ICLR, etc.) to contribute novel, auditable, and reproducible findings Job Requirements: Preferably a Master Degree in Computational Linguistics, Computer Science, or have equivalent practical experience. Required experience includes safety alignment in LLMs, model evaluation for safety or robustness, and a track record of publications in the safety research area. Strong knowledge of Python and NLP concepts is a must. Experience with LLM Inference frameworks (i.e., Ollama or vLLM) is a must. Experience with Generative AI and LLMs (i.e., Llama, Gemma, Qwen, etc) is a must, along with competence in designing leaderboards and visualisations. Good communication skills for our collaborative environment. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Student-Administration_R00025400": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Student Administration",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences is seeking a dedicated and proactive Senior Executive to join the Undergraduate Academic Office. Reporting to the Manager, you will play a pivotal role in supporting the school’s academic team, ensuring the smooth delivery of academic services, and enhancing students’ learning journeys. Job Description Admission Oversee administration of student programmes (e.g. internships, attachments, exchange, integrated programme, and special initiatives). Coordinate student mobility opportunities and liaise with internal/external stakeholders. Manage student applications and required documentation. Prepare official correspondence for students. Handle general enquiries via phone, email, and in person. Academic Services Administer course registration and related academic processes. Manage online learning platforms and course evaluations. Process applications for academic support and financial assistance. Provide secretariat support for reviews and quality assurance. Manage instructor hiring for courses. Deliver general academic support services (e.g., scheduling, waiver handling). Examinations Support planning and logistics for assessments. Administer exam-related documentation and formatting. Assist with the administration of exam scripts checking. Events Organize student-related events and trips, including logistics and budgeting. Manage procurement requests for event needs. Prepare and disseminate event communications. Coordinate venue bookings and related arrangements. Other Administrative Duties Manage role-based email accounts. Prepare official letters and certificates. Administer students/faculty awards. Support ad hoc administrative tasks as assigned. Requirements Bachelor’s degree with at least 1 year of relevant experience or Diploma with 3-4 years of relevant experience. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite and relevant software. Strong organizational and project management skills. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Strong problem-solving and analytical abilities. Strong ability to communicate (verbal and written) effectively with students, faculty and team members. Familiarity with higher education policies and regulations is a plus. Responsible and reliable. Proactive and positive attitude towards work tasks. Possesses characteristics of being assertive and meticulous. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager--Research-Development_R00024733": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager, Research Development",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences in NTU invites applications for the position of Senior Assistant Manager for Chair’s Office Central Administration. The successful candidate will play a pivotal role in strengthening School’s research funding portfolio by supporting funding strategy development, preparing large competitive research grant proposals, and assisting faculty in overseeing research grant expenditure. The appointee will work closely with Principal Investigators (PIs) to identify strategic funding opportunities, coordinate multidisciplinary inputs, and facilitate high-quality submissions to national, industry and international funding programmes. Key Responsibilities Develop and implement strategic funding initiatives to expand School’s research portfolio and align proposals with national and international research priorities. Identify and evaluate funding opportunities from national agencies, industry partners and international programmes, advising PIs on the alignment with NTU / School strategy and funding criteria. Drive and coordinate the preparation of large competitive research grant proposals, including drafting technical narratives, consolidating multidisciplinary inputs, and ensuring alignment with funding agency requirements. Manage the end-to-end proposal development process, including timeline coordination, budget planning and compliance checks. Collaborate with PIs to refine research concepts, articulate project significance and innovation, and position proposals to maximize funding potential. Provide advisory support on grant budgeting during proposal development and coordinate with relevant offices on post-award financial matters. Support faculty in post-award activities, including progress reporting, grant variations and administrative coordination where required. Support the implementation of School’s research data governance practices as School’s Research Data Governance Manager, advise faculty on compliance with institutional and funder requirements. Requirements Advanced Degree (Master’s or PhD) in Science or Engineering, or a related discipline. Minimum 5 years of relevant experience in research development, grant writing, funding strategy or research management, preferably in a university, research institute, or R&D environment. Familiarity with Singapore research funding landscape (e.g., NRF, MOE, A*STAR) is advantageous. Experience in preparing large competitive research grant proposals or coordinating multi-investigator submissions. Excellent technical writing, analytical, organisational, and stakeholder engagement skills. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Executive---Senior-Executive--Teaching-Lab_R00025231": {
      "title": "Executive / Senior Executive, Teaching Lab",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJoin Our Team at the School of Biological Sciences, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore The School of Biological Sciences (SBS), part of the College of Science at Nanyang Technological University, was established in 2002 with a mission to advance excellence in biological and biomedical sciences. Our research spans diverse and impactful areas including infectious diseases, immunology, neurodegenerative disorders, telomere biology, and genome function. SBS is home to a vibrant, international community of scientific leaders, researchers, and professionals dedicated to innovation, discovery, and education. We are seeking a motivated and proactive Executive / Senior Executive (Teaching Laboratory) to support the planning, preparation, and smooth operation of undergraduate teaching laboratories. Job Description Teaching Laboratory Operations Support the planning, preparation, and delivery of undergraduate laboratory practical sessions. Liaise with course coordinators on practical requirements, schedules, and laboratory safety matters. Prepare laboratory reagents, consumables, specimens, and equipment required for practical sessions. Set up, calibrate, and relocate laboratory equipment as required for teaching activities. Brief Teaching Assistants on laboratory procedures, experimental protocols, and safety requirements. Provide safety and technical support to undergraduate students during laboratory practical. Conduct trial runs of new and existing practical protocols, troubleshoot technical issues, and ensure experiments are reproducible and effective. Procurement and Inventory Management Assist in the preparation and monitoring of teaching laboratory budgets. Procure laboratory consumables, chemicals, equipment, and other teaching-related materials. Maintain accurate procurement records and documentation according to University’s policies. Maintain inventory records for assets, consumables, chemicals, and teaching materials. Support inter-department activities on asset sighting. Laboratory and Equipment Management Ensure laboratories are well-maintained, organised, and operational. Perform routine cleaning, maintenance, and functional checks of laboratory equipment before and after semester periods. Coordinate equipment servicing, repairs, and preventive maintenance. Monitor stock levels of laboratory consumables and chemicals and replenish supplies as required. Report laboratory infrastructure defects and coordinate rectification with relevant stakeholders. Laboratory Safety and Compliance Maintain proper storage, handling, and documentation of chemicals and biological materials in compliance with University and Workplace Safety & Health (WSH) requirements. Ensure timely updating of chemical inventories. Oversee and handle safe disposal of laboratory waste. Reinforce laboratory safety practices and procedures during practical sessions. Participate in emergency preparedness activities, including first aid, chemical spill response, and fire drills. Prepare and review Risk Assessments for laboratory activities and experimental protocols. Ensure compliance with University and School’s safety policies and updates for audit preparation. School Support Provide administrative support for teaching laboratory operations. Assist in school events, outreach activities, and other duties as assigned. Requirements Diploma in Life Sciences or a related discipline. Entry-level candidates are welcome to apply. Candidates with relevant experience in teaching or research laboratory, preferably within an Institution of Higher Learning, will have an advantage. Basic knowledge of laboratory operations, reagent preparation, and laboratory housekeeping. Familiarity with laboratory techniques in molecular biology, biochemistry, cell biology, and mammalian and/or insect cell culture is preferred. Proficiency in the operation of common laboratory equipment, such as biological safety cabinets, centrifuges, compound microscopes, and pH meters. Good understanding of laboratory safety practices and chemical handling procedures. Good organisational, communication, and interpersonal skills. Able to work independently as well as collaboratively in a team environment. Adaptable and able to respond effectively to changing operational requirements. Demonstrates initiative, attention to detail, and a strong sense of responsibility and accountability. Able to identify operational issues, troubleshoot effectively, and implement appropriate solutions. Experience in data recording, analysis, and presentation would be an advantage. The School of Biological Sciences seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Research---Partnership_R00024732": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Research & Partnership",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe are seeking a proactive and detail-oriented Senior Executive, Research & Partnerships to join the School’s growing central administration team. This role provides key administrative, operational and engagement support, contributing directly to the School’s mission of advancing research excellence and strengthening global partnerships. You will work closely with faculty members, research staff and institutional stakeholders to ensure smooth delivery and effective implementation of research-related central administrative functions and initiatives. Key Responsibilities:              Research Manpower Administration Serve as Superuser for RISE as Unit Manpower Officer (UMO), supporting end-to-end research hiring, contract renewals and transfers for Division Principal Investigators (PIs). Advise PIs on RISE processes and provide hands-on troubleshooting support. Handle researcher manpower cost matters, including tracking and analysis. Work with PIs to monitor funding utilisation and flag potential shortfalls. Coordinate with HR and Finance to ensure accurate WBS setup and correct cost charging. Research Events & Engagement Support the administration and coordination of research events such as symposiums, colloquia, conferences, and workshops. Prepare materials, compile information, and coordinate event communications to deliver impactful and well‑run engagements. Contribute to continuous improvement of administration processes. Perform any other duties as assigned to support the team’s and school’s objectives. Executive & Administrative Support Provide administrative and operational support for school research activities and related initiatives to facilitate efficient coordination. Requirements: Degree or Diploma from a recognised university, with at least 1 year of relevant experience, preferably in a university or research environment. Proficient in Microsoft Office Suite & relevant software. Strong organisational skills with attention to detail and accuracy. Ability to manage deadlines and perform reliably under pressure. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, with service‑oriented mindset. Team player with initiative, adaptability and positive attitude. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Deputy-Chief-Information-Officer---IT-Director_R00025388": {
      "title": "Deputy Chief Information Officer / IT Director",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAs the Deputy Chief Information Officer (CIO) / IT Director, you will serve as a key executive partner to the CIO, providing operational leadership and strategic guidance across the university's central technology division. You will oversee multi-disciplinary IT teams, drive large-scale digital transformation initiatives, and ensure that IT infrastructure, services, and governance align seamlessly with NTU's academic, research, and administrative goals. Key Responsibilities: Strategic IT Leadership: Partner the CIO in defining and executing the university’s multi-year digital and AI roadmap, ensuring technology initiatives actively support research excellence, education, and administrative operations. End-to-End Operational Excellence: Enterprise IT operations—including IT infrastructure, enterprise applications, cybersecurity, cloud architecture, and end-user support services—maintaining high reliability and performance. Lead operational transformation through AI-driven operations to increase efficiency and user satisfaction. Digital Transformation & Enterprise Architecture: Lead complex enterprise-wide transformation programs, modernizing legacy systems, optimizing workflows, and integrating cloud-native solutions. Exploit AI-assisted coding tools, automated testing, and CI/CD pipelines in enterprise application development workflows. Institutional AI & Data Hub Adoption: Champion the adoption of the university-wide Data Hubs and Enterprise AI Platform across administrative units and academic schools, bridging strategic vision with operational reality. Governance, Risk & Compliance: Ensure robust enterprise cybersecurity, data privacy, business continuity, and regulatory compliance frameworks across all digital platforms and university assets. Support the CIO in formulating enterprise data policies and institutional AI frameworks. Resource & Financial Stewardship: Manage multi-million-dollar capital and operational IT budgets, establishing rigorous financial modelling, ROI tracking, and procurement governance. People Leadership & Capability: Mentor, empower, and develop a high-performing team of IT directors, managers, and technical specialists, fostering a culture of continuous learning, agility, and service excellence. Vendor & Stakeholder Engagement: Manage strategic vendor relationships, evaluate major IT investments, and maintain strong, collaborative relationships with academic deans, administrative leaders, and governance committees. Job Requirements: Must-Have Qualifications & Skills: Education: A Master’s or Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Computer Engineering, Business Information Systems, or a related field. Experience: At least 20 years of extensive progressive leadership experience in complex, large scale IT environments, with at least 5 years in a senior IT management role. Proven Executive Leadership: Demonstrated track record of leading large, multi-disciplinary IT teams and managing multi-million dollar technology budgets and enterprise portfolios. Complex Operational Management: Proven track record of managing end-to-end IT operations within large, decentralized, or matrixed organization, ensuring high operational resiliency, strict service-level agreements, and seamless business continuity. Transformation Expertise: Proven success delivering enterprise-grade digital transformations, cloud migrations, modernizing legacy enterprise systems, and scaling AI Ops or AI workflows in complex enterprise environments. Cybersecurity & Governance: Good understanding of enterprise risk management, cloud and AI governance frameworks, and modern cybersecurity principles. Communication & Influence: Superior stakeholder management, communication and negotiation skills, with a proven ability to present complex technical strategy clearly to executive stakeholders. Good-To-Have Skills: Executive industry certifications (e.g., ITIL, CISSP, TOGAF, PMP), in cloud platforms (AWS/Azure/GCP Architect), AI Operations, or data management (e.g., TOGAF, CISM, CDMP). Leadership experience within higher education, public sector, or research-intensive organizations. Hands-on familiarity with enterprise AI applications, AI platforms integration or big data virtualization tools. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Sales-Manager--Nanyang-Executive-Centre--Hospitality-_R00025366": {
      "title": "Sales Manager, Nanyang Executive Centre (Hospitality)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe NTU Office of Commercial and Auxiliary Services (OCAS) is responsible for the strategic planning, management, and marketing of commercial real estate, hospitality (including Nanyang Executive Centre) and auxiliary services (car parks and shuttle bus services) in NTU main campus and NTU@one-north. The Nanyang Executive Centre (NEC) is located at the NTU Main Campus. NEC features 150 refurbished guestrooms and refreshed event spaces that aims to offer a premier venue for high-level conferences, workshops, executive programmes, and industry engagements.    We are seeking a results-driven Sales Manager to drive room sales and event bookings, develop new business opportunities, and build strong client relationships to maximise NEC's revenue and occupancy. Key Responsibilities Business Development Establish and execute sales plan aligned with NEC’s revenue targets and objectives. Prioritise NTU's educational and institutional needs. Identify and pursue affiliated business opportunities, such as training programmes and events, to optimize NEC’s revenue. Develop strategies to drive room sales and maximise facility utilisation. Build and maintain strong relationships with internal NTU stakeholders and external clients to develop business leads. Establish and build rapport with all business partners. Handle contract negotiations and client inquiries professionally. Achieve monthly and annual targets for room revenue, occupancy, and average rates. Sales Administration Maintain accurate records and prepare monthly sales reports. Analyse sales performance and provide recommendations to improve results. Contribute insights to annual business planning and pricing strategies. Conduct market analysis and stay up to date on the industry trends and competitor activities. Requirements Bachelor’s degree in Sales & Marketing, Hotel Management or relevant discipline. Diploma holders with extensive experience may be considered. Minimum 2 years of experience in Sales, preferably in hospitality industry. Proven track record of achieving sales targets. Capable of dealing skilfully with new environment, new or difficult situations and overcoming challenges creatively. Adaptability and agility. Strong relationship-building/ management and negotiation skills. Team player.  Excellent communication skills. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Technical_R00025317": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Technical",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Chemistry, Chemical Engineering and Biotechnology (CCEB) hosts world-class education and research programmes in organic and inorganic chemistry, physical chemistry, chemical engineering, bioengineering and process engineering and synthetic chemistry. We aim to nurture future-ready graduates with the ability to tackle new challenges in chemicals manufacturing, healthcare, energy, food, and other important sectors. We are looking for a highly motivated Senior Executive to support CCEB’s technical and administrative activities, ensuring the smooth and safe functioning of the laboratory in enabling the Students, Researchers and Faculty to accomplish their academic and research objectives effectively, efficiently and safely. The Senior Executive, Technical will be responsible for preparing lab consumables, managing equipment, delivering training, and assisting with experimental procedures and equipment maintenance. Responsibilities: Support Bioengineering undergraduate and PG teaching experiments in Biomolecular and cellular engineering, such as PCR, Plasmid isolation, Image & microscopy technology, Bacterial & cell culture, Cell labelling and visualization etc., including preparing materials, performing lab trials, revising lab manuals, conducting and supervising lab classes. Coordinate lab schedules, student groupings, attendance records, and make-up lab sessions to ensure smooth teaching operations. Support continuous improvement initiatives to enhance laboratory operations, teaching effectiveness, and student learning outcomes. Participate in the design, development, implementation, and evaluation of new teaching experiments and laboratory activities. Provide technical and logistical support for student competitions, projects, and innovation activities involving laboratory equipment and facilities. Ensure adequate lab consumables and manage purchasing of materials and inventory control. Ensure good lab housekeeping and safe laboratory practices. Liaise with suppliers on timely equipment setup, repair and maintenance. Carry out strategic budget proposals, tracking expenses associated with laboratory equipment and consumables. Conduct training for new users, guide inexperienced users in operation of lab equipment.  Support the manager to perform diagnostic tests and in-house repair process in the event of equipment failure, engage vendor for periodic calibration and preventive maintenance. Maintain accurate records of lab chemicals, consumables, assets and equipment maintenance. Support lab and management, with experience in writing standard operating procedures and risk assessments. Perform any other duties as assigned by the reporting officer and school management. Skills and qualifications: A recognized degree in Biomedical Engineering, Bioengineering, Biotechnology or a related field. Diploma holder with 3 years’ relevant experience will also be considered. Experience handling, operating and maintaining scientific & laboratory equipment such as Micro plate reader, Gel imager, microscope, Autoclave, Rheometer, etc. Analytical thinker with strong problem-solving and troubleshooting skills. Good awareness of laboratory safety. Excellent verbal & written communication. Good learning ability and able to work independently with minimal guidance. Be proactive and independent. Effective time management. Good team player with service orientation. The School of Chemistry, Chemical Engineering and Biotechnology seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Deputy-Director--Digital-Platforms---AI-Transformation_R00025343": {
      "title": "Deputy Director, Digital Platforms & AI Transformation",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe role presents an exciting opportunity to shape NTU’s digital future by driving digital transformation and AI initiatives that enhance the university’s operations and campus experience. Reporting to the Director of Enterprise IT, the job holder will provide strategic vision, governance, and technical leadership across core enterprise platforms, including NTU’s websites, mobile applications, chatbots, and IT solutions and services. Acting as a key bridge between central IT leadership and decentralised business units, the job holder will lead the delivery of innovative AI and digital solutions that optimise operations, enable organisational growth, and transform the campus living experience. The role will also ensure that NTU’s technology landscape remains secure, sustainable, scalable, and aligned with long-term enterprise architecture and strategic priorities. Responsibilities: Engage stakeholders across multiple domain areas to understand their needs, define and implement technology solutions and enhancements; and assist them in planning and managing budget for their digital transformation initiatives. Stay abreast of emerging technologies, formulate multi-year strategic technology roadmaps and present business cases to executive steering committees and senior stakeholders. Lead the planning and implementation of technology solutions, overseeing the overall design, development, integration, and deployment of multiple systems/platforms. Drive change management and digital adoption strategies to ensure smooth transitions and minimal operational friction for end-users. Oversee the digital platforms and services, ensuring adherence to best practices, security standards, and performance optimisation. Manage procurement processes, contract renewals, and operational expenditure budgets to maximise technology return on investment. Oversee external system integrators, technology partners, and software vendors to ensure full SLA compliance, fiscal discipline, and project delivery velocity. Maintain rigorous IT audit readiness, ensuring zero high or medium risk findings across all managed digital ecosystems. Requirements: Bachelor’s Degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Software Engineering or related discipline; or Bachelor's degree in Business Administration or Marketing, coupled with relevant technical experience. Minimum 15 years of experience in IT-related industries with at least 10 years of progressive leadership experience in enterprise IT management, digital transformation or platform engineering within large and complex organisation. Proven track record in orchestrating multi-site web enterprise consolidations and decentralised operational models. Possesses strong technical understanding of cloud architectures, enterprise content management systems, GenAI chatbot workflows, mobile app development, and API integrations. Ability to communicate complex technical concepts through storytelling capabilities to a diverse group of users, including senior stakeholders. Excellent stakeholder management, interpersonal, and managerial skills, with strong change management capabilities. Ability to multi-task, work under pressure and deliver results in a timely manner. Tenacity to take on challenges and handle ambiguity; and manage diverse views and seek consensus through open discussion. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Chemical-Store_R00025619": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Chemical Store",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe are seeking for a dynamic individual to assist the Store manager with daily operations and safety of the Chemical Store at the School of Chemistry and Chemical Engineering and Biotechnology (CCEB). The Senior Executive supports the Chemical Store Assistant Manager in managing the high-volume needs of students, research teams, and faculty at the School of Chemistry, Chemical Engineering, and Biotechnology (CCEB). Responsibilities include handling bulk purchases of chemicals and consumables, forecasting, data analysis, negotiating with suppliers, managing deliveries, and overseeing the online inventory system. The role also involves monitoring stock availability, managing monthly invoicing and intra-billings for research teams, and coordinating chemical waste disposal. Responsibilities Safety compliance Adhere to and promote safety protocols and procedures to ensure and uphold safety compliance. Implement proper handling and storage practices for hazardous materials. Assist the safety committee in maintaining a safe and organized work environment. Ensure storage of chemicals and solvents is kept within the allowed maximum capacity approved by statutory authorities. To work closely with the Safety committee and safety officer on the safety regulations for the Chemical Store at both Nanyang Link and Nanyang Drive. To assist the safety officer with the safety regulations and enforcement for flammable hazardous substances, bio and chemical waste regulations, SCDF and SPF-regulated chemicals such as explosive precursors, etc. Ensure proper documentation of controlled chemicals. Conducting regular safety inspections on chemical storage facility, arranging repairs or maintenance, and providing training to staff/intern student on safe handling procedures. Daily Store Operations Accept supplier deliveries and process delivery orders for the research groups and Chemical Store, inspecting and checking that actual item received are in satisfactory condition. To execute product and material handling and movement within the chemical store in compliance with established policies, procedures and standards. Organize received items within the receiving area or designated storage locations. Ensure that items are stored safely and securely to prevent damage or loss. Processing of internal purchases by research groups. Perform periodic cycle counts on goods. Sourcing quotations and negotiating with suppliers to enable competitive bulk purchasing, achieving cost savings and financial efficiency for the Chemical Store. Forecasting and monitoring inventory availability in the Chemical Store to ensure continuous supplies to meet the demands of the undergraduate teaching labs and research labs activities. Regular stock availability updates in the in-house CBC Store Online Inventory System. Communicate, negotiate and provide feedback to vendors on any issues pertaining to the above. Assisting in any other ad-hoc duties assigned by the reporting manager. Waste Management Proper waste management in accordance with current government regulations and safety requirements from collection to disposal. Submission of NEA E-tracking documentation for waste collection. Ensure all waste disposal by research groups adheres to safety requirements as set down by the relevant statutory authorities, including NEA and SCDF. Work closely with internal Safety Team in waste management, ad-hoc disposal of chemicals. Finance On-time generation and processing of monthly invoices from the inventory system to research groups. Maintain an up-to-date record of invoices, accounts and special grants. Liaising with all stakeholders including inter / intra schools and departments to ensure all transactions are processed and credited into the school operating budget. Process billing and intrabilling for Chemical Store supplies, laboratory equipment, shared facilities teaching laboratories and other chargeable services. Maintain detailed records of all financial transactions involving chemical store. Requirements Possess at least a Diploma/Degree in Logistics/Warehousing/Chemistry/Engineering/science-related discipline. 1-3 years prior experience in the educational/logistics/warehouse with a science background is preferred. Possess knowledge of basic chemistry/biology/engineering, safety regulations, waste management, basic finance. Knowledge in SAP System is an added advantage. Ability to use data and apply robust analytics to analyse cost, impact, risk and benefits. Knowledge of chemical safety regulations and best practices. Effective negotiation skills and resourceful in finding competitive pricing for the consumables/ chemicals/solvents for stakeholders. Resourceful and independent. Ability to work effectively under pressure. Proactive and a positive attitude towards work tasks. Conscientious team player. The School of Chemistry, Chemical Engineering and Biotechnology seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager--Student-Sports_R00025455": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager, Student Sports",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Student and Academic Services Department (SASD) provides comprehensive support across the student life cycle—from admission and matriculation to graduation and beyond. SASD works closely with schools, colleges, and autonomous institutes to ensure a seamless and enriching academic journey.  Within SASD, the Student Affairs Office (SAO) plays a central role in shaping student life through leadership development, student-led activities, residential life, integration efforts, community engagement, arts, and sports. The successful candidate will contribute to broader initiatives aimed at supporting and strengthening NTU’s student-athlete ecosystem through the administration of high-performance athlete support frameworks, recruitment of high-performance athletes, management of student sports organisations, and coordination of key partnerships and sporting initiatives. Key responsibilities  Student-Athlete Support & Programmes Manage engagement with external stakeholders such as Singapore Sports School (SSP), the High Performance Sport Institute (HPSI) and other government agencies or stakeholders to advance student-athlete development and high-performance sport outcomes. Coordinate collaborative initiatives and maintain effective working relationships with external organisations. Where applicable, be the point-of-contact to liaise with the relevant National Sport Association and/or other relevant organisations for major events (e.g., ASEAN University Games 2030). Administer support for national and high-performance student-athletes to align with the University’s objectives. This includes liaising with Office of Admissions and Schools to facilitate admissions processes and/or funding programmes, preparing for athlete onboarding and working with College/Schools to facilitate athlete-friendly academic arrangements during the semesters. Maintain database of prospective high-performance athlete, monitor athletes’ progress and provide coordination of support services. Support planning and execution of university, inter-varsity, and national sporting events. Support outreach, engagement activities, and recruitment initiatives. Assist in policy development, planning, and stakeholder coordination efforts. Student Sports Management & Governance Oversee operations of assigned varsity teams and recreational sports clubs. Guide and support student leaders in programme planning, governance, and operations. Ensure compliance with university policies, safety, and risk management standards. Assist in strengthening processes and frameworks for student sports organisations. Requirements Degree in Sports Science/ Sports Management, or a related discipline. Relevant experience in student affairs, sports administration, programme management, or stakeholder engagement. Strong stakeholder management and partnership-building capabilities. Experience managing events, programmes, and operational activities. Ability to work independently while coordinating multiple stakeholders and priorities. Strong communication, organisational, and interpersonal skills. Knowledge of sports development, athlete support frameworks, and university sports environments is advantageous. Familiarity with governance, compliance, and risk management practices. Passion for student development and sports excellence. Able to work irregular hours as there will be rotating duty roster across weekday evenings and/or weekends to support sports events. Where applicable, appropriate time off will be given.  We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Transition---Integration_R00025087": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Transition & Integration",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Student and Academic Services Department (SASD) is a dedicated team committed to delivering comprehensive support across the entire student life cycle—from admission and matriculation to graduation and beyond the classroom. SASD works collaboratively with schools, colleges, and autonomous institutes to ensure a seamless and enriching academic journey for all students. This position sits with the Student Affairs Office (SAO), which is one of the functions within SASD. The SAO plays a key role in co-creating a meaningful and enriching student life experience through student-led activities, leadership development initiatives, residential life programmed, integration efforts, community engagement initiatives, arts and sports. The Assistant Manager designs and delivers Transition & Integration initiatives. Specifically, Transition initiatives aim to enable students to transit effectively into and through their university journey, while Integration initiatives aim to enable a positive international student experience and meaningful social integration between local and international students. Through these efforts, the role promotes intercultural understanding, a strong sense of belonging, and student success across the community. Key Responsibilities: International Student Experience and Integration Manage the design, implementation, and continuous improvement of targeted initiatives that support international students’ transition across academic, social, and cultural domains. Develop university-wide Integration initiatives that promotes meaningful social mixing between local and international students, including buddy programmes, intercultural dialogues, and community projects. Partner with schools, student organisations, residential halls, and central offices to embed integration agenda into the broader student experience. Develop metrics and evaluation frameworks to assess Integration outcomes for continuous improvement.  Transition Journey Mapping and Programmes Support the planning, execution, and continuous improvement of centralised Transition programmes with the aim of delivering a robust first year transition experience for freshmen. Manage the development of a Transition journey map as a guide for students to transit effectively in their first semester, including ensuring its dissemination and active adoption by students. Scholars Engagement Collaborate with various internal stakeholders to ensure that the wellbeing of S&T and ASEAN scholars, both academic and co-curricular, are taken care of throughout their undergraduate years.  Prepare university-wide reporting to MOE with regards to Integration matters and scholar status. Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in any discipline. At least 3 - 5 years of relevant experience which involves considerable interaction with students; experience in the tertiary education sector will be advantageous. Experience in youth development and/or IHL orientation programmes and integration of international students. Project management skills in coordinating large-scale projects. Proven track record in stakeholder management.  We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager--Examination_R00024107": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager, Examination",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nEstablished in 1981, the School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering (EEE) https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research. It is one of the largest EEE schools in the world, with more than 120 faculty members and an enrolment of more than 4,000, of which about 2,000 are graduate students. We invite applications for the position of Senior Assistant Manager at EEE, NTU. The role is to manage the examination management process and serve as one of the key points of contact for examination matters to ensure excellence in delivery and execution while maintaining high level of integrity and confidentiality.  Key Responsibilities: Contributing as a key staff in the Curriculum and Examination Team on undergraduate assessment, examination and award matters. Managing examination mark processing and administer Mark Entry System (MES), including preparing reports for School Board of Examiners (BOE) meeting. Acting as a key liaison between the team and key stakeholders to drive critical processes such as BOE, exam paper preparation, student results appeal and special student arrangements for assessment. Coordinating the nomination and award of academic medals and book prizes in accordance with academic policy and guidelines. Qualifications:  Bachelor's degree in a relevant field. Minimum of 5 years of experience in educational administration or program management. Strong interpersonal, communication, and analytical skills. Ability to work collaboratively in a diverse team environment. Previous experience in data analytics and workflow improvement is advantageous. Familiarity with higher education policies and accreditation standards is beneficial. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Administrative-Support_R00023682": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Administrative Support",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-07\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe role supports the administration and coordination of EEE research programmes and related graduate research activities under EEE Graduate (Research Studies) office. Key Responsibilities: Provide administrative and operational support as part of the EEE Graduate (Research Studies) team. Assist ACG in the administration of EEE research degree programmes, including student academic matters, curriculum administration, examinations, and progression matters. Coordinate and manage graduate academic related activities and events, including programme outreach, publicity, orientation, and other ad hoc student activities. Liaise with internal and external stakeholders to ensure timely and accurate programme administration. Perform other duties as assigned by the supervisor. Job Requirements: A bachelor’s degree in relevant discipline; prior experience in academic or programme administration will be an advantage. Experience working in a tertiary education institution is preferred. Meticulous, organised, and able to manage multiple tasks in a dynamic environment. A proactive team player with the ability to work independently and collaboratively under tight timelines. Strong written and verbal communication skills, with good interpersonal abilities. IT savvy, with proficiency in Microsoft Office applications and administrative systems. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Manager--Talent-Strategy-_R00025318": {
      "title": "Manager (Talent Strategy)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nIntroduction The NTU Honours College (NHC) is the premier undergraduate college at Nanyang Technological University (NTU), dedicated to nurturing high-achieving students as future leaders who make meaningful contributions to society. Through an interdisciplinary, intellectually rigorous, and experiential learning environment, NHC empowers students to undertake advanced coursework, engage in collaborative research, and tackle real-world challenges. With a strong emphasis on leadership, innovation, and global impact, NHC offers curated opportunities such as interdisciplinary seminars, personalised mentorship, and exclusive networking engagements with industry and academic leaders. Summary NTU Honours College (NHC) is seeking a dynamic and experienced professional to lead its admissions, outreach, and scholarship management portfolio. As a premier undergraduate college, NHC is home to high-achieving students who aspire to lead and serve with global impact. The Manager will play a pivotal role in shaping the College's student body by overseeing the admissions process, managing prestigious scholarship programmes, and driving high-impact outreach and engagement initiatives. This is a unique opportunity to contribute strategically to the development of future-ready scholar-leaders while working at the intersection of academic excellence, talent development, and global engagement. Key Responsibilities Lead NHC’s end-to-end admissions cycle, including application review, and candidate shortlisting, and interviews. Manage the placement, tracking, and engagement of scholarship recipients under the Nanyang Merit Scholarship (NMS), Nanyang Global Scholarship (NGS), and NTU President’s Award (NTUPA). Lead and coordinate closely with the Faculty Leads and Fellows to create development opportunities for scope scholars. Plan and deliver NHC’s flagship events (e.g. Freshmen Welcome Reception, Scholar Engagement Series, Open House, and outreach briefings). Oversee the content development and maintenance of the NHC website and related digital platforms to ensure accuracy, branding alignment, and effective outreach. Build and maintain strong working relationships with key internal stakeholders and engage external partners where relevant. Lead in student engagement as well as the formation of NHC Student Club and the respective Signature Programme sub-clubs. Track outcomes, monitor processes, and identify opportunities for continuous improvement in admissions and scholarship strategy. Job Requirements A Bachelor’s degree in any discipline. A postgraduate qualification is advantageous. Strong understanding of university-level admissions, scholarships, and student development. Familiarity with higher education outreach, stakeholder engagement, and digital communications. Working knowledge of content management systems, CRM tools, and event planning best practices. At least 10 years of experience in higher education, admissions, programme management, or student affairs. Proven ability to manage high-performing student populations and cross-functional collaborations. Excellent communication, interpersonal, and stakeholder engagement skills. Strong planning and organisational skills with the ability to manage concurrent deadlines. Strategic thinker with data-driven decision-making capabilities. Data Analysis and management reporting: Ability to monitor, collect and analyse data to evaluate results, and create reports and/or presentations. Ability to assess the accuracy, validity and integrity of the data. Experience in working with database management applications. Manage Work Processes: Ability to measure and evaluate work processes and services to achieve goals. Ability to redesign processes using most appropriate methods and technology to meet or exceed organisational needs. Ability to identify opportunities, implement solutions, and measure impact. Proficiency in Microsoft Office suite applications; knowledge of web editing tools and Customer Relationship Management (CRM) systems is a plus. Professional, discreet, and student-focused. Adaptable, resourceful, and collaborative. Passionate about nurturing the next generation of leaders and scholars. Ability to multi-task and pay attention to details. Highly motivated and driven. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant--Computer-Science-Computer-Engineering-Electrical-Engineering-_R00025616": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Computer Science/Computer Engineering/Electrical Engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nYoung and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is ranked among the world’s top universities. NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science (CCDS) is a leading college that is known for its excellent curriculum, outstanding and impactful research, and world-renowned faculty. A hot bed of cutting-edge technology and groundbreaking research, the College aims to groom the next generation of leaders, thinkers, and innovators to thrive in the digital age. Located in the heart of Asia, NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science is an ‘exciting place to learn and grow. We welcome you to join our community of faculty, students and alumni who are shaping the future of AI, Data Science and Computing. Key Responsibilities: The Research Assistant will conduct research on cellular network security, with a particular focus on 4G/5G mobile networks and core network systems. The candidate will analyse cellular network architectures, protocols, and implementations to identify potential security vulnerabilities. The candidate will design and conduct experiments to validate identified security issues and evaluate their practical impact. The role may also involve developing experimental testbeds, prototypes, and security analysis tools. The candidate will contribute to research publications, technical reports, presentations, and other project deliverables, and work closely with the PI and research team. Job Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or a related field. Good knowledge of computer networks and network security. Good programming and experimental research skills. Familiarity with cellular networks, including 4G/5G systems and core network architectures. Experience in network protocol analysis, system security, or security research. Demonstrated research experience in cellular network security, as evidenced by publications in high-quality venues. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant--Computer-Science-Computer-Engineering-Mathematics-_R00025617-1": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Computer Science/Computer Engineering/Mathematics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nYoung and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is ranked among the world’s top universities. NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science (CCDS) is a leading college that is known for its excellent curriculum, outstanding and impactful research, and world-renowned faculty. A hot bed of cutting-edge technology and groundbreaking research, the College aims to groom the next generation of leaders, thinkers, and innovators to thrive in the digital age. Located in the heart of Asia, NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science is an ‘exciting place to learn and grow. We welcome you to join our community of faculty, students and alumni who are shaping the future of AI, Data Science and Computing. Key Responsibilities: Responsible for the design, implementation, and testing of software prototypes and algorithms related to security, privacy-preserving technologies, and digital trust. Conduct comprehensive literature reviews on state-of-the-art methodologies, identifying gaps and opportunities in current computer science and security research. Assist in drafting and editing technical reports, project deliverables, and research manuscripts for submission to top-tier academic conferences and journals. Collaborate closely with the Principal Investigator (PI), postdoctoral fellows, and graduate students to troubleshoot technical challenges and ensure project milestones are met on time. Job Requirements: Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Mathematics, or a related field. Good knowledge of computer security. Experience in computer science research. Good programming and experimental research skills. Familiarity with large language models and secure multi-party computation. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
