    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager-Manager--Events_R00025210": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager/Manager, Events",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-19\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University's College of Engineering is one of the largest engineering colleges in the region, bringing together five schools under a single College Office. The College Office is looking for an experienced Events Senior Assistant Manager/Manager to own its full event portfolio, from institutional ceremonies and high-profile visits to community and cultural events and fundraising engagements. Responsibilities: Own the College event calendar and standards across institutional, cultural, and fundraising events. Plan and deliver flagship engagements, including Visiting Committee visits and donor events, to an exacting standard. Lead end-to-end event management, including budgeting, procurement, vendor management, logistics and on-site operations. Collaborate with internal and external stakeholders across the College to ensure seamless event planning and delivery. Evaluate every event and raise the bar over time. Requirements: Must-haves: A recognised university degree. At least 6 to 8 years' end-to-end event management experience with budget accountability. A track record with high-profile or VIP events and external vendors. Good to have: Experience across institutional, cultural, and fundraising events. Higher-education, institutional, or non-profit experience. Why join us: Ownership and visibility: you will own the College's entire event portfolio, working directly with senior leadership and delivering the events that shape how the College is seen by its community, its partners, and its donors. A clear career pathway: this role sits on NTU's Events Management track, with structured progression toward Assistant Director, Senior Assistant Director, and Director-level roles as you grow. Breadth that builds your career: few events roles span institutional, cultural, and philanthropic events in one portfolio, giving you an unusually rich base of experience. Development and support: budget and vendor ownership, cross-functional partnership with Communications and Advancement, and NTU's learning and development opportunities and staff benefits. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager-Senior-Assistant-Manager--Administrative---Governance-Support_R00025209-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager/Senior Assistant Manager, Administrative & Governance Support",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-19\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University's College of Engineering is one of the largest engineering colleges in the region, bringing together five schools under a single College Office that sets standards and supports the schools to deliver. The College Office is looking for an Assistant Manager/Senior Assistant Manager to work as the right hand of the Deputy Director: a broad, high-trust role for someone who enjoys both driving things to completion on behalf of a senior leader and keeping day-to-day operations running smoothly. Responsibilities: Act on the Deputy Director's behalf to move College-wide priorities to closure, working with function heads and school administrators. Review and develop SOPs and business processes and recommend improvements to standardise, simplify and streamline workflows. Identify and drive automation opportunities where feasible to enhance efficiency, productivity and service delivery. Keep governance records and action tracking accurate, and ensure commitments are followed through. Coordinate office administration and facilities so the College Office runs without a hitch. Support and deliver events, from internal staff functions to high-profile institutional visits. Provide office-level safety coordination and handle confidential information with care. Requirements: Must-haves: A recognised university degree. At least 5 to 7 years of relevant experience in executive/management support and office administration in a complex organisation. Strong judgement, discretion, and follow-through. Good to have: Higher-education or public-sector experience. Exposure to governance, events, or facilities coordination. Why join us: You will work at the centre of a large College, with exposure to senior leadership and genuine breadth of responsibility, alongside NTU's learning and development opportunities and staff welfare benefits. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Manager-Senior-Asst-Manager--Office-of-Patient-Engagement--LKCMedicine-_R00025550": {
      "title": "Manager/Senior Assistant Manager, Office of Patient Engagement [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-19\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. The Office of Patient Engagement (OPEN) at LKCMedicine is a dedicated Centre in Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine that integrates patient and public voices into health research and medical education, ensuring research is shaped with those who have lived experience. OPEN supports researchers and educators to embed meaningful patient and public involvement (PPI) across the research lifecycle and engages with a diverse patient partner network that collaborates on research, education, and engagement activities. Through training programmes for patient partners, researchers, clinicians, and educators, and a dedicated research programme, OPEN builds capability and fosters partnerships that strengthen the quality, relevance, and impact of health research and education, contributing to broader efforts to improve healthcare through evidence generation. As the Manager/Senior Assistant Manager, Patient and Public Involvement (PPI) Advocacy, you will be part of the OPEN team to grow and advocate for patient and public involvement (PPI) for health research, shaping how PPI is communicated and understood by patient partners, researchers, clinicians and healthcare professionals. You will be working with patient partners and multi-stakeholders in Singapore’s research and healthcare eco-system on developing PPI in research through a national guidance document on patient and public involvement (PPI) in health research in Singapore. You will play a key role to develop the communications and outreach strategy for the national guidance document and PPI in research, strengthening its narrative and leading the development of a website. This also includes activating the national guidance document through producing the guidance document with the Research team for the diverse target audience (researchers, clinicians and patient partners) and managing the outreach strategy and plan. We are looking for a dynamic individual, with strong communication expertise who has a strong interest in patient and community involvement in research and healthcare. Responsibilities: Advocate for PPI in research through the development of an effective communication and branding strategy for PPI in research and the Guidance Document.  Manage and develop the outreach strategy plan for the dissemination of the PPI Guidance Document and to advance PPI in the health research eco-system Drive the production of the PPI Guidance Document for the different target audience Lead the creation and management of the website for PPI in research and the PPI Guidance Document.  Manage the development of quality communication materials (eg. EDMs, web and social media content) on the PPI Guidance Document project and assigned projects for outreach to researchers, clinicians, healthcare professionals and patient partners. Build strong relationships with stakeholders (including patient partners) involved in developing PPI Organise meetings, workshops, seminars and events to advocate for PPI in research and the Guidance Document. Contribute to the administration of the PPI Guidance Document Project Requirements: Degree from an accredited university Possess at least 6 years of relevant working experience Proven experience in developing communication and branding strategy and managing communications and outreach project with multi-stakeholders Excellent editorial and written communication skills and experience in health communications, including websites and online content Experience in Patient and Public Involvement and Engagement (PPIE) and working in healthcare is an added advantage. Excellent interpersonal communication skills and versatility in working with people from diverse backgrounds : from researchers and clinicians to patients advocates Strategic thinking, strong organizational and administrative skills Resourceful and possess strong initiative to drive change Team-player with pleasant disposition and outgoing personality This is a 2 years contract appointment. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Academic_R00024783-1": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Outreach and Student Admin",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-19\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJoin Our Team at the School of Biological Sciences, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore The School of Biological Sciences (SBS), part of the College of Science at Nanyang Technological University, was established in 2002 with a mission to advance excellence in biological and biomedical sciences. Our research spans diverse and impactful areas including infectious diseases, immunology, neurodegenerative disorders, telomere biology, and genome function. SBS is home to a vibrant, international community of scientific leaders, researchers, and professionals dedicated to innovation, discovery, and education. Key Responsibilities Coordinate and support student administration matters, including leave applications, academic progression monitoring, and student support initiatives. Support the planning and execution of outreach and recruitment activities, including Open House, Tea Parties, school visits, and student engagement events. Provide administrative and logistical support for major School events, such as Science Discovery Camp, Convocation, and other student-related activities. Coordinate undergraduate admissions and scholarship interviews, including scheduling, communication with candidates and faculty members, and preparation of interview materials. Support the administration of Final Year Projects, including event logistics, documentation management, faculty workload reporting, and coordination with stakeholders. Support Accelerated Poly Pathway Programme, including admissions, registration, fee collection, and certification processes. Support examination administration and academic operations for undergraduate and postgraduate programmes. Maintain accurate records and ensure compliance with University policies and procedures. Requirements Bachelor’s degree from a recognised university; fresh graduates are welcome to apply. Candidates with a Polytechnic diploma and relevant working experience may also be considered. Knowledge of academic administration processes within a higher education environment, student lifecycle management, programme administration, and event coordination. Familiarity with Microsoft Office applications and database systems is preferred. Preferably 2-4 years of relevant administrative experience in higher education, student services, admissions, or programme administration. Strong organisational, coordination, and multitasking skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities and deadlines effectively. Excellent interpersonal, communication, and stakeholder management skills. Good analytical and problem-solving abilities, with proficiency in Microsoft Office applications. Meticulous, detail-oriented, and service-oriented, with a strong commitment to student experience. Adaptable and able to work both independently and collaboratively in a team environment. Professional, proactive, resourceful, and able to exercise initiative in a fast-paced environment. The College of Science seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager---Senior-Executive--Alumni-Engagement_R00025554": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager / Senior Executive, Alumni Engagement",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-19\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nYoung and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is ranked among the world’s top universities. NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science (CCDS) is a leading college that is known for its excellent curriculum, outstanding and impactful research, and world-renowned faculty. A hotbed of cutting-edge technology and groundbreaking research, the College aims to groom the next generation of leaders, thinkers, and innovators to thrive in the digital age. Located in the heart of Asia, NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science is an ‘exciting place to learn and grow'. We welcome you to join our community of faculty, students and alumni who are shaping the future of AI, Data Science and Computing. We invite suitable candidates to apply for Assistant Manager / Senior Executive, Alumni Engagement. The incumbent will support the Alumni Engagement Team at CCDS including furthering the relationship between CCDS and alumni, supporting initiatives that tap on the strength of our alumni to support our student body and ensuring the successful running of alumni events. Job Responsibilities: Alumni Engagement Activities Oversee, manage and support events together with the CCDS Alumni Association (CCDS AA) Facilitate meetings with relevant Alumni stakeholders Plan, organize and provide support for students and alumni activities and events Manage news write-ups and social media platforms to enhance CCDS Alumni Office’s engagement with existing students and alumni Serve as a point of contact to build enduring relationships with the CCDS AA and individual alumni to encourage ongoing involvement Address all alumni enquiries and coordinate engagement opportunities Alumni Strategies Design and implement comprehensive alumni engagement strategies that align with College’s interests and strengthen the alumni network Regularly assess alumni interests and motivations and create clear metrics that evaluate the success of events along with conducting continuous improvement proposals for future events Report and propose improvements to existing alumni strategies to the respective Alumni Leads Continuous Improvement Create clear metrics that evaluate the success of alumni events Conduct After Action Reviews (AARs) on all alumni events Establish SOPs for the running of events, budgeting and work responsibilities between CCDS AA and the College Improve existing SOPs to increase alumni engagement and efficacy of alumni programmes Maintain and update the Alumni SharePoint to ensure accurate documentation General Departmental Support Provide support across various departmental tasks and events within the College Coordinate logistics for departmental events and activities Address inquiries and assist the Deanery, faculty, students, and alumni   Alumni Finance Matters Monitor departmental budget, review allocated fund utilization and expenditure  Recommend purchases which align with the department’s needs Job Requirements: Bachelor's degree with at least 5 years of work experience in stakeholder management and partnership development. Working knowledge of event management, with experience in planning and executing large-scale events considered an advantage. Experience in stakeholder engagement and industry partnership management will be highly valued. Proficient in Microsoft Office applications and database management systems. Comfortable learning and working with new data and event management platforms. Able to work independently while contributing effectively in a team environment. Strong communication, interpersonal, and customer service skills. Willing to work weekends when required to support student and alumni events. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
