    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Guest-Service-Officer--NEC-_R00025243": {
      "title": "Guest Service Officer (NEC)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe NTU Office of Commercial and Auxiliary Services (OCAS) is responsible for the strategic planning, management, and marketing of commercial real estate, hospitality (including Nanyang Executive Centre) and auxiliary services (car parks and shuttle bus services) in NTU main campus and NTU@one-north. The Nanyang Executive Centre (NEC) is located at the NTU Main Campus. Currently undergoing refurbishment, the NEC features 150 guestrooms and aims to offer a premier venue for corporate training, retreats and private events. We are looking for a proactive, service-oriented professional to join NEC as Guest Service Officer . As the welcoming face of NEC, you will be responsible for creating exceptional first impressions and delivering personalised service throughout each guest's stay. You will support front desk operations, orientate guests, anticipate their needs, and ensure every touchpoint reflects the NEC's commitment to hospitality excellence. Key Responsibilities Greet and provide a warm welcome to arriving guests to ensure a welcoming first impression. Assist with guest check-in and check-out procedures, coordinate VIP and special guest arrivals and departures, in accordance with established SOPs.   Provide room orientation to the guests and introduce NEC facilities. Manage and coordinate special requests from guests to ensure personalized service delivery (e.g. celebrating special occasions). Collate and document guest feedback into the Property Management System. Ensure the lobby and guest-facing areas are always neat and clean. Proactive in meeting guests requests and needs throughout their stay. Handle guests request and redirect the request to the appropriate department(s) if request is not within scope and capacity of Front Office. Listen to guest’s complaint or concerns and resolve their issue in a timely manner. Be familiar with NTU and NEC facilities and functions as well as major city attractions and events. Provide guests with accurate information as requested. Perform any other duties as may assigned by Duty Manager/Front Office Manager. Requirement Nitec/Higher Nitec/Diploma in Hotel Management or relevant discipline. Experience:  Experience in the hospitality industry with a minimum of 1 year in a similar capacity. Communication Skills:  Good spoken and written communication skills in order to interact well with guest. Professional disposition : Well-groomed, display a professional disposition with strong interpersonal skills. Proactive : Proactive and prompt in meeting guest’s requests and needs. Able to work rotating shifts, including weekends and Public Holidays. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Housekeeping-Supervisor--Nanyang-Executive-Centre-_R00025470": {
      "title": "Housekeeping Supervisor (Nanyang Executive Centre)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 22 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe NTU Office of Commercial and Auxiliary Services (OCAS) is responsible for the strategic planning, management, and marketing of commercial real estate, hospitality (including Nanyang Executive Centre) and auxiliary services (car parks and shuttle bus services) in NTU main campus and NTU@one-north. The Nanyang Executive Centre (NEC) is located at the NTU Main Campus. Currently undergoing refurbishment, the NEC features 150 guestrooms and aims to offer a premier venue for corporate training, retreats and private events. We are looking for an experienced and service-oriented Housekeeping Supervisor to oversee and coordinate the daily operations of the housekeeping staff to ensure the highest standards of cleanliness and guest satisfaction. This is a leadership-focused role that involves training, scheduling, inspecting work, and managing inventory. This role reports to the Housekeeping Manager. Key Responsibilities: Staff management and training Schedules shifts, assigns daily tasks, and organizes replacements for staff absences. Provides training and coaching for new and existing housekeeping staff on cleaning procedures, safety protocols, and company standards. Monitors staff performance, provides feedback, and handles any disciplinary issues. Motivates team members to maintain high morale and foster a positive work environment. Quality assurance and guest satisfaction Inspects guest rooms, public areas (like lobbies and hallways), and other hotel spaces to ensure they meet cleanliness and safety standards. Responds promptly and professionally to guest requests, concerns, and complaints. Communicates with other departments, such as the front desk and maintenance, to provide timely updates on room statuses and to report any repair needs. Inventory and operations Manages inventory of cleaning supplies, linens, and in-room amenities, placing orders as needed. Ensures that all equipment is in working order and coordinates repairs or replacements. Adheres to and enforces health, safety, and sanitation regulations, including the proper handling of chemicals. Administrative function Maintains records of housekeeping activities, such as completed rooms and inventory counts. amenities, placing orders as needed. Helps with hiring and onboarding new staff. Assist with cleaning duties during staff shortages or high-volume periods.  Requirements: A diploma or equivalent in Hospitality Management, Tourism, or a related field Previous experience in a housekeeping or hospitality role is essential, with prior supervisory experience preferred. Leadership and team management: Strong ability to supervise, motivate, and train a team. Organizational and time management: Excellent skills for planning schedules, delegating tasks, and managing time-sensitive deadlines. Attention to detail: A meticulous eye for cleanliness and presentation is crucial. Communication and interpersonal skills: The ability to communicate effectively with staff, management, and guests. Problem-solving: Aptitude for resolving issues, from guest complaints to staffing conflicts. Adaptability: Capacity to work under pressure and adapt to changing workloads and schedules. Able to work rotating shifts. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager--Strategic-Initiatives--Disciplinary-and-Office-Management_R00024709-1": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager, Strategic Initiatives and Administration",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 22 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThis role is part of the Programme and Office Management (POM) team within the NBS Undergraduate Programmes Office (UPO) and plays a key leadership role in supporting the effective delivery of undergraduate education. The Senior Assistant Manager drives strategic initiatives, strengthen governance frameworks, and leads operational excellence across curriculum implementation, financial aid administration, and student management processes. Working closely with School leadership, Programme Directors, and central offices, the role contributes to institutional strategy, policy development, academic excellence, educational innovation, institutional integrity, and a high‑ quality student experience in support of the University’s mission . Responsibilities: Strategic Initiatives Support School leadership and Programme Directors in planning and implementing strategic academic initiatives, including curriculum launches, industry embedded learning, and internationalisation. Provide end to end administrative and project management support for new programmes, pathways, majors, and curriculum enhancements. Coordinate curriculum approvals, system set up, timetable readiness, and stakeholder communications to ensure smooth roll out and transition. Monitor implementation progress and consolidate feedback to support post implementation reviews and continuous improvement. Administration of Dean’s Global Immersion Award Oversee the end ‑ to ‑ end administration of the NBS Dean’s Global Immersion Award in accordance with the approved Rules of Administration, ensuring compliance with funding purpose, eligibility criteria, and usage conditions. Oversee and monitor award utilisation across the awardee’s candidature, including tracking of claim submissions and adherence to approved funding quantum. Ensure compliance with awardee obligations, including the submission of post ‑ engagement reflection reports after each funded trip, and adherence to stipulated academic performance and conduct requirements. Oversee record ‑ keeping and data management, including awardee profiles, utilisation status, reflections received, and engagement participation, to support governance, audit, and reporting needs. Administration of NBS Financial Aids Plan and oversee the end‑to‑end administration of undergraduate NBS financial aid schemes in accordance with approved policies and guidelines. Coordinate the application process, including document verification, shortlisting, interviews, and preparation of recommendations for selection committees. Liaise with the NTU Financial Aid Office and Finance to support financial verification and timely disbursement of approved funds. Ensure accurate documentation, proper governance, and compliance with the Rules of Administration (ROA) and Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs). Administration Support to Associate Deans and Deputy Director Provide administrative and coordination support for faculty appointments and renewals. Lead UPO budget planning, consolidation, monitoring, and reporting in alignment with school and university priorities. Evaluate and support funding requests for new initiatives, ensuring financial viability and value‑for‑money. Prepare budget utilisation and financial status reports for senior management oversight. Administrative Support to UPO Operations Support the day‑to‑day operational needs of the Undergraduate Programmes Office to ensure continuity and service quality. Coordinate onboarding and offboarding processes, including access provisioning and role‑based account management. Maintain distribution lists and shared resources to support effective communication across faculty and administrative stakeholders. Ensure administrative practices comply with data protection, IT security, and audit requirements. Disciplinary Matters Manage and support the administration of student disciplinary processes, including Preliminary Inquiries (PI) and Committees of Inquiry (COI). Maintain case files, draft reports, and prepare official correspondence related to disciplinary outcomes. Coordinate with faculty, Student Disciplinary Officers, and the Board of Discipline where cases are escalated. Ensure disciplinary processes are managed in accordance with University policies, SOPs, and governance standards. Requirements: Bachelor’s Degree Minimum 4 – 6 years of working experience (candidates with background and experience in IHLs will have an advantage) Strong project management and coordination skills Ability to work effectively with senior stakeholders and cross‑functional teams High level of professionalism, judgement, and discretion in handling sensitive matters Strong organisational, analytical, and communication skills Proficient in Microsoft Office applications Strategic thinking and problem-solving ability Excellent stakeholder management and communication skills Strong analytical and data interpretation skills Experience in process improvement or policy development preferred Able to manage multiple priorities and complex workflows Able to handle a large volume of data Able to multitask We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager---Senior-Executive--Research-Grant-Administration_R00025539": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager / Senior Executive, Research Grant Administration",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nYoung and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is ranked among the world’s top universities. NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science (CCDS) is a leading college that is known for its excellent curriculum, outstanding and impactful research, and world-renowned faculty. A hotbed of cutting-edge technology and groundbreaking research, the College aims to groom the next generation of leaders, thinkers, and innovators to thrive in the digital age. Located in the heart of Asia, NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science is an “exciting place to learn and grow”. We welcome you to join our community of faculty, students and alumni who are shaping the future of AI, Data Science and Computing. Key Responsibilities but are not limited to: To lead and manage a team of MSOs to support the operations of the Research Office. Oversee and manage the research grants administration (including RCAs), research finance, research staff hiring, and ensuring corporate governance of research projects and research integrity. Organise research events (research seminars/conferences/workshops), and handle research industry collaborations. To handle research data reporting (statistics/data required by various offices in NTU, external agencies, government organizations and P&T/contract renewals/faculty appraisals). Job Requirements: At least a bachelor’s degree Preferably with at least 5 years’ experience in research administration/ graduate program management in a tertiary education institution, with at least 3 years of supervisory experience leading a dynamic administrative team. Financial accounting knowledge preferred Strong leadership, stakeholder management and engagement skills Equipped with strong analytical skills with the ability to solve complex issues and work effectively under pressure. Possess excellent interpersonal and communication skills. High level of commitment and initiative. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Scientist--Mechanical-Materials-Manufacturing-Engineering-_R00025538": {
      "title": "Research Scientist (Mechanical/Materials/Manufacturing Engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Singapore Centre for 3D Printing (SC3DP) is a research centre conducting fundamental and applied research in all aspects related to additive manufacturing. Our vision is to be the world leader in 3D Printing and a wellspring of knowledge, delivering state of the art and innovative solutions to the industry. SC3DP is at the forefront of developing advanced technologies and high-impact research in areas such biomedical, construction, aerospace, marine and offshore. It is one of the very few research centres globally with multi-sector 3D printing expertise. SC3DP’s research achievements, high-level industry collaboration, comprehensive facilities and resources have positioned it as a leading hub for 3D printing research and innovation globally. The Research Scientist is expected to help the principal investigator to carry out a research project on laser additive manufacturing in collaboration with an industrial partner. Key Responsibilities: Manage the project with the defined milestones and deliverables. Carry out hands-on experiments to meet deliverables and KPIs. Write and prepare communications content and interface with the industry and funding agency. Job Requirements: Bachelor qualification degree in mechanical, materials or manufacturing engineering or related field At least 8 years of relevant experience in engineering research / technical hands-on experience in additive manufacturing or related field Proficiency in experimental skills in microstructural characterization, including metallograph and EBSD. Proficiency in experimental skills in mechanical testing, such as hardness testing. Demonstrated experience in laser directed energy deposition additive manufacturing. Knowledge of the relationship between microstructures and mechanical properties of metallic materials. Good written and oral communication skills Entry level candidates are welcome to apply We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturer-in-the-School-of-Mechanical-and-Aerospace-Engineering--MAE-_R00025543": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer in the School of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering (MAE)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe are looking for part-time instructors in the areas of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering within the College of Engineering, School of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering. Qualifications Applicants should possess minimally a recognized MEng degree, preferably PhD, in Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering or a closely related field, have extensive industry and/or academic experience with a passion for teaching. Instructors are expected to excel at teaching and work closely with students. As we are expanding our course offerings, we seek versatile individuals who can teach multiple courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Teaching Hours Classes are mainly conducted during the day/night on weekdays; or on Saturdays for make-up classes (if needed). In view of the current COVID situation, online teaching and assessments are expected to be conducted where required. In addition, applicant must be prepared to act according to the situational changes in number of CAs, CA formats, etc. when required by the School.   Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/IT-Manager--NEC---Hospitality-Systems-_R00025002": {
      "title": "IT Manager (NEC - Hospitality Systems)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe NTU Office of Commercial and Auxiliary Services (OCAS) is responsible for the strategic planning, management, and marketing of commercial real estate, hospitality (including Nanyang Executive Centre) and auxiliary services (car parks and shuttle bus services) in NTU main campus and NTU@one-north. The Nanyang Executive Centre (NEC) is located at the NTU Main Campus. It features 150 guestrooms and aims to offer a premier venue for corporate training, retreats and private events. We are looking for an experienced and service-oriented IT manager to oversee system operations, integrations, and technology enablement during NEC’s ongoing refurbishment and lead up to full opening. Key Responsibilities: 1. Systems Administration & Operation Partner with NEC’s Brand IT Team and NTU’s Centre for IT Services (CITS) to design, implement and maintain a resilient network architecture. Oversee daily operation of all NEC IT systems including PMS, POS, CRS, telecommunication, internet, and back-office systems. Ensure system uptime, reliability, and data integrity across all NEC functions. Manage server administration, data backups, and network configurations. Monitor system performance and proactively resolve issues to minimise downtime. 2. User Support & Training Develop and maintain functional documentation, SOPs and training materials for all NEC systems. Provide technical support to all NEC functions, troubleshooting hardware, software, and network issues in a timely manner. Coordinate user access rights, password controls, and compliance with IT policies. Provide staff training and systems onboarding to ensure smooth adoption of IT tools and cybersecurity awareness. 3. Cybersecurity & Data protection Implement and enforce data security protocols, antivirus measures, and system access controls. Ensure compliance with PDPA (Personal Data Protection Act) and required information security standards. Maintain regular updates and patch management for all systems and software. 4. Vendor & Contract Management Liaise with external vendors for system maintenance, upgrades, and technical support/troubleshooting. Review and manage IT-related service contracts, ensuring optimal service and cost efficiency. Evaluate new technology solutions and make recommendations to management. 5. Project Implementation Work closely with NEC team to analyse business needs to translate them into system requirements. Support NEC management team with technological insights to align IT strategies with overall business goals and objectives. Lead IT-related projects including system upgrades, new software implementation, and integration with third-party solutions. Coordinate with the brand IT team or corporate office on group initiatives and audits. Support technology requirements for events, conferences, and new operational setups. 6. Budgeting and Asset Management Prepare and manage the annual IT budget, ensuring cost control and resource optimisation. Maintain an accurate inventory of all IT hardware, software licenses, and related assets. Ensure preventive maintenance schedules and timely replacement of aging equipment. Requirem ents: A degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Software Engineering or related disciplines. Minimum 6 years of relevant IT experience, with a significant portion dedicated to supporting PMS systems in the hospitality industry. Hands-on experience with Opera integrations. Expertise in hospitality system integrations, particularly Oracle Opera PMS and interface management. Proficiency in network administration (LAN/WAN, wireless setups, firewalls). Familiarity with hospitality IT standards and third-party hospitality solutions. Demonstrated ability to liaise effectively with user departments and vendors. Strong troubleshooting, issue-tracking, and documentation skills. The appointment title offered will be commensurate with candidate’s prior work experience. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Tunnelling---Excavation-_R00025537": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Tunnelling & Excavation)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Civil and Environmental Engineering (CEE) at Nanyang Technological University is a leading school for Sustainable Built Environment. It has over 60 faculty members and more than 1,500 students and is rapidly expanding its range of education and research activities. The School of Civil and Environmental Engineering (CEE) aims at exploring and utilizing the underground space in a sustainable manner. Key Responsibilities: Responsible for developing explainable machine learning algorithms for Tunnel Boring Machine (TBM) tunnelling and excavation Developing large language model enhanced IoT system for TBM tunnelling and excavation Writing and publication of results in peer-reviewed journals Assist in securing external funding through grant applications and proposals Job Requirements: PhD in Civil Engineering or related field At least 2 years of relevant experience in technical hands-on experience for TBM tunneling and excavation Excellent programming skills, such as Python, MATLAB, or other competent languages. A good record of publications in reputable peer-reviewed journals or conferences  Proficiency in written and verbal communication Previous experience in proposal writing is a plus We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Waveguide-Integrated-Superconducting-Nanowire-Single-Photon-Detectors-_R00025534": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Waveguide-Integrated Superconducting Nanowire Single-Photon Detectors)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJoin Our Team at the Centre for Disruptive Photonic Technologies (CDPT) and the National Centre for Advanced Integrated Photonics (NCAIP), Nanyang Technological University, Singapore A Research Fellow / Research Engineer position is currently available across the Centre for Disruptive Photonic Technologies (CDPT) and the National Centre for Advanced Integrated Photonics (NCAIP), Nanyang Technological University (NTU), Singapore. The Research Fellow (Project Leader) will integrate Superconducting Nanowire Single-Photon Detectors (SNSPDs) with state-of-the-art quantum Photonic Integrated Circuits (PICs). The role will scale and advance the fabrication, testing, and packaging workflows for waveguide-integrated SNSPDs, with the goal of developing a commercially-viable single-photon detection system prototype. The position combines device development with exploration of use cases and pathways to commercialization, and directly supports NTU’s mission to develop and commercialize emerging quantum computing and networking technologies. Key Responsibilities: As an integral part of the project, the Research Fellow is expected to: Design PIC components and integrate SNSPDs with photonic integrated circuits. Scale and optimize fabrication and cryogenic testing workflows. Characterize detector and system performance, including detection efficiency, dark count rate, timing jitter, and yield. Develop packaging solutions compatible with the cryogenic environment, and manage and document process, design, and measurement data. Operate and maintain research laboratories, including cryostats and optical setups, in compliance with safety and laboratory protocols. Participate in the Venture Creation Program and pilot tests with research groups and industry partners, and explore potential use cases for the developed prototype. Contribute to progress reports, IP disclosures, grant proposals, and disseminate results through publications and at international conferences. Job Requirements: The applicant should: Hold a Ph.D. or Doctorate in Physics, Optical/Photonic Engineering, Electronic or Semiconductor Engineering, Information Science, or closely related disciplines. Have relevant research or industrial experience in one or more of the following: semiconductor/superconductor nanofabrication processes (thin-film deposition, photo- and electron-beam lithography, and etching); design and testing of cryogenic (< 10 K) electronic devices (e.g. superconducting devices, cryo-CMOS); or heterogeneous integration. Preferably be familiar with single-photon detection, heterogeneous integration, and quantum technologies concepts. Preferably have experience with photonic device/circuit design and simulation tools (e.g. Lumerical, Ansys, or similar). Have competence in data acquisition/analysis and scripting for instrument control (e.g. Python/MATLAB/LabVIEW). Demonstrate the ability to work both independently and within a collaborative research team, with strong communication and interpersonal skills. NTU seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Admin-Support_R00025193": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Admin Support",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Chemistry, Chemical Engineering and Biotechnology (CCEB) is seeking an experienced and highly motivated Senior Executive to join our team. The School is committed to developing programmes that offer cutting-edge lifelong learning solutions and globally recognized qualifications accessible by aspiring professionals and lifelong learners. This incumbent plays a critical role in supporting the school’s postgraduate office by providing administrative and operational support for the smooth running of master’s programmes. The role ensures that all processes related to student administration, academic operations, and postgraduate services are executed efficiently, in compliance with institutional policies and academic regulations. The position also supports continuous improvement initiatives to enhance service quality and operational effectiveness. This role reports to the Head of Graduate Office and Associate Chair (Graduate). Programme Operations: Academic Administration Administer postgraduate student life cycle activities including admission registration, enrolment, module registration, academic progression, examination, and graduation. Maintain accurate student records in university systems and ensure data integrity for reporting and audit purposes. Coordinate with academic departments, supervisors, and graduate committees to facilitate academic and administrative processes. Support the implementation of academic policies, guidelines, and quality assurance procedures for postgraduate programmes. Programme Operations: Operations & Process Management Manage day-to-day postgraduate office operations to ensure timely and accurate execution of academic and administrative tasks. Monitor key operational timelines such as course registration periods, examination schedules, and graduation deadlines. Prepare operational reports, statistics, and documentation for management review. Assist in process improvement and digitalisation initiatives to enhance efficiency and service delivery. Programme Operations: Outreach/Marketing Activities Organise outreach events for prospective students, current students, and alumni. Raise purchase requests for catering services via the Ariba system. Prepare ITQ documents for outreach/marketing-related activities. Prepare workshop/seminar announcements for posting in CCEB. Book venues for information sessions and seminars. Other Administrative Duties Manage the onboarding processes for part-time lecturers. Manage a role-based email account. Assist in the preparation and consolidation of data for reporting purposes where required. Assist the programme director in tracking the financial status of the programme and making accurate financial projections. Develop and maintain SOPs for the administration of the MSc programme. Liaise with University offices to ensure the smooth running of the programme. Attend meetings of College/University-level committees on MSc programmes. Assist in any ad hoc matters as delegated and required. Requirements Educational Qualification(s) Reputable Diploma or Bachelor’s degree. Specialisation in science or engineering disciplines is preferred but not essential. Knowledge Required Familiarity with admission cycles, matriculation processes, student records management, and academic progression tracking. Proficiency in basic productivity tools such as Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint), Microsoft Teams, and Adobe software. Ability to prepare, manage, and interpret administrative and academic data for operational and reporting purposes. Basic understanding of budget monitoring, cost tracking, and financial forecasting in an academic context. Relevant Experience 1–3 years of administrative experience, preferably in a higher education setting. Prior exposure to postgraduate or academic programme coordination is strongly preferred. Experience working with cross-functional stakeholders (faculty, students, and university departments). Skills & Competencies Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Ability to convey important information clearly and effectively. Responsible and independent, with strong time management skills. Skilled in multitasking while maintaining attention to detail. Good situational awareness and the ability to assess and respond to dynamic conditions effectively. Other Personal Attributes Proactive and positive attitude towards work tasks. Strong service orientation. Eagerness to learn new skills and systems. Self-motivated, with a proactive approach to challenges. Analytical thinker with strong problem-solving capabilities. The School of Chemistry, Chemical Engineering and Biotechnology seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Director--Community-Engagement-and-Partnerships_R00025090-1": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Director, Community Engagement and Partnerships",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Asian School of the Environment (ASE) ( https://www.ntu.edu.sg/ase ) is an interdisciplinary school at Nanyang Technological University (NTU) that uses Earth and environmental science, engineering, technology, and the social sciences to address key environmental challenges. ASE is a school within the NTU College of Science (CoS). The Earth Observatory of Singapore (EOS) ( https://earthobservatory.sg/ ) is a research institute with the mission to conduct fundamental research on earthquakes, volcanic eruptions, tsunamis and climate change in and around Southeast Asia, toward safer and more sustainable societies. We are seeking a Senior Assistant Director, Community Engagement and Partnerships, to lead the communications, events, education-marketing, brand management and partnerships function across EOS and ASE. The ideal candidate will have a strong interest in environmental sustainability and in contributing to a more resilient environmental future for Singapore and the region. The incumbent will report to the Interim Director of EOS and/or Chair of ASE. The role supervises three sub-functions and their leads, and is responsible for setting strategy, driving functional restructuring, and advancing financial sustainability for the community engagement and partnerships office. You will play a pivotal role in building and maintaining relationships that translate our science into public understanding, policy influence, and regional collaboration. This is an exciting opportunity to have significant impact in education, storytelling and stakeholder engagement across Earth and environmental sciences, working with a fantastic group of scientists, staff and students dedicated to forging a more sustainable and resilient future for our planet and communities. Key responsibilities Lead the restructuring of a newly merged Community Engagement and Partnerships office, and develop a five-year strategy across communications, events, education marketing, and partnerships. Drive the overall growth and expansion of the office to support EOS and ASE’s growth and reputational impact, including EOS’s ambition to serve as a national centre for translational and interdisciplinary Earth and environmental research. Oversee integrated communications and media functions, including social media, press relations, and media training to raise visibility across the full breadth of EOS and ASE science. Build strategic storytelling and reputation management for EOS and ASE, translating complex research into compelling narratives for policymakers, funders, media, and the public. Own the EOS and ASE brand and messaging framework, set editorial and visual standards across all channels, and advise leadership on reputational and crisis communications. Monitor communications performance through analytics and regular reporting, using the insight to refine strategy and demonstrate impact. Oversee external engagement programmes including schools’ outreach, delegations, open houses, student recruitment, conferences booths, and signature events and set the annual engagement calendar. Lead strategy and execution of partnerships across industry, government, and academia, and strengthen EOS/ASE’s international academic reputation. Lead workshop planning and convenings for foresight-and-futures and science-to-policy translation programme bringing together academics, government and industry stakeholders. Develop the financial sustainability of the office through grants, continuing-education revenue, and external partnerships. Manage the communications budget, external vendors and a high performing team across all sub functions. Work collaboratively with other key communications teams across NTU and Singapore, including the NTU Corporate Communications office and the College of Science engagement team. Requirements A bachelor’s degree in communications, journalism, public policy, environmental science, or a related discipline is required. A relevant postgraduate qualification is an advantage. Significant senior experience (15 years+) in community engagement, communications, and partnership building, ideally including a journalism or media background. At least 3-5 years of experience in a leadership or supervisory role. Proven experience leading and developing multi-disciplinary teams, including managing team leads, with the ability to work collaboratively across functions at a strategic level. Demonstrated strategic leadership including building and delivering multi-year strategy, leading organisational or functional restructuring, and driving high-profile projects from concept to impact. Proven track record of building and maintaining strong relationships with government, industry, and academic stakeholders, ideally in Singapore and/or Southeast Asia. Experience developing financial sustainability through grants, earned revenue (e.g. continuing education), and institutional or industry support would be a plus. Exceptional strategic storytelling skills with the ability to craft a compelling narrative from complex or politically sensitive environmental data and communicate them effectively to diverse stakeholders and the public. Working knowledge of the Singapore and ASEAN environmental-policy landscape (e.g. the Singapore Green Plan 2030, the National Biodiversity Strategy and Action Plan, and relevant ASEAN environmental agreements) would be beneficial. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, sound judgement; and the ability to operate confidently across media, science, policy, and public-facing contexts. Experience in digital communications and brand management, including establishing a consistent brand and messaging framework and editorial and visual standards across publications, websites, and digital channels. Experience managing external vendors and agencies as well as communications budgets to deliver cost-effective creative, media, and digital services, and using communications analytics to measure performance and inform strategy. We seek a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. Please submit a CV and Cover Letter to apply. All applications and materials submitted will be held in strict confidence. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Outreach---Engagement--NBS-Undergraduate-Programme-Office_R00025428-1": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Outreach & Engagement, NBS Undergraduate Programme Office",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAs a leading business school in Singapore and globally, Nanyang Business School competes with top business schools from around the world to attract applicants from diverse backgrounds to join its undergraduate programmes. The Senior Executive will report to the Manager (Outreach & Engagement) with dotted-line reporting to the Senior Assistant Manager (Outreach & Engagement). The incumbent plays an important role and is responsible for supporting the team in implementing activities related to brand awareness and positioning, marketing of assigned programmes, and achieving the enrolment goals of the UG programme. This role will collaborate closely with the other team members by supporting marketing, student outreach and recruitment functions to attract the best students to apply.   Key Responsibilities include but not limited to the following: Assist in the execution of the UG marketing plan to achieve the recruitment goals, which are measured by size of intake, quality and diversity Independently plan, coordinate, and execute assigned small-scale outreach activities Demonstrate ownership and accountability for assigned initiatives. Build and maintain strong relationships with internal and external stakeholders Coordinate multiple parties to deliver outreach activities successfully Support the analysis of market trends, candidates’ insights, programme trends and competitors’ analysis to build programme strategy Initiate, organize and run information sessions/webinars/experience days locally as well as internationally (as and when required) Manage stakeholder communications proactively Demonstrate ability to draft briefing notes, and presentations with high accuracy and minimal supervision Coordinate a portfolio of over 40 annual outreach and recruitment activities Supports both physical and virtual recruitment engagements across multiple target audiences Support budget tracking Draft responses to school outreach request. Prepare simple event plans and briefing notes for student ambassadors Any other marketing-related projects as assigned by the Senior Assistant Manager (Outreach) Key competencies and qualifications requirements: Degree in any field; Business or Marketing preferred. 1-2 years of relevant experience would be advantageous Familiar with media strategy, channels, content marketing, and social media marketing Experience in event marketing and management Excellent competency in using MS Office applications Proficiency in creating effective MS PowerPoint and delivering presentations to an audience of potential UG candidates Strong organizational and time management skills with the ability to coordinate and manage multiple projects concurrently Excellent interpersonal and collaborative spirit Strong verbal and written communication skills, and comfortable in presenting to internal and external stakeholders High results and achievement orientation High level of integrity and credibility Keen eye for detail The following competencies would be advantageous: Able to work after-office hours/weekends when required (Due to the nature of work for outreach and events) Enjoy meeting and connecting with new people We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Project-Officer-Research-Associate-Research-Fellow--Computer-Science-Mathematics-Statistics-_R00024774": {
      "title": "Research Engineer II (Computer Science/Mathematics/Statistics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nYoung and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is ranked among the world’s top universities. NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science (CCDS) is a leading college that is known for its excellent curriculum, outstanding and impactful research, and world-renowned faculty. A hot bed of cutting-edge technology and groundbreaking research, the College aims to groom the next generation of leaders, thinkers, and innovators to thrive in the digital age. Located in the heart of Asia, NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science is an ‘exciting place to learn and grow. We welcome you to join our community of faculty, students and alumni who are shaping the future of AI, Data Science and Computing. The candidate will work in Prof Ong’s Research Group, where cutting-edge research is carried out on a wide range of topics ranging across programming language (especially Bayesian statistical probabilistic programming), statistical machine learning, generative AI, and AI Safety. Job Responsibilities: Manage own academic research and administrative activities. This involves small scale project management, to co-ordinate multiple aspects of work to meet deadlines. Carry out original research, including adapting existing and developing new mathematical models, scientific techniques and experimental protocols, and building software tools and carrying out empirical studies where appropriate. Write, publish and disseminate results, including give research presentations at meetings. Contribute and develop ideas for new research projects and for generating research income, and present detailed research proposals to senior researchers Act as a source of information and advice to other members of the group on scientific protocols and experimental techniques. Represent the research group at external meetings / seminars, either with other members of the group or alone. Assist the PI in mentoring, supervising and coordinating the activities of junior researchers and students of the research project. Assist the PI in research collaboration and coordinating activities with project partners and collaborators from other institutions. Work with industry and government partners to understand their research needs and formulate solutions. Contribute to outreach, communications and reporting as required to funders and stakeholders. Represent the research group at external meetings/seminars, either with other members of the group or alone. Help organise and actively participate in regular meetings and seminars within the group. Assist in raising research funds through grant applications. The postholder may have the opportunity to teach. This may include lecturing, small-group teaching, and tutoring of undergraduates and graduate students. Job Requirements: Essential Criteria Candidates must have a PhD (or be near completion) in Computer Science or Mathematics or Statistics with a strong background in one or more of the following: AI, machine learning, Bayesian statistics, programming languages, logic and algorithms, formal methods, probability and measure theory. For senior research fellow role, candidates must hold a relevant PhD with significant track record of research excellence and substantial research leadership experience. Strong publication record and familiarity with the existing literature and research in the field of statistical machine learning, and deep learning or large language models. Possess sufficient specialist knowledge, research skills and interests in statistical machine learning, and deep learning or large language models to work within established research programmes and contribute ideas and solutions. Ability to independently plan and manage a research project, including a research budget. Possess strong collaboration abilities in person, on paper and over electronic channels. Excellent communication skills, including the ability to write for publication, present research proposals and results, and represent the research group at meetings. Desirable Criteria Experience of supervising staff. Experience of managing a research budget. Ability to raise research funds through making grant applications. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Human-Resource_R00025533": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Human Resource",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAs a key member of the HR team, you will play an essential role in supporting the HR Business Partner (HRBP) by managing a range of HR matters within the designated business unit(s). Your contributions will ensure the efficient and effective delivery of HR services, fostering a positive workplace environment. Key Responsibilities: You will support the HRBP in ensuring timely HR service delivery in the following key areas: Recruitment – collaborating with the Talent Acquisition and HR Shared Services team, you will support the administrative processes to ensure that the Business Unit is able to bring in the right talents in a timely manner Contract renewals of staff – you will work with key stakeholders to manage the administration of contract renewals of staff Performance management – you may also be expected to support the HRBP during the performance management cycle and this may include tracking timelines, helping People Managers to understand performance management tools and practices and consolidating data to facilitate discussions. HR Data – you will ensure that HR data is accurate and assist in preparation of HR reports/key updates to facilitate decision-making Provide HR advisory services regarding the university's policies and work processes Collaborate with the HRBP and HR Centres of Excellence on HR projects, including policy and process reviews. Qualifications: Degree with at least 3 years of experience in human resources administration or a related field. Candidates with prior experience of working in an educational / academic/ research environment would have an added advantage Highly attentive to details, possess the ability to multi-task and to manage deliverables under tight timelines Strong verbal and written communication skills; ability to interact effectively with diverse stakeholders Flexibility to adapt to changing priorities and evolving HR needs Ability to work collaboratively in a team environment while also being self-motivated Candidates with prior experience in using Workday system would have an advantage We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Director--Public-Programmes_R00025528": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Director, Public Programmes",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University is a leading global university recognised for excellence in education and research. Nanyang Business School (NBS) is one of Asia’s premier business schools, committed to delivering impactful education and driving innovation in teaching and engagement. The candidate will be leading Nanyang Executive Education’s Public Programmes. Key Responsibilities: To take ownership and lead business development efforts in the Public programmes To understand the executive education market, and perform analyses e.g. market research, competitor landscape, segmentation, growth trends, value proposition etc and make strategy recommendations To think strategically and to analyse and synthesize information into strategic actions as part of growing the NEE portfolio, in alignment with NBS/NEE overall business direction To service existing clients, in addition to adding new clients, as part of growing the pipeline and portfolio To work with closely with faculty to create learning proposals and programmes, through putting together information and persuasive ideas, that will meet manpower training needs and requirements To ensure high levels of client satisfaction as well as build trusted relationships with clients To grow strong relationship with key stakeholders, both internal and external, and find mutually beneficial ways of collaboration To identify and contextualize internal and external stakeholder issues and engage appropriately To assist in new corporate initiative development that will lead to better corporate processes and client experience Competencies and Qualification Requirements: A good bachelor’s degree, with at least 10 years’ working experience, preferably in the executive education, L&D department of an organization, or in consulting. A proven revenue-generation track record through business development, sales and bidding management Ability to work independently, as well as inter-dependently, within a team, and across teams Customer-oriented disposition, with excellent interpersonal skills, and to be able to work with all levels Good business acumen, with ability to develop proposals for clients in the areas of leadership and business management training Self-starter and problem-solver, who is adaptable to a changing environment, and is able to proactively address any challenges that may arise Excellent written, oral, presentation and facilitation skills Displays leadership skills and takes interest in nurturing and coaching junior members of the team We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Director--Major-Gifts_R00022794": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Major Gifts",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe NTU University Advancement Office (UAO) supports the University’s giving mission by fostering meaningful relationships and strategic partnerships with philanthropists, alumni, business community partners, corporations, foundations and friends that result in goodwill and philanthropy towards education and research.   We are seeking a highly motivated and passionate individual to join the Major Gifts team. The key responsibilities are: To develop and manage relationships and activities related to the cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship of donors and major gifts to maximise the University’s philanthropic outcomes. To take a strategic approach to fundraising which include major gifts, capital fundraising, corporate donations, grants and bequests. To leverage on the University leadership, faculty, and volunteers, in collaboration with other UAO colleagues, to advance relationships and gift discussions and ensure alumni, friends and corporate partners and foundations are best positioned to provide maximum levels of philanthropic support for NTU’s campaign priorities. To lead and facilitate gift structuring to optimise donor’s gift purpose and manage the process of closing the gift and work with the UAO Stewardship Team to cultivate and steer donors to the next level of giving.   Requirements: A Bachelor’s Degree in any discipline. Experience in Higher Education/Not-For-Profit fundraising with an ability to achieve monthly activity targets as a key metric of performance, is preferred. Candidates with appropriate business development/consultative sales experience may also be considered. Demonstrated experience managing complex and diverse relationships and the proven ability to collaborate effectively with multiple stakeholders. Exceptional interpersonal skills with proven ability to liaise, consult and negotiate confidently and professionally with donors, faculty, staff, and other stakeholders at all levels. Excellent written communication skills with extensive experience in developing business cases, proposals, and presentations. Well-developed planning and organisational skills with the ability to prioritise workload, meet deadlines and work under pressure in a fast-moving team environment. Sound acumen and strong professional presence as well as a collegial work style that promotes teamwork, creativity and open communication. Awareness of and sensitivity to a diverse range of stakeholders. A global, socially conscious mindset with an understanding and appreciation of cultural and intercultural sensitives. A proactive and solutions-oriented approach. Ability to influence without authority.   Appointment titles offered will commensurate with candidate’s prior work experiences.   We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Administrative-Support_R00025524": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Administrative Support",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-07\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Singapore Centre for 3D Printing (SC3DP) offers a full range of additive manufacturing services, from design and infrastructure to production and validation. With advanced technologies such as topology optimization, generative design, and bioinspired design, SC3DP creates optimized products using a variety of novel materials and printing processes, including hybrid printing, post-processing, and emerging technologies. Sustainability is a top priority for SC3DP, which offers material development and control services that combine artificial intelligence, big data, and other digital tools for process optimization, as well as non-destructive testing for AM parts. Backed by a team of experts and a state-of-the-art facility equipped with the latest equipment and technologies, SC3DP is committed to leading the way in sustainable additive manufacturing research and development.  The successful applicant will be responsible for providing operational and administrative support to the Centre, coordinating office activities, managing administrative processes, and ensuring effective support for faculty, research staff, and students. Job Responsibilities: Provide executive administrative support to the Executive Director, including managing schedules, coordination of meetings, and follow-up on operational matters. Support the overall administration and daily operations of the Centre, ensuring efficient coordination of activities and smooth workflow. Manage office IT and physical assets, including asset tracking, inventory management, and equipment allocation to support operational requirements. Plan, coordinate, and execute Centre events, ensuring effective organisation, timely implementation, and successful delivery of outcomes. Oversee event-related activities, including publicity and communications, preparation of presentation and event materials, logistical arrangements, and post-event follow-ups. Develop and coordinate corporate communications materials, including newsletters, annual reports, and ad-hoc announcements. Manage and maintain website content to ensure information is accurate, updated, and aligned with the Centre’s communication objectives. Requirements: Diploma/Degree in Business Administration or a related discipline with relevant experience in administrative and operational support, preferably in a higher education, research, or corporate environment. Proven experience in executive administrative support, office operations, asset management, and coordination of resources to support organisational needs. Strong organisational and coordination skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities, timelines, stakeholders, and operational activities effectively. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with experience in preparing reports, newsletters, presentations, corporate communications, and managing digital content platforms. Proactive, detail-oriented, and service-oriented individual with strong interpersonal skills, problem-solving abilities, and the ability to work independently while handling confidential information with discretion. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Student-Administration_R00025296": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Outreach and Student Admin",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJoin Our Team at the School of Biological Sciences, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore The School of Biological Sciences (SBS), part of the College of Science at Nanyang Technological University, was established in 2002 with a mission to advance excellence in biological and biomedical sciences. Our research spans diverse and impactful areas including infectious diseases, immunology, neurodegenerative disorders, telomere biology, and genome function. SBS is home to a vibrant, international community of scientific leaders, researchers, and professionals dedicated to innovation, discovery, and education. Key Responsibilities Process and administer student-related matters, including Leave of Absence (LOA) and Short Leave of Absence (SLOA) applications, in accordance with University policies and procedures. Monitor and follow up on student cases relating to academic warning, termination, withdrawal, special needs, and students who are missing in action, and provide administrative support and advice on academic matters. Support the planning and execution of undergraduate and postgraduate outreach, recruitment, and student engagement activities, including Open House, Tea Parties, school visits, Science Discovery Camp, Convocation, and related events. Coordinate event logistics and administration, including registration, communications, venue setup, stakeholder liaison, catering, and operational support to ensure smooth event delivery. Coordinate undergraduate admissions and scholarship interview processes, including interview scheduling, preparation of interview materials, communication with applicants and faculty, and maintenance of interview records. Provide administrative support for Final Year Project (FYP) assessments and presentations, including coordination of logistics, venue setup, IT support, thesis and Turnitin report archival, and tabulation of faculty supervision and assessment hours. Administer academic programme activities, including the Accelerated Poly Pathway Programme (APP), course registration, fee collection, certificate issuance, and examination administration for undergraduate and postgraduate programmes. Maintain accurate student, programme, and examination records, and ensure compliance with University regulations, policies, and timelines. Requirements Bachelor’s degree from a recognised university; fresh graduates are welcome to apply. Candidates with a Polytechnic diploma and relevant working experience may also be considered. Knowledge of academic administration processes within a higher education environment, student lifecycle management, programme administration, and event coordination. Familiarity with Microsoft Office applications and database systems is preferred. Preferably 2-4 years of relevant administrative experience in higher education, student services, admissions, or programme administration. Strong organisational, coordination, and multitasking skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities and deadlines effectively. Excellent interpersonal, communication, and stakeholder management skills. Good analytical and problem-solving abilities, with proficiency in Microsoft Office applications. Meticulous, detail-oriented, and service-oriented, with a strong commitment to student experience. Adaptable and able to work both independently and collaboratively in a team environment. Professional, proactive, resourceful, and able to exercise initiative in a fast-paced environment. The College of Science seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow---Senior-Research-Fellow--Wireless-Localization---Sensing-_R00025504": {
      "title": "Research Fellow / Senior Research Fellow (Wireless Localization & Sensing)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 26 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research. With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 2,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 4th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2025 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee We are looking for a Research Fellow/Senior Research Fellow (Wireless Localization & Sensing) to conduct experimentally driven research on radio-based localization, tracking, and sensing for future 6G communication and Internet-of-Things systems. The Research Fellow/Senior Research Fellow will develop localization and sensing algorithms, implement them on real hardware platforms, design and conduct measurement campaigns, and build demonstrable prototypes in realistic indoor environments. The Research Fellow/Senior Research Fellow will work closely with the Principal Investigator and collaborators/students across NTU Singapore to deliver high-quality research, experimental testbeds, reusable datasets and software, peer-reviewed publications, intellectual property, and follow-on research proposals. Key Responsibilities: Conduct original research on wireless localization, tracking, and sensing techniques, with a strong emphasis on practical implementation and experimental validation. Identify potentially patentable research outcomes and fill in patent application forms. Write and publish high-quality research papers. Assist in the preparation and writing of research grant proposals. Co-supervise undergraduate and/or graduate students. Job Requirements: PhD in electrical and electronic engineering, communication engineering, signal processing, radar engineering, remote sensing, or related discipline. Strong publication record and hands-on experience in one of the following areas: wireless localization, wireless sensing, AI/machine learning for communications, or signal processing. Ability to conduct experimental research independently and collaboratively within a team. Good written and oral communication skills in English - essential for data analysis and communication with stakeholders We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/NIE-Overseas-Graduate-Scholarship--Mathematics---Mathematics-Education-_R00024927": {
      "title": "NIE Overseas Graduate Scholarship (Mathematics & Mathematics Education)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 26 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nOBJECTIVE The National Institute of Education Overseas Graduate Scholarship (NIE OGS) will sponsor outstanding candidates to pursue full-time doctoral studies overseas. Upon completion of their doctoral studies, candidates will return to NIE to serve as educators and academics. ELIGIBILITY CRITERIA The applicant must fulfill the following criteria: Be a Singapore Citizen. Has excellent academic records with very good Honours or Master’s degrees (or professional qualifications of equivalent standing), with relevant teaching and some research experience. Has the passion to pursue a challenging career in academia. TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF SCHOLARSHIP The scholarship is tenable for a period of three years. The scholarship will provide: Two sets of economy class air tickets (one at commencement and completion of doctoral studies, and one to return to Singapore for data collection for doctoral thesis). Overseas maintenance allowance. Stipend. Pre-studies allowance (at commencement of doctoral studies). Thesis allowance (upon completion of doctoral studies). Tuition and other compulsory fees. Conference and fieldwork grants (by application). A scholar studying in the United States may be considered for a fourth year of sponsorship if the required minimum period of candidature is at least 4 years. The scholar may be required to serve a few months in the Ministry of Education (MOE) Headquarters before embarking on his/her doctoral studies (if applicable). The scholar will be required to enter into a bond to serve the National Institute of Education Nanyang Technological University (NIE NTU) as an employee for a period of five years upon obtaining the doctoral degree. NIE NTU reserves the right to revise the terms and conditions of the scholarship as it deems fit. AREA OF STUDY Mathematics or Mathematics Education The Mathematics & Mathematics Education (MME) Department at the NIE leads in academic and curriculum studies in Mathematics and Mathematics Education for pre-service teachers and in-service teachers. We are committed to exploring innovative methods of instruction aligned to the latest international trends in mathematics and mathematics education and seeking to develop excellent practices in our collaboration with our partners, both schools and other universities. We invite applicants who are interested to pursue a PhD in either Mathematics or Mathematics Education . For Mathematics Education, the research topic should be an area that is of direct relevance to the Singapore education. For Mathematics, the research topic could be one that can preferably be useful to the School Mathematics curriculum (e.g., an area in Discrete Mathematics). The applicant should be a Singapore school teacher with very good Honours degree or a Master’s degree. Applicants who demonstrate ongoing engagement in research prior to his/her PhD will be preferred. Applicants should meet the following criteria: Familiarity with the Singapore education system, with at least three years of teaching experience. For Mathematics Education, at least three years of K-12 teaching experience is required. At least a Second Class Honours (Upper Division) degree or a Master’s degree in Mathematics or Mathematics Education or a related field. Experience in either content research, education research, or related disciplines prior to PhD studies is highly preferred. Publications in international peer-reviewed academic journals will be an advantage. Demonstrated passion and commitment to serving as an academic staff member at NIE, particularly in teaching, research, and service in areas related to Mathematics or Mathematics Education. APPLICATION PROCESS The following supporting documents must be submitted together with the application form to NIE NTU, through Workday, by the closing date : a. Curriculum Vitae (which should include academic qualifications, employment history, scholarships & awards, a brief description of your research experience and publication list if available). b. A succinct write-up (2 pages) on the research topic which you intend to pursue. c. A succinct write-up (4 pages) on your commitment and interest in the area of study applied for and the expected contribution to NIE, schools and the Singapore education system. d. An abstract of any thesis previously written. e. Copies of two pieces of research work that you consider to be your most significant works (if available). f. All relevant educational certificates and transcripts including GCE ‘O’ Level, GCE ‘A’ Level, Polytechnic Diploma, University Degree(s). g. Letters for scholarships, prizes, other awards, memberships in academic & professional societies (if available). h. A copy of the letter(s) of offer from each university applied to for admission to doctoral studies (if available). i. A copy of the letter(s) of offer for other scholarships and/or awards applied for and the outcome of these applications (if available). j. A minimum of two confidential referees’ reports (preferably from academic referees) printed on the official letterhead, to be sent directly to hrdacad@nie.edu.sg . CONTACT INFORMATION For clarification or more information, please contact: Area of Study Head, MME for Mathematics or Mathematics Education here . Terms and Conditions of Scholarship NIE Human Resource Department - Email to hrdacad@nie.edu.sg . CLOSING DATE All applications, together with the required documents (a) to (j), must be submitted by 30 September 2026 . Please note that NIE reserves the right to consider only complete applications accompanied by all required documents. Each application will be assessed on its own merits. Only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/NIE-Overseas-Graduate-Scholarship--Visual---Performing-Arts-_R00024928-1": {
      "title": "NIE Overseas Graduate Scholarship (Visual & Performing Arts)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 26 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nOBJECTIVE The National Institute of Education Overseas Graduate Scholarship (NIE OGS) will sponsor outstanding candidates to pursue full-time doctoral studies overseas. Upon completion of their doctoral studies, candidates will return to NIE to serve as educators and academics. ELIGIBILITY CRITERIA The applicant must fulfill the following criteria: Be a Singapore Citizen. Has excellent academic records with very good Honours or Master’s degrees (or professional qualifications of equivalent standing), with relevant teaching and some research experience. Has the passion to pursue a challenging career in academia. TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF SCHOLARSHIP The scholarship is tenable for a period of three years. The scholarship will provide: Two sets of economy class air tickets (one at commencement and completion of doctoral studies, and one to return to Singapore for data collection for doctoral thesis). Overseas maintenance allowance. Stipend. Pre-studies allowance (at commencement of doctoral studies). Thesis allowance (upon completion of doctoral studies). Tuition and other compulsory fees. Conference and fieldwork grants (by application). A scholar studying in the United States may be considered for a fourth year of sponsorship if the required minimum period of candidature is at least 4 years. The scholar may be required to serve a few months in the Ministry of Education (MOE) Headquarters before embarking on his/her doctoral studies (if applicable). The scholar will be required to enter into a bond to serve the National Institute of Education Nanyang Technological University (NIE NTU) as an employee for a period of five years upon obtaining the doctoral degree. NIE NTU reserves the right to revise the terms and conditions of the scholarship as it deems fit. Music The Visual & Performing Arts (VPA) Department at the NIE offers a vibrant and intellectually rich environment for the preparation of arts educators in drama, music and visual art. Deeply rooted in arts education and attentive to developments in contemporary artistic practice, the department values both strong practitioner expertise and rigorous theoretical grounding. Committed to Singapore’s context and internationally engaged in outlook, VPA prepares arts educators for both pre-service and in-service settings, while also offering graduate programmes in the arts and arts education. This call is open to applicants who wish to pursue a PhD in Music within a dynamic and forward-looking academic setting. Proposed research should be grounded in strong disciplinary foundations in music while engaging contemporary developments in a technology-pervasive world. Projects may span both musical art and sound arts, and should speak meaningfully to Singapore’s multicultural context while contributing to wider conversations in Music and Music Education. Applicants should meet the following criteria: Familiarity with the Singapore education system, with at least three years of teaching experience in a K-12 or pre-tertiary institution. At least a Second Class Honours (Upper Division) degree, or a Master’s degree, in Music or a related field. Experience in music-related research, academic publishing, and presenting at international and/or regional conferences is highly preferred. A strong record of artistic or professional practice, or creative works, including areas such as performance, composition, conducting, or music production, where relevant. Demonstrated passion and commitment to serving as an academic staff member at NIE, particularly in teaching, research, and service in areas related to Music and Music Education. APPLICATION PROCESS The following supporting documents must be submitted together with the application form to NIE NTU, through Workday, by the closing date : a. Curriculum Vitae (which should include academic qualifications, employment history, scholarships & awards, a brief description of your research experience and publication list if available). b. A succinct write-up (2 pages) on the research topic which you intend to pursue. c. A succinct write-up (4 pages) on your commitment and interest in the area of study applied for and the expected contribution to NIE, schools and the Singapore education system. d. An abstract of any thesis previously written. e. Copies of two pieces of research work that you consider to be your most significant works (if available). f. All relevant educational certificates and transcripts including GCE ‘O’ Level, GCE ‘A’ Level, Polytechnic Diploma, University Degree(s). g. Letters for scholarships, prizes, other awards, memberships in academic & professional societies (if available). h. A copy of the letter(s) of offer from each university applied to for admission to doctoral studies (if available). i. A copy of the letter(s) of offer for other scholarships and/or awards applied for and the outcome of these applications (if available). j. A minimum of two confidential referees’ reports (preferably from academic referees) printed on the official letterhead, to be sent directly to hrdacad@nie.edu.sg . CONTACT INFORMATION For clarification or more information, please contact: Area of Study Head, VPA for Music here . Terms and Conditions of Scholarship NIE Human Resource Department - Email to hrdacad@nie.edu.sg . CLOSING DATE All applications, together with the required documents (a) to (j), must be submitted by 30 September 2026 . Please note that NIE reserves the right to consider only complete applications accompanied by all required documents. Each application will be assessed on its own merits. Only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager--Faculty-Affairs_R00022769": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager, Faculty Affairs",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 26 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe College of Engineering (CoE) at Nanyang Technological University (NTU) is seeking a dynamic and detail-oriented Senior Assistant Manager to join our Faculty Affairs team. This strategic role works closely with the Head of Faculty Affairs to support the Associate Dean (Faculty) in managing critical faculty-related matters across all Engineering schools, ensuring operational excellence and supporting the College’s mission to attract, develop, and retain world-class faculty talent. Key Responsibilities: 1. Faculty Recruitment Coordinate faculty recruitment activities across CoE schools, including global faculty recruitment outreach events and campus visit programmes (e.g. Emerging Scholars Forum). Liaise with schools’ Faculty Administrators (FAs) and Human Resource Business Partners (HRBPs) to manage recruitment timelines and processes. Support the preparation of faculty appointment dossiers and documentation for the College committee’s review. Track schools’ search progress and recruitment metrics to prepare reports for the College leadership. 2. Faculty Appointments and Reappointments Manage the administrative processes for new faculty appointments, contract renewals, and reappointments. Coordinate with schools to ensure timely submission of appointment/reappointment documentation and compliance with University policies. Maintain accurate records of faculty appointments and contract terms across all CoE schools. 3. Faculty Performance Appraisal Oversee the annual faculty appraisal exercise across the College and CoE Schools to ensure adherence to timelines and processes. Coordinate with schools’ FAs and HRBPs to compile and track appraisal submissions. Prepare reports on appraisal outcomes for College leadership review. Support the implementation of performance management initiatives. 4. Faculty Development and Culture Assist in organising faculty development programmes, workshops, and engagement activities. Support initiatives to enhance faculty experience and foster a positive academic culture. Coordinate with schools on onboarding programmes for new faculty members. Facilitate communication of faculty-related policies and resources. 5. Faculty Promotion and Tenure Coordinate the promotion and tenure review processes across CoE schools. Work with school FAs to ensure complete and timely submission of promotion dossiers. Maintain documentation and tracking systems for promotion cases. Support the preparation of materials for College committees' review. 6. Strategic Support and Process Improvement Contribute to the review and streamlining of faculty-related processes to enhance efficiency. Prepare presentations, reports, and briefing materials for College committees and leadership. Maintain comprehensive databases and management information systems for faculty affairs. Support ad-hoc projects and initiatives related to faculty matters at the College level. Qualifications and Requirements: Education and Experience: A recognised university degree, preferably in engineering, business management, or a related field. At least 3-5 years of relevant experience in human resources, faculty academic administration, or related fields. Experience with faculty affairs is highly advantageous. Skills and Competencies: Strong organisational and project management skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills to work effectively with diverse stakeholders, including faculty, administrators, and senior leadership. High attention to detail and commitment to accuracy in documentation and processes. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite, M365 productivity tools, data analysis, and database management. Analytical mindset with the ability to prepare clear reports and presentations. Ability to handle sensitive and confidential information with discretion. Self-motivated with the ability to work independently and collaboratively in a team. Personal Attributes: Proactive problem-solver with strong service orientation. Adaptable and resilient in a fast-paced academic environment. Strong work ethic with commitment to excellence. Cultural sensitivity and ability to work in an ‘international’ environment. Note: We recognise that not every candidate will fulfil every qualification listed. If you believe you have the relevant experience, transferable skills, and motivation to succeed in this role, we encourage you to apply. Why Join Us? NTU College of Engineering is consistently ranked among the world’s top engineering colleges. You will work at the strategic heart of the College, supporting critical decisions that impact faculty recruitment, development, and excellence across our diverse engineering disciplines. This role offers a unique opportunity to collaborate with distinguished academic leaders, engage with international faculty talent, and contribute to innovative initiatives that enhance faculty experience and organisational excellence. With exposure to high-level strategic planning and direct involvement in processes that shape the academic community, you’ll develop specialised expertise in faculty affairs within one of Singapore’s premier universities. How to Apply: Interested applicants are invited to submit their detailed resume and cover letter through NTU’s career portal. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Visiting-Associate-Professor_R00025518": {
      "title": "Visiting Associate Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 26 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nVisiting Associate Professor Position in Nanophotonics Young and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University (NTU Singapore) is ranked 12th globally. It is also placed 1st among the world's best young universities. The Division of Physics and Applied Physics (PAP) at NTU invites applications for positions at the rank of Visiting Associate Professor in Photonics. We are looking for candidates holding a Ph.D. degree in physics, photonics, optoelectronics or a closely related area. The Visiting Associate Professor will collaborate with PAP colleagues to work in the area of quantum and topological photonic metamaterials and metasurfaces, time-crystal photonics, and nanoimaging. He/she will get involved in collaborative externally projects with PAP colleagues, as well as explore collaborations with colleagues from other Schools within NTU, with the aim of deepening institutional links between NTU and the candidate’s institution. The candidate should have more than 10 years of experience in cutting edge research in nanophotonics materials and devices, and deep knowledge in the latest research directions in metamaterials and metasurfaces. He/she should also be an expert in nanofabrication and nano-optics characterization techniques. He/she should have demonstrated an ability to obtain external grants, plus regularly publish in top-tier journals such as the Nature and Science family of journals. Enquiries about the position can be addressed to Professor LEW Wen Siang. Applications will be accepted until the positions are filled. All applications and materials submitted will be held in strict confidence. Only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Emoluments and General Terms & Conditions of Service The commencing salary will depend on the candidate's qualifications, experience and the level of appointment offered. Information on emoluments and general terms and conditions of service is available in the section on Terms and Conditions of Service for Academic Appointments. Application Procedure To apply, please refer to the Guidelines for Submitting an Application for Faculty Appointment at: http://www.ntu.edu.sg/ohr/career/submit-an- application/Pages/Faculty-Positions.aspx and send your application package and any enquiries to PAPrecruit@ntu.edu.sg. All applications and materials submitted will be held in strict confidence Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Visiting-Associate-Professor_R00025519": {
      "title": "Visiting Associate Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 26 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nVisiting Associate Professor Position in Network Security/Cryptography Young and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University (NTU Singapore) is ranked 12th globally. It is also placed 1st among the world's best young universities. The College of Science seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We are seeking a Visiting Associate Professor to teach one or more courses in the MSc in Cybersecurity - Applied Cryptography program. The program and curriculum structure can be found on Master of Science in Cybersecurity - Applied Cryptography | NTU Singapore. The preferred candidate should have a proven track record in teaching at the graduate level in a variety of formats (preferably including online instruction). The course format consists of 13 weeks for 3.0 AU course. The instructor will be responsible for leading lectures and tutorials for at least 3.50 hours per week in addition to syllabus planning, class preparation, marking for assessments and student consultations. Enquiries about the position can be addressed to Associate Professor Guo Jian,at guojian@ntu.edu.sg . Applications will be accepted until the positions are filled. All applications and materials submitted will be held in strict confidence. Only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Computer-Engineering-Computer-Science-Electronics-Engineering-_R00025520": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Computer Engineering/Computer Science/Electronics Engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 26 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nYoung and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is ranked among the world’s top universities. NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science (CCDS) is a leading college that is known for its excellent curriculum, outstanding and impactful research, and world-renowned faculty. A hot bed of cutting-edge technology and groundbreaking research, the College aims to groom the next generation of leaders, thinkers, and innovators to thrive in the digital age. Located in the heart of Asia, NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science is an ‘exciting place to learn and grow. We welcome you to join our community of faculty, students and alumni who are shaping the future of AI, Data Science and Computing. MMLab@NTU at CCDS is a research lab at Nanyang Technological University focused on advancing computer vision, multimodal AI, generative AI, and embodied AI. Founded in 2018, the lab has grown into a vibrant research group with around 40 members comprising faculty, research staff, and PhD students. Our members develop both foundational methods and practical systems, with recent research covering areas such as large multimodal models, generative intelligence, 3D content creation, scene understanding, and efficient vision models for real-world deployment. We are seeking Research Fellow to join a university-level research centre collaborating with industry. The position is for one year, renewable subject to satisfactory performance. Successful candidates will be involved in a project that is related to generative design. Key Responsibilities: To independently undertake research in machine learning.   To produce research reports and/or publications as required by the funding body or for dissemination to the wider academic community.   To provide guidance and support to any students associated with the project.    To attend, contribute, and where necessary lead relevant meetings.   To undertake any other duties relevant to the programme of research.  Job Requirements: PhD degree in Computer Engineering, Computer Science, Electronics Engineering or equivalent. Strong background in machine learning and computer vision. Strong publication records in top-tier machine learning or computer vision conferences/journals, such as TPAMI, IJCV, CVPR, ICCV, ECCV, NeurIPS, ICML and AAAI. Knowledge of scientific or engineering software like PyTorch.                                                                Assist in postgraduate student supervision. Capacity to conduct small group teaching such as undergrad labs and tutorials. Ability to initiate collaboration research in multidisciplinary team. Oversee and report project progress. Ability and willingness to work some flexible hours. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager---Assistant-Manager--Content-Creation_R00025522": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager / Assistant Manager, Content Creation",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 26 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nYoung and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is ranked among the world's top universities. NTU's College of Computing and Data Science (CCDS) is a leading college that is known for its excellent curriculum, outstanding and impactful research, and world-renowned faculty. A hotbed of cutting-edge technology and groundbreaking research, the College aims to groom the next generation of leaders, thinkers, and innovators to thrive in the digital age. Located in the heart of Asia, NTU's College of Computing and Data Science is an 'exciting place to learn and grow'. We welcome you to join our community of faculty, students and alumni who are shaping the future of AI, Data Science and Computing. We are seeking an experienced and dynamic Content Writer to be involved with the College’s branding campaigns and activities. What You Will Do: 1. Strategic Communications Develop and drive the College's integrated communications strategy to strengthen brand positioning, reputation, and stakeholder engagement locally. Collaborate closely with faculty members, researchers, and corporate stakeholders to drive communication initiatives. Lead the development of compelling thought content, executive communications, speeches, media features, strategic publications, and digital storytelling initiatives. 2. Content Creation Develop and implement internal and external communication strategies, ensuring alignment with the College’s branding and objectives. Create and manage high-quality communication materials, including press releases, presentations, website content, and corporate collaterals. Oversee and maintain the College’s websites, ensuring accuracy, relevance, and up-to-date content. Optimise the user experience (UX) and interface of the College’s websites to ensure they are visually appealing, accessible, and user-friendly. Monitor and analyse social media performance metrics, using data-driven insights to refine content and campaign strategies. Stay informed of emerging social media trends and best practices, continuously improving digital engagement strategies. 3. Branding and Promotion Support the development and execution of publicity campaigns to enhance the College’s visibility and brand awareness. Ensure that event publicity materials and marketing collaterals created by event organisers align with the College’s branding and communication guidelines. Oversee the planning and execution of College events, ensuring they are effectively promoted and successfully delivered. 4. Editing and Proofreading Review, edit, and refine content for clarity, accuracy, consistency, and adherence to brand style guidelines. Ensure all written materials maintain high editorial standards, with precise grammar, spelling, punctuation, and tone. 5. Performance Analytics and Reporting Establish communication effectiveness metrics and dashboards to evaluate campaign performance and stakeholder engagement. Analyse audience insights, website analytics, media coverage, and social media trends to inform strategic decision-making. Who You Are: Minimum a bachelor’s degree in mass communications, Literary Arts, New Media, Marketing, or a related field. At least 7 years of relevant experience in corporate communications and media, preferably within an educational institution. Tech-savvy and proficient in Microsoft Office and digital marketing tools, including Google Analytics and SEO. Well-versed in the digital economy, with experience managing digital public relations platforms and online engagement. Exceptional writing, editing, and proofreading skills, with strong attention to detail. Ability to craft clear, concise, and compelling narratives—from brand storytelling to impactful reports—demonstrating a strong sense of structure and storytelling techniques. A meticulous, dedicated, and proactive team player, who thrives on challenges and can multi-task effectively. Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to interpret data and optimise communication strategies. Strong interpersonal and communication skills (both verbal and written), with the ability to engage diverse stakeholders. Self-motivated, responsible, and proactive, with a positive work attitude and a commitment to excellence. Ability to manage high-pressure situations, demonstrating resilience and adaptability. Strong organisational skills, with the ability to prioritise and manage multiple projects simultaneously . We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Bioengineering-_R00025515-1": {
