    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Programme-Director--Talent-Management-_R00025506": {
      "title": "Programme Director (Talent Management)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 27 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe CyberSG R&D Programme Office (CRPO) is a new national centre at Nanyang Technological University, Singapore. CRPO will focus its efforts on three main thrusts to advance cybersecurity comprehensively: cutting-edge research and development, advancements in technology and translational development, and fostering ecosystem/industry growth and training. CRPO aspires to propel Singapore to the forefront of cybersecurity innovation and implementation, fueled by funding from the Cybersecurity Agency of Singapore (CSA). This financial backing empowers CRPO to finance visionary projects proposed by diverse entities, including research institutes (RIs), institutions of higher learning (IHLs), and industries. The scope of these initiatives spans the entire Technology Readiness Level (TRL) spectrum, from nascent concepts at TRL 1 to advanced, field-tested solutions at TRL 9, all within the dynamic realm of cybersecurity. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/crpo/crpo-verticals/translation-management . We are looking f or a Programme Director for Talent Management who will oversee a team of officers. The role will focus on i dentification of translational opportunities from cybersecurity research across IHLs in Singapore funded by the NRF. Key Responsibilities: Facilitate and matchmake stakeholders across startups, academia, and industry towards Talent Management. Oversee financial stewardship and budget allocation for all projects, ensuring efficient and accountable use of funds, adherence to cost guidelines, and alignment with institutional policies. Monitor Talent management events performance, including milestones, deliverables, risk management, and reporting, to ensure projects achieve high-impact outcomes in cybersecurity talents and events. Drive Talent Management team goals by identifying gaps, recommending enhancements, and integrating lessons learned from past projects to strengthen effectiveness. Provide leadership and guidance to Talent management team, ensuring clarity of roles, professional development, and effective coordination Ensure strategic alignment of matching talents within funded projects with CRPO’s mission to build Singapore’s national cybersecurity capabilities and foster innovation Collaborate and render support across verticals to ensure smooth operation and achieving KPI Job Requirements: Minimum requirement is bachelor’s degree qualification in talent management, entrepreneurship, business management or related field At least 10 years of relevant experience in Director’s role with hands-on experience in similar responsibilities and scope is necessary Familiarity with required scope in translation management is crucial Good written and oral communication skills (necessary) Proficiency in project performance management is crucial and acquired through minimum 10 years industry and practical training (on the job) Competent in talent management design and deployment is necessary Interpersonal skill as competent team leader with ability to work under tight timelines and develop solutions within Grantor’s criterion Ability to build rapport and influence stakeholders at all levels Possesses international experience, with a strong network of contacts in the region. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Research-Administration-and-Support-Services--LKCMedicine-_R00025446": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Research Administration and Support Services [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nThe Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. We are looking for a detail-oriented individual to join the Department of Research Administration and Support Services (RASS) at LKCMedicine. The role manages research grant administration across the full grant lifecycle, working with academic faculty members, University offices, external stakeholders and funders. Responsibilities: Manage assigned grant matters across the grant lifecycle from grant calls and proposal submissions to award set-up, variations, reporting and closure, in line with funder and University requirements. Review grant budgets, utilisation, expenditure and financial documentation to support compliance and audit readiness. Advise faculty members and research teams on funder guidelines, institutional processes, documentation requirements, approval routes and compliance expectations. Coordinate with University offices, funders and external stakeholders to resolve grant-related queries, submissions, operational issues and follow-up actions. Maintain accurate grant records, trackers and supporting documentation to support management reporting, monitoring, funder reporting and audit readiness. Contribute to broader grant operations and team priorities, including process improvement, reporting and cross-coverage of grant matters where required. Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in Business, Science or a related discipline. Relevant experience in administration, research, grants, finance, compliance or stakeholder support would be advantageous. Strong organisational and analytical skills, with the ability to manage multiple deadlines, track deliverables and follow through on outstanding matters. Good communication skills and comfortable working with different stakeholders. Adaptable and willing to learn Proficient in using digital tools for tracking, documentation and collaboration; familiarity with grant management systems would be an advantage. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Student-Engagement-and-Development--Undergraduate-Programmes-_R00024782-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Student Engagement and Development (Undergraduate Programmes)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 27 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nA young and research-intensive university, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) has 33,000 undergraduate and postgraduate students in engineering, business, science, humanities, arts, social sciences, education and medicine. Ranked among the world’s top universities, NTU Entrepreneurship Academy (NTUpreneur) is the focal point of entrepreneurship education within the University, Singapore and the region. We are seeking an Assistant Manager (Student Engagement and Development). The incumbent will play a vital role in enhancing the undergraduate experience at NTUpreneur. Reporting to the Assistant Director/Lead, this position is central to promoting the Second Major in Entrepreneurship (SMiE) and Minor in Entrepreneurship (MiE) programmes, strengthening student engagement, and building a vibrant NTUpreneur community. A key performance indicator (KPI) is increasing enrolment for each programme cohort, making effective communication of the programmes’ value and offerings essential. Through targeted marketing efforts, outreach events, leadership programmes, and community-building initiatives, the role supports NTUpreneur’s mission to develop entrepreneurial-minded students and foster a dynamic and supportive environment within the Academy. The incumbent will plan and execute undergraduate outreach, student engagement, and community-building initiatives, while also owning the operational framework for sourcing and tracking high-potential entrepreneurial students and venture projects. Through integrated marketing, engagement strategies, and the development of a structured student and venture pipeline, the role contributes to enrolment outcomes and strengthens the NTUpreneur student ecosystem. Key Responsibilities: Plan, Develop and Organise Programme Marketing and Outreach Develop and implement marketing strategies for SMiE and MiE Oversee production of marketing materials (brochures, posters, social media) Manage social media channels and create engaging campaigns Collaborate with NTU Schools for cross-departmental Promotions Plan, Develop and Organise Outreach Events and Activities Plan and execute roadshows, Open House, info sessions, etc. Coordinate and support NTUpreneur’s participation in NTU/external events Organise visits for stakeholders Plan, Develop and Organise Student Engagement and Development Initiatives Implement onboarding sessions and community-building events Rebuild and manage Student Ambassador Programme and NTUpreneur Student Club Mentor student leaders and guide student club in event and programme execution Develop co-curricular initiatives that foster entrepreneurship Ensure Student Club follows NTU’s governance framework Own the sourcing and tracking framework for high-potential entrepreneurial students and venture projects, including procedures, systems and data governance Responsible for Data Management and Administration for the Undergraduate Team Responsible for data management and act as PDPA focal point Manage and maintain event calendar, reports, programme accounts Ensure updated programme content online (eg. Website and intranet) Responsible for Budgeting and Reporting on Student Engagement and Development functions Ensure proper tracking of budget and work with Lead on budget planning for student engagement activities Collect data, analyse trends and report on programme improvements Requirements: Bachelor’s degree from a recognised Institute of Higher Learning. 3–5 years of relevant experience in student engagement, student development, or programme/event management within a tertiary-education environment, with supervisory exposure. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications, with familiarity in social-media tools, digital communications and basic design applications. Strong planning, organisational and multi-tasking abilities to manage student-related projects, events and outreach activities effectively. Excellent interpersonal and communication (oral and written) skills, with the ability to collaborate across teams, build rapport and engage a diverse range of stakeholders. Demonstrated ability to collect, analyse and report data for programme evaluation and improvement. Empathy and sensitivity in working with students, with the ability to foster inclusion, collaboration and a positive student experience. Strong social-media awareness and creativity in producing engaging digital content; experience in video editing or graphic-design tools will be an advantage. Proactive, resourceful and student-centred, demonstrating initiative, sound problem-solving and effective time-management skills. Team-oriented and adaptable, able to work independently and perform under pressure while maintaining professionalism and integrity. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Manager-Senior-Assistant-Manager--Academic-Learning_R00024778": {
      "title": "Manager/Senior Assistant Manager, Academic Learning (Undergraduate Programmes)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 27 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nA young, research-intensive university, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) has 33,000 undergraduate and postgraduate students in engineering, business, science, humanities, arts, social sciences, education and medicine. Ranked among the world’s top universities. NTU Entrepreneurship Academy (NTUpreneur) is the focal point of entrepreneurship education within the University, Singapore and the region. We are seeking a Manager/Senior Assistant Manager, Academic Learning to lead the planning, governance, and delivery of NTUpreneur’s undergraduate programmes, ensuring the effective execution and continuous development of the Second Major in Entrepreneurship (SMiE) and Minor in Entrepreneurship (MiE). This role is accountable for maintaining academic quality, ensuring compliance with University policies, and driving programme enhancements through curriculum development, stakeholder alignment, and process optimisation to support NTU’s strategic educational objectives. K e y Responsibilities: 1. Oversee Academic Planning and Programme Management Develop and implement academic operational initiatives, policies, and guidelines to ensure good governance. Oversee planning, management, and coordination of SMiE and MiE Initiate inter-school collaborations and curriculum enhancements Oversee execution of university-wide academic initiatives and strategic plans 2. Manage Academic Programme Operations a. Oversee and monitor student enrolments, withdrawals, and academic progress b. Manage programme and course administration such as: Academic proposal submissions Timetable scheduling Instructor engagement and deployment Instructor appreciation Course registration Teaching facilities and logistics Results review and processing Ensure proper setup of course sites (NTULearn) Student Feedback in Teaching (SFT) and instructor evaluation student progression tracking Student Advisory (academic) c. Coordinate with Office of Academic Services (OAS) on candidature matters eg. verify SMiE and MiE awards for graduation d. Manage course approvals, submissions, and course mapping for outbound exchanges for students across the University e. Oversee inbound exchange students with course selections and approvals 3. Ensure Academic Governance & Policy Compliance Ensure adherence to NTU’s academic guidelines, practices, policies, and university-wide regulations. Review and implement academic policy updates periodically or when required, ensuring all curriculum changes and practices are aligned with NTU’s framework. Develop and maintain processes to track curriculum compliance, course approvals, and regulatory adherence. 4. Strengthen Stakeholder Engagement           Act as the liaison between faculty, NTU administration, and Joint Programme Partners. Manage relationships with academic partners, industry associations, and professional bodies to enhance programme offerings. Collaborate with faculty and external stakeholders to support cross-disciplinary entrepreneurship education. 5. Manage Process Improvement & Quality Assurance  Conduct regular curriculum reviews and teaching evaluations to maintain programme excellence. Review and optimise academic workflows and operational processes. Ensure adherence to academic integrity, governance, and quality standards. Implement best practices to improve efficiency in academic operations. 6. Plan and Oversee Publicity & Course Development   Initiate collaborations with the Student Engagement and Development (SED) arm to execute marketing strategies to increase enrolment for SMiE, MiE, and elective courses. Work with academic leadership to analyse student demand and design/develop new/enhanced credit-bearing courses. Oversee the process of recruitment and engagement of faculty and instructors. Collaborate with SED to implement outreach initiatives to promote NTUpreneur’s academic programmes. 7. Manage Sub-team & Budget Planning          Oversee and mentor the Academic Management and Operations team to ensure high performance. Develop and monitor budget allocations for academic operations. Prepare and present reports for management and key stakeholders. Ensure the team meets annual performance targets and strategic goals. Requirements: Bachelor’s degree from a recognised university with at least 6 years of experience in academic administration, programme management, or higher education operations Strong background in faculty coordination, curriculum development, and academic policy implementation Proven ability to manage teams, ensuring smooth academic operations and effective collaboration with faculty and instructors. Excellent organisational and problem-solving skills to handle multiple academic processes efficiently Strong analytical and critical thinking abilities to assess programme performance, policy implications, and operational improvements. Meticulous attention to detail to ensure accuracy in academic records, reporting, and policy implementation Proficiency in Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint) and academic management systems Effective interpersonal and communication (written and verbal) skills and the ability to collaborate effectively with students, faculty, University and external stakeholders Proactive, self-motivated, and adaptable, capable of working independently and within a team in a fast-paced academic environment We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Director--Graduate-Career-Development_R00025115": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Director, Graduate Career Development",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nNanyang Business School competes with leading business schools globally to attract high-calibre professionals from diverse backgrounds to its graduate programmes. As part of Graduate Studies, the Career Development Office supports postgraduate students in their career development, leadership growth and employment outcomes throughout their learning journey. The position holder will provide leadership for the MBA Cluster within the Career Development Office, overseeing career development initiatives, leadership programmes, student engagement and employment outcomes across the MBA, Executive MBA (EMBA), Professional MBA (PMBA) and Nanyang Fellows (NF) programmes. Working closely with internal and external stakeholders, the role will drive strategic initiatives to enhance student success, strengthen industry partnerships and maintain the School's reputation for delivering outstanding graduate outcomes. What you will be working on: 1. Career Development strategy and implementation: Engage with leadership to identify and drive strategic initiatives to keep career services at the forefront of providing optimal and efficient services; Provide thought leadership to the team on initiatives to capitalise or respond to changes in environmental/ social/ economic factors impacting jobs for MBAs; Lead the careers team in providing multi-faceted career workshops, networking events and company presentations, to get students career-ready. Work closely with Graduate Studies leadership to develop and implement strategic initiatives that enhance student success and career outcomes. Analyse employment trends, student feedback and market intelligence to inform career development strategies and service enhancements. 2. Drive leadership and strategy for MBA Cluster: Develop and execute the strategic vision for the MBA Cluster, aligning career development offerings with student needs and market trends; Lead cross-functional initiatives to enhance the MBA career journey, from student onboarding through to post-graduation outcomes; Collaborate closely with Employer Engagement team to strengthen industry relationships and expand recruitment opportunities for MBA talent; Monitor industry shifts and student feedback to continuously refine the MBA career strategy and service delivery model. Lead initiatives to strengthen employment outcomes, student engagement and graduate employability across MBA programmes. Ensure career development initiatives support programme objectives, rankings performance and institutional priorities. 3. Lead and oversee Career Leads and Senior Career Fellows within the MBA Cluster: Lead, coach, and develop a team of Career Leads to deliver high-impact career advisory services to students; Set team goals, monitor performance metrics, and provide regular feedback to ensure alignment with office-wide objectives; Facilitate regular team meetings and one-on-one check-ins to drive collaboration, professional development, and knowledge sharing; Collaborate with other departments (e.g., academic programs, employer relations) to align career support with broader NBS goals; Oversee the recruitment, onboarding, deployment and performance of Senior Career Fellows to ensure high-quality coaching services. Establish quality standards and monitor the effectiveness of coaching interventions delivered by Senior Career Fellows. Facilitate collaboration and knowledge sharing among Career Leads and Senior Career Fellows to ensure a consistent student experience. 4. Lead career offerings for EMBAs, PMBAs and NFs Spearhead engagement with postgraduate students enrolled in these programmes, to deliver targeted leadership career offerings; Identify leadership needs of EMBAs and PMBAs, and recommend updates to content of career offerings by the team ; Manage the design and delivery of leadership development programmes, including identifying and engaging qualified instructors, industry leaders and Senior Career Fellows to deliver impactful learning experiences. 5. Provide guidance on all matters related to career development offerings for MBA students: Lead MBA team in delivering a suite of career offerings to MBA students, with view to helping students achieve their career aspirations; Work with NTU/NBS and external stakeholders in ensuring all relevant job and internship opportunities are availed to MBA students in a timely manner; Develop MBA engagement strategies to keep student satisfaction at a high level; Provide counselling to MBA students where required; Work with MBA team to identify skills required to help MBAs be career-ready; Ensure the integrity, accuracy and timely submission of employment outcomes data for MBA and NF programmes to support rankings, accreditation and institutional reporting requirements . 6. Partner employer engagement team to secure full-time jobs and internship opportunities for MBA students: Provide insights on job aspirations of MBAs to employer engagement team, and co-develop employer engagement strategies to help place MBA students in good jobs; Maintain understanding of market factors (national & global) relative to employer organisations, and build partnerships with companies providing jobs and internships/industry projects; Manage relationships with industry leaders with a view to having these leaders provide industry insights and career coaching to students. Analyse employment outcomes and hiring trends to identify opportunities to strengthen employer engagement strategies and student outcomes. Partner with Employer Engagement colleagues to develop targeted employer outreach strategies for MBA talent. What we are looking for in the person: Bachelor's degree from a recognised university is required. MBA or other relevant postgraduate qualification is preferred. At least 15 years of relevant professional experience, including leadership responsibility for teams, programmes, projects or stakeholder networks. Demonstrated track record in developing and executing strategic initiatives and managing complex stakeholder relationships. Strong understanding of talent markets, career development, leadership development and workforce trends. Experience engaging and influencing senior executives, industry leaders and postgraduate students. Proven coaching, facilitation and counselling experience, with the ability to support professionals at different career stages. Experience in career services and/or higher education, preferably within a business school environment, is advantageous. Excellent communication, presentation and stakeholder management skills. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to translate market insights into actionable strategies. A collaborative and proactive team player who demonstrates initiative, sound judgement and a commitment to excellence. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Head--Administration_R00024411": {
      "title": "Head, Administration",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 27 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAs the School Head of Administration, this role leads the development and implementation of organizational strategies, policies, standards, structures, systems and practices to achieve the overall goals of the School. Overseeing business operations, processes, initiatives and resources, the role provides integrated efficient and effective administrative services within the school, that are aligned with the School’s strategic goals and objectives and the University’s policies and processes. This role provides foremost support to the School Management on strategizing and setting up of new initiatives, such as Capital Campaigns, Continuing Education, Community Engagement and External Relations. Job Responsibilities: Strategic Planning and Implementation Work closely with the Chair in charting the strategic directions and roadmaps of the School in alignment with the University’s goals. Work with the central administrative offices and College to align and coordinate workflow processes between functions and departments within NTU. Drive administrative excellence as a potential strategic advantage for the University. Oversee strategic communications at the School Oversee and coordinate technical operations in the school including close collaboration with IT and pathway coordinators for Animation/Games, Visual Communication/Photography, Cinematic Arts and Transversal Design. Organization and Operations Excellence Accountable for all functional operations and administrative matters of the School. This includes (but is not limited to) areas in outreach and communications, specialized technical and technological laboratory support, international relations, research and grant administration, student care, facilities and general administration. Partner with respective functional business partners to address the school’s needs related to human resources, IT, finance and procurement. Oversee and optimize the use of resources and develop systems and processes to support the initiatives of the School with adherence to corporate policies and guidelines. Proactively develop, review and drive improvements in the School’s structure, systems, policies, processes and work to enhance organizational effectiveness. Analyze statistical data and make recommendations on report and proposal submissions to the Chair. Oversee planning and execution of student exchange programs and the School’s major events. Budget Planning and Allocation Oversee the overall financial operations of the school including financial reporting and analysis, budget planning and monitoring, as well as asset management, for financial effectiveness. Serve as an advisor to the Chair and Associate Chairs to ensure that the overall School’s operations are in accordance with the University’s policies and guidelines. Job Requirements: Degree from a recognized university with at least 15 years of relevant professional experience, including leadership responsibilities in administration or operations. Extensive relevant work experience, including leadership experience in operations, administration, or a related field. Experience in a Senior Managerial or Leadership role with a track record of effective performance will be advantageous. Experience in higher education or a related environment will be an advantage. Familiarity with technical operations or IT processes relevant to art, design, or media environments is beneficial. Strong stakeholder management, collaboration and conflict resolution skills . Strong operational experience, IT savvy and proven managerial experience in strategic and financial budgeting planning Demonstrated ability to lead cross-functional teams and drive operational improvements Demonstrated strategic thinking and analytical capabilities with initiative, sound judgement and resourcefulness in problem solving. Highly adaptable, self-motivated and proactive in managing evolving priorities and new challenges Excellent interpersonal and communication skills to build a sense of community within the school. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager--Academic-Learning_R00017784": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager, Academic Learning",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 27 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nA young and research intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) has 33,000 undergraduate and postgraduate students in engineering, business, science, humanities, arts, social sciences, education and medicine. Ranked among the world’s top universities. NTU Entrepreneurship Academy (NTUpreneur) provides entrepreneurship education within the University and the region. The Senior Assistant Manager is responsible for leading and executing the business development initiatives and overall operation of Master of Science in Technopreneurship and Innovation Programme (MSc TIP) and FlexiMasters in Technopreneurship and Innovation (FM TIP). The incumbent will work closely with the lead of the postgraduate team, Academic Director and Deputy Director of NTU Entrepreneurship Academy (NTUpreneur) for successful delivery of MSc TIP and FM TIP. The incumbent will be driving marketing and outreach, carrying out student recruitment and admission, student and alumni engagement, budgeting and financing, and ensuring all policy and procedures are adhered to. S/he will provide/present marketing strategy and analysis for information and decision, oversee and track follow up actions, work closely with lead, PG team to ensure quality, quantity and diversity of recruitment. S/he will also work with the various NTUpreneur teams and the various Offices in the university for cross programme promotion and inter-department joint activities. The incumbent will oversee various I&E activities and engagements to enhance the experiential learning. S/he will also support venture internship, expanding the industry network for placement of venture internship. The incumbent is expected to supervise executive / senior executive to ensure strong value proposition and to achieve excellence in administration.  Key Responsibilities 1. Lead and execute the business development Initiative of the Masters and FlexiMasters in Technopreneurship and Innovation Programme (MSc TIP and FM TIP) Conduct market researches, data analysis and organise information for marketing strategy for MSc TIP and FM TIP. Organise and coordinate programme outreach in a timely and cost-effective manner. Initiate and organise discussion with various partners and stake holders for program outreach. 2. Oversee marketing and recruitment.  Plan and organise programme info sessions and lead the content development for programme publicity. Organise and coordinate local and overseas roadshows and info sessions.  Prepare programme collaterals Oversee digital marketing campaign Create social media contents and consolidate alumni success stories 3. Track and follow up on effectiveness of outreach and adjust the marketing approach accordingly Follow up on various marketing efforts to track the effectiveness. Enhance programme branding. 4. Oversee student management, student wellbeing, alumni engagement and oversee administrative support  Attend to student queries, well being and integration. Plan and execute student engagement activities. Oversee administrative support required for sound implementation of the Programme 5. Oversee experiential learning Oversee the experiential learning such as company visit or ecosystem exposure. Oversee the Venture Internship elective module to ensure proper running and documentation. 6. Plan and oversee the operating budget and grant of the Programme Plan and oversee the operating budget for running both MSc TIP and FM TIP.. Process claims from grants, where available. Attend to audit query and exercise. Key Competencies & Qualification Bachelor degree in any discipline from a recognized university Preferably with 3 to 5 years relevant work experience in university environment  Knowledge in entrepreneurship and the start-up ecosystem Knowledge in marketing, branding and project management Demonstrated ability to build and maintain relationships with diverse stakeholders Experience in working with professors and students, government agencies and international organisations will be advantageous Good verbal and written communication skills We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager--Programme-Management-and-Student-Administration_R00024245": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager, Programme Management and Student Administration",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 27 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThis position is part of the academic arm within the Undergraduate Programmes Office (UPO) and is required to lead and support the daily operations in UPO, enhancing the overall NBS student experience. Responsibilities: Oversee the proper planning, implementation and smooth delivery of the programme with Programme Director. Provide timely UAPP updates and reports to management. Oversee and manage the administration of undergraduate mid-term scholarships processes, University/College-level awards, and NBS Financial Aid applications. Oversee and manage with Academic Support Units to manage the Student Feedback on Teaching (SFT). Process students’ requests to manage appeals and provide recommendations. Reviewing and approving Students’ Leave of Absence applications. Review, provide advisory to all matters relating to candidature matters and assess any anomalies in progression pathways. Referral to respective support as and when necessary, such as UPO Student Care Team. Process Re-admission, withdrawal and termination student matters. Responsible for all freshmen credit transfer annually. Review, evaluate, update and provide advisory on course exemption matters. Provide academic advisory to students. Support ad hoc projects, events, and outreach activities. Requirements: A Bachelor’s degree from a recognized university. Possess minimum 6 years of relevant working experience, preferably in the education sector. Prior experience in a relevant administrative role in an institution of higher learning will be advantageous. Strong people management and leadership skills; Supervisory experience is required. Influencer with good interpersonal and communications skills to work well with people collaboratively. Self-motivated, resourceful, and flexible in adjusting and responding to changing priorities. Ability to work independently and as a team, personal initiative, and team spirit in the effective implementation of projects. Ability to lead the team by providing clear direction, supporting team members, and ensuring tasks are completed effectively and on time. Ability to manage multiple stakeholders, multi-task and deliver with quality and timeliness. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, planning and organizational abilities. Organised and meticulous with an eye for details. Proficient in Microsoft Office application. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
