    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Manager--Corporate-Services_R00024691": {
      "title": "Manager, Administration",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Manager, Administration supports the Head of Corporate Services in strengthening operational governance, management reporting, and administrative coordination across the School. Acting as central liaison between senior leadership teams, administrative units, central university departments, the role supports the oversight of internal operations and coordination of across functional teams such as finance, HR, IT, planning, compliance and resource management. Additionally, the role focuses on improving visibility of operational and financial information, developing structured dashboards and reporting frameworks, and supporting cross-functional coordination among administrative units. The Manager will also contribute to process improvements, risk monitoring, and the consolidation of information relating to key school initiatives, including events and collaborations across units. Working closely with the Head of Corporate Services and in coordination with the Chief of Staff, the role supports leadership discussions by providing structured insights and improving the clarity and consistency of operational information to support implementation and execution. Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in Business, Management, Finance, Public Administration, or a related discipline. At least 6–10 years of relevant experience in operations management, administration, consulting, or programme management roles. Strong analytical skills with the ability to consolidate and interpret operational or financial data. Experience in preparing management reports or dashboards to support leadership decision-making. Strong stakeholder management and communication skills. Ability to coordinate initiatives across multiple departments in a complex organisational environment. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Counsellor---Counsellor--BEACON-_R00025492": {
      "title": "Senior Counsellor / Counsellor (BEACON)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 27 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout the role Student wellbeing and support is a top priority and a key foundation for NTU Education 2025. It enables NTU students to thrive and flourish in their educational journey. As a Counsellor in NTU, you will play a crucial role to enable NTU to fulfil its mission for student wellbeing and support. As a team member of the University Counselling Centre, you will provide counselling for undergraduate and graduate students and engage with various internal and external stakeholders to promote a NTU campus community approach to mental health. BEACON is a satellite counselling service provided by the University Counselling Centre, designed to make professional counselling more accessible and convenient for students. The BEACON Counsellor provides short-term counselling support to students experiencing mild mental health issues, academic stress and interpersonal issues within the assigned colleges and/or schools. This includes provision of clinical services through different modes of counselling, i.e. face-to-face or online, developing strategies, planning and implementing counselling-related programmes, including referrals to relevant agencies. The Senior Counsellor / Counsellor will conduct practice-based research and facilitates outreach, trainings and programmes for the NTU community. A proactive, resourceful and compassionate professional, the BEACON Counsellor works under supervision as part of a collaborative team. The key responsibilities include: Counselling assessments and interventions Provide short-term professional counselling services, including conducting risk and need assessments and delivering intervention plans over a variety of modes and approaches such as in person or online, within the assigned colleges and/or schools Facilitate case formulation, including preparation of assessment reports, delivery of case presentations, and referrals to relevant organisations within social services ecosystem Provide guidance to less experienced BEACON counsellors in challenging cases in alignment with protocol for escalation of emergency cases Escalate and co-lead sensitive crisis cases with more experienced mental health practitioners Provide consultation to staff on concerns they have regarding students at-risk Identify gaps in counselling tools and frameworks for local contexts and propose recommendations for greater cultural contextualisation to supervisors Provide inputs for improvements in counselling programmes and services Design, develop and/or facilitate wellbeing training initiatives and wellbeing portfolio / project annually Maintain professional, legal and ethical standards Adhere to professional standards in clinical, legal and ethical practices, ensuring client consent and confidentiality and proper data privacy protocol in counselling Monitor staff adherence to professional standards in clinical, legal and ethical practices and assist in the development of clear data privacy protocol Assist in development of quality improvement projects to improve client care and services Document and maintain proper clinical records in accordance with policies and procedures of the University Counselling Centre. Use data-driven insights to identify gaps and drive improvements to counselling in line with the organisation's strategic direction Demonstrate expertise in counselling, pursuing additional trainings in specialised areas and developing a professional point of view Community approach to case intervention Work collaboratively with and make recommendations to schools, student service offices, Halls of Residence, Support and Care Team, etc. to facilitate a campus community approach towards managing students with mild to moderate mental health issues Work in inter-disciplinary teams (e.g. Educational/Clinical/ Counselling Psychologist, Counsellor) to provide evidence-based psychotherapeutic interventions/treatment to students with mild to moderate mental health issues and/or co-morbid issues (e.g. Special Education Needs and mental health issues) Leads NTU community, i.e. colleges and schools, outreach initiatives Liaise with other professionals (e.g. psychiatrists, doctors) and Social Service Agencies to mobilise community resources to provide care and support for the students Refer and/or recommend external service interventions (e.g. family therapy) as part of the student’s overall treatment plan Administrative support in University Counselling Centre (UCC) Support the daily operations of UCC, ensuring efficient and effective functioning Engage in data analysis and collation Perform additional duties as assigned by Head, UCC or Director, UWO The requirements include : Master’s degree in counselling Clinical member and registered counsellor with the Singapore Association for Counselling (SAC) At least five (5) years of professional counselling experience Proficiency in professional counselling approaches and tools to help clients with diverse issues and conditions Experience in working with young adults, preferably in an educational setting Experience in working in a multi-disciplinary team is advantageous Strong attention to detail and commitment to maintaining accuracy in all operational aspects Strong organisational and multitasking skills, with the ability to prioritise and manage multiple tasks and responsibilities Possess professional values that are in line with the Code of Ethics of SAC Possess good interpersonal and communication skills Proficiency in IT skills (e.g. Microsoft 365, use of Apps, appointment booking systems, case management systems) A good team player who is able to work independently We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant--Advanced-Micro-Nano-Device-Technologies-_R00025486": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Advanced Micro/Nano Device Technologies)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 27 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research.  With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 1,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 4th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2025 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee Innovative Electronic & Electromagnetic Devices Laboratory (i – Lab@NTU) led by Prof. Mohammad Samizadeh Nikoo is seeking for a research assistant. The role will focus on fabrication, simulation, and characterization of high-speed nano-devices. Key Responsibilities: Experimental characterization, simulation, and analysis of ultrafast devices. Design of ultrafast circuits operating based on i–Lab innovative devices. Providing general research support to i–Lab@NTU. Job Requirements: Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Electrical Engineering, Physics, or related field Familiarity with micro and nano device fabrication and characterization Proficiency in fundamentals of electrical engineering, in particular electromagnetics theory and numerical techniques Good written and oral communication skills We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Research-Fellow--Wireless-Power-Transfer-_R00025485": {
      "title": "Senior Research Fellow (Wireless Power Transfer)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 27 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research. With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 2,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 4th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2025 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee We are looking for a Senior Research Fellow (SRF) who will develop, optimise, and validate wireless power transfer (WPT) systems for electric vehicle charging roadway applications. The SRF will contribute to Double-D coil-based WPT system design, electromagnetic simulation, magnetic coupling enhancement, electromagnetic shielding evaluation, and laboratory validation in a multidisciplinary research project involving civil and electrical engineering. Key Responsibilities: Developing and optimising Double-D coil-based WPT systems Simulating WPT efficiency, electromagnetic field distribution, impedance matching, and misalignment tolerance using electromagnetic simulation tools. Designing and evaluating surfaces and/or dielectric matching layers to improve magnetic coupling Evaluating electromagnetic shielding performance and electromagnetic field safety compliance Developing laboratory measurement setups to validate WPT efficiency, shielding effectiveness, lateral misalignment tolerance, and system robustness. Analysing simulation and experimental results, preparing technical reports, publishing research findings, and supporting project milestones. Working closely with PhD/MSc students, undergraduate students, and collaborators from civil and electrical engineering disciplines. Job Requirements: PhD in Electrical and Electronic Engineering, Applied Electromagnetics, Power Electronics, Wireless Power Transfer, or closely related fields. More than 5 years of research experience in wireless power transfer, electromagnetic compatibility/interference, electromagnetic shielding, antenna/coil design, or related areas. Experience in electromagnetic simulation tools Experience in WPT coil design, resonant inductive coupling, impedance matching, magnetic-field analysis, and efficiency optimisation. Experience with laboratory measurements for WPT, electromagnetic shielding, or RF/low-frequency electromagnetic systems. Good publication record in relevant research areas. Proficiency in MATLAB, Python, C/C++, or equivalent tools for simulation, data analysis, and automation. Good written and oral communication skills, with the ability to work in a multidisciplinary research team. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Power-System-Risk-_R00025490-1": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Power System Risk)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 27 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research. With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 2,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 4th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2025 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee We are looking for a Research Fellow to work on a project in the area of power system risk modeling and assessment .  Key Responsibilities: Develop a probabilistic security assessment framework for heterogeneous operational uncertainties and contingencies Develop a comprehensive framework for evaluating the criticality of contingency events considering multiple impacts  Develop a coordinated and risk-averse optimization framework for interconnected power grid operation considering low-probability-high-impact contingency events Job Requirements: PhD degree in Electrical Engineering or related subjects. Expert knowledge in power system risk analysis We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Power-System-Stability-_R00025489-1": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Power System Stability)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 27 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research. With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 2,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 4th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2025 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee We are looking for a Research Fellow to work on a project in the area of interconnected power system stability analysis and control .  Key Responsibilities: Develop a measurement-based approach to derive the static and dynamic equivalence of the external grids Establish a stochastic differential algebraic equation (SDAE) based analytic framework for interdependent electromechanical and electromagnetic dynamics modelling and analysis Design data-driven methods for power system stability assessment and control with stochastic resources Job Requirements: PhD degree in Electrical Engineering or related subjects. Expert knowledge in power system stability area We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Analog-in-memory-computing-macros-_R00025491": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Analog in-memory computing macros)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-07\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research. With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 2,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 4th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2025 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee We are looking for a  Research Fellow to conduct research in the area of analog/mixed-signal integrated circuit design . The role will focus on the development of analog in-memory computing macros for AI accelerators. Experience in tape-outs and industry will be highly appreciated for this role. Key Responsibilities: Leading analog in-memory-computing macro design Leading analog-to-digital converter development Leading test chip development Leading test chip testing Job Requirements: PhD qualification degree in integrated circuit design or related field At least 2~3 years of relevant experiences in industry / technical hands-on experience in analog/mixed-signal integrated circuit design Familiarity with research environment Good written and oral communication skills Proficiency in industry-standard design tools and tape-out flows Competent in presentation skills We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Integrated-Polaritonic-Devices-_R00025479": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Integrated Polaritonic Devices)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Research Fellow at NTU’s National Centre for Advanced Integrated Photonics (NCAIP) will support the development of integrated polaritonic devices and waveguides, focusing on long-range polariton propagation, low-energy switching, few-particle modulation of condensate nonlinearities, integrated polaritonic circuit functions, and coupling of polaritonic states with on-chip detection and readout architectures. The role will involve advanced optical spectroscopy and characterization techniques, including real-space and Fourier-space imaging, polarization- and time-resolved measurements, room-temperature and cryogenic testing, while working closely with device integration teams to advance integrated polaritonic systems. Key Responsibilities: As an integral part of the project, the Research Fellow is expected to conduct research in integrated polaritonic devices and waveguides, including the design, fabrication, optimization and experimental characterization of polaritonic waveguides, polariton lasers, cavity/waveguide networks, and polaritonic circuit elements. Design, fabricate, assemble, optimize and experimentally characterize integrated polaritonic devices and waveguides. Develop and operate optical spectroscopy setups involving real-space/Fourier-space imaging, polarization-resolved spectroscopy, time-resolved photoluminescence, electroluminescence, and room-temperature and/or cryogenic measurements. Investigate low-power and few-particle polaritonic effects, including condensate nonlinearities, low-energy switching, single- or few-polariton emission regimes, photon-correlation behaviour, and routes toward polaritonic logic or routing functions. Develop long-range polaritonic waveguiding platforms, polariton propagation measurements, electrical or optical routing schemes, and integration of polaritonic waveguides with single-photon detection where relevant. Collaborate with photonic device integration teams and CDPT partners to support device fabrication, assembly, testing and prototype demonstration. Operate and maintain research laboratories, including advanced microscopy and spectroscopy equipment, in compliance with safety and laboratory protocols. Perform data analysis and interpretation, prepare scientific publications, contribute to research reports and IP disclosures, and present findings at international conferences. Collaborate with internal and external partners on joint research projects and technology development. Contribute to progress reports, project meetings, day-to-day laboratory operations, future grant proposals, and the development and protection of intellectual property. Requirements: PhD in Physics, Optical/Photonic Engineering, Materials Science, Electrical Engineering, or a related discipline. Relevant research experience in experimental optics, optical spectroscopy, photonics, exciton-polariton physics, nonlinear optics, semiconductor optics, polaritonic waveguides, or related fields. Proven publication record in reputable international peer-reviewed journals. Hands-on experience in optical system design, alignment, operation, and advanced characterization techniques, including laser-based and imaging setups. Competent in scientific programming and data analysis (e.g., Python/Matlab), with strong communication skills and the ability to work independently and collaboratively within a research environment. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Material-Science-and-Engineering-_R00025483": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Material Science and Engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Materials Science and Engineering (MSE) provides a vibrant and nurturing environment for staff and students to carry out inter-disciplinary research in key areas such as Computational Materials Science, Characterisation Materials Science, Defence Composite Materials, Functional Composite Materials, Energy, Nanomaterials, Low Dimensional Materials, Biomaterials Materials, Biological Materials, Bioinspired Materials and Sustainable Materials. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/mse/research. We are seeking a highly motivated research fellow to join our dynamic team at the School of Materials and Science Engineering at Nanyang Technological University, Singapore. The successful candidate will contribute to cutting-edge research at the intersection of materials science, advanced manufacturing, robotics, and sensing. Key Responsibilities: Conduct independent research in areas related to soft materials for actuation and/or sensing Develop and implement actuation technology Optimization of formulation for polymer synthesis and functionalization for actuators fabrication Contribute to ongoing soft robotics research Collaborate with faculty and other researchers on interdisciplinary projects Publish research findings in peer-reviewed journals and present at top conferences Assist in mentoring students Job Requirement: Ph.D. in Material Science, Engineering, Actuators and Polymer Synthesis Strong background in materials formulations or synthesis Experience in printing technology or coating techniques Expertise in Actuator device fabrication   Expertise in AI and machine learning is advantageous Excellent written and verbal communication skills Ability to work independently and as part of a team We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Material-Science-and-Engineering-_R00025482": {
      "title": "Research Fellow Material Science and Engineering",
      "description": "Careers Skip to main content Sign In Search for Jobs The page you are looking for doesn't exist. Search for Jobs © 2026 Workday, Inc. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Computer-Science-_R00025488": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Computer Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nYoung and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is ranked among the world’s top universities. NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science (CCDS) is a leading college that is known for its excellent curriculum, outstanding and impactful research, and world-renowned faculty. A hot bed of cutting-edge technology and groundbreaking research, the College aims to groom the next generation of leaders, thinkers, and innovators to thrive in the digital age. Located in the heart of Asia, NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science is an ‘exciting place to learn and grow. We welcome you to join our community of faculty, students and alumni who are shaping the future of AI, Data Science and Computing. Key Responsibilities: To conduct research into the WebAssembly programming language. To produce publications in top conferences and journals. To offer assistance to any students involved in the project. To collaborate with industrial and academic partners. To perform any other duties related to the research program. Job Requirements: A Masters in Computer Science or relevant fields. Background in formal verification and programming language theory. Experience in interactive theorem proving and/or Web programming is valuable. Capable of handling multiple tasks across projects and research activities. Showing excellent communication skills, and willingness to learn. Able to work under limited supervision and excel as an effective team member. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Scientist--Satellite-Communications-_R00025480": {
      "title": "Research Scientist (Satellite Communications)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAt Temasek Laboratories@NTU, our mission is to undertake cutting-edge research in defence science and technology, driving new solutions and advancements across various research areas, including Microsystems Technology, Hardware Assurance, Signal Processing, Advanced Materials, Advanced Laser Technology, and Emerging Technologies. We take immense pride in our people, recognizing them as our greatest asset. Committed to nurturing professional development, we support personal aspirations and growth. Furthermore, we advocate for a healthy work-life balance, fostering yearly engagement and team bonding activities. We invite you to join our Centre for Communications and Signal Processing as a Research Scientist. This centre focus on developing advanced communications and signal processing capabilities for the Singapore defense community. The four key research areas are sensor array, signal processing systems, urban sensing and signal research. We are looking for a Research Scientist with a strong foundation in all aspects of Satellite communications. The researcher is expected to contribute towards addressing the detection, classification and localization of satellite communication terminal. Key Responsibilities:  The candidate will be expected to conduct research in passive detection, classification and geolocation of specifically the localization of unknown ground terminals from LEO NTN signals in harsh environments. The candidate will be responsible for both theoretical development and experimental design to validate the developed methods against real data. Supervise interns and students; review state-of-the-art literature; plan and execute R&D activities to meet project objectives and deadlines; generate and publish novel scientific contributions and support research proposals. Administrative duties may include safety management, asset management, and other assigned responsibilities. Job Requirements:  PhD in Electrical & Electronics Engineering, Communications, or a related field. Strong background in statistical signal processing, estimation theory, detection and classification, waveform-based geolocation, and machine learning/deep learning, with demonstrated research experience in passive localization and tracking using signals of opportunity from LEO NTN systems such as Starlink, Iridium, or similar satellite constellations. Proficiency with SDR platforms, particularly Ettus USRP devices and GNU Radio / UHD programming. Proficiency in Python and/or MATLAB; C++ is an advantage. Proficiency in satellite communications systems, NTN architectures, satellite ephemeris correction methods, and orbital simulation tools (STK, GMAT, Orekit, or equivalent) is desirable. Strong publication record commensurate with career stage. Strong communication skills, with the ability to convey complex technical concepts clearly and concisely. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Scientist--Satellite-Communications-_R00025478": {
      "title": "Research Scientist (Satellite Communications)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAt Temasek Laboratories@NTU, our mission is to undertake cutting-edge research in defence science and technology, driving new solutions and advancements across various research areas, including Microsystems Technology, Hardware Assurance, Signal Processing, Advanced Materials, Advanced Laser Technology, and Emerging Technologies. We take immense pride in our people, recognizing them as our greatest asset. Committed to nurturing professional development, we support personal aspirations and growth. Furthermore, we advocate for a healthy work-life balance, fostering yearly engagement and team bonding activities. We invite you to join our Centre for Communications and Signal Processing as a Research Scientist. This centre focus on developing advanced communications and signal processing capabilities for the Singapore defense community. The four key research areas are sensor array, signal processing systems, urban sensing and signal research. We are looking for a Research Scientist with a strong foundation in all aspects of Satellite communications. The researcher is expected to contribute towards addressing the detection, classification and localization of satellite communication terminal. Key Responsibilities:  The candidate will be expected to lead and conduct research in passive RF sensing, specifically the detection, characterization, and parameter estimation of NTN waveforms from LEO satellite systems in harsh environments. The candidate will be responsible for both theoretical development of waveform estimation methods and hands-on SDR experimental design to validate the developed methods. Additional responsibilities include supervise interns and students; review state-of-the-art literature; plan and execute R&D activities to meet project objectives and deadlines; generate and publish novel scientific contributions and support research proposals. Administrative responsibilities may include safety management, asset management, and other duties as required. Job Requirements:  PhD in Electrical & Electronics Engineering, Communication Engineering or a related field. Strong expertise in wireless communications, digital signal processing, physical-layer waveform analysis, and passive RF interception, with experience in LEO satellite communications and NTN systems (e.g., Starlink, Iridium). Proficiency in satellite link budget analysis, NTN architectures, orbital mechanics, and tools such as STK, GMAT, or Orekit for LEO pass and Doppler analysis. Experience in wireless channel modelling for LEO satellite links, including atmospheric propagation effects. Proficiency in Python and/or MATLAB; C++ is an added advantage. Knowledge of machine learning/deep learning for signal processing and receiver design is desirable. Experience with SDR platforms, particularly Ettus USRP devices, and GNU Radio/UHD development is an advantage. Strong publication record commensurate with career stage. Strong communication skills, with the ability to convey complex technical concepts clearly and concisely. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Scientist--Wireless-Cellular-Security-_R00025477": {
      "title": "Research Scientist (Wireless/Cellular Security)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe invite suitable candidate to join a strong research team in Temasek Laboratories@NTU with the following requisites: Key Responsibilities:  The candidate is expected to conduct and guide research in Wireless and Cellular Security, in particular the discovery of novel wireless attacks and their detection and mitigations. The candidate is expected to conduct both theoretical development of methods and experiment design to validate the developed methods. Other research responsibilities include supervising junior researchers/interns/students, carrying out detailed literature reviews and assessment of the state-of-the-art technologies. planning and executing detailed R&D activities to meet project objectives and deadlines, generating novel scientific or technological concepts for application of breakthrough nature and contributing to research proposals. Administrative responsibilities may include safety, asset management and other aspects related to being a member of Temasek Labs@NTU. Job Requirements:  PhD degree in Computer Science, Computer & Electronics Engineering or other related fields Strong background and knowledge in at least one or preferably more of the following fields: Cybersecurity, Deep Learning and software engineering with at least 3-5 years of research experience (including PhD training) in related fields. Proven track record in research and development of cybersecurity and/or Deep Learning technologies. Strong publication record in top cybersecurity or systems conferences/journals (e.g., USENIX Security, NDSS, ASE, TSE, TIFS, ICSE, FSE, ICST etc.) Strong programming skills in C/C++, python etc. Knowledge of Electrical or Software Engineering and Cybersecurity are plus. Good writing skills for writing proposals, reports and publications in good academic journals Completed application forms with detailed resumes may be submitted via email to Dr Sirajudeen Gulam Razul (esirajudeen@ntu.edu.sg) with the subject ‘Application for the Position of Research Scientist (Wireless / Cellular Security)’. Appointment grade and starting salary will depend on the candidates’ qualification and relevant experience. Qualified applicants are invited to send in their application on the prescribed form obtainable form: http://www.ntu.edu.sg/ohr/career/submit-an-application/Pages/Research-Positions.aspx Electronic submission of applications is highly encouraged. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Ultrafast-Spectroscopy-of-Nanomaterials-_R00025481": {
