    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Psychology-_R00024589": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Psychology)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-07\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Social Sciences at NTU is an interdisciplinary research and teaching hub covering psychology, economics, sociology, and public policy. It focuses on rigorous, high-impact research that informs policy and practice in Singapore and beyond. The School fosters collaboration across academia, government, and industry, supported by strong research infrastructure and a vibrant scholarly community. It is committed to developing future researchers through mentorship, training, and active involvement in research projects. Key Responsibilities: The Research Associate will support the implementation of research projects under the supervision of the Principal Investigator(s). The role involves coordinating participant recruitment and data collection across multiple settings (e.g. preschools, hospitals, and laboratories), while ensuring smooth day-to-day research operations. Key responsibilities include managing and executing studies, supervising and training research assistants and students, and supporting project timelines and administration. The Research Associate will also handle data management (including cleaning, coding, and analysis), ensure compliance with ethical and institutional requirements, and contribute to grant reporting. In addition, the role includes supporting research dissemination efforts, such as preparing manuscripts for peer-reviewed journals and assisting with conference presentations. Job Requirements: Degree in psychology or a related social science field (Master’s preferred) Experience in research with human participants, especially children or families Strong organisational, data management, and project coordination skills Ability to supervise and work collaboratively with students and research staff Good written and verbal communication skills Willingness to work flexibly across different settings and schedules We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Entrepreneurship-Development-Programme_R00025330": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Corporate Leadership and Innovation Programme",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nA young and research intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) has 33,000 undergraduate and postgraduate students in engineering, business, science, humanities, arts, social sciences, education and medicine. Ranked among the world’s top universities. NTU Entrepreneurship Academy (NTUpreneur) provides education within the University and the region. The incumbent is responsible for developing, promoting and overseeing the business development and implementation of local and international executive programmes. This role will oversee and implement all marketing and promotional activities, to ensure learners’ objectives are met with quality executive programmes. The incumbent is also responsible for ensuring the profitability and sustainability executive programmes, through active seeking and initiating of collaboration opportunities with industry partners and key stakeholders, including Enterprise Singapore and others, and engagement of NTU Entrepreneurship Academy’s (NTUpreneur) Innovation and Entrepreneurship (I&E) and alumni networks. The incumbent will report to the Senior Assistant Director of Corporate Leadership and Innovation Programme (CLIP)  to uphold and enhance the reputation of NTUpreneur, while supporting strategic initiatives of the I&E Office and NTU. Job Responsibilities: 1. Plan marketing strategies to increase business of NTUpreneur’s executive programmes Develop a viable marketing strategy for implementation and design marketing collaterals (digital for social media and global marketing platforms and print for roadshows). Seek potential corporate clients, global executive training platforms and seek business development opportunities. Prepare presentation deck to prospective corporate clients. 2. Facilitate and coordinate to design new and customised executive programmes Oversee the coordination between corporate clients, faculty/ Programme Director and Senior Assistant Director (SAD, CLIP ) to design customised courses for corporate clients. Identify and suggest trending topics, and potential markets for developing new executive programmes. 3. Oversee the implementation of processes to ensure smooth execution of key operations, policies and processes and efficiency in resource management Ensure relevance and quality of courses and quality of instructors hired to teach these courses. Coordinate with NTUpreneur’s Academic Director and NTU’s Professional and Continual Education (PaCE) to oversee the onboarding processes of instructors, mentors and industry partners Plan course schedule and ensure availability of faculty and instructors. Oversee the operation and logistical arrangements of classes to create positive learning experience and environment. Gather and analyse participants feedback, identify areas for improvement, design and implement solutions. 4. Engage stakeholders and develop professional partnerships opportunities Identify individual and corporate stakeholders for partnership. Leverage on their strengths and strong network for the benefit of NTU executive programme learners. Design and implement stakeholder and corporate engagement activities to retain interest, and increase awareness of NTUpreneur’s executive programmes. Identify training grant opportunities and secure collaborations leading to access of these grants for our learners. 5. Oversee Programme’s budget and expenditure plan Oversee annual budget and expenditures and track business performance to ensure a healthy stream of revenue and profits. Plan and deploy resources effectively according to the University’s guidelines. Prepare monthly financial reports and statistics for PaCE and the Director, NTUpreneur. Identify and facilitate the submission of grant application proposals to funding agencies. Oversee the submission of courses to SkillsFuture/ SSG to secure funding support for participants. Requirements: Degree in business or entrepreneurship with at least 3 years of experience in leading CET programme in Institute of Higher Learning or equivalent Experience in working with the government/ quasi-government agencies and administering grant processes and overseeing auditing processes Possess a good network consisting of entrepreneurs, intrapreneurs and industry partners Possess excellent writing and oral communication and presentation skills We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Tactile-Sensor-_R00025448": {
      "title": "Research Fellow Tactile Sensor",
      "description": "Careers Skip to main content Sign In Search for Jobs The page you are looking for doesn't exist. Search for Jobs © 2026 Workday, Inc. All rights reserved."
