    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturer-in-CH6261-Renewable-Energy-and-Fuels--CCEB-_R00025390": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer in CH6261 Renewable Energy and Fuels (CCEB)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-03\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University, School of Chemistry, Chemical Engineering and Biotechnology is looking for a part-time lecturer carry out teaching and assessment of a postgraduate level course in Renewable Energy and Fuels as part of the MSc in Chemical Engineering Programme. Your responsibilities would include, but not be limited to, the following: Development, coordination and preparation of course outline, learning plan and all matters pertaining to assessments. Coordination of the preparation of course notes and instructional materials. These have to be submitted to the CCEB MSc team by the deadlines given. Conducting classes according to the course syllabus and learning plan. Providing students formative and timely feedback; keeping track of student learning throughout the course. Setting, marking and submission of the results of any assessment as part of the teaching requirement. Coordination with the CCEB MSc team on all matters related to the successful delivery of the programme. Ensuring that NTU’s rules, practices and codes of conducts on intellectual property rights and academic integrity are strictly adhered to. Any other task that may be necessary for the successful delivery of the course. You must be an expert in Advanced Reaction Engineering. You must have a Ph.D in Chemical engineering, Advanced Reaction Engineering, or in a closely related discipline. You must be a current practitioner of Advanced Reaction Engineering processes or research. You must be an excellent communicator in English, both verbally and written. You must be familiar with the operation of a research-intensive university in Singapore, such as Nanyang Technological University You must have outstanding team-working capabilities and excellent interpersonal skills. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Math-Foundation-of-AI-_R00025397": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Math Foundation of AI)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-03\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences (SPMS) at NTU Singapore hosts research and education activities in two divisions: Division of Mathematical Sciences (MAS) and Division of Physics and Applied Physics (PAP). MAS covers diverse topics ranging from pure mathematics to the applications of mathematics in cryptography, computing, business, and finance. PAP covers many areas of fundamental and applied physics, including quantum information, condensed matter physics, biophysics, and photonics. Over the years, SPMS has attracted talented individuals from around the world and Singapore to join as scientific leaders and researchers. The group of Wang Zhongjian is looking for postdocs working on scientific computing and machine learning related topics. The funding is currently under a MOE grant entitled: Towards Infinite Dimensional Generative Models. The contract period of the position is up to three years subject to funding availability. Applicants should be familiar with and have track records in at least one of the following fields: approximation of neural networks, convergence of Langevin/MC sampling, analysis and algorithm design of interacting particle systems, operator learning, regularity theories in inverse/scattering problems. Once successful, the candidate is expected to transfer their expertise to machine learning/scientific computing in collaborations with other group members (phd students, exchange graduate students, etc). When projects are required, the group will provide reasonable GPGPU computing resources from the NSCC. The review of candidates will be conducted monthly until all the positions are filled. Once applied on Workday, the candidate may drop an email with application packages for faster screening. Key Responsibilities: Research Paper/proposal writing Teaching assisting Graduate student mentoring Job Requirements: A PhD degree in Mathematics or related areas, with focus on numerical analysis or machine learning. Experience in computational math. Proficient in coding languages, such as C, C++, Fortran, and Python. Strong written and verbal communication skills Strong publication record We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
