    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager--Brand---Digital-Communications_R00025059": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager, Brand & Digital Communications",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University is a leading global university recognised for excellence in education and research. Nanyang Business School (NBS) is one of Asia’s premier business schools, committed to delivering impactful education and driving innovation in teaching and engagement. The Senior Assistant Manager, Brand & Digital Communications leads high-impact brand and digital initiatives for NBS. Working closely with the Senior Assistant Director, Brand Communications, this role translates school-level strategies into integrated communications programmes that strengthen NBS's visibility, positioning, and digital performance. The role combines execution excellence with strategic input on brand application, digital optimisation, and performance measurement. Responsibilities: Branding Lead end-to-end delivery of flagship brand initiatives and high-profile College activities, managing vendor coordination, logistics, stakeholder engagement, and quality assurance. Research market trends, competitor activity, and consumer behaviour to inform brand strategy and campaign decisions. Act as brand guardian, ensuring all NBS activations align with brand standards and positioning across communications, campaigns, and internal/external touchpoints. Develop and execute brand content for social and digital platforms to support campaign objectives and NBS positioning. Coordinate with various teams within NBS and central functions to align brand and digital initiatives with institutional priorities. Guide the design and production of collateral and activations in partnership with in-house designer and/or agencies. Website and Digital Assets Lead the NBS Website Revamp, managing content mapping, stakeholder engagement, and user experience enhancement. Establish sustainable website maintenance and optimisation processes, ensuring SEO and AEO compliance, up-to-date content, and continuous improvement guided by performance data. Oversee key digital assets (website, social media, intranet) to ensure alignment with NBS's brand and value proposition. Develop monthly performance reports on website traffic, campaign engagement, and digital performance, with data-driven recommendations for optimisation using marketing analytics and performance management tools. Requirements: Bachelor's degree in Marketing, Communications, or a related discipline Minimum 5-6 years of relevant experience in marketing, communications, or brand management, including leading end-to-end projects Excellent written and verbal communication skills with proven stakeholder management capability Strong technical proficiency across digital platforms and tools, including content management systems, analytics and performance measurement platforms, social media channels, and SEO and AEO principles. Proficiency in content creation and ability to work with AI-assisted tools Data-driven mindset with strong analytical and problem-solving skills Proven project and complexity management capability with ability to deliver under tight timelines Strategic thinking combined with strong execution capability Curious and adaptable, able to work effectively in ambiguity and changing priorities Collaborative team player who works effectively across functions and with external vendors High level of ownership, accountability, and professional reliability We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Environmental-Engineering-Microbiology-_R00025386": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Environmental Engineering/Microbiology)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Materials Science and Engineering (MSE) provides a vibrant and nurturing environment for staff and students to carry out inter-disciplinary research in key areas such as Computational Materials Science, Characterisation Materials Science, Defence Composite Materials, Functional Composite Materials, Energy, Nanomaterials, Low Dimensional Materials, Biomaterials Materials, Biological Materials, Bioinspired Materials and Sustainable Materials. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/mse/research. We are looking for a Research Fellow (RF) with expertise and experience in Environmental Engineering / Microbiology. The RF will engage in innovative research focused on the formation, structure, and function of bioflocs in climate-resilient aquaculture systems. This position provides an exceptional opportunity to engage in impactful, interdisciplinary research in a multidisciplinary, multi-institutional research team. It also provides opportunities to closely interact with industry leaders in aquaculture. Key Responsibilities: The candidate would be required to lead a project under a larger research programme between Singapore and China. The candidate should fulfill the following responsibilities: Design, perform, and optimize experiments with scientific rigor; Collect, analyze, and interpret experimental data; Communicate findings clearly through technical reports, papers, and presentations; Work collaboratively with researchers from diverse backgrounds Job Requirements: The candidate should possess the following qualifications, skills and experience: PhD degree in environmental engineering, biochemical engineering, environmental biotechnology/microbiology or a related field in science or engineering; Solid foundation in microbial biotechnology, as evidenced by documented research experience, e.g., journal publications; Excellent written and oral communication skills; Ability to work independently as well as collaboratively within a multidisciplinary research team; Research experience in biofilm- or biofloc-related topics is highly desirable. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Wireless-Security-_R00025380": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Wireless Security)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research. With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 2,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 4th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2025 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee We are looking for a Research Fellow (Wireless Security) to conduct research on AI-aided wireless security for 6G communications. The recruited Research Fellow will focus on ONE of the following research directions: 1) developing and validating AI-enabled methods for security-oriented RF design, 2) low-detectability/covert wireless transmission, or 3) radio-frequency (RF) fingerprinting-based device authentication. The work will involve theoretical analysis, algorithm development, simulation, and hardware-in-the-loop experimentation. The Research Fellow will work closely with the Principal Investigator and collaborators/students across NTU Singapore to deliver high-quality research, demonstrable prototypes, peer-reviewed publications, intellectual property, and follow-on research proposals. Key Responsibilities: Conduct original research on AI-aided wireless security, with emphasis on secure and resilient physical-layer technologies for future 6G communication systems. Identify potentially patentable research outcomes and fill in patent application forms. Write and publish high-quality research papers. Assist in the preparation and writing of research grant proposals. Co-supervise undergraduate and/or graduate students. Job Requirements: PhD in electrical and electronic engineering, communication engineering, signal processing, RF/microwave engineering, or related discipline. Strong publication record and hands-on experience in one of the following areas: wireless security, wireless communications, AI/machine learning for communications, covert communications, signal processing, and/or RF design. Ability to conduct research independently and collaboratively within a team. Good written and oral communication skills in English - essential for data analysis and communication with stakeholders We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant--Additive-Manufacturing-_R00025383": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Additive Manufacturing)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Singapore Centre for 3D Printing (SC3DP) offers a full range of additive manufacturing services, from design and infrastructure to production and validation. With advanced technologies such as topology optimization, generative design, and bioinspired design, SC3DP creates optimized products using a variety of novel materials and printing processes, including hybrid printing, post-processing, and emerging technologies. Sustainability is a top priority for SC3DP, which offers material development and control services that combine artificial intelligence, big data, and other digital tools for process optimization, as well as non-destructive testing for AM parts. Backed by a team of experts and a state-of-the-art facility equipped with the latest equipment and technologies, SC3DP is committed to leading the way in sustainable additive manufacturing research and development. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/sc3dp/ Key Responsibilities: Perform fabrication using Laser powder-bed fusion systems (Adequate training will be provided). Perform metallurgical sample preparation of metal additively manufactured specimens, including sectioning, mounting, grinding, polishing, and etching. Conduct microstructural characterisation using optical microscopy, scanning electron microscopy (SEM), and electron backscatter diffraction (EBSD). Assist in materials analysis, interpretation of microstructural features, and documentation of experimental results. Support mechanical and metallurgical testing activities related to metal additive manufacturing research projects. Maintain laboratory equipment, ensure proper calibration and safe operation of characterisation facilities, and support general laboratory management activities. Assist in experimental planning, sample tracking, data collection, and preparation of technical reports, presentations, and research publications. Collaborate closely with researchers, students, and industrial partners to support ongoing research and development activities in advanced manufacturing and materials engineering. Experience in technical documentation, preparation of research reports, or contribution towards intellectual property development such as technical disclosures and laboratory know-how will be advantageous. Job Requirements: Bachelor’s degree or above in Mechanical Engineering, Metallurgical Engineering, Aerospace Engineering or a related field. Experience in metallurgical sample preparation, materials characterisation, and microscopy techniques such as optical microscopy, scanning electron microscopy (SEM), and electron backscatter diffraction (EBSD) is highly advantageous. Knowledge of metal additive manufacturing processes such as Laser Powder Bed Fusion (LPBF) and Directed Energy Deposition (DED) will be preferred. Familiarity with metallurgical analysis, microstructural interpretation, and materials testing techniques is advantageous. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in an interdisciplinary research environment. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--AI--Fintech--Finance-_R00025378": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (AI, Fintech, Finance)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNTU’s Global Institute of Finance, Technology, and Society (GIFTS) is a university-wide interdisciplinary institute advancing knowledge and practice across finance, technology, and society in the digital age with special emphasis on artificial intelligence, digitisation, financial technology, digital assets, and the governance of emerging economic systems>. Aligning strongly with NTU’s interdisciplinary ambitions and with Singapore’s long-term positioning as a trusted global hub for finance, responsible innovation, and digital governance, GIFTS is designed to amplify cross-school collaboration, attract global talent, catalyse external funding, and build long-run research leadership in areas where AI, markets, and institutions increasingly interact. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/gifts . We are looking for a Research Fellow to spearhead the development of economic world models that bridge AI models with quantitative finance theory . The role will focus on developing economic world models with generative AI and theory-informed neural networks . Job Responsibilities: Conducting theoretical and empirical studies on economic world models, with a strong emphasis on critical finance applications including asset pricing, volatility modelling, risk management etc.  Developing the framework of economic world models, with generative AI algorithms such as diffusion models and theory-informed algorithms such as PINN, SKINN. Building agentic economic world models that are incorporated with theory and knowledge structures and connecting them with reinforcement learning and generative modelling for finance. Deploying the agentic economic world models and the transformer architecture for AI-driven financial econometric tasks such as covariance matrix estimation and time-series forecasting. Collaborating with scholars from computer science and statistics to support the multidisciplinary research of economic world models. Promoting the research on economic world models in the world-leading finance, economics and AI conferences. Job Requirements: PhD in Fintech, Finance, Economics, Statistics, or related field. Very strong quantitative background (for example a Bachelor in Statistics, Mathematics, or a related field). Decent programming skills, especially in Python or JAX. Familiarity with finance theory (asset pricing, derivative pricing, risk management etc.). Familiarity with machine learning or deep learning theory. Hands-on experience with machine learning or deep learning models for finance or economics. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Ability to work independently, manage deadlines, and write clean, reproducible code. Strong interest in AI for finance research. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/CleanTech-One/Programme-Director--Techno-commercial-Marketing--NTUitive-_R00025375": {
      "title": "Programme Director, Techno-commercial/Marketing [NTUitive]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University – NTUitive Pte Ltd (NTUitive), Nanyang Technological University's innovation and enterprise company, hosts the Separation Technologies Applied Research and Translation (START) Centre. START Centre, a national facility, was launched in June 2016 to develop and de-risk the commercialisation of innovative separation and filtration technologies. START bridges a critical gap in the ecosystem, between lab-scale R&D carried out in local as well as overseas research entities, and eventual market adoption, by focusing on translation, technology scale-up and piloting to accelerate the commercialisation process. START collaborates with leading local and global Institutes of Higher Learning (IHLs) and various industrial partners to achieve this goal.  Industry projects have been an important part of START’s portfolio, and will gain increasing importance in the coming years. START has also been focused on addressing Singapore’s National Priorities. Seawater desalination, one of our national taps, will be critical towards increasing the availability of water for Singapore’s industrial and commercial growth, as will the ability to drive Industrial Wastewater reuse and Resource Recovery. Starting October 1, 2026 (RIE 2030), START Centre will host SG MEM, Singapore Membrane Consortium, which is an industry-facing national entity with paid participation from 30 industrial members, in addition to experts from translational centres and IHLs.  SG MEM is the umbrella organization, coordinating and facilitating collaborations between industry partners, and also with translational centres and academia. The Programme Director, Techno-commercial/Marketing will report to the Managing Director, START and work closely with the Managing Director and senior technical leaders on growing the organization.  Some of the key responsibilities include the following: Working closely with the Managing Director on Strategic Planning, towards increasing financial self-reliance for START. Actively seeking out opportunities for new industry projects and collaborations. Developing and implementing a competitive pricing model for industry projects. Analysing and valuing START’s Intellectual Property. Acting as back-up to the Managing Director during the MD’s absence. Mentoring technology leaders in writing funding proposals, including for projects and collaborations and vetting the same for costing and timelines. Leading the operations of SG MEM, which will be hosted by START from October 1, 2026.  Leverage the strong relationship with our 30 paid industry members and develop new opportunities for growing SG MEM and START. Co-ordinating outreach activities for START and SG MEM. The candidate needs to have a Degree in Business Management (added knowledge of engineering would be a plus), Engineering or Science and a proven record of customer engagement and relationship management, techno-commercial skills, industry project costing, outreach and marketing, budget management, and personnel leadership.  The role requires at least 10 years of industry experience (techno-commercial sales and/or marketing), with at least 5 years in managerial roles. The skillsets for the role include the following: Managing customer base and developing new customers. Developing project and sales proposals, including costing and timelines. Strategic thinking and growth mindset. Team leadership and management. Appointment may vary and will be commensurate with the candidate’s experience. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTUitive"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager-Manager--Business-Development---Programmes--co11ab--LKCMedicine-_R00025382-1": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager/Manager, Business Development & Programmes, co11ab [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nco11ab is Singapore's first biomedtech incubator located within Novena Health City. Established through a tripartite partnership between NTU, A*STAR and NHG, co11ab accelerates the translation of biomedical and healthcare innovations by connecting startups with clinicians, researchers, investors, industry partners and healthcare institutions. As a collaborative innovation hub, co11ab provides access to laboratories, makerspaces, clinical expertise, strategic partnerships and commercialisation opportunities, enabling startups to progress from concept and prototype development through clinical validation and market adoption. Joining co11ab means becoming part of a dynamic ecosystem dedicated to advancing healthcare innovation and improving patient outcomes. Reporting to the Deputy Director, the Senior Assistant Manager/Manager (Business Development & Programmes) is responsible for developing and executing co11ab's business development and ecosystem growth strategy to strengthen its position as Singapore's leading biomedical innovation hub. The role provides strategic leadership in startup attraction, partnership development, programme governance and ecosystem engagement, while driving organisational growth through high-impact collaborations, sustainable membership growth, clinical collaborations and successful delivery of strategic initiatives and grant-funded programmes. Success in this role will be measured by sustained startup pipeline growth, strategic partnership outcomes, successful programme delivery, achievement of organisational and grant KPIs, membership growth and ecosystem impact. Key Responsibilities: Business Development & Growth Strategy • Develop and execute business development strategies to attract high-potential biomedical, medtech and healthtech startups from Singapore and overseas. • Establish strategic sourcing channels with accelerators, universities, research institutes, hospitals, corporates, investors and government agencies. • Lead startup recruitment, conversion and membership growth initiatives to strengthen occupancy and ecosystem quality. • Analyse market trends, identify new growth opportunities and recommend initiatives to enhance co11ab's competitiveness. • Represent co11ab at regional and international ecosystem engagements to position co11ab as a leading biomedical innovation hub. Strategic Partnerships & Ecosystem Development • Develop, manage and expand strategic partnerships with NTU, NHG, A*STAR, healthcare institutions, research organisations, investors, corporates and government agencies. • Identify and drive collaborations that accelerate clinical validation, translational research, commercialisation and market access for startups. • Build long-term stakeholder relationships and develop initiatives that strengthen co11ab's ecosystem and strategic positioning. • Support strategic planning and ecosystem expansion initiatives together with the Deputy Director. Programme Leadership & Governance • Provide strategic leadership for flagship programmes, including the Singapore Healthcare Gateway Accelerator and other strategic initiatives. • Oversee programme planning, budgets, KPIs, grant compliance, risk management, delivery timelines and quality assurance. • Manage programme delivery partners, mentors, speakers and vendors to ensure successful execution. • Evaluate programme performance and implement continuous improvements to maximise participant and organisational outcomes. Community & Ecosystem Engagement • Develop and implement an annual ecosystem engagement strategy aligned with business development objectives. • Oversee seminars, workshops, innovation challenges, networking sessions and delegation visits to strengthen ecosystem engagement. • Drive thought leadership initiatives and enhance co11ab's visibility across local and international innovation ecosystems. • Foster collaboration among startups, clinicians, researchers, investors, industry partners and government agencies. Startup Support & Strategic Reporting • Facilitate strategic connections between startups and clinicians, researchers, investors and industry partners to support validation, commercialisation and internationalisation. • Develop dashboards to monitor business development, partnership and programme KPIs. • Prepare management reports, grant reports and presentations for senior management, Steering Committee and funding agencies. • Recommend strategic improvements based on ecosystem trends, stakeholder feedback and programme performance. Qualifications & Experience • Bachelor's degree or higher in Business, Biomedical Sciences, Healthcare or a related discipline. • 6-8 years of progressively responsible experience in business development, strategic partnerships, innovation ecosystem development or programme leadership, preferably within biomedical, medtech, healthtech or deep-tech sectors. • Strong understanding of Singapore's healthcare, biomedical innovation and startup ecosystem, with regional or international ecosystem exposure. • Demonstrated ability to lead complex cross-functional initiatives and influence senior stakeholders. • Excellent stakeholder management, negotiation, networking, communication and presentation skills. • Strong analytical, project management and performance reporting capabilities. • Commercially minded, proactive, collaborative and adaptable, with strong strategic thinking and organisational leadership. Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/HR-Executive--Human-Resource-Department---NIE-_R00025374": {
      "title": "HR Executive (Human Resource Department) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout the National Institute of Education (NIE) The National Institute of Education (NIE), Singapore , is Singapore's national teacher education institute and we are proud to be an integral part of the nation's education service. We play a key role in the preparation of teachers and in the provision of teacher professional and school leadership development programmes. We are committed to our vision of being An Institute of Distinction: Leading the Future of Education and our mission to Inspire Learning, Transform Teaching and Advance Research . Read more about NIE here . About the Role NIE HR partners the Institute across the full range of its people’s decisions, from day-to-day operations through to workforce planning and capability building. How we work reflects that. We use AI and digital tools to take the effort out of routine work, sharpen our insights and raise the quality of advice we give to staff and stakeholders. We are looking for an HR Executive who is comfortable working this way. You do not need a technical background. You do need good judgement, a bias for improving how things are done, and the discipline to verify what a tool gives you before it reaches a stakeholder. Responsibilities Assist in providing support for HR systems, including requirements gathering, user acceptance testing and post-implementation adoption. Support the full spectrum of HR functions such as appointment, contract renewal, leave, benefits and exit. Prepare HR reports and dashboards and help turn workforce data into clear observations that leaders can act on. Use approved AI and digital tools to draft, summarise and analyse — for example, first-cut correspondence and FAQs, thematic analysis of exit interview and survey feedback, and drafting of process documentation — always with human review before release. Review HR processes and procedures with an automation and simplification lens, and propose improvements where a workflow, template or tool would remove manual effort. Manage queries and provide advice to stakeholders such as line managers and employees, using our knowledge base and tools to respond accurately and quickly. Help maintain the quality of our HR knowledge base and templates so that our digital tools draw on current and correct information. Apply data protection, confidentiality and responsible-use standards in all use of AI tools, including on the handling of personal and sensitive employee data. Provide support in HR projects and initiatives. ​ Requirements A Polytechnic Diploma, preferably in Business Studies with specialisation in Human Resource Management. Preferably 2-3 years of relevant working experience in an HR role. Familiar with the Employment Act, local immigration rules and work pass application procedures. Meticulous, detail-oriented and comfortable working with numbers and data. Strong digital skills, including high proficiency in Microsoft Office. Comfort with spreadsheets beyond basic use (lookups, pivot tables) will be an advantage. Demonstrated practical use of AI tools in a work or study setting, with an understanding of their limits. You should be able to describe how you have used one, what you checked, and where you would not rely on it. Sound judgement on confidentiality and data handling. Able to take initiative, work independently and collaboratively in teams. Good written and spoken communication skills. Experience using Workday will be advantageous. Interest in pursuing IHRP certification will be viewed favourably. Closing Date The closing date of the advertisement is 13 August 2026 . We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Other Information NIE staff can take chartered buses at their own expense from or near their homes to the NIE campus. This is subject to the availability of seats. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--LKCMedicine-_R00025353-1": {
      "title": "Research Fellow [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. The Molecular and Cellular Dysfunction in Diabetes Laboratory, led by Associate Professor Yusuf Ali, combines in vitro systems biology, advanced imaging, in vivo models and multi-omics technologies to elucidate pathways critical to type 2 diabetes mellitus pathogenesis, with focus on pancreatic and immune function. The team is moving into molecular nutrition, harnessing the power of novel ingredients and prebiotics to mitigate the rise of persons living with diabetes. A laboratory under the Nutrition, Metabolism and Health programme, our work seeks for causality so that we can translate mechanistic insights into therapeutic strategies for mitigating type 2 diabetes and related metabolic conditions.   For more details, please view: https://dr.ntu.edu.sg/cris/rp/rp00609 We are seeking a passionate and motivated Research Fellow to contribute to a high-impact project exploring how intracellular lipid regulation is altered under different diets and how the endocrine pancreas can be better protected under obesity and metabolically dysregulated conditions. As type 2 diabetes is also a condition of low grade chronic inflammation, expertise on studying how circulating immune cells interact with tissue-specific immune cells will be a plus. The project investigates molecular mechanisms underpinning cell stress and resilience, integrating in vitro and in vivo studies using genetically modified mouse models, human islets, and multi-omics approaches. This position is ideal for researchers with a strong interest in lipid metabolism, autophagy/lipophagy, and diabetes pathophysiology. Key Responsibilities: Conduct various in vitro assays/experiments, including histology, western blotting, immunofluorescence microscopy, etc. Perform in vivo experiments, animal studies Computational biology to integrate results and generate list of perturbed pathways Contribute to research grant proposal applications, including literature review and preliminary data Contribute to research deliverables, such as manuscript writing, attending local and/or international conferences Mentor and supervision of undergraduate/PhD students and junior research staff Collaborate effectively with the research teams to achieve overall research goals and objectives Required educational qualification, experience, skills and competencies: PhD in Life Sciences, Biomedical Sciences, or related field At least 2-3 years of relevant experience in molecular biology, cell culture, imaging, or metabolic disease models Strong technical proficiency in laboratory techniques such as immunoblotting, immunofluorescence microscopy, qPCR, and animal handling Familiarity with regulatory standards, good laboratory practices and experience with IACUC protocols Excellent written and oral communication skills, with demonstrated ability to draft scientific manuscripts and presentations Strong organizational, motivational and self-driven skills, with a team-plater attitude (Entry-level candidates with strong experimental skills and interest in metabolic disease research are welcome to apply) Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
