      "title": "Research Fellow Neuroimaging Adolescent Mental Health",
      "description": "Careers Skip to main content Sign In Search for Jobs The page you are looking for doesn't exist. Search for Jobs © 2026 Workday, Inc. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Resident-Relations_R00025354": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Resident Relations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-29\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Office of Campus Housing (OCH) serves to make NTU the hub and destination to deliver best-in-class campus for learning, working, and living. OCH is a critical department responsible for student and faculty housing on campus, the sports and recreational facilities, and its related services. We are looking for an individual who has a strong passion for delivering exceptional service to residents of the University’s student and faculty housing, and athletes and users of sports & recreation facilities on campus.   The role provides the successful candidate with the opportunity to develop and contribute holistically across areas of excellence in customer relationship management, facilities & contracts management and/or quality and corporate functions (e.g. finance / billing, quality management, etc.) within the Department. If you are a diploma holder with at least 3 years of relevant working experience in residential management / services, customer service / resident relations management, or housing operation support and contract management, quality, and corporate service (finance / billing), you may be the one whom we are looking for. Having experience in student hostels, staff housing or hospitality services would be a plus for this role!  The incumbent is required to: Hostel application processing and the assignment of rooms / housing units, including the management of waitlist and students’ appeal for on-campus accommodation. Ensure the high quality of rooms / housing units for students’ check-in through comprehensive inspections. Ensure accurate billing of hall fees and other payable items as well as timely collection and follow-up where necessary. This includes accurate and timely refunds to students where applicable. Collaborate with colleagues and external vendors / contractors to get update on the status of maintenance / repairs to student hostels. Proactively engage student residents in understanding and addressing residents’ needs and contributing to problem-solving and resolution of concerns. This includes addressing and resolving student residents’ requests, feedback, and complaints promptly to meet SLA requirements. Communicate and inform student residents in advance on scheduled maintenance, adhoc repairs and other matters that may cause inconvenience to residents. Conduct routine walkthroughs of OCH managed premises to evaluate safety and security measures. This includes follow-up actions for enhancement and refinements of measures. Conduct investigations and compile supporting documentation for incident reports. This includes proposal of suitable sanctions for rule violations based on the severity and frequency of infractions, and prompt escalation of persistent and / or severe breaches for further enforcement measures, as well as implementation of approved sanctions. Maintenance of up-to-date and precise records, including resident details, occupancy status, and availability, to facilitate billing processes and management reporting. Ensure that facilities reservations are made through established booking channels, and all pre-event and post-event arrangements are properly managed. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Manager--Finance--AISG-_R00023794": {
      "title": "Manager, Finance (AISG)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThis role is deployed to AISG and is a 2-year full time contract. Key Responsibilities include: Monitor all grants managed by AISG to ensure availability and grant compliance Ensure all financial procedures align with university policies and support year-end audit/tax filing processes Ensure SOPs are properly documented Manage research project financial data and system to ensure timely and accurate grant submission in accordance with the NTU policies and processes, grant T&C and harmonised guidelines Prepare periodic grant expense claim reports and management reports for Senior Management Coordinate with research teams for budgeting and financial reporting purposes Liaise with internal and external auditors on the grant certification audit & year end audit Mentor, guide and motivate staff Identify training needs and opportunities for staff Requirements Degree in Accounting, Finance, or related discipline; CA/CPA/ACCA preferred 8–10 years of finance experience, with at least 5 years in research grant finance (university / research institute / public sector) Strong experience managing high‑volume research grants, including budgeting, utilisation monitoring, claims, and compliance with grant T&Cs and harmonised guidelines Proven ability to support grant certification audits and year‑end audits, and liaise with internal and external auditors Hands‑on experience with finance and research grant systems and strong financial reporting skills Experience supervising and mentoring staff, and working closely with researchers and senior management Detail‑oriented, organised, and able to manage multiple deadlines in a fast‑paced research environment We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Earth-Science-Geophysics-_R00025342": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Earth Science/Geophysics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Asian School of the Environment (ASE) at Nanyang Technological University (NTU) is an interdisciplinary school focusing on the connections between geosciences, ecology, society and Earth systems. Our approach integrates these disciplines to examine big hazards and environmental challenges both in Southeast Asia and globally. We conduct cutting-edge research on topics that include geohazards, climate change, sea-level rise, environmental sustainability, conservation of environment and biodiversity, and interactions between environment and society. We seek a Research Fellow to work on using dense seismic arrays, particularly distributed acoustic sensing (DAS), for hazards and coastal monitoring. The candidate will work under the supervision of Asst Prof Voon Hui Lai. The successful candidate should demonstrate expertise in seismic data processing and modelling, dense array analysis, distributed acoustic sensing, and seismoacoustics, and a strong track record of publishing impactful research in areas relevant to the position. Key Responsibilities: Develop methodologies to detect, characterize, and model seismic, coastal hazards and other environmental signals recorded on dense seismic and fibre-optic sensing data Plan and conduct field deployments using seismic and distributed acoustic sensing systems Publish research findings in peer-reviewed journals and present results at national and international conferences Provide scientific leadership and mentorship to undergraduate students, Research Assistants, and Research Associates, supporting their research development while fostering a collaborative, inclusive, and high-performing research environment. Build and maintain effective collaborations with project team members, researchers, and external partners, contributing to research planning, scientific discussions, and the successful achievement of project objectives and deliverables. Job Requirements: PhD in Earth science, geophysics, or a related field. Demonstrated expertise in seismic source detection, seismoacoustics, signal processing, waveform modelling, and/or environmental seismology. Proven experience in the analysis and interpretation of dense seismic array data and/or distributed acoustic sensing. Proven experience planning and conducting geophysical field deployments. Strong programming skills in Python or MATLAB. Strong track record of publishing research relevant to the position in leading Tier 1 journals Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English, as the position requires engagement with stakeholders in an international research environment. Proven ability to prepare scientific manuscripts for publication in peer-reviewed journals and present research findings at international conferences. Demonstrated ability to conduct independent research while working effectively in a multidisciplinary and collaborative team environment. Interested applicants should submit a CV, research statement, list of referees, and list of publications and their relevance to position. For additional information, please email Asst. Prof. Voon Hui Lai at voonhui.lai@ntu.edu.sg . Applications will be reviewed on an ongoing basis. We seek a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status, family responsibilities, or disability. We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Biomaterials-_R00025337": {
      "title": "Research Fellow Biomaterials",
      "description": "Careers Skip to main content Sign In Search for Jobs The page you are looking for doesn't exist. Search for Jobs © 2026 Workday, Inc. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Engineer--Embedded-AI-ML---MetaSense-Project-_R00025344": {
      "title": "Research Engineer (Embedded AI/ML - MetaSense Project)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering (MAE) is a robust, dynamic and multi-disciplinary international research community comprising of world-class scientists and bright students. MAE prides itself in its excellent research capabilities in areas including advanced manufacturing, aerospace, biomedical, energy, industrial engineering, maritime engineering, robotics, etc. The school is equipped with state-of-the-art research infrastructure, housing a comprehensive range of cluster laboratories, test bedding facilities, research centres/institutes and corporate laboratories. Cutting-edge research in MAE addresses the immediate needs of our industries and supports the nation’s long-term development strategies. In the new era of industrial 4.0 and sustainable living, MAE is rigorous in developing new competencies to support the growth and competitiveness of our engineering sector in the global landscape. MAE has grown to be leader in Engineering Research, ranking amongst the top engineering schools in the world. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/mae/research . We are looking for a Research Engineer, Embedded ML to join the MetaSense project — a wearable cardiometabolic sensing platform built on patent-pending dual-point photoplethysmography (2PPG) and ECG. This is a 1-year, closely supervised role, spanning embedded hardware, software, and biocomputational AI/ML development for continuous, non-invasive cardiometabolic monitoring. About MetaSense Project MetaSense is a cuffless cardiometabolic wearable platform under development at NTU's School of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering, in close collaboration with the National Heart Centre Singapore (NHCS/SingHealth) and A*STAR. Built around a patented dual point photoplethysmography (2PPG) modality, the project seeks to develop wearable systems and AI learning models for continuous hemodynamic biomarkers. MetaSense is a biooptics platform for continuous Cardiometabolic monitoring by replacing episodic measurements with continuous, non-invasive Al-powered biomarker tracking. Patent:  https://patentscope.wipo.int/search/en/WO2024205510 Why Join MetaSense? Exposure to embedded firmware and resource-constrained machine learning for implementation in wearable biosensing. Exposure to how physiological ML models are trained, validated for clinical applications. Exposure to the translational path from academic research toward regulatory-grade cuffless blood pressure wearables (e.g. HSA/FDA pathways). Direct, hands-on mentorship from the project's Research Fellow and Principal Investigator. Real translational research experience: contribute to a patent-pending wearable cardiometabolic platform working toward clinical validation, alongside NHCS/SingHealth and A*STAR. Key Responsibilities: You will support biocomputational AI/ML development, assist with embedded firmware and hardware bring-up for wearable PPG/ECG sensors, help prepare and validate physiological datasets, and support dashboard and visualisation tools — all under close guidance from the project’s Research Fellow and Principal Investigator. Support biocomputational AI/ML development — signal processing, pulse waveform morphology, and hemodynamic feature extraction — for cardiometabolic disease applications, under close PI/Co-I guidance. Assist with embedded firmware and hardware bring-up for wearable PPG/ECG sensor front-end, including microcontroller integration and sensor interfacing (I²C/SPI). Assist in preparing, cleaning, and validating physiological datasets (clinical and public) for model training and evaluation. Support development of dashboards and visualization tools for live sensor data and model outputs. Maintain clear technical documentation and take part in regular discussions with collaborators across NTU, NHCS/SingHealth, and A*STAR. Take on ad hoc technical tasks as directed by the Principal Investigator or project supervisors. Job Requirements: Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Computer Science, Electrical & Electronic Engineering, Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering, or a related field Confident proficiency in Python; familiarity with embedded electronics (microcontrollers, I²C/SPI/UART) and Git Comfortable working across hardware, software, and data domains Self-motivated and a good communicator, comfortable in a small, closely supervised team. We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant--Quantum-Sensing-_R00024727": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Quantum Sensing)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nTemasek Laboratories@NTU TL@NTU explores the frontiers in science and develops strategic technologies to enhance the defence and security of Singapore. TL@NTU forms part of the defence technology community in Singapore alongside DSO National Laboratories, Defence Science and Technology Agency (DSTA), Temasek Laboratories @ NUS and @SUTD and the local defence industry. The Centre for Quantum Sensing Technology (CQST) advances the science and engineering of next‑generation quantum sensors, with core programmes in cold‑atom sensing, quantum photonics, quantum materials, and superconducting sensor technologies. Key Responsibilities: The successful candidate will be involved in experimental work related to quantum sensing materials development and characterization, device fabrication and instrumentation work as needed. The job scope includes To assist in research operations (procurement of lab supplies, experimental setup, checking of literature and product specifications, establish safe work processes, etc.) To ensure conduct and proper documentations of experiments in consultation with project leader To assist in monitoring, repair and maintenance of equipment and process tools To support events, publications, proposals, planning, monitoring, reporting related to the project as relevant.  Job Requirements:  Minimally BSc/BEng in physics, engineering, materials engineering with 1-2 years of industry work experience would be advantageous Relevant prior experience in quantum related work would be advantageous We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Administration---Communications_R00025347": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Administration & Communications",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Assistant Manager will play a key role in supporting the Institute of Advanced Studies (IAS) through the effective facilitation of academic programmes, operational administration, and institutional communications. As IAS continues to expand its portfolio of high-profile academic visits, frontiers research conferences and public lectures, this role will be integral to ensuring the smooth planning, delivery, and promotion of the Institute's activities. Science at the highest level is the hallmark of IAS. The Institute fosters collaboration with Nobel Laureates, Turing Award winners, Millennium Technology Prize winners, and other leading global researchers. With a growing number of flagship events and strategic initiatives, dedicated administrative and operational support is essential to sustain the Institute's continued growth and excellence. Working closely with faculty members, researchers, University offices, and external partners, the incumbent will facilitate programme administration, event operations, stakeholder engagement, and selected communications activities, including the preparation of publicity materials, website content, and event summaries. The incumbent will contribute to the efficient execution of IAS programmes by supporting financial and procurement processes, maintaining programme records and documentation, and strengthening operational workflows that enhance the Institute's visibility, effectiveness, and long-term institutional capabilities. Key Responsibilities: Event Management and Operations Facilitate the planning and execution of academic events, including conferences, seminars, colloquia, workshops, public lectures, and distinguished visitor programmes. Manage event logistics, venue bookings, scheduling, registrations, travel arrangements, catering, and on-site operational support. Liaise with internal stakeholders, external speakers, vendors, and service providers to ensure the successful delivery of events. Prepare meeting agendas and minutes, facilitate RSVPs, and maintain event documentation. Track event statistics, attendance, registrations, and feedback for reporting and continuous improvement. Communications and Publicity Develop and facilitate publicity materials for academic events, including event announcements, newsletters, website updates, and social media content. Produce speeches, event summaries, and other communication materials that accurately represent IAS programmes and initiatives. Prepare basic publicity collateral such as posters, digital graphics, and promotional materials using standard design tools. Manage digital content across IAS web and social media platforms to strengthen institutional visibility and outreach. Editorial Support Work closely with researchers, faculty members, and communications offices to ensure the accuracy and quality of scientific information. Proofread and edit communication materials to maintain consistency, clarity, and editorial standards across IAS publications. Stakeholder Engagement and Administrative Support Serve as a key liaison between IAS and internal units, researchers, external collaborators, and service providers. Facilitate administrative processes related to academic visits, institutional partnerships, and programme activities. Support procurement, budget tracking, and operational administration associated with academic engagements. Contribute to the continuous improvement of operational processes and event delivery. Competencies and Qualification Requirements: A recognised degree in Science or Engineering or equivalent with at least 3 years of relevant administrative experience Experience in event management, programme facilitation, or administrative operations, preferably within a higher education, research, or public sector environment. Experience in digital publishing, content management systems (CMS), and basic graphic design or multimedia tools (e.g. Canva, Adobe Creative Suite or equivalent). Strong writing, editing, and copyediting skills, with the ability to produce clear and accurate communications for diverse audiences. Excellent organisational, project facilitation, and administrative skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities simultaneously. Strong interpersonal and stakeholder management skills, with experience working across multidisciplinary teams. Meticulous, resourceful, and able to work independently while maintaining high standards of accuracy. Interest in science communication and public engagement would be an advantage. This is a 3-year contract appointment. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Chemistry-Biomedical-Engineering-Material-Science-_R00025338": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Chemistry/Biomedical Engineering/Material Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Chemistry, Chemical Engineering and Biotechnology (CCEB) invites applications for the position of  Research Fellow . Job Description This post is being created to support the successful development, management, implementation, and dissemination of research projects led by the Principal Investigator (PI), Professor Chen Peng. The Postdoctoral Research Fellow will work within the PI's research group, leading research projects in nanomedicine related to the development of advanced therapeutic technologies for metabolic disorders and cancers. The successful candidate should possess a strong publication record and demonstrated expertise in nanomaterials synthesis and characterization, cell culture, molecular biology techniques, and mouse experiments. Key Responsibilities:  Conduct innovative research independently Take a leading role in multi-disciplinary research projects. Develop research collaborations across NTU and with external collaborators Supervise undergraduate students Contribute to writing research grant applications Publish in high-impact peer-review journals  Present the research to a variety of audiences at seminars and conferences Job Requirements:  PhD in Chemistry, Biomedical Engineering , Material Science or related disciplines A strong publication record in peer-review journals Leading research projects Proven high level quantitative and qualitative research skills A significant track record in attracting research grant funding Extensive experience in leading the design of research programs Experience of supervision of PhD / Masters / Undergraduate students Experience in teaching research lab s A strong publication record in peer-review journals Proven high level and comprehensive research skills Training in mouse experiments Experience in materials synthesis and characterizations Training in cell culturing, molecular biology techniques, histological analyses ​ We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Deputy-Director--Branding-and-Communications_R00025336": {
      "title": "Deputy Director, Branding and Communications",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University is a leading global university recognised for excellence in education and research. Nanyang Business School (NBS) is one of Asia’s premier business schools, committed to delivering impactful education and driving innovation in teaching and engagement. The Deputy Director, Branding and Communications drives the development and implementation of strategic communications, branding, media engagement and marketing initiatives across Nanyang Business School. Reporting to the Deputy Dean, the role oversees the College’s branding, media relations, stakeholder engagement, corporate communications and high-level events management efforts. The incumbent works closely with programme offices, research centres, faculty, alumni and the University’s Corporate Communications Office (CCO) to strengthen institutional visibility and reputation. The role also oversees Dean’s communications, editorial outputs, social media platforms and strategic communications initiatives, while leading the Marketing Communications team to ensure effective and consistent communications support across the College. Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in Communications, Marketing, Business, Media or related disciplines. At least 15 years of relevant communications, branding or marketing experience. Strong experience in media relations, stakeholder engagement and strategic communications. Experience leading communications or marketing teams. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Strong stakeholder management and project management capability. Experience in higher education or large institutions would be advantageous. Familiarity with digital marketing, social media platforms and communications analytics. Experience supporting senior leadership communications. Ability to assess reputational considerations and provide sound communications advisory. Competencies Leadership and Strategic Agility Provides strategic leadership while driving operational excellence and execution. Leads and develops high-performing teams, navigating ambiguity and competing priorities effectively. Leverages AI, automation and emerging technologies to enhance communications and branding outcomes while fostering innovation and continuous improvement. Innovation and Creativity Develops creative, impactful branding and communication strategies. Demonstrates strong storytelling skills and the ability to translate complex ideas into compelling narratives. Embraces experimentation and new approaches to strengthen audience engagement. Digital and AI Fluency Possesses strong knowledge of digital platforms, AI-enabled tools, analytics and emerging technologies. Applies AI and automation to improve efficiency, content development and stakeholder engagement. Understands the ethical, governance and quality considerations associated with AI-driven communications. Stakeholder and Relationship Management Builds trusted relationships and influences a broad range of stakeholders, including senior leaders and external partners. Manages complex stakeholder environments and aligns diverse interests towards shared objectives. Provides strategic communications and reputation management counsel to leadership. Execution Excellence Delivers high-quality outcomes with strong responsiveness and attention to detail. Effectively manages multiple priorities and projects in a fast-paced environment. Demonstrates strong project management capabilities from planning through execution. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
