    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Scholarships-and-Convocation_R00024266": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Scholarships and Convocation",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNTU offers a collaborative and vibrant working environment where staff contribute to shaping the future of education and research. Staff members benefit from opportunities for professional development, career progression, and participation in university initiatives and staff engagement programmes. The School of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering (MAE) is one of the largest and most established engineering schools in the world, offering a dynamic environment that supports academic excellence, student development, and industry collaboration. About the Role The School of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering invites applications for the position of Senior Executive, Scholarships and Convocation . In this role, you will provide administrative and operational support for student scholarships, awards, bursaries, and convocation-related activities. You will work closely with internal stakeholders to ensure smooth coordination of student recognition programmes and maintain accurate student records and reporting. This position offers the opportunity to contribute to meaningful student initiatives while supporting the School’s mission to recognize and celebrate student achievements. Key Responsibilities: Administer and coordinate student scholarships, awards, and bursaries , including nominations, verification, and documentation. Support the planning and execution of convocation-related activities and student recognition events. Maintain and manage student records and databases , ensuring data accuracy and compliance with university procedures. Source and prepare reports related to student achievements, scholarships, and awards . Coordinate with internal stakeholders such as academic staff and administrative teams to facilitate student-related processes. Provide administrative support for school outreach, engagement activities, and student-related events when required. Manage end-to-end undergraduate admissions processes for diverse applicant groups, including Polytechnic, A-Level, Aptitude-Based Admissions, Adult Learners, and flow-through applicants . Requirements: A recognised Bachelor’s degree with relevant administrative or operational experience. Strong organisational and coordination skills with the ability to manage multiple tasks. Good interpersonal and communication skills. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications and data management. Ability to work collaboratively with stakeholders in a fast-paced environment. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Project-Manager_R00024985": {
      "title": "Project Manager",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAI Singapore (AISG) is a national AI programme launched by the National Research Foundation (NRF) to anchor deep national capabilities in Artificial Intelligence (AI). Hosted by the Nanyang Technological University (NTU), AISG and brings together all Singapore-based research institutions and the vibrant ecosystem of AI start-ups and companies developing AI products to perform use-inspired research, grow the knowledge, create the tools, and develop the talent to power Singapore's AI efforts. We're looking for a Project Manager with a strong business analyst streak to join the Data Platform team within AI Products at AISG — someone who can hold the rhythm of a complex international programme while translating partner needs into clear platform requirements. This hybrid role bridges business needs and technical solutions, manages project timelines, resources, and deliverables across multiple workstreams. This role calls for strong analytical skills, effective communication, and the ability to coordinate several initiatives simultaneously. This position will be hosted at the Nanyang Technological University (NTU) under VP (Artificial Intelligence & Digital Economy)’s office and we welcome you to join our community. Duties & Responsibilities: Programme coordination and stakeholder management Coordinate and chair regular working sessions with external partners, research collaborators, and community contributors across multiple time zones ensuring meetings are well-prepared, well-documented, and produce clear follow-ups. Track action items, decisions, risks, and milestones across the programme; surface blockers proactively; and maintain a single source of truth for programme status, with regular updates to leadership and funders. Requirements gathering and business analysis Elicit, document, and validate data requirements from internal teams and external partners covering data types, formats, sourcing protocols, licensing, quality standards, and cultural/linguistic considerations. Translate partner and community needs into structured requirements (user stories, data specifications, process flows) for engineering and data teams, and facilitate alignment where partners' needs, timelines, or constraints differ. Partnerships, legal and procurement support Support the partnerships team across the MOU lifecycle (drafting, version control, legal review, execution tracking) and prepare NDAs and collaboration agreements as needed. Work with legal to develop and maintain platform policies (e.g. data sharing, consent, IP, acceptable use) and ensure these are reflected in partner-facing documentation. Lead procurement workstreams in line with AISG's hosting institution policies and preparing documentation, onboarding vendors, and tracking purchase orders, deliverables, and payments. Data analytics, metrics and reporting Define, track, and report on programme KPIs (data contributions, partner engagement, platform usage, quality) in collaboration with the platform and partnerships teams. Prepare metrics reports and KPI updates for leadership, funders, and stakeholders; build and maintain dashboards that give the team real-time visibility into programme health. Conduct ad-hoc analyses to support decision-making such as partner performance reviews, dataset coverage gaps, or funding milestone readiness. Requirements: Some technical aptitude is expected — preferably hands-on experience using AI tools in your day-to-day work and you should be familiar enough with AI, data science, and modern data infrastructure to converse credibly with academics and technical experts. The ideal candidate would have: A degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or equivalent; knowledge of AI or data science is highly desirable. At least 3 years of experience conceptualising, implementing, or managing technology-related research projects or programmes, ideally with an international or multi-stakeholder dimension. Hands-on experience using AI tools and workflows in day-to-day work (e.g. for drafting, summarisation, requirements analysis, or process automation). Demonstrated business analysis experience through eliciting needs from non-technical stakeholders and translating them into actionable requirements. Experience supporting procurement, vendor management, and contracting workflows (MOUs, NDAs, collaboration agreements). Comfort working with data such as defining metrics, building reports and dashboards, and analysing programme performance with tools like Excel or SQL. Strong analytical and strategic thinking; resourceful and proactive, able to work around ambiguity. Excellent written and verbal communication, with the ability to facilitate meetings across cultures and time zones. Bonus: knowledge of data governance concepts and practices (e.g. data classification, stewardship, lineage, access policies, retention, and compliance frameworks); experience engaging government agencies or international partnerships. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Director--Stakeholder-Engagement_R00024427": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Stakeholder Engagement",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nRanked among the world’s top universities. NTU Entrepreneurship Academy (NTUpreneur) provides education within the University and the region. The Assistant Director, Stakeholder Engagement is responsible for leading and implementing the existing and new initiatives to drive, facilitate and execute new opportunities for students’ I&E growth journeys as part of a holistic entrepreneurship education. The incumbent is responsible for identifying and facilitating collaboration between NTU community and external stakeholders, such as ESG, ACE, SGInnovate, Social Impact Catalyst, raiSE etc and government or government funded institutions. The incumbent will facilitate to connect NTU students to available resources (for example, equipment) and facilities (Innovation Ports and Makers’ Labs) on campus. This role will work with the relevant managers of these resources to provide the necessary support and accelerate students’ I&E journeys. The incumbent will play a strategic role in designing and curating high-impact Innovation and Entrepreneurship (I&E) initiatives that bridge students with industry, ecosystem partners, and global opportunities. This role focuses on expanding and strengthening students’ I&E pathways, through curated activities and collaborations with strategic partners to enhance relevant industry knowledge, expertise, and real-world experience to enrich learning and venture-building outcomes. Working across institutions of the NTU I&E and NTU schools, the role focuses on enabling students across disciplines to translate ideas into viable startups through structured, outcome-based initiatives, as well as strengthening NTUpreneur’s position within the local and global entrepreneurship ecosystem through strategic partnerships and stakeholder engagement. The successful candidate can look forward to a rewarding career at NTU with ample opportunities for growth and development. Job Responsibilities: Drive, design, strengthen, and promote NTU Innovation and Entrepreneurship (I&E) Pathway for Students Provide leadership to strengthen existing I&E Pathway for NTU students.  Conceptualise, and organise impactful and outcome-driven co-curricular I&E programmes, to increase entrepreneurial skillsets and experience in real-world situations and exposure to industry, Grow student leadership in I&E activities through targeted strategy, for example, proactive engagement with relevant students’ Clubs and Societies, and other student networks to lead I&E activities on campus. Lead Stakeholder Engagement and Industry Partnership Development Identify, build, and sustain strong relationships with alumni, local and international industry partners, startups, venture capitalists, accelerators, and ecosystem players. Through partnerships, create meaningful opportunities to increase knowledge on venture creation, opportunities for venture incubation, increase local and global exposure to the I&E ecosystem. Increase NTU I&E visibility and reputation locally and internationally, through active participation and by organising representatives in events organised by high-profile institutions/ organisations. Drive internal collaboration towards NTU I&E Alignment Identify opportunities and drive collaborations with faculty, Leads of the undergraduate, postgraduate teams, and experiential learning (student venture support) teams to align programmes and their objectives for stronger outcomes. Support cross-functional initiatives within NTUpreneur and the broader NTU I&E ecosystem. Oversee the design and implementation of major University I&E events to ensure effective outcomes and implement effective outreach strategies to reach the targeted audience Conceptualise I&E engagement activities with strong value proposition to attract students to pursue entrepreneurship education and entrepreneurship in major university-level events such as the annual Open House, Freshmen Orientation, and NTUpreneur Day, the annual Chua Thian Poh Pinnacle Prize and Distinguished Speakers Series. Engage strategic partners of other NTU’s departments such as NTUitive, International Engagement Office, Alumni Engagement Office to organise I&E activities etc. Drive, and oversee the implementation of  effective outreach and marketing materials to promote NTUpreneur’s activities Conceptualise effective and targeted marketing and outreach strategies to promote our academic, experiential learning (I&E Pathways) programmes. Oversee and coordinate with academic programme teams to ensure that NTUpreneur’s website is updated promptly and check on compliance of NTU I&E Corporate Guidelines for all EDMs and brochures. Manage by creating or coordinating content creation of NTUpreneur’s social media. Report engagement results on a monthly basis. Requirements : Bachelor’s (Hons) Degree (Preferably in Entrepreneurship or Business) At least 5 years relevant work experience in a university and multi-disciplinary environment. Experience in the startup ecosystem is a plus. Experience in fact-finding and analysing data to ensure effective outcomes Demonstrated ability to build and maintain relationships with diverse stakeholders Experience in working with professors, I&E government funding agencies, MNCs with innovation arm. Good communication skills Knowledge in entrepreneurship, start-up development and ecosystem Knowledge of best practices in venture support in world-class universities as part of a holistic entrepreneurship education Knowledge in government grants, and other available support from related agencies for startups in Singapore Experience in budget planning, managing and processing claims in grants Enjoy working with students, empowering and helping them to accelerate their I&E journeys Capability to work independently to drive the execution of projects, but with strong attributes of a team player Demonstrated resourcefulness, strong problem-solving skills, and the ability to multitask efficiently, even under tight deadlines Meticulous and eye for details in organising information and tracking work progress Creative and refreshing ideas and demonstrated experience in organising large-scale events We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant--AI--Technology--Medicine-_R00025329": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (AI, Technology, Medicine)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-27\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Division of Information Technology and Operations Management at Nanyang Business School is inviting applications for a Research Assistant position. Job Responsibilities: The RA is expected to plan, organize and implement research projects, in collaboration with the principal investigators. The successful candidate will work closely with professionals in the field of AI, technology and medicine. Conduct literature reviews, coordinate schedules for data collection with survey and interview participants Assist in data collection, data transcription and analysis Contribute to the dissemination of research findings Job requirements: Minimally a bachelor’s degree in a related field (i.e. Business, AI, Technology or Medicine) Excellent oral and written communication skills are required Able to work independently and meet deadlines Experience with qualitative methods and data analysis We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Computer-Science---Computer-Engineering---Cybersecurity---Artificial-Intelligence-_R00025324": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Computer Science / Computer Engineering / Cybersecurity / Artificial Intelligence)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-27\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nYoung and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is ranked among the world’s top universities. We are seeking a highly motivated Research Associate to contribute to the design and implementation of simulation environments, intelligent testing and traffic analysis frameworks, automated security evaluation tools, experimental studies and technical documentation Job Responsibilities: Develop and maintain the simulation and testing environment for drone communication protocols. Design and implement intelligent frameworks for protocol fuzz testing and security evaluation. Develop traffic analysis methods for anomaly detection, behaviour classification and attack inference. Conduct experiments to assess protocol robustness, security and resilience under abnormal and adversarial conditions. Develop automated methods for validating identified vulnerabilities and evaluating potential attack scenarios. Analyse experimental results and contribute to the improvement of the developed frameworks and methodologies. Develop LLM-based agentic frameworks for generating intelligent and diverse fuzzing inputs. Prepare technical documentation, project reports, research publications and presentations, and work with the research team to achieve project milestones and deliverables. Job Requirements: Master’s degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Cybersecurity, Artificial Intelligence or a related discipline. Relevant experience in software development, cybersecurity, network protocols, artificial intelligence or related research areas. Good programming skills in languages such as Python, C or C++. Familiarity with Linux-based development environments, software debugging and testing tools. Knowledge of network communication, protocol analysis, vulnerability assessment or traffic analysis. Experience with machine learning, large language models, automated testing or security research would be advantageous. Strong analytical, problem-solving and technical documentation skills. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a multidisciplinary research team, with good written and verbal communication skills. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Computer-Science---Software-Engineering---Artificial-Intelligence-_R00025323": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Computer Science / Software Engineering / Artificial Intelligence)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-27\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nYoung and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is ranked among the world’s top universities. We are seeking a highly motivated Research Fellow to conduct research in formal verification, machine learning and artificial intelligence system assurance. The successful candidate will develop new techniques and tools for analysing, verifying and improving the correctness, robustness and reliability of deep neural networks and AI-enabled software systems.   Job Responsibilities: Develop novel methods and algorithms for the verification, testing and robustness analysis of deep neural networks and AI-enabled systems. Explore techniques such as abstraction, invariant learning, convex approximation, symbolic analysis and high-dimensional geometric analysis to improve the scalability and precision of AI verification. Evaluate the developed techniques through experiments, benchmark datasets and real-world AI applications. Publish research findings in reputable conferences and journals, and prepare project reports and technical deliverables. Collaborate with the Principal Investigator, research team and external partners, while mentoring junior researchers and students. Job Requirements: PhD in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Artificial Intelligence or a closely related discipline. Demonstrated ability to conduct independent research and develop novel research methods. Proven research track record with publications in reputable conferences or journals. Ability to work independently and collaboratively, with good analytical, communication and mentoring skills. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTUGillman-Singapore/Research-Assistant--Social-Science-Arts-Humanities-_R00025249": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Social Science/Arts/Humanities)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-27\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Climate Transformation Programme (CTP) is spearheaded by the Earth Observatory of Singapore (EOS). It aims to develop, inspire and accelerate knowledge-based solutions and educate future leaders to establish the stable climate and environment necessary for resilient, just, and sustainable Southeast Asian societies. The Climate Transformation Programme–Sustainable Societies Cluster works collaboratively across the CTP themes from Climate and Biodiversity, Mitigation, to Climate Processes and Extremes, to develop a suite of programmes that form a synergistic relay of interdisciplinary research and external outreach. The initiatives aim to cultivate a critical multiplicity of voices, perspectives, and knowledges from both within and outside academic realms in the formation of ‘Sustainable Societies’ that engage with questions of climate change. The position supports the Sustainable Societies (Arts Sub-Group) Cross-Cutting Cluster under the MOE Tier 3c Climate Transformation Programme (CTP). The CTP is spearheaded by the Earth Observatory of Singapore (EOS). The Sustainable Societies (Arts Sub-Group) Cluster is co-led by Principal Investigator (PI) Professor Laura Miotto. Under the supervision of Professor Miotto, the position serves as a key contact in coordinating projects and initiatives led by the cluster, from the administration and preparation of materials for reporting to the coordination of internal and external stakeholders. The role will assist in general administration and coordinate with various NTU departments as required, from the Finance department to the Administrative Office of EOS. The role will also contribute to content development and the organization of research and educational public programmes such as the Climate Transformation: Sustainable Societies Lecture Series and adjacent gatherings. This position is for an 8-month contract. The candidate will be based at the NTU Centre for Contemporary Art Singapore at Gillman Barracks. For more information, visit the website https://ntu.ccasingapore.org/ . Key Responsibilities: Key administrative contact for various project stakeholders such as co-investigators, local and international collaborators, research fellows and other internal and external parties, including vendors. Provide general administrative support, day to day management, and organisational logistics of the research project. Prepare all project materials for all reporting obligations (both grantor and NTU) and ensure timely completion and submission. Assist in the preparation of field trips in all matters, ranging from visa to travel and accommodation arrangements. Assist Research Associate/Research Fellow/PI in data management and executions of any meetings, conference and exhibitions where necessary. Undertake any other duties relevant to the research project such as corresponding with stakeholders and working with other departments (e.g. Finance and event management) Support the PI, as well as the Co-I in all grant administration matters. Job Requirements: Possess at minimum a Bachelor’s degree in a relevant social science, arts or humanities discipline. Demonstrated professional experience in academic, research or educational institutions. Strong skills in organisation/administration, project and time management in order to meet competing deadlines. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills to liaise with internal and external stakeholders and collaborators. Proficiency in Microsoft Office, Excel, Adobe CS, social media programmes Demonstrated writing skills for grant applications. Experience with A/V equipment assisting with video and audio recording. Highly motivated and able to work independently with minimal supervision. The closing date of the advertisement is 14th August 2026 . We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Manager--Provost-s-Office_R00025326": {
      "title": "Manager, Provost’s Office",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-27\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Manager, Provost’s Office will report to the Director (Provost’s Office) and provide support in: Execution of Provost’s strategic projects and initiatives that strengthens faculty recruitment and development in NTU.  As part of this task, the manager will develop policy papers, project proposals, agreements, execute and monitor project timeline, and report on key projects.  Managing projects related to AI Singapore, a national R&D platform funded by the Ministry of Digital Development and Information, the Info-communications and Media Development Authority, and the Singapore National Research Foundation; and Managing the operations and administration of the Provost’s Office. The Manager will be responsible for the following: Managing strategic projects of Provost’s Office Support the Director (Provost’s Office) in the implementation and tracking of strategic projects and initiatives. Provide secretariat support and follow-through for meetings. Work closely with stakeholders including the project leads, track taskforces, administrative heads, and finance to ensure successful planning, execution, and completion of initiatives. Monitor project timelines, budgets, and deliverables. Collate data for reports as required for reporting to the Board of Trustees. Managing projects related to AI Singapore Assist the Director of Planning and Operations of AI Singapore in managing and overseeing the implementation of applied and translational initiatives, including facilitating approvals in accordance to the governance structure within AI Singapore. Interact with and manage internal administrative team within AI Singapore, Directors, as well as external stakeholders to AI Singapore such as funders, professors, and the respective institution’s administrative team. Managing operations and administration of Provost’s Office Support the management of Provost’s Office which may include the budget, assets, and physical space. Prepare monthly budget projections and reports to keep track of expenses. Requirements: Bachelor’s Degree or equivalent practical experience. Strong project management skills, with ability to manage one or more projects concurrently. Strong verbal and written communication skills. Ability to work independently and as a team We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow---Computer-Science---Mathematics---Information-Theory---Cybersecurity---Electrical-Engineering-_R00025312": {
      "title": "Research Fellow  (Computer Science / Mathematics / Information Theory / Cybersecurity / Electrical Engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University’s National Centre for Research in Digital Trust (DTC) is a Trust Technology Research Centre to execute a national program to help put Singapore into a strong trust hub. The key objective is to support efforts to create a trusted digital environment for people and businesses in the digital transformation by providing businesses and consumers with greater assurance and confidence as they digitalize.  We are seeking a highly motivated Research Fellow to conduct cutting-edge research on trustworthy digital content, AI systems, and advanced forensic technologies for financial crime detection and anti-money laundering (AML). The successful candidate will contribute to the design, development, and validation of innovative approaches for detecting financial crimes, identifying illicit activities, and enhancing trust in digital financial ecosystems. Key Responsibilities: Responsible for research and development of trust technologies such as Digital Forensics for Financial Investigations, Graph Analytics and Criminal Network Discovery, Suspicious Activity Detection, Digital Content Provenance and Authenticity, etc., which are important components to strengthening trust, security, and resilience in the digital economy. Responsible for technologies system development/implementation, and delivery working prototypes/demo. Lead/Involved in research/industrial projects. Prepare reports and scientific papers. Job Requirements: Ph.D. degree in Computer Science, Mathematics, Information Theory, Cybersecurity, Electrical Engineering, or a related field. Strong publication record in top-tier conferences and journals related to AI, security, privacy, digital forensics, or trustworthy computing. Solid background in Machine Learning, Digital Forensics, Security, and AI Generation Models. Experience with deep learning frameworks such as PyTorch or TensorFlow. Proficiency in programming languages including C/C++, Python, Java, and Go. Familiarity with Digital Content Forensics, Machine Learning, AI Generation Models. Experience with privacy-preserving technologies (e.g., homomorphic encryption, federated learning, secure computation) is an advantage. Excellent communication skills, self-motivation, and the ability to deliver high-quality research outcomes under tight schedules. Ability to work independently as well as collaboratively in a multidisciplinary research team. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Integrated-Polaritonic-Devices-_R00025314": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Integrated Polaritonic Devices)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Research Fellow at National Centre for Advanced Integrated Photonics (NCAIP) will contribute to the development of integrated polaritonic devices and waveguides, with emphasis on long-range polariton propagation, low-energy switching concepts, few-particle modulation of condensate nonlinearities, integrated polaritonic circuit functions, and coupling of polaritonic states to on-chip detection/readout architectures. Key Responsibilities: As an integral part of the project, the Research Fellow is expected to conduct research in integrated polaritonic devices and waveguides, including the design, fabrication, optimization and experimental characterization of polaritonic waveguides, polariton lasers, cavity/waveguide networks, and polaritonic circuit elements. The role includes developing and operating advanced optical spectroscopy setups; measuring propagation, emission, nonlinear response, switching behaviour, photon-correlation behaviour, and coupling to detection/readout platforms; and supporting the development of long-range polaritonic waveguiding platforms and polaritonic logic or routing functions. The Research Fellow is expected to work, generate ideas and experimentally prove them both independently and within team-working efforts with other researchers working on the project to deliver state‑of‑the‑art single‑photon imaging capabilities, and to disseminate results through publications, reports, and IP contributions. Requirements: PhD in Physics, Photonics, Optical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Materials Science, or a related field. Strong research background in experimental optics, photonics, optical spectroscopy, exciton-polariton physics, nonlinear optics, semiconductor optics, or related areas. Proven publication record in internationally recognized peer-reviewed journals. Experience in designing, aligning, and operating advanced optical setups involving lasers, microscopy, spectroscopy, and imaging systems is preferred. Experience in polariton devices, photonic waveguides, topological photonics, photonic crystals, or single-photon measurement techniques is advantageous. Proficiency in scientific programming and data analysis tools such as Python or MATLAB. Strong analytical, communication, teamwork, and problem-solving skills, with the ability to work independently in a research environment. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Integrated-SNSPD-Detectors-_R00025315": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Integrated SNSPD Detectors)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Research Fellow at National Centre for Advanced Integrated Photonics (NCAIP) will contribute to the development of integrated superconducting nanowire single-photon detector (SNSPD) technologies for on-chip quantum photonic and sensing platforms. Key Responsibilities: As an integral part of the project, the Research Fellow is expected to conduct research in integrated SNSPD detectors and readout technologies, including the development and experimental validation of waveguide-integrated SNSPD devices; process integration; optical coupling optimization; on-chip detection-efficiency measurement; timing-jitter characterization; photon-number-resolving operation; and detector integration with quantum photonic circuits. The role also includes nanofabrication and process development for integrated photonic and detector structures, including thin-film deposition, lithography, etching, wafer- or chip-scale process flow optimization, and materials/device characterization. The Research Fellow will also develop SNSPD integration in MWIR topological waveguides and waveguide-integrated MWIR detector platforms, including device fabrication/assembly, coupling to MWIR waveguides, and optimization of detector performance. The role further includes development of SNSPD detector arrays and readout architectures, including multi-pixel detector arrays, space- or time-multiplexed effective-pixel arrays, photon-number-resolving detection, integrated electronic boards for control/readout, hybrid cryogenic electronics, biasing, amplification, thresholding, digitization, and detector-array performance benchmarking. The Research Fellow is expected to support cryogenic packaging and system-level integration, including fiber-array coupling, electrical interconnects, compact packaging of detector chips, low-noise readout interfaces, and reliability/yield/stability assessment of integrated detector prototypes. The Research Fellow is expected to work, generate ideas and experimentally prove them both independently and within team-working efforts with other researchers working on the project to deliver state‑of‑the‑art single‑photon imaging capabilities, and to disseminate results through publications, reports, and IP contributions. Requirements: PhD in Physics, Photonics, Electrical Engineering, Materials Science, Nanotechnology, or a related discipline. Strong research background in integrated photonics, nanophotonics, nanofabrication, photonic device fabrication, superconducting detectors, or related fields. Proven publication record in reputable peer-reviewed journals. Experience in cleanroom fabrication processes and advanced materials/device characterization techniques is preferred. Familiarity with photonic waveguide platforms and detector integration technologies is advantageous. Experience with SNSPDs, superconducting materials, cryogenic measurements, MWIR photonics, detector arrays, readout electronics, or cryogenic packaging will be an added advantage. Proficiency in scientific programming, data analysis, simulation, and modeling tools (e.g., Python, MATLAB, TCAD, photonic simulation software). Strong analytical, problem-solving, communication, and teamwork skills, with the ability to work independently in a research environment. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Human-Factors-_R00025308": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Human Factors)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAir Traffic Management Research Institute (ATMRI) is a research institute at Nanyang Technological University (NTU), Singapore, supported by the Civil Aviation Authority of Singapore (CAAS). The key objective of ATMRI is to support research and innovation in air traffic management. ATMRI focuses on developing practical and data-driven solutions for complex aviation systems, in close collaboration with industry and international partners. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/atmri . We are looking for a Research Fellow to conduct research on human factors and cognitive systems in air traffic management (ATM), with a focus on operator cognitive load, situational awareness, and decision-support interfaces for air traffic controllers. The role will involve designing and evaluating human-in-the-loop tools using methods such as eye-tracking, physiological sensing, and uncertainty visualization, contributing to the advancement of research and innovation at Nanyang Technological University. Key Responsibilities: Conduct research on human factors and cognitive systems approaches to support air traffic management studies and applications. Design, develop, and evaluate decision-support interfaces and operator-facing tools using operational and simulated data. Support research activities on controller cognitive load, situational awareness, and resilience under current and future ATM concepts. Work collaboratively with researchers and engineers to develop prototype solutions and human-in-the-loop evaluation frameworks. Conduct user studies and analyse results (e.g. eye-tracking, physiological sensing) to assess the performance and usability of developed tools in realistic operational scenarios. Prepare technical reports, research papers, and project deliverables, and participate in project meetings and reviews. Publish research findings in top-tier journals and conferences in relevant fields (e.g. human-computer interaction, human factors, ATM). Contribute to research proposals, technical documentation, and other project-related activities as required. Job Requirements: PhD qualification in Human-Computer Interaction, Cognitive Science, Human Factors, Air Traffic Management, Transport, or other related fields. At least three (3) years of relevant research experience in human factors, cognitive systems, or related technical research roles, ideally within transport, aviation, or other safety-critical operational domains. Familiarity with research related to cognitive load assessment, decision-support interfaces, or human-in-the-loop systems for complex operational environments (e.g. air traffic management, control rooms). Good written and oral communication skills, with the ability to prepare technical reports and academic publications. Proficiency in job-specific technical skills, including programming for research and data analysis purposes (e.g. Python or similar languages), experience with eye-tracking or physiological sensing methods, as well as strong numerical and analytical skills. Competent in general research-related skills and professional attributes, including problem-solving and analytical thinking. Strong interpersonal skills, with the ability to work independently and collaboratively, develop solutions under defined timelines, and demonstrate good organisational and time management skills. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Quantum-Materials-Physics-_R00025309": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Quantum Materials Physics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research.  With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 2,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 4th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2025 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. The Belopolski Research Group (QuantumX Labs) is hiring ambitious & creative Research Fellows to explore topological quantum materials. Our group aims to discover new topological quantum phases of matter, explore their physics and apply them to address challenges in electronics, photonics, quantum computing, catalysis and biology. We use molecular beam epitaxy (MBE) to synthesize atomically precise crystals, we integrate them with two-dimensional exfoliated materials, and we characterize them using transport and angle-resolved photoemission spectroscopy (ARPES). We have immediate need for enthusiastic postdocs to synthesize novel quantum anomalous Hall phases by MBE, characterize altermagnets and p -wave magnets by ARPES, pursue scalable wafer-scale moiré epitaxy, develop epitaxial superconductors for quantum computing and integrate machine learning for automated high-throughput MBE. We are particularly excited to recruit postdocs with experience in optics, two-dimensional materials and a strong theoretical background. Applicants should have a Ph.D. in quantum physics, electrical engineering or a related field. Key Responsibilities The Research Fellow will pursue scientific research broadly on topological quantum materials at QuantumX Labs, the research group of Prof. Ilya Belopolski, https://www.quantumx.science . Researchers will have the opportunity to, Synthesize atomically precise thin films of new topological materials using molecular beam epitaxy (MBE) Develop innovative approaches to accelerate MBE materials development using in situ characterization & machine learning Integrate epitaxial synthesis with exfoliated two-dimensional materials & devices Characterize resistivity, Hall response, non-linear transport and magnetization Explore electronic structure with angle-resolved photoemission spectroscopy (ARPES) at synchrotrons such as Diamond Light Source in the UK or the Advanced Light Source in the USA Develop theoretical models of topological materials to understand & interpret experimental data Leverage nanofabrication facilities & collaborate with other leading research groups at the School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering (EEE) and the School of Physical & Mathematical Sciences (SPMS) at Nanyang Technological University, Singapore Collaborate worldwide to identify new candidate materials, perform ab initio calculations and complement our results with additional experimental techniques Build out additional in-house experimental capabilities in optics, microwaves and quantum sensing The researcher is also encouraged to bring in physics & techniques from their Ph.D. which augment or resonate with the interests of our group & the community at NTU. Job Requirement Ph.D. in quantum physics, electrical engineering or a related discipline; familiarity with superconductivity, magnetic skyrmions, topological insulators, Mott insulators and/or quantum spin liquids Technical experience with experimental synthesis, transport & optics techniques, such as: Low-temperature transport & characterization by PPMS, MPMS and/or dilution fridge Second harmonic generation, photoluminescence, Raman spectroscopy & other optical techniques Materials synthesis by molecular beam epitaxy (MBE), pulsed laser deposition (PLD) etc. Exfoliation & device fabrication of two-dimensional materials such as graphene & chalcogenides Strong theoretical & mathematical background Interest in leading scientific breakthroughs, as well as working closely with a team, to deepen our understanding of emergent phenomena in quantum physics and pioneer applications to electronics, photonics, quantum computing, catalysis and biology We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Research-Fellow--Soundscape-Engineering-_R00025307-1": {
      "title": "Senior Research Fellow (Soundscape Engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research. With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 2,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 4th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2025 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee We are looking for a Senior Research Fellow to push the development of the AIoT system, which is a key thrust in a Soundscape project. This is a big project where there is a strong emphasis in deployment, testing and scaling up in building. There are many diverse factors to come up with a robust and stable system to made it more industry ready that focus on cross-platform instead of current single platform. Furthermore, the success of this thrust will help to increase university engagement with industry that facilitate tech transfer that benefited university and industry. The role will focus on data curation, AI model training, edge-AI deployment, subjective evaluation, and AIoT implementation. Key Responsibilities: Writing, debugging, optimizing and testing of source code with an emphasis on audio applications Maintenance and improvement of existing audio algorithm code base including noise reduction, acoustic echo cancellation, automatic gain control, voice activity detection, packet loss compensation and other audio enhancements Supporting Research and Feasibility Studies including defining the scope and goals of audio research tasks and completion of detailed reports on results and recommendations for development activities Software development of new algorithmic audio processing solutions including the existing areas mentioned above and additionally including state of the art audio codecs, audibility and intelligibility enhancements, microphone array processing, soundscape and other audio enhancements Project management tasks including creation and maintenance of requirements and schedule documentation for assigned projects, project budget etc. Publish journal and conference papers as dictated by the assigned projects. Provide guidance of Master/Undergraduate students Need more than 5 years of industry experience working in this area. Job Requirements: PhD qualification degree in soundscape engineering and evaluation or related field At least 5 years of relevant experiences in soundscape engineering / technical hands-on experience soundscape evaluation Familiarity with soundscape ISO standards Good written and oral communication skills Proficiency in AI (python) programming and R programming Competent in designing subjective experiments and evaluation Ability to work independently, develop solutions under strict timelines, meticulous and eye for details / excellent organizational and time management skills and have experiences in publishing soundscape engineering papers, Ability to build rapport and influence stakeholders at all levels Ability to work collaboratively in a fast-paced environment. Possesses international experience, with a strong network of contacts in the region We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
