    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Business-Systems-Specialist-Analyst--Digital-Solutions-Department---NIE-_R00023948": {
      "title": "Business Systems Specialist/Analyst (Digital Solutions Department) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-23\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nABOUT THE NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF EDUCATION (NIE) The National Institute of Education (NIE), Singapore , is Singapore’s national teacher education institute and we are proud to be an integral part of the nation’s education service. We play a key role in the preparation of teachers and in the provision of teacher professional and school leadership development programmes. We are committed to our vision of being An Institute of Distinction: Leading the Future of Education and our mission to Inspire Learning, Transform Teaching and Advance Research . Read more about NIE here . The National Institute of Education (NIE) invites suitable candidates to join the Division of Academic Computing & Information Services (ACIS) as a Business Systems Specialist/Analyst (19-month contract). This role is instrumental in supporting various project management initiatives within the organization, with a strong emphasis on stakeholder management. We are seeking a dynamic IT professional who excels in project management and is an effective team player. If you are looking for an exciting opportunity to contribute to the advancement of educational systems in the academic domain, we encourage you to apply. Join us in shaping the future of education at NIE! Job Description As a member of the Digital Solutions department responsible for project management initiatives for Academic’s Domain , your responsibilities will include: Strategic Visibility & Stakeholder Management : Act as the primary advocate for the user community, ensuring all stakeholders are engaged regarding their system concerns and feel heard by the Digital Solutions department. Proactively communicate project roadmaps and keep the university and institution informed about the progress of institute strategic initiatives. Manage change effectively by ensuring users are well-informed of enterprise-level changes, system updates, and ongoing technology refresh of legacy applications. Establish real-time dashboards to enhance performance transparency, making project health and support metrics visible to Digital Solutions leaders and the wider division. Collaborate closely with the Development Team to provide visibility on project plans, stakeholder feedback, and institutional changes. Support Strategy & Triage Governance : Oversee the classification of support requests by domain to protect project timelines and ensure effective resource allocation. Define and monitor Service Level Agreements (SLAs) for all user-facing requests to maintain high institutional satisfaction through timely responses. Innovation Delivery & Data Integrity : Continuously seek to implement innovations driven by AI, data, and automation across institutional applications. Lead initiatives to ensure data integrity and accuracy, addressing any discrepancies proactively. Collaborate with the Development team to enhance the efficiency of processes and implement automated solutions where feasible. Utilize AI-driven insights to monitor project performance and identify areas for improvement before they impact the user community. Requirements A University degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Engineering, or a related field. At least 2 years of experience in a project management or related role, with specific exposure to stakeholder management and support. Proven expertise in project management methodologies and techniques. Strong communication and interpersonal skills to engage with a diverse range of stakeholders. Familiarity with data governance and compliance principles. Quick learner who is passionate and willing to learn new languages and technologies. Experience in the Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC) framework and Agile project management methodologies. Knowledge of cloud platforms (e.g., AWS, Azure) is a plus. Fresh graduates with a keen interest in AI-assisted development and project management are welcome to apply. Excellent problem-solving skills and attention to detail. Self-motivated team player with a positive attitude, capable of adapting to changes. Ability to work under tight deadlines and manage fluid requirements. Closing Date The closing date of the advertisement is 6 August 2026 . We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Other Information NIE staff can take chartered buses at their own expense from or near their home to the NIE campus. This is subject to the availability of bus routes and seats. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Gesture-Sign-Linguistics--Computational-Linguistics-_R00025303": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Gesture—Sign Linguistics, Computational Linguistics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-23\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe are looking for a Research Fellow to support the Principal Investigator in advancing research on gesture, sign language, and computational linguistics. The role will focus on designing and conducting experiments, analysing gesture and sign language data, and collaborating with the PI and project partners on related publications and deliverables. Key Responsibilities: Design and conduct experiments on gesture and sign language; Annotate and analyse video/motion-capture data; Apply statistical methods to linguistic data Collaborate with the PI and partners on findings and publications; Supervise junior student assistants; Prepare reports and contribute to publications; Ensure compliance with ethical guidelines and project timelines. Job Requirements: PhD in Linguistics, Sign Language Studies, Cognitive Science, or a related field; Relevant experience in gesture studies, sign language research, or experimental linguistics; Proficiency in video/motion-capture annotation tools and statistical/computational analysis (e.g. R, Python, ELAN); Strong written and oral communication skills; Ability to work independently and collaboratively across disciplines. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Research-Fellow--AI-in-Mental-Health--LKCMedicine-_R00025294-1": {
      "title": "Senior Research Fellow AI in Mental Health LKCMedicine R00025294 1",
