    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--AI-in-Medicine_R00025293-1": {
      "title": "Research Fellow, AI in Medicine",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-23\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCentre of AI in Medicine is a university-level research centre with the mission to bridge the gap between cutting-edge Artificial Intelligence (AI) technologies and practical applications in healthcare, The key objective is to spearheadresearch and development to revolutionise patient care and inform public health policies. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/c-aim We are looking for a Postdoctoral Fellow to play a central role in galvanising and advancing the Centre’s efforts in research collaboration and grant applications. The Postdoctoral Fellow will provide critical leadership and support across C-AIM’s portfolio of AIML projects strategic planning, grant writing, review of research agreements, and ensuring the smooth operation of the Centre’s flagship projects. The role will focus on: Developing strategic plans to advance research capability of the Centre: Formulate and implement short-, medium-, and long-term research strategies that strengthen the Centre’s research capacity, competitiveness, and impact. Monitor research performance indicators and recommend initiatives to enhance research productivity, quality, and sustainability. Building and extending research collaboration efforts with key partners within a dynamic multidisciplinary environment Cultivate and strengthen strategic partnerships with academic institutions, healthcare organisations, industry partners, government agencies, and community stakeholders. Initiate, coordinate, and manage collaborative research projects that leverage expertise across multiple disciplines and sectors. Identify opportunities for national and international collaborations that enhance the Centre’s research profile and expand its research ecosystem. Designing and conducting research aligned with the Centre’s research pillars, including literature reviews, data collection, and data analysis. Lead the conceptualisation, design, and execution of research studies that align with the Centre’s strategic research themes and priorities. Conduct comprehensive literature reviews and environmental scans to identify evidence gaps, inform study design, and support the development of research proposals. Develop robust research methodologies, protocols, and data collection instruments using qualitative, quantitative, or mixed-methods approaches as appropriate. Oversee data collection activities, ensuring compliance with ethical, regulatory, and institutional requirements. Perform rigorous data management, statistical analysis, and interpretation of findings using appropriate analytical tools and methodologies. Prepare research reports, policy briefs, presentations, and manuscripts that effectively communicate findings to academic, professional, and stakeholder audiences. Advancing Centre’s performance in publications and grant applications Drive the development and submission of high-quality grant proposals to secure competitive research funding from local and international funding bodies. Identify funding opportunities and coordinate multidisciplinary teams in the preparation of grant applications, budgets, and supporting documentation. Lead and contribute to the publication of research findings in high-impact peer-reviewed journals and other scholarly outlets. Required educational qualification, experience, skills and competencies: PhD graduates, in medical AI, healthcare informatics, bioinformatics, computer science, AI implementation science, or related disciplines, Have graduated within four years from their respective PhD programs at the time of application. Received at least two years of graduate training (including the PhD duration) Demonstratable familiarity in ideally two or more of the following disciplines: biomedical informatics, clinical research, medicine, public health, implementation science and data science Excellent track record of research accomplishments Keen to embark on exciting and innovative projects involving the development of medical AI technologies, working with stakeholders in education and implementation, healthcare AI governance and regulation, and other topics pertaining to the successful deployment of AI into healthcare systems, especially in Singapore. Keen to embark on exciting and innovative projects in AI in Medicine Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Admissions--Projects-and-Electives--LKCMedicine-_R00025298": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Admissions, Projects and Electives [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-23\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. LKCMedicine is looking for a Senior Executive who is resourceful, thrives in complexity and works well in a team. Responsibilities: Scholarly Projects Provide secretariat support to the Scholarly Projects Committee. Administer the annual call for projects and coordinate the allocation of projects to students. Support the processing and approval of Scholarly Project results. Work closely with faculty members and project supervisors to ensure sufficient project offerings and smooth programme delivery. Policies, Procedures and Systems Maintain up-to-date knowledge of Scholarly Project policies, requirements, and processes. Drive the digitalisation and continuous improvement of work processes. Develop, review, and update Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) within the assigned portfolio. Ensure compliance with institutional policies and quality assurance requirements. Admissions and Overseas Electives Provide support for admissions activities, including the planning and administration of Multiple Mini Interviews (MMIs) and outreach initiatives. Support the administration of overseas elective programmes and related student processes. Assist with operational activities across the admissions and overseas electives portfolios. Administration Assist in LKCMedicine events as rostered, including examinations and School events Other department level administrative tasks Requirements: A recognised degree in any discipline Proficiency in statistics and Microsoft Office applications Strong aptitude and experience in IT and data management Resilient, meticulous and analytical Ability to multi-task and work independently under time pressure Excellent communication skills (written and verbal) We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Centre-Manager--Centre-for-AI-in-Medicine--C-AIM-_R00025297-1": {
      "title": "Centre Manager, Centre for AI in Medicine (C-AIM)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-22\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCentre for AI in Medicine (C-AIM) was established in 2023 as a multi-disciplinary team including clinicians, engineers, scientist, social scientist and educator focusing on AI research and education. This includes clinical studies, human-machine interaction as well as implementation science. It also aims to promote education and training of healthcare providers on the future of medical practice with AI. Reporting to the Centre Director, the Centre Manager shall support the daily administration and operations of the Centre. Responsibilities Support the governance of the Centre including organizing and staffing of Advisory Board meeting Manage Centre budget including research administration of funds and grants awarded to the Centre and preparation of annual budget requirements and reporting Support staffing and work closely with HR partners on research staff recruitment plans Facilitate the procurement process at the centre, working closely with NTU Procurement Facilitate research collaboration agreements including liaison and negotiation with collaborators. This includes working with NTU/LKCMedicine Principal Investigators, external parties and legal office to execute research-related agreements Coordinate meetings and working with internal and external collaborator parties to coordinate meetings for grant proposals and workshops Plan and organize symposiums and workshops led by the Centre Prepare publicity materials including brochures and website for the Centre, working closely with NTU Corporate Communications Facilitate and supporting visiting academics to the Centre including preparation of visit programmes, and arranging collaborative meetings Any other duties/ad-hoc projects as assigned Requirements Good honours degree in Computer Science and Engineering/ Biomedical/Social Sciences. A Masters degree is advantageous At least 5 years of relevant working experience in a university, healthcare or research institute environment at a managerial level Having project or programme management experience will be advantageous Good working knowledge of the Singapore research and healthcare landscape Proven experience and familiarity working across corporate functions such as Finance, Human Resource, Procurement and Research Administration in a university, healthcare or research institute setting Proficient in budgetary matters, well versed in communication skills  Proficient in Microsoft applications and standard office IT applications  Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Project-Officer--Climate-Transformation-Programme--CTP--_R00025287-1": {
      "title": "Project Officer (Climate Transformation Programme (CTP))",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-22\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Earth Observatory of Singapore (EOS) at Nanyang Technological University in Singapore invites applications for the position of Project Officer to support the Climate Transformation Program (CTP). The CTP is an interdisciplinary research program with the mission to develop, inspire and accelerate knowledge-based solutions and educate future leaders to establish the stable climate and environment necessary for resilient, just and sustainable SEA societies. The incumbent will provide comprehensive administrative, financial, and operational support for research programmes and projects, with a strong focus on ensuring compliance with funding agency and University policies governing grant management and fund utilization. This includes but not limited to tracking of grant-related documentation and handling of procurement and logistics needs. The role will also contribute to various type of report preparation, project management and  research-related activities to support the successful delivery of project objectives. Key Responsibilities: Provide support for the day-to-day management of research projects, including finance, procurement, and project coordination. Process procurement transactions (Purchase Requisitions, Purchase Orders, Goods Receipts), reimbursement claims, and financial documentation in accordance with University and funding agency policies. Monitor project budgets and expenditures, maintain accurate financial records, and support budget tracking and reporting. Coordinate project meetings, workshops, seminars, travel arrangements, and other programme activities, including logistical support for local and overseas collaborators. Liaise with Principal Investigators (PIs), researchers, funding agencies, NTU Shared Services, and other internal and external stakeholders to facilitate the smooth implementation of research projects. Monitor project progress, maintain project records and databases, and track key deliverables, milestones, and performance indicators. Prepare and compile progress reports, financial reports, and supporting documentation for funding agencies, audits, and management reporting. Ensure compliance with University policies, funding agency requirements, and governance procedures, while providing general support to research teams. Perform other project-related and ad hoc administrative duties as assigned. Job Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in Project Management, Science, Finance or a related discipline, with at least 3 years of relevant working experience in project administration, finance or grant management. A strong finance background is preferred. Demonstrated ability to work independently and collaboratively in a multi-cultural team environment. Excellent interpersonal, planning and coordination skills Excellent written and verbal communication skills, able to interact professionally with stakeholders at all levels Excellent organizational, analytical and problem-solving skills with the ability to multitask and prioritize tasks in a fast-paced environment. Experience in managing government-funded research grants and familiarity with Singapore’s research grant management guidelines will be an advantage. Interested applicants should submit a CV, and a statement of interest. Incomplete applications will not be considered. NTU seek a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Electrical-and-Electronic-Engineering--Computer-Science-_R00025276": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Electrical and Electronic Engineering/ Computer Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-22\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research.  With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 1,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 10th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2024 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee We are looking for a talented and responsible researcher to support the scientific research and the engineering practice in perception and embodied intelligence. Key Responsibilities: The Research Associate will work on a project to conduct research on development general robotic manipulation system used in household service and manufacturing. The roles of this position include: Develop robotic foundation models with online reinforcement learning for general manipulation based on vision-language-action models Develop efficient data sampling policy for reinforcement learning reduce the data demand for policy learning Develop a mobile bimanual manipulation system to complete diverse tasks in household environment and in manufacturing deployment scenarios Job Requirements Master in Electrical and Electronic Engineering, Computer Science or related field 1-year research experience in related area Expertise in robotic manipulation systems Knowledge in robotic foundation models  Publication track record is an advantage Proficiency in basics of programming languages such as ROS and Python Excellent communication skills, written and verbal – able to communicate complex concepts clearly and accurately We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.  Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Electrical-and-Electronic-Engineering--Computer-Science-_R00025277": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Electrical and Electronic Engineering/ Computer Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-22\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research.  With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 1,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 10th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2024 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee We are looking for a talented and responsible researcher to support the scientific research and the engineering practice in perception and embodied intelligence. Key Responsibilities: The Research Associate will work on a project to conduct research on development of mobile and bimanual robotic manipulation system used in household service and manufacturing. The roles of this position include: Develop robotic foundation models for general mobile manipulation based on vision-language-action models Develop efficient manipulation learning framework from human instructional videos and reduce the data demand for policy learning Develop a mobile bimanual manipulation system to complete diverse tasks in household environment and in manufacturing deployment scenarios Job Requirement Master in Electrical and Electronic Engineering, Computer Science or related field 1-year research experience in related area Expertise in robotic manipulation systems Knowledge in robotic foundation models  Publication track record is an advantage Proficiency in basics of programming languages such as ROS and Python Excellent communication skills, written and verbal – able to communicate complex concepts clearly and accurately We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.  Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Electronic-Engineering--Computer-Science--Mechanical-Engineering--_R00025278": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Electronic Engineering/ Computer Science/ Mechanical Engineering )",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-22\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research.  With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 1,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 10th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2024 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee We are looking for a talented and responsible researcher to support the scientific research and the engineering practice in perception and embodied intelligence. Key Responsibilities: The Research Fellow will work on a project to conduct research on learning from human demonstrations for robot manipulation used in household service and manufacturing. The roles of this position include: Develop robotic foundation models for general manipulation based on vision-language-action models Develop learning from human demonstration (LfD) framework for vision-language-action models Develop multi-embodiment retargeting framework with safety constraints Develop a mobile bimanual manipulation system to complete diverse tasks in household environment and in manufacturing deployment scenarios Job Requirement PhD in Electronic Engineering, Computer Science, Mechanical Engineering or related field 3-year research experience in related area Expertise in robotic manipulation systems Knowledge in robotic foundation models  Publication track record is an advantage Proficiency in basics of programming languages such as ROS and Python Excellent communication skills, written and verbal – able to communicate complex concepts clearly and accurately We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be informed. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Neural-Tissue-Engineering-_R00023073": {
      "title": "Research Associate (In Vivo Neural Tissue Engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-22\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe invite applications for a Research Associate to join an interdisciplinary research team led by Dr. Sing Yian Chew (NTU) and Prof. Shawn Je (Duke-NUS). The successful candidate will contribute to an ongoing research program focused on neural tissue engineering,  in vivo spinal cord injury (SCI) models, and regenerative biomaterials. The project aims to assess innovative cell transplantation strategies and tissue-engineered scaffolds for promoting  in vivo neural tissue regeneration. The candidate will assist rat SCI microsurgery, carry out behavioural assessments and advanced tracing, as well as imaging approaches to study scaffold-cell-tissue interactions. The focus of this project is to evaluate cell transplantation and tissue engineered scaffolds for in vivo neural tissue regeneration. We are seeking an individual who is experienced in working with rodents and interested in assisting in animal implantation studies, as well as carrying out behavioural tests; and characterizing/evaluating scaffold-cell/tissue interactions through immunofluorescent and histochemical staining and imaging. The candidate will be jointly supervised by Prof. Sing Yian CHEW and Prof. Shawn JE. This position offers a unique opportunity to apply in vivo experimentation skills to neural tissue engineering, through strong collaborative efforts with scientists and engineers across different local and overseas institutions (SMART/MIT, University of Osaka, Nagoya University, NUS). Key responsibilities: Conduct and assist in vivo experiments using rat SCI models Assist in microsurgical procedures, cell/scaffold implantation, and conduct animal behavioral evaluations Carry out tract tracing, immunofluorescent and histochemical staining and confocal imaging Assist in data analysis, interpretation of experimental outcomes, and preparation of manuscripts for publication Supervise and train junior researchers and contribute to laboratory management Participate in multidisciplinary collaborations within and beyond NTU Job Requirements: Master’s in biomedical engineering, Neuroscience, or a related discipline Demonstrated expertise in handling rodents and carrying out behavioral tests. Demonstrated expertise in animal surgery, preferably SCI microsurgery in rodents is a plus Hands-on experience with tract tracing, tissue sectioning, immunofluorescence, histology, and confocal microscopy Experience with western blotting and qRT-PCR is advantageous Strong written and oral communication skills Highly motivated, well-organized, and capable of independent work and teamwork We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Postgraduate---Continuing-Education-Programmes--LKCMedicine-_R00025273": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Postgraduate & Continuing Education Programmes [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-22\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. LKCMedicine is seeking a detail-oriented and organised Senior Executive to join the Graduate Programmes team. The successful candidate will provide essential administrative support for our CET programmes, ensuring smooth operations, seamless digital course delivery, and a positive learner experience. The Senior Executive will be a primary point of contact for learners and adjunct faculty, ensuring a smooth and positive experience for all stakeholders. This role is central to the successful delivery of our programmes, involving the coordination of programme logistics, management of learner support, and assistance with financial administration. Responsibilities: Programme Administration & Logistics Coordinate the end-to-end logistics for all CET programmes, including scheduling, booking of venues or virtual platforms, and managing catering. Provide administrative support to Course Directors, including scheduling programme meetings, preparing minutes, and assisting with programme reviews. Manage digital dissemination of course content; set up courses on the Learning Management System (LMS) and ensure all online learning materials are current and accessible. Provide on-site or online administrative support during programme sessions to assist faculty and learners, and to manage attendance. Administer pre and post-programme activities, including the collection of feedback, collation of results, and generation of reports. Learner & Stakeholder Support Serve as the primary front-line support for CET programmes, handling all enquiries from prospective learners, current participants, and the public via email and phone. Manage the full learner registration and enrolment process, from application processing and matriculation to fee collection and issuance of confirmations. Maintain accurate learner records and manage the issuance of course certificates, transcripts, and other relevant documentation. Liaise with adjunct faculty and instructors to coordinate schedules, gather teaching materials, and process administrative and payment-related requests. Finance & Administrative Support Assist the Manager with financial administration for the CET portfolio. Coordinate with the Office of Faculty Affairs to facilitate the appointment, renewal, and onboarding of trainers and adjunct faculty. Process procurement requests, including raising purchase orders and ensuring compliance with university procurement policies. Handle the processing of invoices and claims for payment from external vendors, part-time lecturers, and adjunct faculty. Perform data entry and maintain accurate records for programme finance and learner enrolment. Requirements: A recognised diploma in any discipline. A degree in Business, Communications, or a related field is an advantage. Minimum 2–3 years of hands-on experience in an administrative, operational, or customer service role. Excellent organisational and multitasking skills, with a proven ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines. Meticulous with a keen eye for detail, particularly in record-keeping and processing information. Strong interpersonal and communication (both written and verbal) skills, with a customer-centric mindset. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook). A proactive and collaborative team player who is also able to work independently. This is a 3 years contract appointment. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
