    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Advanced-power-electronics-and-energy-systems-_R00025268": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Advanced power electronics and energy systems)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-21\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research. With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 2,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 4th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2025 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee We are looking for a Research Fellow to support research and development activities in advanced power electronics and energy systems. The role involves the design, development, control, and experimental validation of high-efficiency power electronic converters, including solid-state transformers and advanced power-delivery architectures for data centres. The technologies developed may also support renewable energy integration, energy storage, DC distribution, and smart-grid applications. The Research Fellow will contribute to project execution, research proposal preparation, industry collaboration, and the dissemination of research outcomes through technical reports, publications, and presentations. Key Responsibilities: Conduct research and development in power electronic converters, solid-state transformers, data-centre power-delivery systems, converter control, and energy systems. Design, model, simulate, and develop advanced power electronic converter topologies and associated control algorithms. Investigate high-efficiency and high-power-density power-conversion architectures for data-centre power delivery, DC distribution, renewable energy integration, energy storage, and grid-connected applications. Support the development of solid-state transformer technologies, including converter topology design, control, protection, system integration, and performance evaluation. Design and build laboratory-scale power converter prototypes, control platforms, and associated hardware systems. Perform experimental testing, data acquisition, data analysis, and evaluation of system efficiency, power density, reliability, and dynamic performance. Develop simulation and system-level models using tools such as MATLAB/Simulink, PLECS, PSCAD, or equivalent software. Support the integration and testing of power electronic converters, magnetic components, sensors, control systems, and laboratory hardware. Contribute to research proposal preparation, including literature reviews, technical writing, development of research concepts, and preparation of work plans. Prepare technical reports, project documentation, research publications, and conference presentations. Collaborate with faculty members, research staff, graduate students, external collaborators, and industry partners. Support the supervision and technical guidance of graduate students, undergraduate students, and research assistants when required. Ensure compliance with laboratory safety procedures and support the proper operation and maintenance of laboratory equipment. Job Requirements PhD degree in Electrical Engineering, Power Electronics, Power Engineering, or a closely related field. Strong background in power electronic converter design, modelling, modulation, and control. Knowledge or experience in one or more of the following areas is preferred: Solid-state transformers; Data-centre power-delivery architectures; High-frequency and high-power-density power conversion; DC distribution systems; Wide-bandgap semiconductor-based converters; Renewable energy and energy storage systems. Experience with simulation tools such as MATLAB/Simulink, PLECS, PSCAD, or equivalent software. Experience in power converter hardware design, prototyping, control implementation, laboratory testing, and experimental validation is preferred. Familiarity with digital control platforms, power semiconductor devices, magnetic components, protection systems, or thermal management would be advantageous. A good research publication record in power electronics or a related area is preferred. Prior experience in research proposal writing, technical grant preparation, or industry-funded research projects would be advantageous. Competencies Strong analytical, technical, and problem-solving capabilities. Ability to independently develop and execute research activities. Ability to work effectively within a multidisciplinary research team and collaborate with academic and industry partners. Good technical writing, presentation, and communication skills. Ability to manage multiple research activities, project deliverables, and deadlines. Strong interest in high-efficiency power conversion, solid-state transformers, data-centre power delivery, and sustainable energy technologies. Commitment to high-quality research, experimental rigour, and laboratory safety. We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Embodied-AI-_R00025271": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Embodied AI)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-21\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering (MAE) is a robust, dynamic and multi-disciplinary international research community comprising of world-class scientists and bright students. MAE prides itself in its excellent research capabilities in areas including advanced manufacturing, aerospace, biomedical, energy, industrial engineering, maritime engineering, robotics, etc. The school is equipped with state-of-the-art research infrastructure, housing a comprehensive range of cluster laboratories, test bedding facilities, research centres/institutes and corporate laboratories. Cutting-edge research in MAE addresses the immediate needs of our industries and supports the nation’s long-term development strategies. In the new era of industrial 4.0 and sustainable living, MAE is rigorous in developing new competencies to support the growth and competitiveness of our engineering sector in the global landscape. MAE has grown to be leader in Engineering Research, ranking amongst the top engineering schools in the world. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/mae/research . Our team is seeking a highly motivated Research Fellow to contribute to cutting-edge research in embodied AI and robotic manipulation. This role will support our mission to advance AI-driven robotic systems for real-world applications, including human-robot interaction, robotic perception, and intelligent control. The successful candidate will assist in developing novel algorithms and integrating them into robotic platforms, helping to push the boundaries of embodied intelligence in both research and practical deployment. Key Responsibilities: Develop and implement perception and control algorithms for robotic arms and embodied AI systems. Assist in integrating multimodal AI models (vision, language, force sensors) with robotic systems. Conduct experiments in both simulated and real-world environments, testing AI-driven robotic behavior. Work with hardware platforms, including robotic manipulators and mobile robots. Support the preparation of research publications, reports, and presentations. Collaborate with faculty, postdocs, and industry partners on AI and robotics research projects. Assist in the maintenance and operation of research lab equipment and robotic systems. Job Requirements: PhD degree with at least 3 first-author papers in Computer Science, Robotics, Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or a related field. Experience in robotic perception, control, or learning-based methods. Proficiency in Python and C++ for AI and robotics applications. Familiarity with robotic middleware (e.g., ROS, MoveIt) and hardware integration. Knowledge of machine learning, reinforcement learning, or vision-language models for robotics is a plus. Hands-on experience with robotic arms (e.g., UR5, Franka Emika, or similar) is desirable. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate-Research-Fellow--Plant-Biology-and-Molecular-Biology-_R00023891-1": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Plant Biology and Molecular Biology)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-21\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Chemistry, Chemical Engineering and Biotechnology (CCEB) at NTU Singapore, in collaboration with Wageningen University & Research (WUR), is part of Singapore Indoor Farming System (SingFarm)—a CREATE-NRF programme focused on building a sustainable, data-driven food production model with strong industry relevance to contribute Singapore’s ambition in achieving 20 per cent local production of its fiber (vegetables, mushrooms etc.) by 2035. The candidate would be working in a multinational team at the forefront of Singapore’s agricultural innovation and food security. The position of Research Associate/Research Fellow will focus investigating the metabolic basis of agronomic and nutritional traits in Brassica crops through advanced metabolomics and multi-omics integration. The candidate will apply high-resolution metabolic profiling and data-driven approaches to uncover phytochemical diversity, identify metabolite–gene associations, and elucidate pathways underlying traits such as disease resistance, quality, and nutritional value. The role will contribute to linking metabolite composition with genetic variation and gene expression, enabling the discovery of key regulatory mechanisms and supporting targeted metabolic engineering strategies to enhance crop performance and nutritional quality. Key Responsibilities:  Perform metabolite profiling of segregating plant populations to identify compounds associated with traits such as disease resistance, quality, and shelf life Integrate metabolomic and genetic datasets to uncover metabolite–gene relationships Identify candidate metabolic pathways and underlying genes associated with target traits Conduct functional characterization and validation of candidate genes to elucidate their biological roles Research Associate (Master’s level) Master’s degree in Plant Biology, Biotechnology, Molecular Biology, Genetics, or a related field Strong biochemistry and plant genetics background Experience with plant molecular biology techniques Strong analytical skills and ability to work independently and as part of a team Independent and proactive working attitude Open and clear communication Research Fellow (PhD level) PhD degree in Plant Biotechnology, Molecular Genetics, Plant Physiology, or a closely related discipline Demonstrated experience with biochemistry, plant genetics and plant molecular biology techniques Strong analytical skills and ability to work independently and as part of a team Independent and proactive working attitude Open and clear communication Proven ability to lead experiments, analyze data, and publish research We seek a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive-Assistant-Manager--Content-Development---Writer--Science-Engineering-Tech-_R00025266": {
      "title": "Senior Executive/Assistant Manager, Content Development & Writer (Science/Engineering/Tech)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-21\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThis role supports the College of Engineering’s communications function through development of research-based content and supporting the coordination and administrative processes required for content delivery. Working closely with the Head of Communications, the role contributes to translating scientific and engineering concepts into accessible content, while supporting content pipelines, stakeholder coordination, and operational tasks across multiple schools. The position complements digital and design functions by supporting content development, organisation, and workflow management to enable consistent and timely communications outputs. Key Responsibilities: Scientific Content Development, Research Translation, & Writing Pitch, research, write, and edit technical stories, features, and profiles on faculty, students, research projects, and publications Conduct interviews with researchers and translate complex scientific concepts into clear, structured narratives Ensure scientific accuracy, clarity, and alignment with editorial standards Provide scientific, research and academic insight for team members and copy/content reviews as assigned Content Pipeline & Stakeholder Engagement Assist in the development of content pipeline system and campaigns Proactively identify and track potential content opportunities Maintain and update a centralised content pipeline tracker (stories in progress, upcoming opportunities, deadlines) Follow up with stakeholders to gather inputs, materials, and approvals Stakeholder Coordination & Administrative Support Coordinate interviews with faculty and researchers (scheduling, preparation, follow-ups) Manage communication with stakeholders to collect drafts, images, and approvals Support organisation of meetings, editorial calendars, and content planning sessions Publication Support Support preparation of content for website, newsletter, and publications Assist with proofreading, fact-checking, and editorial refinement Contribute to development of longer-form outputs (e.g. Annual Magazine, features) Ad Hoc Duties May Include: Communications calendar and scheduling support, including coordination of timelines, deadlines, and content planning Content intake and documentation, ensuring materials received from stakeholders are complete, organised, and ready for use Preparation of analytics inputs and basic reporting, including data gathering from digital platforms Assist in website maintenance and update General, digital and design function support as needed IDEAL PROFILE A background in science, engineering, or research combined with a strong interest in science communication or journalism; OR a background in science communication or journalism with a strong interest in science, engineering, or research; OR a combined background in both areas Ability to understand and interpret technical material Strong writing skills with attention to clarity and accuracy Understanding of what makes a good narrative Charismatic and comfortable engaging with academic stakeholders Organised and detail-oriented, with ability to manage multiple inputs We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Prof-Assoc-Prof-of-Ageing-Research--LKCMedicine-_R00024337-2": {
      "title": "Professor/Associate Professor of Geroscience [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-21\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nACADEMIC FACULTY APPOINTMENT:  The Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine A Professor/Associate Professor of Geroscience at Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine is expected to contribute to the development of research and teaching at the School. He/she is expected to undertake high quality internationally leading research, in line with the overarching research strategy of Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine, in addition to any other duties as assigned by the Vice Dean, Research and Dean. Job Purpose: The appointee will be expected to undertake high quality research in the broad area of ageing research, in line with the research strategy of the School and in conjunction with other recent appointments, obtain research funding and supervise research staff and students. The appointee is expected to undertake teaching and educational responsibilities for the training of medical students and postgraduate research students. Teaching methods will include extensive use of team-based learning and e-learning. The appointee is expected to contribute to integration of science relating to the broad area of ageing research into the MBBS curriculum and to ensure the delivery of excellence in these areas, including the team-based delivery of the curriculum. Key Responsibilities: Undertake high quality research activities by sustaining a personal research plan, developing innovative research proposals and funding bids, managing and undertaking research activities, publishing in international peer reviewed journals, reviewing manuscripts and grant applications when appropriate. Seek competitive grant and collaborative industry funding to develop a sustainable research programme. Contribute to, support and develop teaching and educational activity at undergraduate level and supervise undergraduate and graduate students. Develop and support research projects (including interdisciplinary research) with other faculty in the field of ageing research at LKCMedicine and across the wider NTU community, as well as with relevant clinical partners. These may include research that pertains to all health aspects relating to ageing, including, but not limited to, cognitive dysfunction, neurodegeneration, metabolic disorders, cancer, inflammation, and innovative therapeutic interventions. Supervise and mentor junior faculty members and research staff at LKCMedicine. Participate in academic committees and meet other administrative requirements as appropriate. Job descriptions cannot be exhaustive, and the appointee may be required to undertake other duties which are broadly in line with the above key responsibilities as assigned by the Vice Dean, Research and Dean. Person Specification Qualifications, Knowledge and Experience: MBBS/MD and/or PhD degree(s) Relevant postdoctoral or clinical experience Significant experience and outstanding record of translational clinical research and teaching with a high level of scientific achievement, productivity and impact in the field of ageing research or related fields Management and Teamwork: Ability to lead and work as part of a multidisciplinary team Ability to work co-operatively with medical and non-medical staff Ability to supervise research staff and students Communicating and Influencing: Ability to communicate effectively with staff and students Ability to motivate others Strong presentation skills Ability to work in a team Desirable attributes: Experience and desire to participate in undergraduate and postgraduate medical education and training. Demonstrated ability to develop teams and to create networks. Fully conversant with patient-centred approach to modern medicine and the use of new technologies in both education and patient care. Understanding of the academic and administrative needs of internationally recognised universities. Ability to work in and develop teams and to create networks at both a national and international level. Track record of having supervised graduate students to successful completion of PhDs. Time Commitment The level of effort for this appointment is at 1.0 full time equivalent (FTE) employment. The closing date for applications is 24 September 2026. Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
