    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager---Research-Achievements--Impact-and-Strategic-Enhancement--LKCMedicine-_R00025256": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager,  Research Achievements, Impact and Strategic Enhancement [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-21\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. The Research Achievements, Impact and Strategic Enhancement (RAISE) Office is established to develop strategies to enhance the research impact, visibility, and reputation of the school institutionally, nationally and internationally. It sits within the ambit of the LKCMedicine Research Administration and Support Services Department under the Vice Dean of Research Office. Reporting to the Head of RAISE, you will be part of a dynamic team at the vanguard of highlighting and reporting on the school’s research impact and achievements. You will also work with other departments including the School Faculty, Finance, Office of Innovation and Enterprise (OIE) and Office of Patient Engagement (OPEN). Responsibilities: Research Impact metrics, Data Analytics & AI Automation Evaluate and leverage platforms such as Altmetrics to capture non-traditional research impact metrics, including policy influence, societal engagement, and economic contributions etc Establish systematic frameworks to monitor, analyse, and report research impact metrics, incorporating AI-enabled analytics to identify trends, correlations, and emerging impact signals Compute and deliver reports on grant income of the School, incorporating automations to derive reporting needs such as breakdown of annualised grant quantum, update of grant end date etc  Perform multi-level data analyses related to research grants, including external grant return ratios at the school, programme, and individual faculty levels Design and implement AI-driven automation solutions (e.g., scripting, machine learning models, or workflow automation tools) to streamline data extraction, integration, validation, and reporting processes, reducing manual effort and enhancing scalability Consolidate, clean, and harmonise data from various sources (e.g., internal databases, research systems) to ensure consistency and reliability across datasets Develop and maintain interactive dashboards and data visualisations (e.g., using Power BI, Tableau, Programming or similar tools) to support research performance monitoring  Collaborate with internal stakeholders (e.g., IT, research systems teams) to strengthen data infrastructure, integrate AI-enabled tools, and develop solutions for real-time tracking of research impact and performance  Track and analyse research-related metrics that contribute to university rankings, and identify opportunities to strengthen the school’s research performance and ranking outcomes Research Communications & Visibility Build and maintain strong working relationships with faculty members to identify and track high-impact research publications for dissemination across appropriate publicity platforms, including the school website, social media channels, press releases, magazines, and other communication channels Organise and support events and activities that enhance the school’s research impact, reputation, and visibility Work closely with the Communications and Outreach Department to profile and publicise the achievements of research faculty Collaborate with programme and centre directors to coordinate and deliver the school’s annual publication on research impact and achievements Management Reporting Track, collate and synthesize updates from faculty and the wider research community, including media coverage, publication highlights, awards, and other key milestones Assist the team in preparing the Dean’s Management Report (quarterly), reporting to Governing Board and Board of Trustees, ensuring data accuracy and consistency Organise and support internal team and research programme meetings, including scheduling, preparing agendas, documenting minutes, and following up on action items Undertake ad-hoc tasks where required Requirements: Any Bachelor Degree / Diploma Some background or experience in data analytics / academic / healthcare industry / research communications would be preferred. More than 5 years of experience in data analytics, designing infographics, creating professional and attractive powerpoint slides for management.   Proficient in Microsoft Office especially MS Excel, MS Powerpoint Meticulous and good at designing dashboards, data visualizations, infographics Self-starter and ability to explore and evaluate new impact metrics with minimal supervision Demonstrated ability to build and maintain relationships with diverse stakeholders Positive attitude, able to multi-task, and work under pressure and tight deadlines Resourceful, strong analytical and problem-solving skills and ability to develop new ideas and provide conceptual solutions Added advantage if candidate has some knowledge in Programming, R, Python, RPA or related languages We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Wallenberg-NTU-Presidential-Postdoctoral-Fellow_R00025261": {
      "title": "Wallenberg-NTU Presidential Postdoctoral Fellow",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-20\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nYoung and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is ranked among the world’s top universities. NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science (CCDS) is a leading college that is known for its excellent curriculum, outstanding and impactful research, and world-renowned faculty. A hot bed of cutting-edge technology and groundbreaking research, the College aims to groom the next generation of leaders, thinkers, and innovators to thrive in the digital age. Located in the heart of Asia, NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science is an ‘exciting place to learn and grow'. We welcome you to join our community of faculty, students and alumni who are shaping the future of AI, Data Science and Computing. We are seeking a research fellow to join a university-level research centre. The position is for one year, renewable subject to satisfactory performance. Successful candidates will conduct research and develop multimodal models. Candidates are expected to have a strong background in relevant areas. Key Responsibilities: To independently undertake research in computer vision and machine learning. To produce research reports and/or publications as required by the funding body or for dissemination to the wider academic community. To provide guidance and support to any students associated with the project. To attend, contribute, and where necessary lead relevant meetings. To undertake any other duties relevant to the programme of research. Job Requirements: PhD degree or at least 8 years working experience in Computer Engineering, Computer Science, Electronics Engineering or equivalent. Strong background in machine learning and computer vision. Prior experience in 3D vision is preferable. Strong publication records in top-tier machine learning or computer vision conferences/journals, such as TPAMI, IJCV, CVPR, ICCV, ECCV, NeurIPS, ICML and ICLR. Knowledge of scientific or engineering software like PyTorch, TensorFlow, Keras, etc. Proven research ability as evidenced through a portfolio of publications and/or conference papers and/or patents. Strong background in R&D with self-motivation and initiative. Ability to develop and manage R&D projects with good understanding of industrial needs. In-depth knowledge relevant to the project domain. Demonstrated capability to conduct innovative research. The ability and willingness to adapt and incorporate novel ideas and approaches in scientific industry. Demonstrated ability to formulate hypothesis and design effective experimental plans. Ability to design and implement new experimental methods. High-level expertise in the required experiment or modelling methods. Good knowledge in laboratory work as well as engineering of prototype system. Assist in postgraduate student supervision. Capacity to conduct small group teaching such as undergrad labs and tutorials. Ability to initiate collaboration research in multidisciplinary team. Oversee and report project progress. Ability and willingness to work some flexible hours.                                                                 We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Director--Partnership-and-Global-Education-Development_R00025260": {
      "title": "Assistant Director Partnership and Global Education Development",
