analysis of video data. Apply data-driven dynamical system modeling tools using specialized software packages to elucidate neural computations involved in emotion. Assist in maintaining specialized software repositories created by the lab. Prepare and contribute to grant applications and conference presentations. The candidate is also expected to write and draft research publications in top neuroscience and AI journals.  Attend a weekly lab meeting and journal club and present data and/or papers as necessary. Key Competencies and Requirements: Bachelor’s degree (for Research Assistant) and Master’s degree (for Research Associate) in computer science, neuroscience, computational biology, psychology, life science or relevant fields. We also invite candidates with interdisciplinary backgrounds to apply. Strong programming skills in Python and Matlab. Familiarity with analyzing large-scale neural data (such as imaging datasets, electrophysiology datasets or video data) is highly desirable. Proficiency in popular deep learning, computer vision and/or user-interface software frameworks (such as Pytorch, TensorFlow, OpenCV, PyQt, Gradio etc). The candidate is expected is have a strong numeric and analytical background. Competent in information visualization. A working knowledge of Adobe Illustrator is a strong advantage . Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a multidisciplinary environment. Entry level candidates are welcome to apply We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: LKC"
