    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Quantum-Photonics-_R00025225": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Quantum Photonics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-16\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research. With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 2,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 4th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2025 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee We are looking for a research fellow to carry out the research project and be responsible for administrative and logistical upkeep pertaining to laboratory operations. The project is for product design and engineering for quantum photonics. Experience in Quantum photonics is preferred. Key Responsibilities: Conduct research activities related to product design and engineering for quantum technologies. Apply optics and electronics design knowledge in the development and optimization of quantum technology and quantum photonics systems. Job Requirements: PhD in Electrical Engineering or Quantum Engineering. Familiarity with quantum technologies Good written and oral communication skills Highly motivated in multidisciplinary research Proven experience in product design, project leading and optics alignment. We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Engineer-II--Computer-Science---Cyber-Security---Artificial-Intelligence-_R00025211": {
      "title": "Research Engineer II (Computer Science / Cyber Security / Artificial Intelligence)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-16\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Alibaba-NTU Global e-Sustainability CorpLab (ANGEL) represents a key collaboration between Alibaba Group and Nanyang Technological University (NTU). Supported by the Singapore RIE2025 Fund, ANGEL creates and deploys impactful green digital technologies for global sustainability. ANGEL’s mission aligns seamlessly with Singapore’s national objectives, such as the Singapore Green Plan 2030 and the Singapore Smart Nation Initiative. ANGEL’s work in developing sustainable and equitable digital solutions and promoting a sustainable and green lifestyle will contribute to a smaller carbon footprint. Its holistic approach will help to secure a brighter, more sustainable future for humanity.  ANGEL will also cultivate human talents equipped with both advanced technical skills and a solid understanding of sustainable practices. They will enable Singapore to realise its environmental and technological ambitions. We are seeking to appoint a Research Engineer II who will contribute to NTU’s mission of advancing trustworthy AI and cyber security research, with a particular focus on the safety and access control of autonomous LLM agents. The Research Associate will conduct research on environment-aware, task-oriented access control for computer-use (“Claw-like”) agents, designing and implementing mechanisms for structured context profiling, least-privilege policy generation, and runtime adjudication of agent actions. The role will contribute to NTU’s strategic initiatives in building secure, reliable, and resilient AI agent ecosystems, while supporting collaborations across academia and industry under the guidance of senior researchers. Key responsibilities: Conduct research on environment-aware, task-oriented access control for computer-use (“Claw-like”) agents, including context profiling and least-privilege policy generation. Design and implement a Profile-and-Policy Agent that constructs structured authorization context and generates task-oriented least-privilege permissions. Develop and evaluate a Runtime Guard Agent that reviews agent tool calls during execution and applies adaptive controls such as masking, logging, and approval. Implement and experiment with optimization methods (e.g., reinforcement learning) to improve profiling and policy generation. Construct attack payloads and benchmarks (e.g., OpenClaw scenarios, WildClawBench) and benchmark against representative baselines. Contribute to manuscript drafts for top-tier (CCF-A) venues and support proposal and grant documentation. Requirements: A Master's degree in Computer Science, Cyber Security, Artificial Intelligence, or a related discipline. Research or applied experience in AI/LLM agent safety, access control, system security, or trustworthy machine learning through coursework, projects, internships, or research. Familiarity with LLM-based and computer-use (“Claw-like”) agents, tool use, and multi-step reasoning. Knowledge of access-control concepts, least-privilege design, and runtime policy enforcement; RL experience is an advantage. Hands-on experience in fine-tuning large language models (e.g., supervised fine-tuning, reinforcement learning, or parameter-efficient methods such as LoRA) using frameworks such as PyTorch. Proficiency in programming languages such as Python, C/C++, and Java. Ability to contribute to academic writing and research outputs for international top-tier (CCF-A) conferences. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Climate-Risk-Assessment-and-Climate-Change-_R00025219": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Climate Risk Assessment and Climate Change)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-16\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nIn this rapidly changing world, the Centre for Climate Change and Environmental Health (CCEH) is advancing research on how climate change, hydroclimate variability, and extreme environmental conditions affect human health, infrastructure, ecosystems, and society. By bringing together expertise across climate science, hydroclimate analysis, environmental science, exposure assessment, public health, artificial intelligence, and predictive modelling, CCEH develops evidence-based solutions to support climate risk assessment, disaster preparedness, adaptation planning, and more climate-resilient communities in Singapore and across Asia. Within CCEH, the Climate and AI team, led by Prof. Steve Yim, focuses on climate change, hydroclimate variability, extreme weather events, environmental hazards, and their implications for climate risk assessment and societal resilience. The team uses integrated observations, reanalysis datasets, climate model simulations, artificial intelligence, and statistical approaches across multiple spatial and temporal scales to improve the prediction and assessment of climate-sensitive risks. Its research generates scientific evidence to support early warning, disaster preparedness, risk-informed decision-making, and climate adaptation strategies. Key Responsibilities : The position will support research on hydroclimate variability and change, with a particular focus on Asian monsoon dynamics, hydroclimatic extremes, climate risk assessment, and early warning systems. The role will contribute to research on the understanding, prediction, and risk assessment of heavy precipitation, drought, flooding, monsoon variability, compound extreme events, and other climate-sensitive hazards across Singapore, Southeast Asia, and the wider Asian region. The successful candidate will analyse and integrate climate, hydrological, environmental, health, and socioeconomic datasets using statistical, spatiotemporal, climate diagnostic, and artificial intelligence methods; develop and evaluate predictive models, high-resolution risk assessment frameworks, climate scenario analyses, and early warning tools; contribute to research publications, technical reports, and decision-support outputs; and collaborate with academic, government, and stakeholder partners to strengthen disaster preparedness, climate adaptation, resilience planning, and evidence-based decision-making. Job Requirements : Have a Ph.D. degree in atmospheric science, climate science, hydroclimate science, hydrology, environmental science, geography, data science, artificial intelligence, computer science, or another related discipline. Have strong research experience in hydroclimate variability, Asian monsoon dynamics, climate extremes, climate risk assessment, climate change impacts, environmental modelling, early warning systems, artificial intelligence, machine learning, or related fields. Have strong programming and computational skills in Python, R, MATLAB, or related analytical and machine learning frameworks, such as PyTorch, TensorFlow, or Scikit-learn. Have experience in analysing large-scale climate, hydrological, environmental, reanalysis, remote sensing, climate model, or socioeconomic datasets. Have good organisational and communication skills, with evidence of the ability to work independently and collaboratively across interdisciplinary and multi-institutional teams. Have the ability to contribute to peer-reviewed publications, technical reports, and other research outputs. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Spatial-Environmental-Health-and-AI-based-Exposure-Modelling-_R00025217-1": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Spatial Environmental Health and AI-based Exposure Modelling)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-16\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nIn this rapidly changing world, the Centre for Climate Change and Environmental Health (CCEH) is advancing research on how climate change, air pollution, and extreme environmental conditions affect human health. By bringing together expertise across environmental science, exposure assessment, epidemiology, and public health, CCEH develops evidence-based solutions to support healthier and more climate-resilient communities in Singapore and across Asia. Within CCEH, the Environmental Health team, led by Prof. Steve Yim, investigates the interactions between climate, air quality, and human health using integrated measurement, modelling, and statistical approaches. The team works across multiple spatial scales to understand how environmental exposures affect human health and to generate scientific evidence for public health policy and workforce protection strategies. Key Responsibilities : The position will support research on environmental exposure assessment and its implications for human health, with a focus on climate- and environment-related risks such as heat, air pollution, temperature variability, and urban environmental factors. The role will contribute to the collection, integration, analysis, and interpretation of climate, environmental, land-use, remote sensing, socioeconomic, and health-related data. The successful candidate will apply spatial analysis, artificial intelligence, machine learning, land-use regression, and spatiotemporal modelling approaches to develop exposure estimates, generate maps and indicators, support research publications and reports, and collaborate with research partners to strengthen the Centre’s evidence base for environmental health, climate adaptation, and public health policy. Job Requirements : Have a Master’s degree in Geographic Information Science, geospatial science, geography, environmental health, public health, epidemiology, environmental science, data science, climate science, or a related discipline. Have research experience in environmental exposure assessment, spatial analysis, land-use regression modelling, environmental epidemiology, climate change and health, air pollution, heat exposure, or related fields. Have experience in analyzing climate, environmental, land-use, remote sensing, health, or socioeconomic data. Have experience using R, Python, GIS software, Google Earth Engine, or other relevant statistical and geospatial analytical tools. Have good organizational, communication, and academic writing skills, with the ability to work independently and collaboratively in interdisciplinary teams. Candidates with relevant publications, project experience, or experience applying machine learning or artificial intelligence techniques in environmental health research will be advantageous. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Heat-and-Health-_R00025216": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Heat and Health)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-16\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nIn this rapidly changing world, the Centre for Climate Change and Environmental Health (CCEH) is advancing research on how climate change, air pollution, and extreme environmental conditions affect human health. By bringing together expertise across environmental science, exposure assessment, epidemiology, and public health, CCEH develops evidence-based solutions to support healthier and more climate-resilient communities in Singapore and across Asia. Within CCEH, the Environmental Health team, led by Prof. Steve Yim, investigates the interactions between climate, air quality, and human health using integrated measurement, modelling, and statistical approaches. The team works across multiple spatial scales to understand how environmental exposures affect human health and to generate scientific evidence for public health policy and workforce protection strategies. Key Responsibilities : The position will support research on the health impacts of heat exposure, temperature extremes, and climate-related environmental change. The role will contribute to studies examining how rising temperatures affect human health, wellbeing, vulnerability, and broader societal outcomes across populations and regions. The successful candidate will support the analysis and interpretation of climate, environmental, health, and socioeconomic data using statistical and spatiotemporal approaches, contribute to research publications and reports, and collaborate with research partners to strengthen the Centre’s evidence base for climate adaptation and public health policy. Job Requirements : Have a Ph.D. degree in atmospheric science, climate science, environmental health, environmental science, public health, epidemiology, geography, or a related discipline. Have research experience in climate change and health, heat exposure, temperature extremes, or related environmental health research. Have experience in analysing climate, environmental, health, or socioeconomic data, preferably in relation to temperature-related health risks. Have experience in statistical and spatiotemporal analysis using R, Python, MATLAB, or similar analytical tools. Have good organizational and communication skills, and evidence of the ability to work independently as well as collaboratively in interdisciplinary teams. Evidence of strong academic writing skills and the ability to contribute to scientific publications and other research outputs will be advantageous. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive---Assistant-Manager--HR-Faculty--HR-Shared-Services-_R00025208": {
      "title": "Senior Executive / Assistant Manager, HR Faculty (HR Shared Services)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-15\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Senior Executive / Assistant Manager performs and coordinates key HR operational activities for the faculty population, supporting smooth and timely service delivery. Core responsibilities include administering exit management, faculty hiring and contract renewals, as well as managing updates to concurrent appointments, including those involving University Senior Leaders. The position also supports a range of faculty employment matters, such as preparing letter addenda, processing job changes, handling other appointment-related updates, and providing secretariat support for off-site meetings. In addition, the Senior Executive /  Assistant Manager contributes to continuous improvement initiatives by identifying opportunities to automate manual processes, digitalise workflows, and implement technology-enabled solutions that enhance operational efficiency, consistency, and service quality. The incumbent also supports the review and enhancement of operational processes, Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs), and service controls to ensure consistent service delivery, operational excellence, scalability, and compliance with University policies and governance requirements. Responsibilities: Handles the HR administration and advisory support to enable effective HR operations in Faculty matters related to part-time lecturers’ Appointment and Reappointment, Job Changes, Concurrent Appointment and Exit management in alignment with University’s policies and guidelines. Ensure data accuracy in updates of all entries in HRIS, including but not limited to hire data, one-time payment, assigning costing allocations, and concurrent appointment updates in HRIS completed by team members Ensure tasks and enquiries undertaken are resolved and completed in a timely manner in accordance with the service level agreements (SLA) Improve processes and procedures to ensure high standards of service and work quality, efficiency and governance Drive and/or participate in projects and process reviews Collaborate and build good working relationships with stakeholders within the University Requirements Bachelor Degree in Business Administration, or a related discipline ie. Human Resources Good knowledge of the Employment Act and Labour laws of Singapore Comfortable to handle/review a high volume of administrative transactions and multi-tasking. Strong writing skills are essential Strong interpersonal and communication skills Strong organisational and time management skills Meticulous, resourceful and independent Proficient in Microsoft Office applications and PowerPDF Working knowledge of Workday is advantageous We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--MOF---6th-_R00025206": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (MOF – 6th)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-15\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Materials Science and Engineering (MSE) provides a vibrant and nurturing environment for staff and students to carry out inter-disciplinary research in key areas such as Computational Materials Science, Characterisation Materials Science, Defence Composite Materials, Functional Composite Materials, Energy, Nanomaterials, Low Dimensional Materials, Biomaterials Materials, Biological Materials, Bioinspired Materials and Sustainable Materials. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/mse/research . Key Responsibilities: We are looking for a Research Fellow to advance MOF‑based electrochemical and CO2 removal research. Electrochemical process on interface phenomena MOF synthesis, testing under different conditions Simulation of scaled up process. Interface with machine learning group on database set up CO2 removal process Job Requirements: Candidates with strong background in Materials chemistry/Physical chemistry Experience with MOF synthesis, energy storage system or electrochemical system PhD in Chemistry/Materials Science/Physics Encourage initiating activities on MOF development, devising, and analytical process Experience in machine learning will be preferred Good oral and written communication skills Candidates with strong publication/patent records will be preferred We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Photocatalysis-_R00025197": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Photocatalysis)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-15\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Materials Science and Engineering (MSE) provides a vibrant and nurturing environment for staff and students to carry out inter-disciplinary research in key areas such as Computational Materials Science, Characterisation Materials Science, Defence Composite Materials, Functional Composite Materials, Energy, Nanomaterials, Low Dimensional Materials, Biomaterials Materials, Biological Materials, Bioinspired Materials and Sustainable Materials. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/mse/research . We are looking for a Research Fellow to conduct research studied in an NTU lab . The role will focus on development of semiconductor nanostructures for photocatalytic reactions. Key Responsibilities: Participate in the conduct of research project with research team members to ensure completion of deliverables Maintenance of lab equipment and supplies that include procurement and liaison with suppliers Mentor junior PhD student and undergraduate students for their research studies Assist in grant writing and reports that consolidate research findings Job Requirements: PhD degree in engineering or science with first-author journal publications on solution-based synthesis of semiconductor nanostructures (Entry level candidates are welcome to apply) Proficiency in photocatalytic tests and operating gas chromatography equipment Good written and oral communication skills We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Administrative-Support--NTUitive-_R00025190": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Administrative Support [NTUitive]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-14\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNTU Innovation and Entrepreneurship (I&E) advances cohesive and collaborative relationships across various innovation drivers within the NTU community. It seeks to accelerate the University’s efforts in translating scientific discoveries, innovation and creative work into technological and social entrepreneurship activities that benefit industry and society. NTUitive - the University’s innovation and enterprise company - plays a pivotal role in translating research breakthroughs into solutions that benefit society. We support innovators, entrepreneurs and industry partners in translating promising ideas and deep tech into ventures and real-world solutions with commercial and societal impact. As a wholly-owned subsidiary of NTU and a key innovation driver under NTU I&E, NTUitive oversees the cultivation of startups and spin-offs, as well as the related investments. The Assistant Manager, Administrative Support provides executive, operational and programme management support to the Associate Vice President (Technology Transfer) and the NTU I&E Technology Transfer team. The role is responsible for ensuring the effective coordination of executive engagements, stakeholder interactions, office operations and programme activities, while maintaining high standards of governance, compliance and service delivery. Working closely with internal and external stakeholders, he/she supports the administration and implementation of strategic programmes, and contributes to process optimisation, digitalisation and continuous improvement initiatives. Through effective coordination, stakeholder engagement and operational support, the role contributes to the smooth functioning of office operations and the successful planning and implementation of new programmes and initiatives in NTU I&E. Successful candidate can look forward to a rewarding career at NTUitive with ample opportunities for growth and development. Responsibilities: Executive and Stakeholder Support Manage the calendar, appointments, meetings and official engagements of the Associate Vice President (Technology Transfer). Coordinate meeting logistics, prepare agendas and meeting materials. Facilitate communication and correspondence on behalf of the AVP. Monitor and track follow-up actions arising from meetings and engagements. Provide administrative and coordination support for strategic initiatives, projects and activities led by the AVP. Serve as a key coordination point between the AVP and internal/external stakeholders. Coordinate stakeholder engagements, workshops and visits involving industry, government and academic partners, ensuring effective communication and follow-up of agreed actions. Operational Excellence, Governance and Transformation Oversee day-to-day office administration and operational support functions, including facilities, office resources and administrative records. Manage office resources, procurement, IT assets and inventory records. Liaise with corporate departments and vendors on facilities, IT and operational matters. Review operational workflows and administrative procedures, identify opportunities for process optimisation and digitalisation, and support the implementation of improvement initiatives. Ensure proper maintenance of administrative records and assets in compliance with organisational policies, audit requirements and data governance standards. Support internal audits, compliance reviews and reporting exercises by coordinating documentation, records and follow-up actions. Participate in departmental transformation initiatives, including the implementation and adoption of digital systems, automation solutions and process enhancement projects. Programme Administration and Management Support Coordinate end-to-end programme administration, including application processing, proposal evaluation, award administration and related stakeholder communications. Monitor programme milestones, progress reporting, compliance requirements and administrative deliverables to support effective programme implementation. Process fund disbursements in accordance with approved guidelines, financial controls and organisational policies. Maintain complete, accurate and up-to-date programme and financial records in accordance with organisational, funding and audit requirements. Prepare programme statistics, management reports, dashboards and performance updates to support programme monitoring and decision-making. Support programme governance and compliance activities, including record management, audit preparation, risk monitoring and adherence to organisational and funding requirements. Coordinate and manage programme-related events, briefing sessions, outreach activities, workshops and stakeholder engagement initiatives to support programme objectives and outreach efforts. Serve as a key contact point and engage internal and external stakeholders, including applicants, award recipients, reviewers and partners, to facilitate programme delivery, address operational issues and ensure a positive stakeholder experience. Support the review and enhancement of programme administration processes, including the implementation of new systems, process automation initiatives and digital solutions to improve operational efficiency, service quality and user experience. Any other ad-hoc initiatives and projects undertaken by the Office. Requirements: Bachelor's Degree from a recognised university. Good understanding of office administration, records management, procurement and operational support processes. Knowledge of project coordination, process improvement and change management principles. Knowledge of higher education, research, innovation and entrepreneurship ecosystems will be an advantage. Minimum 4-6 years of relevant working experience in administration, programme administration, executive support, operations management or a related function. Experience supporting senior management and coordinating meetings, events and stakeholder engagements will be an advantage. Experience managing administrative processes, records and reporting requirements. Experience coordinating programmes, projects or initiatives involving multiple stakeholders and competing priorities. Strong organisational and coordination skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines concurrently. Good analytical skills and proficiency in Microsoft Office applications, particularly Excel, for data management, tracking and reporting. Good written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to prepare correspondence, reports and meeting materials. Strong interpersonal and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to work effectively with stakeholders at different organisational levels. Ability to exercise sound judgement in prioritising requests, managing competing demands and handling confidential information appropriately. Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively within a team environment. Project coordination skills, including the ability to manage timelines, monitor deliverables and coordinate stakeholders effectively. Meticulous, organised and detail-oriented, with a strong commitment to accuracy and quality. Proactive, resourceful and responsive in addressing issues and following through on tasks. Adaptable and able to work effectively in a dynamic environment with evolving priorities and requirements. Professional and tactful in handling sensitive information and interactions with senior stakeholders. Positive team player with a collaborative mindset and willingness to support departmental initiatives beyond assigned responsibilities. Demonstrates initiative and ownership in driving tasks to completion with minimal supervision. Resilient and comfortable working in a fast-paced environment where priorities and processes may evolve over time. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTUitive"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Director--Overseas-Entrepreneurship-Programme_R00024900": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Director, Overseas Entrepreneurship Programme",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-14\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nA young, research-intensive university, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) has 33,000 undergraduate and postgraduate students in engineering, business, science, humanities, arts, social sciences, education and medicine. Ranked among the world’s top universities, NTU Entrepreneurship Academy (NTUpreneur) provides education within the University and the region. Reporting to the Deputy Director of NTU Entrepreneurship Academy (NTUpreneur), the Senior Assistant Director, Overseas Entrepreneurship Programme (OEP), will provide strategic leadership in driving the growth and implementation of NTUpreneur’s global internship programme across Southeast Asia, East Asia, India, the United States, and Europe. The incumbent will develop and execute strategies to strengthen NTU’s global entrepreneurship network, expand internship opportunities in emerging innovation hubs, and enhance students’ entrepreneurial and international exposure. The role is responsible for building and managing strategic partnerships with startups and key ecosystem stakeholders worldwide, overseeing overseas placement consultants, ensuring programme sustainability, and formulating strategic plans aligned with NTUpreneur’s objectives and the NTU 2030 Strategic Plan. The incumbent will also provide oversight of OEP operations and lead outreach efforts to drive strong student participation. In addition, the Senior Assistant Director will manage the Ministry of Education’s Global Innovation Alliance (GIA) grant and Enterprise Singapore’s Global Ready Talent (GRT) grant, ensuring the achievement of programme targets, full compliance with grant requirements, prudent utilisation of funds, and the timely preparation of reports to support audits and grant claims. Responsibilities: 1. Provide leadership in driving the growth, expansion, and ensuring effective implementation of NTUpreneur’s flagship global internship programm Develop and execute strategies to strengthen NTU’s overseas entrepreneurship internship placements in strategic locations globally. Drive and deliver strategic outcomes that align with NTU’s internationalisation and entrepreneurship objectives. Increase NTU’s presence in the global startup ecosystem. 2. Drive efforts to increase the number and quality of internship opportunities available to NTU students Identify emerging markets in global cities to increase new internship opportunities, assess benefits and viability for implementation, and establish a framework for implementation. Initiate and deepen strategic partnerships with key ecosystem stakeholders worldwide. Ensure meaningful experiential learning experiences that enhance students’ entrepreneurial competencies and global outlook. 3. Oversee the appointment and performance management of overseas placement consultants Identify and hire the best overseas placement representatives to secure internship opportunities, engage and monitor the performance to ensure growing and quality placement opportunities.  Ensure the financial sustainability of the programme. 4. Design and drive pre-OEP and post-OEP events and activities to support student venture creation, and formulate long-term strategic plans that align with NTUpreneur’s objectives and the broader aspirations of the NTU 2030 Strategic Plan Design and organise pre and post OEP I&E themed events and activities with inputs from across relevant stakeholder in NTU. Strengthen student engagement throughout the internship period, and establish an OEP alumni network. Track and report on students’ entrepreneurship or intrapreneurship status post-OEP. 5.Responsible for the strategic management and administration of external grants and achieving programme performance targets Ensure full compliance with grant administration’s terms and conditions. Ensure the proper utilisation of grant funds. Prepare timely financial and operational reports to facilitate audits, grant claims, and stakeholder reporting requirements. Point of contact in negotiating deals and agreements. 6. Leadership in OEP operations and growing team capabilities Lead operations of OEP team, supervise team performance and ensure effective performance. Equip team with business development capabilities to mitigate dependence on overseas representatives in securing internship opportunities for students. Requirements : A degree in any discipline from a recognised university. At least 5 years of experience in corporate partnerships for education purposes. Possess a strong network with innovation and entrepreneurship agencies and corporations overseas. Strong experience in stakeholder and partnership engagement.  A track record experience in overseas internship experience in other IHLs will be an advantag e. Excellent knowledge of overseas startup landscape in strategic cities such as Silicon Valley, Boston, London, Munich, Finland, Sweden, Tokyo, Shanghai, Shenzhen, Hangzhou, Jakarta, Bangkok, Ho Chi Minh and major cities in India. Deep understanding of the education approach to outcome-driven entrepreneurship education is essential. Good knowledge of the startup journey in its scale and operations and the capability gaps in scaling up. Good knowledge of the startup founder’s mindset. Able to contribute effectively to the strategic purpose of entrepreneurship education. Excellent communication skills (verbal and written). Innovation in designing high impact and attractive I&E activities to attract participation.  Able to engage senior leadership in government organisations and startups and negotiate terms. Strong team player who is able to work with stakeholders in NTU and external agencies (local and overseas). Able to understand students’ mindset and willingness to work and support their entrepreneurial aspirations. Highly driven and willingness to work in a fast-paced environment. Excellent project and event management skills. Enjoy working with students and believe in supporting their entrepreneurial aspirations. Good knowledge of what attracts the attention of students / early-career individuals. Meticulous with details and processes . We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Communication-Media-Studies-Computational-Social-Science-Information-Science-Computer-Science-Data-Science-_R00025189-1": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Communication/Media Studies/Computational Social Science/Information Science/Computer Science/Data Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-14\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Wee Kim Wee School of Communication and Information (WKWSCI), together with the Earth Observatory of Singapore, is looking for a Research Fellow to make an important contribution to the research project: “Climate Transformation Program (CTP): Cross Cutting Theme 1 – Sustainable Societies” funded by the MOE Tier 3C Grant. CTP aims to develop, inspire, and accelerate knowledge-based solutions and educate future leaders to establish the stable climate and environment necessary for resilient, just, and sustainable Southeast Asian societies. CTP will generate knowledge and innovation across disciplines including climate and Earth science, ecology, materials science, artificial intelligence, humanities, social sciences and the arts, finance, health, and engineering. It will also translate state-of-the-art scientific results into real world solutions for Singapore, and it will transfer these solutions to Southeast Asia (SEA) and beyond. As part of this programme, “Cross-cutting theme 1: Sustainable Societies”, this theme will leverage climate research in communication, public opinion and psychology, and artistic impressions to shape public attitudes and behaviours towards climate change issues. The Research Fellow will work directly with the PI of the Sustainable Societies theme, Professor Shirley Ho, based in the Wee Kim Wee School of Communication and Information at NTU. Key Responsibilities: The successful candidate will contribute to an interdisciplinary research program by: Conducting literature reviews and supporting manuscript development Collecting and analysing online public discourse data using sentiment and content analysis methods Applying statistical and computational techniques to analyse large-scale textual datasets Contributing to peer-reviewed journal articles and conference presentations Preparing progress reports and final research outputs Supporting dissemination of findings to academic and public audiences Assisting with general project coordination and administrative tasks as required Job Requirements: We are seeking a highly motivated researcher with: PhD in Communication, Media Studies, Computational Social Science, Information Science, Computer Science, Data Science, or a related discipline. Demonstrated expertise in sentiment analysis, opinion mining, or computational analysis of media and public discourse. Candidates should be able to connect computational analysis with communication theories and research questions. Strong quantitative research skills and proficiency in Python or R. Experience with large-scale textual data, natural language processing, machine learning, transformer-based models, or large language models is required. Additional strengths that would be beneficial include: Experience with fine-tuning or prompting large language models for sentiment, emotion, stance, or framing analysis. Experience analysing large-scale textual data from sources such as social media, news, or online communities. Experience collecting data through APIs or web scraping. Experience preparing grant proposals and contributing to funded research projects. Knowledge of open-science practices, including reproducible workflows, preregistration, and research-data management. Ability to lead collaborative projects with third-party data companies, coordinate internal and external stakeholders, and manage project timelines, deliverables, and quality. Prior experience in project management or industry–academia collaboration is preferred. A strong publication record or demonstrated potential to publish in reputable communication, computational social science, or interdisciplinary venues. Candidates should be able to independently develop research questions, conduct analysis, prepare manuscripts, and deliver project milestones. Strong academic writing and presentation skills, with the ability to work effectively in an interdisciplinary team. Experience supervising research assistants, contributing to grant proposals, or managing research projects is advantageous. Why Join Us This position offers the opportunity to: Contribute to an interdisciplinary research programme addressing climate change and sustainable societies in Southeast Asia. Collaborate with researchers from diverse disciplines across NTU and partner institutions. Conduct research with the potential to inform public understanding and societal responses to climate change. Develop a strong research profile through publications, conference presentations, and collaborative projects. Interested applicants are invited to submit a cover letter, full CV and names and contact details of three referees in one document. Enquiries about this position can be made to TSYHo@ntu.edu.sg. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Mathematics-_R00025188": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Mathematics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-14\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences (SPMS) at NTU Singapore is a school dedicated to advancing research and education across the mathematical and physical sciences. It hosts activities in two divisions: the Division of Mathematical Sciences (MAS) and the Division of Physics and Applied Physics (PAP). MAS spans a broad spectrum of topics, from pure mathematics to its applications in cryptography, computing, business, and finance. PAP encompasses numerous areas of fundamental and applied physics, such as quantum information, condensed matter physics, biophysics, and photonics. The key objective is to support efforts to advance scientific knowledge and nurture talented individuals from Singapore and around the world into scientific leaders and researchers. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/spms We are looking for a Research Fellow to join Dr. Kay Jin Lim's research group and contribute to advancing the study of representation theory of finite-dimensional algebras. The role will focus on conducting original research in this area, exploring connections to related fields such as homological algebra, algebraic geometry, or algebraic combinatorics, and disseminating findings through publications and conference presentations. The successful candidate will work closely with Dr. Lim and collaborate with an active research community, with opportunities to co-supervise graduate students and contribute to the intellectual life of the department. Key Responsibilities: Contribute to the development and advancement of research in the representation theory of finite-dimensional algebras, exploring connections to related areas such as homological algebra, algebraic geometry, or algebraic combinatorics. Conduct original research, including problem formulation, theoretical development, and rigorous proof-writing. Preparation of research papers, reports, and presentations to disseminate findings. Participate in regular team meetings and contribute to the overall progress of the project. Job Requirements: A PhD degree in mathematics or a related area, with a strong background in representation theory of finite-dimensional algebras or related fields such as homological algebra, algebraic geometry, or algebraic combinatorics. Solid theoretical and analytical skills, with the ability to develop rigorous mathematical proofs. Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills. Ability to work both independently and collaboratively in a team. Previous research experience and publication record in a related field preferred. Proficiency in mathematical programming languages such as Magma, GAP, SageMath, or similar. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Deputy-Director--Financial-Planning---Analysis_R00024755": {
      "title": "Deputy Director, Financial Planning & Analysis",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-14\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Office of Finance (OFIN) supports the University in planning and executing sound financial management in fulfillment of the University’s mission; implementing and maintaining a robust financial framework that supports management in effective decision-making; providing fiscal stewardship of University’s resources; and ensuring financial governance and compliance with regulatory requirements. The Deputy Director will report to the Director, FP&A. Responsibilities Lead a team of finance professionals to coordinate and consolidate the University‑wide budget, including departmental budgets managed through department cluster leads and finance partners. Develop deep functional expertise and leadership capabilities amongst finance leads/partners so that they can support the operational finance strategy and performance standards for their respective areas of responsibility. Has overall accountability for translating the University and Finance function’s long‑term objectives into coherent, actionable financial plans across departments, in partnership with finance leads and partners. Plan and allocate resources to areas where they will most effectively contribute to long term goals. Possess deep understanding of various internal operational processes related to finance within the University, benchmark best practices amongst higher educational institutions and drive continuous improvements. Support capital / strategic initiatives with financial modelling. The candidate will collaborate with other university corporate functions (including the Office of Human Resources to analyse manpower planning outcomes) and provide financial insights that support the University’s objectives. Requirements Bachelor’s degree in Finance or Accountancy with minimum 15 years of relevant experience in financial planning & analysis and budgeting CA is a pre-requisite Relevant work experience in a supervisory position. Solid knowledge and experience in Audit Administration Strong senior stakeholder management skills Excellent written and verbal communication skills Strong analytical and problem solving abilities Experience working in SAP HANA and Workday environments, including reporting or diagnostics, is advantageous. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Faculty-Ops-and-Support_R00024933": {
