    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Director--Research-and-Infrastructure-Safety_R00024205": {
      "title": "Manager, Chemical Safety",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-13\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Office of Health and Safety (OHS) champions health and safety management at NTU. OHS oversees university-wide programmes including biosafety, chemical safety, radiation safety, laboratory safety and occupational health. We are seeking an experienced Manager, Chemical Safety to lead NTU's institutional chemical safety programme. The successful candidate will serve as the University's subject matter expert on chemical risk management, hazardous materials governance and laboratory chemical safety, supporting world-class research and education activities across the University Responsibilities Develop, implement and review NTU's chemical safety standards, policies and guidance documents to support safe and compliant research, teaching and operational activities. Serve as the University's subject matter expert on chemical safety, providing professional advice on hazardous chemicals, toxic substances, carcinogens, compressed gases, flammable materials and dangerous goods. Lead and manage institutional programmes relating to chemical safety, hazardous materials management and laboratory chemical compliance, including industrial hygiene, wastewater sampling and statutory medical examination programmes. Monitor regulatory developments and provide guidance on emerging requirements and their implications for University operations. Support regulatory inspections, audits and investigations involving chemical safety matters, and liaise with relevant authorities including MOM, NEA, SCDF, SPF and other agencies. Serve as secretariat to institutional safety and health committees, supporting governance, coordination and implementation of safety and health initiatives across the University. Lead enterprise-wide chemical safety initiatives, continuous improvement efforts and digital transformation projects to strengthen safety governance and operational effectiveness. Manage safety and health applications, and perform data analytics on chemical safety trends, programme effectiveness and performance indicators to identify risks, compliance concerns and opportunities for continuous improvement. Develop and deliver chemical safety training, awareness and competency programmes to strengthen stakeholder capabilities across the University. Partner with Colleges, Schools, Research Institutes and administrative units to provide value-added safety and health solutions and promote a strong safety culture across NTU. Requirements Degree in Chemistry, Chemical Engineering, Environmental Engineering, Occupational Hygiene, Safety Engineering, or a related discipline. Postgraduate qualification in Occupational Health & Safety, Industrial Hygiene, Chemical Safety, Environmental Management, or a related field will be an advantage. At least 8 years of relevant experience in chemical safety, laboratory safety, industrial hygiene, hazardous materials management, or occupational safety and health. Background in managing chemical safety programmes within universities, research institutions, pharmaceutical, chemical manufacturing, healthcare, or related sectors would be advantageous. Familiarity with regulatory requirements and chemical compliance programmes, coupled with a good understanding of local workplace safety and health, environmental and public health legislation, as well as permits, licences and regulated equipment administered by agencies such as SPF, NEA, MOM and SCDF. Proven capability in implementing workplace safety and health programmes within office, facilities management and laboratory-based environments. Registered Workplace Safety and Health Officer (WSHO), Registered Fire Safety Manager (FSM), ISO 45001:2018 Lead/Internal Auditor certification, or equivalent professional certifications will be advantageous. Effective communication, report-writing, project management and stakeholder engagement skills. Proficiency in leveraging GenAI tools to enhance productivity and work outcomes. Independent, meticulous and reliable, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and deliver results within timelines. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--AI---Data-Services_R00025179": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, AI & Data Services",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-11\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Office of Health and Safety (OHS) champions health and safety management at NTU. OHS oversees university-wide programmes including biosafety, chemical safety, radiation safety, laboratory safety, occupational health, audits, incident reporting and safety governance. We are seeking an Assistant Manager (AI/Data Systems) to sustain OHS’ digital transformation, data analytics and AI-enabled initiatives. The successful candidate will develop and maintain digital tools, dashboards, automation workflows and data insights that strengthen safety oversight, compliance monitoring and operational efficiency across the University. Responsibilities Develop, configure, maintain and enhance OHS digital systems, dashboards, trackers and workflow tools. Collect, clean, analyse and visualise safety and health data to support management reporting, risk monitoring, audits, inspections and programme evaluation. Identify and implement practical automation, AI-enabled and low-code/no-code solutions to streamline OHS processes and improve productivity. Work with OHS programme owners, Schools, Departments, Centres and system partners to gather requirements, conduct user testing, prepare documentation and support implementation. Prepare dashboards, reports and insights that support evidence-based decision-making, audit readiness and continuous improvement. Provide user support, training materials and continuous improvement recommendations for OHS digital tools. Requirements Degree in Computer Science, Information Systems, Data Analytics, Engineering, Science, Safety & Health, or a related discipline. At least 3 years of relevant experience in data analytics, digital systems, automation, workflow improvement, project management, business analysis or IT-enabled service delivery. Proficiency in Google Gemini, Microsoft 365 tools, Power BI, Power Automate, SharePoint, Excel or similar analytics and workflow platforms. Strong analytical, documentation, project coordination and stakeholder engagement skills. Good understanding of responsible AI use, data governance, information security and validation of digital outputs would be advantageous. Experience in safety and health, higher education, research institutions or regulated environments would be advantageous. Independent, meticulous, reliable and able to manage concurrent priorities under timelines. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
