    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-IT-Security-Analyst--Information-Security-Department---NIE-_R00024901": {
      "title": "Senior IT Security Analyst (Information Security Department) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-10\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nABOUT THE NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF EDUCATION (NIE) The National Institute of Education (NIE), Singapore , is Singapore’s national teacher education institute and we are proud to be an integral part of the nation’s education service. We play a key role in the preparation of teachers and in the provision of teacher professional and school leadership development programmes. We are committed to our vision of being An Institute of Distinction: Leading the Future of Education and our mission to Inspire Learning, Transform Teaching and Advance Research . Read more about NIE here . NIE invites suitable candidates to apply for the position of Senior IT Security Analyst within the Division of Academic Computing & Information Services (ACIS). This is a 3-year contract position. Key Responsibilities   Incident Response Leadership : Oversee the entire Incident Response lifecycle from detection to resolution. Lead investigations of IT security incidents and ensure thorough root cause analysis and remediation. Develop and maintain Incident Response playbooks and procedures. Coordinate with internal, external stakeholders, and vendors during incidents. Conduct post-incident reviews and report findings to management. Manage and coordinate incident response efforts across hybrid IT environments, including on-premises and cloud systems. Monitoring and Detection Develop and implement advanced threat detection and monitoring strategies. Utilize SIEM, EDR, and other security tools for timely incident detection. Perform threat hunting and proactive security assessments. Collaborate with IT teams to deploy and optimize security solutions. Threat Statistics and Reporting Analyze and compile statistics on threats relevant to the Institute. Prepare and present detailed reports on threat statistics to stakeholders. Use data visualization tools to communicate threat trends and insights. Innovation and Continuous Improvement Evaluate and integrate new technologies to enhance security operations. Foster a culture of continuous improvement within the team. Encourage continuous learning and professional development. Security Project Management Support and coordinate cybersecurity projects and initiatives across the Institute. Work with internal stakeholders and vendors to track project deliverables, timelines, risks, and action items. Assist in the implementation, enhancement, and operationalization of security technologies and solutions. Facilitate meetings, prepare project updates, and maintain documentation related to cybersecurity initiatives. Support process improvement and automation initiatives within the Security Operations function. Requirements A University degree in Information Systems, Computer Science, Cybersecurity, or a related field. Professional Certification(s) in incident handling and security analysis preferred. GCIH or its equivalent is preferred. Minimum of 4 years of progressive experience in IT security, with a focus on Incident Response. Minimum of 4 years of experience in a Security Operations Center (SOC), with proven leadership capabilities. Intermediate knowledge of security operations, incident analysis, incident handling, threat hunting, vulnerability management/testing, system patching, log analysis, intrusion detection, firewall administration, and network security assessment tools. Proficiency in Security Information and Event Management (SIEM), Endpoint Detection and Response (EDR), traffic and packet analysis, digital forensics, cloud security, and host-based intrusion detection systems. Experience in Blue/Purple teaming, firewall administration, Intrusion Prevention Systems (IPS), Web Application Firewalls (WAF), virtualization, and cloud technologies. Knowledge and experience in Linux, Windows, and Database technologies preferred. Strong knowledge of industry standards and information security policy frameworks. Ability to conduct gap analysis, improve security monitoring and alerting processes, and identify opportunities for operational improvement. Ability to evaluate Information Security threats, provide response guidance, and ensure appropriate controls and mitigation measures are implemented. Excellent leadership, communication, stakeholder management, and problem-solving skills, with the ability to work effectively under pressure and coordinate with stakeholders at all levels, including University administration. Demonstrated ability to manage security initiatives/projects, coordinate with vendors and stakeholders, and document business requirements. Passionate about cybersecurity, continuous learning, and emerging technologies. Open-minded and adaptable towards adopting new technologies, including Artificial Intelligence (AI), Agentic AI, and security automation. Demonstrates curiosity, innovation, and a forward-thinking mindset in enhancing security operations capabilities. Strong interest in contributing towards the development of an AI-enabled and automation-driven SOC environment. Closing Date The closing date of the advertisement is 24 July 2026 . We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Other Information NIE staff can take chartered buses at their own expense from or near their home to the NIE campus. This is subject to the availability of bus routes and seats. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Computer-Science-_R00025148": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Computer Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-10\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nYoung and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is ranked among the world’s top universities. NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science (CCDS) is a leading college that is known for its excellent curriculum, outstanding and impactful research, and world-renowned faculty. A hot bed of cutting-edge technology and groundbreaking research, the College aims to groom the next generation of leaders, thinkers, and innovators to thrive in the digital age. Located in the heart of Asia, NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science is an exciting place to learn and grow. We welcome you to join our community of faculty, students and alumni who are shaping the future of AI, Data Science and Computing. The College of Computing & Data Science (CCDS) invites applications for the position of Research Associate.   The Research Associate (RA) will play a key role in advancing the research mission of NTU by supporting cutting-edge projects in computer vision, machine learning, physical AI, and spatial AI. The RA will contribute to the development of innovative algorithms, data preparation pipelines, and experimental evaluations that are central to the Physical Vision Group’s long-term goal of building general-purpose physical simulators and spatial intelligent systems.    Reporting to the Principal Investigator, the RA will help ensure a healthy and vibrant research environment within the Physical Vision Group (PVG, https://physicalvision.github.io/  ). This will involve closely collaborating with faculty, postdoctoral researchers, and PhD students, bridging foundational research with real-world applications in robotics, VR/AR, and embodied AI. Key Responsibilities: Conduct individual research within the designed project: process data, develop research methods, build and evaluate computer vision and machine learning algorithms empirically. Author research articles at an international level for peer-reviewed conferences. Engineer software based on the research outcomes of the project and distribute this on the group’s web. Manage own academic research and administrative activities. Adapt existing and develop new scientific techniques and experimental protocols. Test hypotheses and analyse scientific data from a variety of sources. Contribute ideas for new research projects. Develop ideas for generating research income, and present detailed research proposals to senior researchers. Any other duties appropriate with the role. Job Requirements: Hold a relevant Master degree in Computer Science. Sufficient theoretical and practical knowledge of methodologies such as deep and statistical learning. Excellent communication skills, including the ability to write for publication, present research proposals and results, and present the research output at meetings. Independent, highly analytical, proactive and a team player Strong publication record at the principal international computer vision and machine learning conferences will be better. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Director--ACMV_R00025175": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, ACMV",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-10\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University (NTU) is a leading research-intensive university in Singapore, committed to excellence in education, research and innovation. We invite experienced and motivated professionals to join the Office of Development and Facilities Management (ODFM), which oversees the planning, development, operation and maintenance of the University’s buildings and infrastructure. As Assistant Director, ACMV, you will lead the ACMV section in managing campus air-conditioning and mechanical ventilation operations, maintenance contracts, asset renewal and infrastructure upgrading works. You will play a key role in ensuring ACMV services remain safe, reliable, efficient and aligned with the University’s operational and sustainability goals. Responsibilities Lead the ACMV Section in overseeing campus-wide ACMV operations, preventive and corrective maintenance to ensure safe, reliable and efficient service delivery. Manage ACMV maintenance contracts, contractor performance, service standards, contract governance and operational compliance. Oversee ACMV fault management, operational risks, service disruptions and recovery actions to minimise impact on campus operations. Lead ACMV asset renewal, replacement and infrastructure upgrading works, including the review of technical proposals, engineering submissions and implementation strategies. Drive continuous improvements in system reliability, maintainability, operational resilience and energy performance. Lead, mentor and develop the ACMV team by providing technical guidance, setting priorities and overseeing operational, maintenance and project delivery. Build strong partnerships with internal users, consultants, contractors and senior management while promoting workplace safety, regulatory compliance and engineering best practices. Requirements Degree in Mechanical Engineering, Building Services Engineering, Facilities Management or a related discipline. At least 10 years of relevant experience in ACMV or mechanical building services covering operations, maintenance, contract administration and project delivery. Strong knowledge of ACMV systems, asset lifecycle management, contract administration, local engineering codes and operational risk management. Strong leadership, stakeholder management and communication skills with the ability to lead teams, manage contractors and engage a broad range of stakeholders. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities, make sound engineering decisions and lead operations within a live campus environment. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
