    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant--Communication-Studies-Psychology-Social-Science-_R00025172": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Communication Studies/Psychology/Social Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nEstablished in 1992, the Wee Kim Wee School of Communication and Information (WKWSCI) is the only full-fledged communication school in Singapore and is a world-class centre of excellence with an international faculty, state-of-the-art research laboratories, and global institutional affiliations. The Privacy and Emotion Lab in WKWSCI is a research lab that conduct in-depth study about individuals’ usage. The Research Assistant will support the research project that aims to design human-IoT communication that effectively motivates seniors to actively engage in self-directed health prevention, leading to improvements in their mental and physical well-being. Consequently, our project will primarily focus on relatively healthier seniors (aged 60 and above), who do not have serious health conditions requiring intensive medical treatment. Key Responsibilities: Finance: Keep track of expenditure and remaining budget in an organised manner, ensure that the spending is optimised and on track with respect to goals set for the grant; prepare financial and progress reports, presentations, as well as other research-related documents Administrative: Liaise with external vendors to purchase necessary equipment/materials for research studies, including specialised equipment, software, and research participant incentives Subject Recruitment: Responsible for recruiting participants for interview and survey Logistics: Plan the necessary logistics for studies, such as interview scheduling and booking facilities. Basic research: Conduct literature review Data collection: Participate in the data collection process for both qualitative (e.g. interviews) and quantitative (e.g. surveys) studies Data analysis: Analyse data for various projects using tools such as SPSS and Mplus Job Requirements: Bachelor’s degree for Research Assistant in the field of communication studies, psychology, or related social science fields Good project management skills, with multi-tasking ability Skills and basic training in quantitative and qualitative research for social science Academic writing skills Ability to run standard statistical tests Knowledge of advanced statistical tests (e.g. moderation/mediation, hierarchical regression etc.) is preferred A good team player with effective communication skills and the ability to work closely with faculty, staff, students and external collaborators Past experience in a project officer or research assistant role is preferred We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--AI-for-Medicine--LKCMedicine-_R00025063": {
      "title": "Research Associate, AI for Medicine [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. The MVAIT Lab at LKCMed seeks to hire a Research Associate (RA) who will play a role in pioneering research on medical image processing, medical visual technology and LLM, and the interface of AI algorithms with surgical robotics. The RA will design and implement cutting-edge algorithms and also be actively involved in the development AI tools tailored for different medical domains. These are efforts to bridge the gap between advanced computational framework and practical medical use cases. The tools and framework developed by the RA will be meticulously adapted to meet the needs of clinicians, radiologists, and biologists, assisting them in their daily tasks and pioneering research. Ultimately, this position plays a pivotal role in LKCMed's overarching mission to leverage technology to enhance healthcare outcomes and propel the institution to the forefront of medical advancements. Key Responsibilities: Design and implement AI algorithm models to analyze multimodal medical datasets (including MRI, CT, X-ray, OCT, and ultrasound images) for high-precision medical organ segmentation, 3D modeling research, and intelligent diagnosis. Explore and develop the application of large-scale pre-trained models in medical scenarios, including but not limited to intelligent consultation systems based on large language models and disease management systems utilizing multi-modal large model technologies. Develop, test, and optimize AI software systems for various medical tasks, ensuring their applicability and accuracy in real-world medical environments. Utilize data storage technologies to manage multimodal medical data securely and efficiently, ensuring data privacy while providing high storage capacity to accelerate AI model training and inference. Enhance the visualization capabilities of AI software system outputs using VR/AR equipment and 3D visualization technologies, aiding clinical observations and assisting interns in training and rapid learning. Collaborate with the team to systematically complete research and development tasks, assisting in the development of AI-assisted robotic solutions for surgical procedures, including pre-operative planning and intra-operative guidance. Ensure that all research activities adhere to ethical guidelines and patient data privacy regulations. Stay updated on the latest advancements in medical imaging, image processing, robotics, and large language models, ensuring that the research remains at the forefront of the field. Collaborate with external researchers and interdisciplinary teams (including medical professionals, AI experts, and research professors) to ensure the necessity, professionalism, rationality, and practicality of the research. Write research proposals, grant applications, and contribute to the team's strategic research direction. Mentor and train junior researchers, students, and interns, ensuring they possess the necessary skills and knowledge to contribute effectively to the research. Competencies and Qualification Requirements: Master degree in Computer Engineering, Computer Science, or a related field from a prestigious institution. Extensive experience in deep learning, AI, computer vision, 3D reconstruction algorithms, and large-scale Pre-trained Models. A solid research foundation and engineering experience in the AI medical field, proficient in programming languages and frameworks such as Python, C++, Pytorch, Tensorflow, Opencv, and COLMAP. Experience in software system engineering, capable of designing a well-structured system architecture to support the implementation of AI medical software. Proficiency in SQL and other data storage technologies, able to apply them flexibly and effectively in the AI medical field, ensuring data storage performance and security. Experience analyzing and interpreting medical imaging datasets, particularly ophthalmic imaging data, with an understanding of the nuances and peculiarities of such datasets. A deep understanding of ethical considerations, patient data privacy regulations, and other compliance-related aspects of medical research. Ability to collaborate with interdisciplinary teams, including medical professionals, AI experts, and research professors. Proactive and self-driven, capable of developing and managing multiple tasks and projects simultaneously. Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English; proficiency in additional languages is a plus. Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Civil-Engineering-_R00025158": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Civil Engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNTU, CEE is a leading school for Sustainable Built Environment. The job is aimed at developing smart connectors for modular floating breakwaters. Key Responsibilities: Design and fabricate self-sensing concrete. Lab test and analysis of self-sensing concrete. Optimize and evaluate the performance for field trials. Publish several papers in top journals. Write proposals for further development. Mentor students. Job Requirements: PhD degree in civil engineering or related field At least 1 year of relevant experience in structural materials and signal processing. Good written and oral communication skills Proficiency in ABAQUS , and lab test skill Ability to work independently and develop solutions under strict timelines We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Spinal-Cord-Injury-Experiments-for--Neural-Tissue-Engineering-Research-_R00023404": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Spinal Cord Injury Experiments for  Neural Tissue Engineering Research)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nA Research Fellow/ Post-doctoral position is available in the laboratory of Dr. Sing Yian CHEW (Nanyang Technological University, NTU) and Prof. Shawn JE (Duke-NUS) in Singapore, to a highly motivated candidate who has a passion for in vivo Spinal Cord Injury cell/scaffold implantation treatment and neural tissue engineering research.   The focus of this project is to evaluate cell transplantation and tissue engineered scaffolds for in vivo neural tissue regeneration. We are seeking an individual who is experienced in spinal cord injury microsurgery with rats and interested in conducting animal implantation studies, as well as carrying out behavioral tests; and characterizing/evaluating scaffold-cell/tissue interactions through immunofluorescent and histochemical staining and imaging.   The candidate will be jointly supervised by Prof. Sing Yian CHEW and Prof. Shawn JE. This position offers a unique opportunity to apply in vivo experimentation skills to neural tissue engineering, through strong collaborative efforts with scientists and engineers across different local and overseas institutions (SMART/MIT, University of Osaka, Nagoya University, NUS).   Key Responsibilities:    The candidate will be given opportunities and is expected to design and execute experiments independently. He/she is also expected to interpret experimental results, and author papers in high-quality journals in areas that are related to the research. The candidate should demonstrate excellent communication skills and should have a strong passion and commitment to science. He/she will also work closely with the Principal Investigators to help supervise and train students and junior lab members and to ensure smooth functioning of an active research program. The candidate will have the opportunity to explore his/her own interests across functions. Job Requirements: Ph.D. level scientist proficient in animal experiments, particularly in spinal cord injury microsurgery and neural tissue engineering. Expertise in rodent models, immunofluorescent and histochemical staining of tissues, evaluation of tissue response/interactions using fluorescent microscopy (confocal) imaging. Expertise in western blotting, quantitative RT-PCR is a plus. Strong ability to communicate effectively orally and in written form, and experienced in writing manuscripts. Strong ability to perform self-directed work. Strong organizational skills and proactive personality with outstanding motivation, creativity, critical and analytical thinking skills, strong scientific commitment and ability to work as a team. Starting salaries will depend on candidate’s qualification and experience. Candidates are expected to start March 2026. Review of applicants will continue until positions are filled. Applicants should submit a cover letter indicating their area of interest and how they intend to participate and contribute to the research, complete curriculum vitae and addresses of three references in a single PDF document to Dr. Sing Yian CHEW ( sychew@ntu.edu.sg ) and Prof. Shawn Je ( shawn.je@duke-nus.edu.sg ).   We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Earthquake-Engineering-_R00025146-1": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Earthquake Engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-08\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Institute of Catastrophe Risk Management (ICRM) was launched in January 2010 and aims to be the first multi-disciplinary and leading catastrophe risk management research institute of its kind in Asia. The Institute aims to help the regional and international communities to better understand the characteristics of Asia’s risks related to natural disasters such as earthquakes, tsunamis, volcanic eruptions, typhoons, floods and droughts. We are looking for a Research Fellow in Earthquake Engineer to support ICRM’s work in NatCat exposure and risk, as particularly related to earthquake damage and losses to building stocks. The role will focus on modelling of ground motions during earthquakes and structural responses under earthquake-induced ground motions. Key Responsibilities: ICRM is looking for a modeller for earthquake hazards and building structural loss. The ideal candidate should be a self-motivated, pro-active, results-oriented professional with an ability to work with minimal supervision in dealing with data uncertainties. He/she will be responsible for Modelling propagation of earthquake motion from source to site Perform probabilistic seismic hazard analysis (PSHA)   Perform structural calculations to quantify damage and loss under earthquake-induced ground motions Assess occurrence frequencies of such loss events including probabilistic seismic risk assessments Job Requirements: A PhD degree in Civil Engineering or Earthquake Engineering in a closely relevant field. Familiarity with earthquake data, models and software used in earthquake hazard and loss modelling. Demonstrated competence of programming languages, such as Matlab, R, or Python, within a GIS environment Ability to publish and communicate effectively to both technical and non-technical audiences Ability to advance other research areas in emerging risks such as related to urban lifelines and cascading failures We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Project-Officer--AI-Powered-Road-Safety-Management-_R00025141": {
      "title": "Project Officer AI Powered Road Safety Management",
      "description": "Careers Skip to main content Sign In Search for Jobs The page you are looking for doesn't exist. Search for Jobs © 2026 Workday, Inc. All rights reserved."
