    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Early-Warning-System-_R00025138": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Early Warning System)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-08\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nIn this rapidly changing world, the Centre for Climate Change and Environmental Health (CCEH) is advancing research on how climate change, air pollution, and extreme environmental conditions affect human health. By bringing together expertise across environmental science, exposure assessment, epidemiology, public health, and predictive modelling, CCEH develops evidence-based solutions to support healthier and more climate-resilient communities in Singapore and across Asia. Within CCEH, the Climate and AI team, led by Prof. Steve Yim, investigates the interactions between climate, air quality, environmental hazards, and human health using integrated observations, forecasting systems, artificial intelligence, and statistical approaches. The team works across multiple spatial and temporal scales to improve the prediction of environmental health risks and to generate scientific evidence that supports public health policy, workforce protection, and climate adaptation strategies. Key Responsibilities : The position will support the development of environmental health early warning systems and predictive models for climate-sensitive hazards and their impacts on human health. The role will contribute to research on the forecasting and risk assessment of extreme heat, humid heat stress, air pollution episodes, transboundary haze, extreme weather events, and other climate-related environmental hazards across Singapore and Southeast Asia. The successful candidate will analyse and integrate climate, environmental, health, and socioeconomic datasets using advanced statistical, spatiotemporal, and artificial intelligence methods; develop and evaluate hazard forecasting and health-risk prediction frameworks; contribute to research publications, technical reports, and decision-support tools; and collaborate with research partners and stakeholders to strengthen early warning capabilities, climate services, and evidence-based adaptation planning. Job Requirements : Have a Ph.D. degree in atmospheric science, climate science, environmental health, environmental science, computer science, artificial intelligence, data science, public health, epidemiology, geography, or another related discipline. Have strong research experience in artificial intelligence, machine learning, deep learning, environmental modelling, climate-health research, early warning systems, or related fields. Have strong programming and computational skills in Python, R, MATLAB, or related analytical and machine learning frameworks (e.g., PyTorch, TensorFlow, Scikit-learn). Have good organizational and communication skills and evidence of the ability to work independently as well as collaboratively across interdisciplinary and multi-institutional teams. Evidence of excellent report writing skills, and the ability to contribute to scientific publications and other research outputs. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant--AI---Robotics---Automation---Computer-Science-_R00025139": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (AI / Robotics / Automation / Computer Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-08\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering (MAE) is a robust, dynamic and multi-disciplinary international research community comprising of world-class scientists and bright students. MAE prides itself in its excellent research capabilities in areas including advanced manufacturing, aerospace, biomedical, energy, industrial engineering, maritime engineering, robotics, etc. The school is equipped with state-of-the-art research infrastructure, housing a comprehensive range of cluster laboratories, test bedding facilities, research centres/institutes and corporate laboratories. Cutting-edge research in MAE addresses the immediate needs of our industries and supports the nation’s long-term development strategies. In the new era of industrial 4.0 and sustainable living, MAE is rigorous in developing new competencies to support the growth and competitiveness of our engineering sector in the global landscape. MAE has grown to be leader in Engineering Research, ranking amongst the top engineering schools in the world. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/mae/research . The research assistant will focus on Vision-Language Model based situation awareness and decision-making for autonomous vehicles Key Responsibilities: The research assistant will be leading the development of Vision-Language Model based situation awareness and decision-making models for autonomous vehicles. The work will involve model training, test rig set-up, and experimental validation Job Requirements: The candidate must at least have a Bachelor's Degree in AI, Robotics, Automation, Computer Science, etc. Strong background in AI, deep learning, autonomous driving, natural language processing. Candidates having relevant research or working experience in AI, deep learning, natural language processing, and AI decision-making algorithms for end-to-end autonomous driving will be preferred. Good communications skills and the ability to work independently and facilitate projects with minimal supervision. Able to contribute to Journal/Conference papers with good presentation skills. Able to plan and organize well and adhere to deadlines We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Director--Industry_R00025123": {
      "title": "Director, Industry",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-08\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Director (Industry) plays a pivotal role in driving strategic partnerships with industry, public agencies and international universities / institutions to enhance research, innovation, and commercialization efforts. This role oversees engagement initiatives, secures industry funding and aligns academic expertise with industry needs to enhance the university’s impact and reputation. Responsibilities Strategic Planning and Partnership Development Develop and implement a comprehensive strategic plan to identify opportunities for cultivating and building a robust pipeline of partnerships with key industry stakeholders. Formulate and execute strategies to strengthen and expand partnerships with industry leaders, advancing the university’s strategic objectives. Identify and capitalize on university-wide opportunities to collaborate with industry leaders, ensuring alignment with institutional goals. Foster strong partnerships with industry sectors and public agencies, promoting engagement across a dynamic cross-industry ecosystem. Curriculum Innovation and Industry Integration Design strategies to integrate academic curricula with global and industry trends, ensuring relevance and future-readiness of educational programs. Promote greater involvement of industry professionals in curriculum design, teaching, and mentorship programs to bridge the gap between academia and the workforce. Encourage the integration of interdisciplinary and experiential learning opportunities, such as internships, industry-led projects, and hands-on training. Leadership and Oversight Lead and oversee key university-industry partnership initiatives at the university level, ensuring alignment with institutional goals and priorities. Champion innovative university-industry initiatives in research and education, enhancing the university’s competitive edge in global and regional contexts. Work closely with stakeholders across colleges, schools, and research centers to facilitate cross-functional synergies and streamline initiatives for greater impact. Governance and Performance Monitoring Oversee central governance and data management processes to ensure alignment with institutional objectives, track progress, and measure performance effectively. Establish policies for research funding, publication standards, and collaborations with industry to support high-impact initiatives and maintain compliance with global standards. Promote success stories of university-industry collaborations to attract additional partnerships and funding opportunities. Stakeholder Engagement and Communication Organize industry-academia conferences, networking events, and expos to showcase collaborative achievements and strengthen ties with industry stakeholders. Address resistance to change by engaging stakeholders in co-creation processes and maintaining transparent communication throughout all initiatives. Build trust and buy-in among faculty, staff, and external partners through clear and consistent messaging. Capacity Building and Change Management Train faculty and staff to adapt to new collaboration models and evolving industry expectations, fostering a culture of continuous improvement and adaptability. Promote professional development opportunities to equip academic and administrative teams with the skills needed to sustain and grow partnerships. Requirements Minimum Bachelor’s degree with strong administration management experience in a Research & Development environment. Significant experience in a leadership role involving university-industry collaborations, strategic planning or organization development.  Proven track record of successfully managing and expanding large-scale partnerships and initiatives. Proven leadership experience in managing strategic partnerships and collaborations, preferably within an academic or industry setting. Strong understanding of global and industry trends in education, research, and technology. Exceptional communication, negotiation and stakeholder engagement skills. Ability to drive cross-functional initiatives and manage complex projects with multiple stakeholders. Expertise in governance, data management and performance measurement. A visionary mindset with a demonstrated ability to innovate and lead change effectively. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Project-Officer--Materials-Science---Engineering-Materials-Science-Polymer-Chemistry-Chemical-Engineering-Nanotechnology-Physics-Electrochemistry-_R00025126": {
      "title": "Project Officer (Materials Science & Engineering/Materials Science/Polymer Chemistry/Chemical Engineering/Nanotechnology/Physics/Electrochemistry)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-07\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nEstablished in 2010, the Energy Research Institute @ NTU (ERI@N) is a pan-university research institute that focuses on systems-level research for tropical megacities. It performs translational research that covers the energy value chain from generation to innovative end-use solutions, motivated by industrialisation and deployment. ERI@N has multiple Interdisciplinary Research Programmes which focus on translational Research, Development & Deployment which focus on specific area of the energy value chain, and a number of Living labs and Testbeds which facilitate large scale technology deployment enabling validation and demonstration of real-world applications. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/erian Key job purpose : The successful candidate will support the characterisation and evaluation of carbonaceous materials for lithium-ion and next-generation battery applications. The role will involve assisting in materials analysis, electrochemical testing, and data collection to support ongoing research and development activities related to battery materials and electrode performance. The candidate will work closely with the research team to study the structure, morphology, and electrochemical behaviour of carbon materials such as graphite, hard carbon, and conductive additives used in battery systems Key Responsibilities: The candidate’s scope of work will include the following: Assist in the characterisation of carbonaceous materials (e.g., graphite, hard carbon, soft carbon, graphene, carbon nanotubes) used in lithium-ion batteries. Support routine material characterisation and analysis using techniques such as: a. X-ray diffraction (XRD) b. Raman spectroscopy c. BET surface area analysis d. Scanning electron microscopy (SEM) e. Thermogravimetric analysis (TGA) Assist with battery electrode preparation and coin cell assembly. Conduct basic electrochemical testing, including: a. Cyclic voltammetry (CV) b. Galvanostatic charge–discharge testing c. Electrochemical impedance spectroscopy (EIS) Collect, organise, and maintain experimental data and laboratory records. Prepare summaries, technical slides, and reports for internal discussions. Support general laboratory operations, equipment maintenance, and safety procedures. Work collaboratively with team members on battery materials research projects Job Requirements: Possess a Bachelor’s Degree in Materials Science & Engineering. in Materials Science, Polymer Chemistry, Chemical Engineering, or a related discipline (e.g., Nanotechnology, Physics, or Electrochemistry). Basic knowledge in the characterisation of carbonaceous materials or battery electrode materials. Hands-on experience will be advantageous. Basic or prior knowledge in solid-state characterisation techniques, particularly Raman spectroscopy, XRD, SEM/TEM, and BET surface analysis. Experience with Li-ion battery fabrication and electrochemical testing (e.g., coin cells, pouch cells, or prototype assemblies) is strongly preferred. Familiarity with surface functionalisation, defect engineering, and doping strategies for carbon materials is an advantage. Demonstrated ability to support the team and contribute creatively to multidisciplinary R&D projects. Evidence of scientific contribution in relevant research areas is strongly preferred (FYP, URECA). Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English, with the ability to support, prepare technical reports and presentations effectively. A collaborative team player with strong interpersonal skills and a proactive, willingness to learn mindset. Ability to work under pressure, manage multiple tasks, and meet tight project deadlines. Demonstrated sense of responsibility, attention to detail, and commitment to high-quality work We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Physical-Sciences-Engineering-_R00025119": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Physical Sciences/Engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-07\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJoin Our Team at the School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore The School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences (SPMS) at NTU Singapore hosts research and education activities in two divisions: Division of Mathematical Sciences (MAS) and Division of Physics and Applied Physics (PAP). MAS covers diverse topics ranging from pure mathematics to the applications of mathematics in cryptography, computing, business, and finance. PAP covers many areas of fundamental and applied physics, including quantum information, condensed matter physics, biophysics, and photonics. Over the years, SPMS has attracted talented individuals from around the world and Singapore to join as scientific leaders and researchers. Join the laboratory of Prof Lew Wen Siang at SPMS. We are seeking a Research Fellow to contribute to a project focused on the Development of Advanced MRAM Technology for Artificial Intelligence Memory and Smart Sensing .   Key Responsibilities: Design and develop high-performance MRAM devices for advanced computing memory applications. Manage project activities by liaising with international semiconductor companies, research institutes, and foundry partners. Lead the preparation of technical write-ups for quarterly industry press releases related to the joint development programme. Perform physical vapour deposition (PVD) of MRAM structures on 300 mm wafers using the ULVAC Entron system. Coordinate with circuit designers and semiconductor foundries on CMOS front-end wafer development and back-end-of-line integration processes. Conduct MRAM electrical transport measurements using probe stations and bonded memory chips, including device-level reliability testing such as endurance and retention measurements. Fabricate MRAM devices using advanced lithography techniques, including optical lithography and/or electron-beam lithography. Perform device processing using ICP-RIE and/or ion milling techniques. Analyse structural, electrical, and materials characterisation results, including scanning electron microscopy, X-ray diffraction, transmission electron microscopy, and related techniques. Job Requirements: PhD degree in a relevant field of physical sciences or engineering. At least 6 years of relevant experience in a similar role or technical discipline, including PhD research experience in non-volatile memory or a closely related area. Strong experience in semiconductor wafer-level device development. Proficiency in semiconductor processing techniques, particularly those relevant to advanced memory device fabrication. Good programming skills; experience in device modelling or simulation would be an advantage. Strong analytical and data visualisation skills, with the ability to interpret and present complex technical results clearly. Ability to work independently, develop practical solutions under tight timelines, and maintain a high level of accuracy and attention to detail. Excellent organisational and time management skills. Good communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to prepare project reports and deliver technical presentations to academic and industry stakeholders. The College of Science seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager--Postgraduate---Continuing-Education-Programmes--LKCMedicine-_R00025117": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager, Postgraduate & Continuing Education Programmes [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-07\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. LKCMedicine is seeking a proactive and meticulous Senior Assistant Manager to join the Graduate Programmes team. The successful candidate will be responsible for the end-to-end management of Continuing Education and Training (CET) programmes and will oversee all finance-related operations for the CET portfolio. This pivotal role requires strong organisational skills, financial acumen, and the ability to manage multiple complex projects in a fast-paced environment. The Senior Assistant Manager will work closely with faculty, internal stakeholders (e.g., Finance, Legal), and external partners to ensure the successful delivery and financial sustainability of programmes targeted at healthcare professionals. Responsibilities: CET Programme Management & Operations Oversee the end-to-end operational planning and execution of CET programmes, from setup and scheduling to final delivery and feedback collection. Manage the full learner lifecycle, including admissions processing, enrolment, matriculation, learner communications, and post-programme support. Serve as the primary point of contact for CET learners, providing high-quality support and managing all enquiries. Collaborate with faculty, adjuncts, and internal departments to ensure smooth programme delivery. Provide administrative support to Course Directors and assist with programme-related tasks to ensure smooth and efficient operations. Manage all programme logistics, including scheduling, venue/platform booking, and the preparation and distribution of course materials. Continuously review and improve administrative processes to enhance programme efficiency, scalability, and the overall learner experience. Ensure all programmes are compliant with university policies and external requirements. CET Financial Management & Analysis Lead the annual CET budgeting cycle, working with programme leads to develop realistic financial targets. Develop, manage, and monitor individual programme budgets, ensuring alignment with the School's strategic goals and financial targets. Monitor revenue and expenditures closely; conduct regular variance analysis and financial reconciliations for the entire CET portfolio. Develop and maintain financial dashboards and reports to provide management with real-time visibility into programme performance, profitability, and key financial metrics. Prepare and present accurate and timely financial reports, summaries, and insights to senior management to support strategic decision-making. Manage procurement, invoicing, and billing processes, serving as the key liaison with the university's central finance office. Oversee the timely and accurate processing of payments for adjunct faculty, supervisors, and external vendors. Strategic, Contract & Stakeholder Management Manage the financial administration of external funding, including SSG grant claims, reporting, and supporting any related audit requirements. Support the Senior Assistant Director in developing business proposals and detailed financial models for new programme initiatives. Serve as the primary financial and administrative liaison for external partners (e.g., healthcare groups) regarding programme costs, billing, and financial reporting. Contribute to cross-functional projects related to education innovation, system implementation, and operational efficiency. Undertake other duties as required to support the School’s strategic goals. Requirements: A recognised degree in Business, Finance, Accounting or related discipline. Minimum 7–8 years of relevant working experience, preferably in programme management, finance, or administration. Strong financial acumen with hands-on experience in budgeting, financial reporting, and analysis. Excellent project management, organisational, and multitasking skills with a keen eye for detail. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (especially Excel for financial management) and PowerBI (for dashboard creation and management). A proactive and collaborative team player with strong interpersonal and communication skills. Demonstrated ability to work independently, manage competing priorities, and meet tight deadlines. Prior experience in the education or healthcare sectors is highly desirable. Experience working in a higher education or training institute environment. Familiarity with SkillsFuture Singapore (SSG) funding schemes, claims processes, and compliance requirements. This is a 3 years contract appointment. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Communication-Psychology-Public-Health-Behavioral-Sciences-Social-Science-_R00025096-1": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Communication/Psychology/Public Health/Behavioral Sciences/Social Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-07\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University (NTU) is looking for a Research Associate under the project Transforming Health Behaviour Insights through AI Driven Segmentation Models. The advertised position will be based in the Wee Kim Wee School of Communication and Information (WKWSCI) and work under the supervision of Principal Investigator Prof Shirley S. Ho. Focusing on the social science components of the project, the Research Associate will work with the PI and research team to drive the operationalisation of a large-scale lifestyle and values survey aimed at a psychosocial segmentation of the population cohort across Singapore’s adult population. This research will identify attitudinal and socio-cultural variables that underpin trust, risk perception, and receptiveness to health messaging. The scope includes surveys on health behaviours, lifestyle practices, and psychological traits, forming the empirical basis for the AI-driven population segmentation models. The Research Associate is expected to support a range of research and administrative works within the project, from data collection, data analysis, to research presentation, manuscript preparation, and administrative tasks associated with the project and within the team. This job contributes to the overall mission and objectives of NTU by nurturing leaders through research, attracting the right talent that the University needs to sustain organizational growth, and retaining employees to perform and sustain a performance culture. Key Responsibilities: To engage in literature searches and manuscript preparation. To work with vendors to implement and oversee large-scale surveys (approx. 5,000 participants across Singapore). To conduct data cleaning, uploading, and management. To conduct statistical analysis of data. To coordinate with participants and stakeholders. To contribute to research publications, presentations, and progress reports. To engage in the dissemination of research findings with the support of and under the supervision of the Principal Investigator. To carry out administrative work and other research work associated with the project. Job Requirements: Master’s degree in communication, psychology, public health, behavioral sciences or a related social science discipline. Fundamentals of survey research and quantitative data analytical skills (e.g., SPSS, MPLUS, or R). Preference with be given to candidates who meet the following requirements: A team player in a project setting, also with ability to work independently. Experience in a multi-cultural team environment. Initiative and good interpersonal skills. Knowledge of quantitative methodology and (or) computational data analytics. Prior experience in communication, psychology, public health, or behavioural science research. Interested applicants are invited to submit a cover letter, full CV and names and contact details of three referees in one document. Enquiries about this position can be made to Prof. Shirley Ho at tsyho@ntu.edu.sg Kindly note that only short-listed candidates will be contacted for interview. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Engineer-I--Resilient-Urbanisation---Natural-Ecosystems-_R00024870": {
      "title": "Research Engineer I (Resilient Urbanisation & Natural Ecosystems)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Civil and Environmental Engineering (CEE) is a leading school for Sustainable Built Environment. The School plays an integral role in spearheading tertiary education, advancing research innovations and providing professional services in a number of key disciplines in Civil and Environmental Engineering and Maritime Studies fields, with the objective of contributing to the technological and economic advancement of Singapore and beyond. The School’s mission in research is to achieve excellence by providing a conducive and intellectually stimulating environment to enable high quality work in strategic directions that are of significant impact to industry, science and technology. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/cee We are looking for a Research Engineer I to join a CITIES OF TOMORROW (CoT) R&D project for VERTICAL 5: CITY IN NATURE. The project plays a pivotal role in ensuring a resilient urban environment against climate change and contributes to NTU strategic research in Resilient Urbanisation & Natural Ecosystems that is aligned with Singapore’s national Research, Innovation and Enterprise 2025 plan. Key Responsibilities: Assist in field and laboratory tests Develop test protocols Compile test data and maintain database Conduct analysis and evaluation Assist to prepare budgets, reports and papers Job Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in relevant discipline or related field Ability to work both indoors and outdoors Good written and oral communication skills for report writing Knowledge of software like Python and 3D modelling software will be an advantage. Class 3 driving license (Singapore) will be an advantage. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Clinical-Research-Officer--Operations---LKCMedicine-_R00025081-1": {
      "title": "Senior Executive (Clinical Research Officer, Operations) [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. LKCMedicine is looking for a Senior Executive (Clinical Research Officer, Operations) who is self-motivated, proactive in problem solving and a strong team player. The candidate will enjoy staff benefits and be part of the Health for Life in Singapore (HELIOS) Study team, a flagship Singapore population health study jointly conducted by LKCMedicine, National Healthcare Group and Imperial College of London. We aim to profile the health and behavior of up to 100,000 people from the general Singapore population over the next few years. We are conducting (1) surveys on health, lifestyle and dietary habits, (2) physical and functional measurements (e.g. anthropometry, hand grip strength, treadmill walking test, spirometry, ECG, retinal imaging, arterial stiffness and skin physiology assessments and (3) biomarkers for chronic diseases.  The candidate will play a key role mainly in, but not limited to, the following roles: Maintain clear and professional communication with study participants. Able to guide participants through the study, ensuring they complete all required assessments. Administer questionnaires and perform sample and physiological data collection accurately and efficiently. Eager to develop skills and gain exposure to all aspects of study processes and tasks. Ensures minimal disruption to study operations by troubleshooting and addressing equipment failures promptly. Monitor consumables and study supplies, flagging needs for replenishment. Ensure strict adherence to study protocols, including familiarity with the Code Blue Response SOP. Adhere to Good Clinical Practice standards and HBRA requirements throughout the conduct of the study. Assist and work well with the Team Leads and colleagues. Key Competencies and Requirements: Bachelor degree in Allied Health Sciences / Biomedical Sciences or other related fields. Diploma holders with relevant experience may also apply. Ability to work independently with high levels of motivation. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. A team player, able to work well in a team to deliver good research participant care. Must pay attention to detail. Fluent in spoken and written English. Fluent in Tamil, Malay, Chinese or dialects would be of advantage. Phlebotomy skills is an advantage. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Clinical-Research-Officer--Recruitment---LKCMedicine-_R00025077-1": {
      "title": "Senior Executive (Clinical Research Officer, Recruitment) [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. LKCMedicine is looking for a Senior Executive (Clinical Research Officer, Recruitment ) who is self-motivated, proactive in problem solving and a strong team player. The candidate will enjoy staff benefits and be part of the Health for Life in Singapore (HELIOS) Study team, a flagship Singapore population health study jointly conducted by LKCMedicine, National Healthcare Group and Imperial College of London. We aim to profile the health and behavior of up to 100,000 people from the general Singapore population over the next few years. We are conducting (1) surveys on health, lifestyle and dietary habits, (2) physical and functional measurements (e.g. anthropometry, hand grip strength, treadmill walking test, spirometry, ECG, retinal imaging, arterial stiffness and skin physiology assessments and (3) biomarkers for chronic diseases.  The candidate will play a key role mainly in, but not limited to, the following roles: Maintain clear and professional communication with study participants. Screen volunteers for their eligibility to participate in the study. Schedule and send reminders to participants for research session. Maintain the study’s recruitment database. Manage appointment booking system and participant registration properly. Provide weekly recruitment reports to the study investigators. Maintains the confidentiality of personal information acquired pertaining to the study participants. Implement strategies to improve participant recruitment. Preparing and distributing outreach materials. Lead the social media strategy and provide continuous updates on the study progress via social media, as well as to other media channels. Key Competencies and Requirements: Diploma / basic degree in business management and marketing, communication or social sciences. Ability to work independently with high levels of motivation. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Able to work well in a team to deliver good research participant care. Must pay attention to detail. Fluent in spoken and written English. Fluent in Tamil, Malay, Chinese or dialects would be of advantage. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--ABM---Simulation-_R00024701": {
      "title": "Research Associate/ Research Fellow, Agent-Based Modelling & Simulation",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-03\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Civil and Environmental Engineering (CEE), Nanyang Technological University, is the host school for the project “Building Community Resilience Against Sea-Level Rise” (Grant H2_2024-3_T10). The project is funded by the National Parks Board (NParks) under the Marine Climate Change Science Coastal Protection (MCCS) call and brings together CEE and the Wee Kim Wee School of Communication and Information (WKWSCI) to integrate geospatial modelling, behavioural risk-perception research, agent-based simulation, and community engagement design in support of Singapore’s coastal adaptation efforts. We are looking for a Research Associate/Research Fellow to design and deliver Module D of the NParks MCCS project: the agent-based modelling (ABM) and simulation work that forecasts long-term community adaptation to sea-level rise. We welcome applicants from computational social science, complex systems, operations research, or related computational fields. Key Responsibilities: Design, calibrate, and validate an Agent-Based Model for 15-year adaptation forecasting (Module D). Use archetype outputs (from latent-class analysis) as inputs to ABM agent profiles. Conduct scenario planning to forecast long-term adaptation trends. Contribute to project reports, conference presentations, and top-tier journal publications. Job Requirements (Essential): PhD, or a strong master’s in computer science, Computational Social Science, Complex Systems, Operations Research, or a related field. Strong agent-based modelling expertise in Python (Mesa) and/or NetLogo. Experience with empirical ABM calibration. A track record of ABM-related publications (simulation or computational-social-science publications also considered). Job Requirements (Desirable): Experience developing user-facing or handover-ready simulation interfaces (this project includes a simulation interface deliverable, developed by the Research Fellow with support from the project team). Experience with Monte Carlo and sensitivity analysis. Experience contributing to workshops or training materials for agency handover of research tools. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Postdoctoral-Fellow--Chinese-Political-Thought-_R00025046": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Fellow (Chinese Political Thought)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-03\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Social Sciences at NTU Singapore is part of the College of Humanities, Arts and Social Sciences (CoHASS), which promotes interdisciplinary research and teaching across the full range of social science disciplines. Ranked among the world's top universities, NTU combines rigorous scholarship with an orientation toward addressing major societal challenges. The Postdoctoral Fellow will join the research project 1980: The Global Electoral Moment — China and Beyond , hosted at the Public Policy and Global Affairs Programme (PPGA) and led by Nanyang Assistant Professor Simon Sihang Luo. The project examines the lived experience of electoral founding moments in China and beyond, with attention to the political sentiments, institutional visions, and ideological contests they generated. The Fellow will conduct original archival and textual research on modern and contemporary Chinese political thought, develop an independent research agenda within the project's broader themes, and contribute to collaborative publications and working papers. The role also involves participation in project-related academic events and the broader intellectual life of the PPGA. Key Responsibilities Conduct original archival and textual research on modern and contemporary Chinese political thought, with particular attention to Chinese-language primary sources Develop and advance an independent research agenda aligned with the project's themes of electoral politics, institutional imagination, and intellectual history Contribute to collaborative research outputs, including peer-reviewed publications, working papers, and project reports Assist in the organisation of project-related academic events, including workshops, conferences, and invited speaker series Participate actively in the intellectual life of the Public Policy and Global Affairs Programme (PPGA) at NTU Support grant-related administrative tasks and research documentation as required Job Requirements PhD in Political Theory, Intellectual History, or a relevant field, with a focus on Chinese political thought Strong research record commensurate with career stage Native or full professional proficiency in Chinese - essential for data analysis and communication with stakeholders Demonstrated expertise in archival research, including facility with handwritten Chinese-language primary sources Ability to engage with comparative and global frameworks in the study of Chinese political institutions Interested applicants are to apply online with your CV and Cover Letter. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTUGillman-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturer-in-Curating-Residencies_R00025073": {
      "title": "Part Time Lecturer in Curating Residencies",
