    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Assistant-Manager--Operations--Business-Development-_R00024997": {
      "title": "Senior Assistant Manager, Operations (Business Development)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nReporting to the Centre Manager at the NTU Centre in Computational Technologies for Finance (CCTF), the Senior Assistant Manager will lead and manage the full spectrum of operational, financial, and administrative functions related to the Centre’s professional training programmes. The incumbent will play a key role in ensuring seamless programme delivery, stakeholder engagement, and regulatory compliance, while contributing to the strategic development and long-term sustainability of the Centre’s training portfolio. This role requires a proactive and resourceful individual with strong coordination, analytical, and project management skills, capable of driving operational excellence and continuous improvement. •    Programme Development & Strategic Execution Lead the design and development of training programmes aligned with industry needs and organisational goals. Conduct in-depth market analysis and stakeholder engagement to identify emerging trends and learning gaps. Drive the end-to-end programme lifecycle – from conceptualisation to evaluation – working closely with academic and industry experts. Propose new training initiatives and strategic partnerships to expand the Centre’s outreach and impact. •    Business Development & Stakeholder Management Develop and implement strategic outreach plans to grow and diversify the Centre’s customer base (corporate partners, government agencies, and professionals). Build and maintain high-trust relationships with key stakeholders, including C-suite clients, faculty, and external collaborators. Represent the Centre in internal and external engagements to promote the value and impact of our training programmes. Drive customer satisfaction and retention through proactive communication and after-programme engagement. •    Programme Operations & Team Coordination Oversee the full operational management of training delivery – including scheduling, logistics, resource planning, and on-site execution. Supervise junior officers and interns, providing guidance and performance feedback to ensure operational excellence. Lead cross-functional coordination with trainers, vendors, and internal departments to ensure smooth programme delivery. Manage crisis resolution and troubleshooting during programme execution. •    Financial Planning & Budget Oversight Prepare and oversee detailed programme budgets, ensuring optimal resource allocation and cost-efficiency. Track revenue targets and perform variance analysis to support Centre’s financial sustainability goals. Liaise with Finance on invoicing, vendor payments, and grants or fund utilisation, ensuring compliance with audit requirements. •    Governance, Compliance & Quality Assurance Ensure all training activities comply with NTU’s policies, funding requirements, and relevant legal/regulatory frameworks. Champion data protection and uphold PDPA and privacy regulations in all programme operations. Implement and continually refine Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) for quality consistency. Use data analytics and participant feedback to drive continuous improvement in programme design and delivery.  Job Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in a relevant discipline, with substantial experience in programme management, business development, or related fields. Relevant work experience in similar environments will be an advantage. A self-starter, adaptable and able to multi-task in a fast-paced environment. Excellent administrative skills. Good interpersonal and communication skills.  Detail-oriented and strong organisational skills. Motivated self-starter who is comfortable working with a team, as well as independently, under tight deadlines. Strong conceptual and analytical skills. Experience or interest in Blockchain and distributed ledger technologies for applications in diverse domains will be advantageous but not mandatory.  We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate---Research-Fellow--Simulation---BioMEMS-_R00024980": {
      "title": "Research Associate / Research Fellow (Simulation & BioMEMS)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-23\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe are seeking a highly motivated Research Associate/ Research Fellow to join our advanced sensors research team at NTU MAE. The successful candidate will support multidisciplinary research activities in biomechanics, robotics, and advanced materials within the laboratory. Key Responsibilities: Support the team towards comprehensive literature reviews on injury biomechanics, physiological effects, computational modelling and related research topics. Develop, implement and validate computational simulation models for impact and injury prediction using appropriate numerical methods and software tools. Design and conduct experimental studies using instrumented human manikins and other test platforms to evaluate biomechanical responses and validate simulation results. Assist in the design, fabrication, and characterization of tissue simulants and non-Newtonian materials, including support for 3D printing and additive manufacturing processes. Develop and optimize experimental setups, testing protocols and data acquisition systems for biomechanical and robotics-related research. Analyse experimental and simulation data, prepare technical reports, and document research findings. Support the integration of advanced materials and sensing technologies into robotics and other interdisciplinary research initiatives. Inline sensor system developmental work for 3D printing of non-newtonian materials.  Optimization of hardware configurations to maintain a food-grade environment, including development of testing protocols and validation procedures. Collaborate with faculty members, researchers, students and external partners to achieve project objectives and milestones. Assist in the preparation of research publications, presentations, grant reports, and project deliverables. Maintain laboratory equipment and ensure compliance with laboratory safety procedures and research best practices. Liaise with external vendors on custom sensors and related mechanical system development.  Manage technical specifications and acceptance testing.  Coordinate technical discussions with collaborators and project stakeholders.  Track project milestones, risks, and technical deliverables. Requirements PhD's or Master's degree in Mechanical Engineering, Mechatronics, Robotics, or related discipline. Knowledge of multi-physics modelling for non-newtonian materials. Experience with 3D printing technologies, sensors, system integration, experimental testing, or measurement systems will be advantageous. Familiarity with signal processing and analysis, control systems, Python, MATLAB, C++, LabVIEW, or equivalent tools is preferred. Strong analytical, problem-solving, communication, and project coordination skills. Ability to work effectively both independently and within multidisciplinary teams. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Temporary-Executive--Event-and-Communication--LKCMedicine-_R00024978": {
      "title": "Temporary Executive, Event and Communication [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-23\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. The Communications and Outreach team is seeking a highly organised and proactive Temporary Executive, Event and Communication. The role is to support the planning and execution of a large-scale community event and various outreach activities. The successful candidate will coordinate with multiple stakeholders, manage event logistics and procurement processes, and support publicity and VIP engagement to ensure the successful delivery of School events. Responsibilities: Stakeholder and Booth Coordination Coordinate educational booths and meaningful activity stations. Work with participating departments and teams to define booth requirements, manpower deployment, logistics, and programme content. Consolidate operational requirements and ensure alignment with overall event objectives. Programme Management Support the development and execution of the event programme, including stage activities, performances, talks, demonstrations, and community engagement activities. Coordinate speakers, emcees, performers, and programme partners. Develop detailed run sheets and event-day operational plans. VIP and Guest Management Develop and manage VIP and guest invitation lists. Coordinate invitations, RSVPs, seating arrangements, protocol requirements and other arrangements. Prepare administration programme documents and support VIP hosting during events. Requirements: Diploma or degree in communications, event management, marketing, public relations, or a related discipline. Strong organisational and coordination skills, with the ability to manage multiple tasks, timelines and stakeholders concurrently. Good written and verbal communication skills, and able to engage a wide range of internal and external stakeholders professionally. Meticulous, resourceful and proactive, with a willingness to support event planning, logistics, administrative coordination and event-day operations in a dynamic environment. Candidates should be comfortable working in a fast-paced environment with occasional evening or weekend support required during key event periods. This is a 6 months temporary contract. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Communication-Studies---Psychology---Behavioral-Science-_R00024982": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Communication Studies / Psychology / Behavioral Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-23\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Wee Kim Wee School of Communication and Information (WKWSCI), together with the School of Civil and Environmental Engineering (CEE), is looking for a Research Fellow to make an important contribution to the research project: “Building community resilience against sea-level rise: Baseline, engagement strategies, and long-term adaptation” funded by the National Research Foundation. This project aims to enhance Singapore’s resilience to sea-level rise by examining public risk perception, tolerance, adaptation readiness, and long-term behavioural responses for the community (inclusive of residents and businesses). The key objectives are to (1) establish a baseline assessment of risk perception, risk tolerance, and adaptation readiness; (2) identify and analyse their underlying determinants through both self-reported and objective behavioural measures; (3) develop and map resident and business archetypes based on their attitude towards sea-level rise; (4) design targeted engagement strategies tailored to these archetypes; and (5) simulate long-term resident and business responses to adaptation interventions. The Research Fellow will work directly with the Co-PI of the project, Professor Shirley Ho, based in the Wee Kim Wee School of Communication and Information at NTU. The Research Fellow is expected to oversee and implement Modules A and C of the project: Module A: Survey design, behavioural modelling, data collection for risk perception baseline Module C: Design and evaluation of engagement strategies (6×4 factorial experiments) Key Responsibilities:  (1) Survey instruments and focus group/interview guides for resident and business segments (2) Behavioural experiment design and execution for risk perception and adaptation readiness (3) Risk Perception and Adaptation Readiness Report (contributing author on engagement chapters) (4) Data-driven framework for climate risk communication (integrating gamification, VR, behavioural science) (5) Conference presentations (2 international conferences under Prof. Shirley Ho) (6) Contribution to at least 2 journal articles in top 10% journals (7) Work associated with the program of research as necessary. Job Requirements:  (1) PhD in Communication, Psychology, Sociology, Social Science , or a related social science field (2) Strong background in survey design, psychometric instrument development, and behavioural experiments (3) Experience with risk perception, science/climate communication, or public engagement research (4) Proficiency in quantitative analysis (R, Stata, or SPSS): factor analysis, ANOVA; SEM (R/lavaan or SPSS AMOS); LCA (R/poLCA, Mplus, or Stata) (5) Qualitative research skills: focus group facilitation, qualitative data analysis (NVivo) (6) Familiarity with factorial experimental design (7) Strong academic writing skills for top-tier journal publication Interested applicants are invited to submit a cover letter, full CV and names and contact details of three referees in one document. Please note that only shortlisted candidates will be contacted for interview. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive-Assistant-Manager--Research-Admin_R00023662": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Research Admin",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-07\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nEstablished in 1981, the School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering (EEE) https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University (NTU). Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research. It is one of the largest and most research-active EEE schools globally, with more than 120 faculty and over 5,000 undergraduate and postgraduate students.  We are seeking a highly motivated individual to join our Research Administration Office as an Assistant Manager. As an Assistant Manager, you will support the efficient execution and compliance of research grants, manage fund utilisation, and coordinate research manpower and procurement activities. You will work closely with faculty, research groups, and internal administrative units to ensure that research projects are delivered smoothly and in accordance with university and funding requirements. You will also support research-related events and contribute to digitalisation and process improvements within the School. Key Responsibilities: Provide comprehensive administrative support to faculty including procurement, claims, travel arrangements and documentation submissions. Support pre- and post-award grant administration including proposal preparation, reporting, compliance and documentation requirements. Monitor grant expenditure, burn rates, budget utilisation and timelines, and highlight risks for PI intervention. Coordinate procurement for research equipment, consumables, software and services in accordance with DOA and grant funding terms. Support recruitment and appointment processes for research manpower (e.g., RAs, RFs, Postdocs), including contract renewals and onboarding. Organise and support research seminars, academic visits and research-related events, including logistics, funding paperwork and documentation. Liaise with Research Office, Finance, HR, vendors and external stakeholders to resolve budgetary, compliance or process-related issues. Maintain accurate datasets for research reporting and performance indicators for internal and external submissions. Contribute to workflow digitalisation, dashboard development and process improvements to enhance operational efficiency. Support academic processes such as exam administration, and mark entry. Provide secretariat support for committees and meetings, including agenda preparation, minute-taking and follow-up tracking. Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree.  At least 3 years of relevant experience in research administration, grants management, procurement, research finance, or project coordination (experience in a tertiary or research environment preferred). Strong communication, good organisational, and stakeholder management skills. Ability to work collaboratively in a fast-paced diverse team environment.  Previous experience in data analytics or statistical analysis is advantageous. Experience or IT skillsets with workflow automation, data digitalisation, reporting tools or AI-based tools will be considered an advantage. Experience in budget management, project coordination and stakeholder engagement, with capacity to support multiple stakeholders and diverse administrative functions. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Visiting-Associate-Professor-in-Visual-Communication_R00024418": {
      "title": "Visiting Associate Professor in Visual Communication",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-23\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nVisiting Associate Professor Position in Visual Communication The School of Art, Design and Media (ADM) at Nanyang Technological University Singapore (NTU) invites applications for a one-year Visiting Associate Professor position in Visual Communication. ADM is part of the College of Humanities, Arts and Social Sciences (COHASS). This position is intended for eminent overseas academics such as international prize recipients or distinguished scholars whose presence will enhance the academic standing of the faculty. The primary responsibility of this role is teaching. However, there are opportunities for candidates to incorporate their research interest(s) in the course syllabi as well as collaborations with other faculty within ADM. Therefore, candidates should be able to demonstrate a strong teaching track record in a current or previous Associate Professor academic level position. We seek candidates with expertise in one or more areas of Visual Communication, including fields such as, but not limited to, graphic design, editorial design, typography and typeface design, illustration, visual identity, production, concept development, design criticism, motion graphic, curatorial design, and exhibition design. The successful candidate will be responsible for the delivery of undergraduate courses in Visual Communication. There are opportunities to advise on curricular direction and to develop courses, and to provide technical review and feedback on facilities and equipment for pedagogical needs. The candidate is expected to bring international visibility to the school through continued high quality academic scholarship and/or impactful creative activity. The school expects a variety of service duties, including school and university committee service, and coordination of courses. Responsibilities include but are not limited to 1. Deliver 2 courses a semester in Visual Communication 2. Provide advice and expertise to identify and expand areas of curricular development 3. Provide up-to-date technical expertise to review and advise on technologies for teaching needs 4. Take on pathway coordination role and attending academic meetings Successful candidates should have a terminal degree (MFA, PhD or Practice PhD) in Visual Communication/Graphic Design, or equivalent area of expertise. In exceptional cases, an MA supported by significant professional experience can also be considered. The candidate should have a strong track record of teaching experience at the university level. Preference will be given to the candidate with substantial industry experience and good collaborations at the international level. Applicants are invited to submit their applications through the NTU career portal by clicking on the “Apply” button above. Please provide the following in your application: 1. Cover letter; 2. Curriculum vitae (including records of competitive grants and graduate supervision, if applicable); 3. Teaching statement; 4. Teaching evaluation; 5. Research statement; 6. Writing samples or creative portfolio; The closing date for applications is 31 July 2026. Only shortlisted candidates will be notified via email. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Bioimaging-_R00024959": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Bioimaging)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-22\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering (MAE) is a robust, dynamic and multi-disciplinary international research community comprising of world-class scientists and bright students. MAE prides itself in its excellent research capabilities in areas including advanced manufacturing, aerospace, biomedical, energy, industrial engineering, maritime engineering, robotics, etc. The school is equipped with state-of-the-art research infrastructure, housing a comprehensive range of cluster laboratories, test bedding facilities, research centres/institutes and corporate laboratories. Cutting-edge research in MAE addresses the immediate needs of our industries and supports the nation’s long-term development strategies. In the new era of industrial 4.0 and sustainable living, MAE is rigorous in developing new competencies to support the growth and competitiveness of our engineering sector in the global landscape. MAE has grown to be leader in Engineering Research, ranking amongst the top engineering schools in the world. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/mae/research . The School of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering (MAE) is seeking to hire a Research Fellow To design and advance the research activities of the centre in bioimaging projects. Perform research in experimental optics, bioimaging, spectroscopy, metrology and develop novel approaches for optical and nonlinear optical experiments and instrumentation. The position offers the opportunity to do research work in collaboration with external partners. Key Responsibilities: The RF will support focused research activities at COLE. He/ She will assist the Principal Investigators (PIs) in the successful execution of the projects and will also be encouraged to introduce new ideas and projects. The roles of this position include: Design and conduct bioimaging experiments using optical, fluorescence, confocal, multiphoton, photoacoustic, or other advanced microscopy and imaging modalities Prepare and handle biological samples, including cells, tissues, organoids, or in vivo models, in accordance with biosafety and ethical protocols. Conduct and coordinate research within NTU and collaborators in line with its research strategy and under the supervision of the PIs and Collaborators. Manage the research project in a team-based, cross-functional research environment, which includes mentoring students and working collaborators, technical and other support staff. Publish research outcomes in journals of international standing; Attend and present research findings and papers at academic meetings and contribute to the external visibility of the Centre. Draft research reports for PIs and undertake specific roles and management functions as may be reasonably required by the PIs. Assist in drafting project proposals. Attend meetings and participate (where necessary) in other committees and working groups. Ensure compliance with health and safety in all aspects of the research work. The research staff is expected to work with the PI and other team members for doing R&D and take key role for the development of the systems for bioimaging and metrology Conduct and coordinate research within NTU and collaborating partners in line with its research strategy under the supervision of the PIs and collaborators Publish research outcomes in journals of international standing; Attend and present research findings and papers at academic meetings and contribute to the external visibility of the centre. Draft research reports for PIs and undertake specific roles and management functions as may be reasonably required by the PIs. Requirements: PhD in Optical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Precision Engineering, Electronics Engineering, Physics or a similar discipline with optics, bioimaging, spectroscopy and instrumentation background Previous experience in optics, bioimaging, optical measurement technologies, spectroscopy, Raman spectroscopy and metrology are desirable Strong background in biological imaging principles and optical instrumentation Hands‑on experience with one or more bioimaging techniques (e.g. fluorescence microscopy, confocal microscopy, live‑cell imaging, photoacoustics) Expertise in handling and maintenance of high-power CW and pulsed laser systems, spectrometers, high-resolution cameras, and delicate optical components are desirable Expertise in advanced data analysis techniques (Machine learning and Deep learning) would be an added advantage Possess good programming, optical instrumentation, automation and data processing skills (e.g. C++, LabVIEW, Zemax, OSLO, TracePro, MATLAB, Python, ImageJ) Proven publication track record would be an advantage We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Hwa-Chong-International-School---Tooh-Fee-San-Distinguished-Professorship-in-Education-and-Artificial-Intelligence--NIE-NTU-_R00024911": {
      "title": "Hwa Chong International School – Tooh Fee San Distinguished Professorship in Education and Artificial Intelligence (NIE/NTU)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-22\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nHwa Chong International School – Tooh Fee San Distinguished Professorship in Education and Artificial Intelligence National Institute of Education (NIE), Nanyang Technological University (NTU), Singapore Overview The National Institute of Education (NIE) is among the world’s top education institutes, recognised for its excellence in teacher education and educational research.  NIE has played a key and pivotal role in shaping and developing Singapore’s teaching profession and landscape through evidence-informed, practice-focused and values-based programmes and initiatives. An autonomous institute situated within the research-intensive Nanyang Technological University (NTU), NIE is consistently ranked within the top 10 in the world for research impact in the field of Education. The Opportunity NIE invites applications for the Hwa Chong International School (HCIS) – Tooh Fee San Distinguished Professorship in Education and Artificial Intelligence . The distinguished professorship will champion transformative research and innovation at the intersection of artificial intelligence (AI) and education. The HCIS – Tooh Fee San Distinguished Professor in Education and Artificial Intelligence will Lead cutting-edge interdisciplinary research in AI and education Drive innovation in the design, implementation, and evaluation of AI-enabled pedagogies, curricula, and assessment Translate research into real-world educational impact, including collaboration with schools as testbeds for innovation Foster international collaborations with leading academics, industry partners, and educational institutions Contribute to strengthening Singapore’s position as a global hub for AI-enabled education Provide intellectual leadership through teaching, mentorship, and capacity building within NIE and NTU Requirements The ideal candidate should: Be an internationally recognised scholar with a distinguished track record of research and leadership in AI and education or related fields Demonstrate outstanding scholarly achievements, including high-impact publications and sustained research funding Exhibit strong commitment to interdisciplinary collaboration and innovation Have a proven record of academic leadership, mentorship, and global engagement Show the ability to translate research into practice and policy impact in education Application Process Interested candidates should submit their Cover letter and Curriculum Vitae through Workday. For enquiries, interested applicants may write to Ms Yilian Wu . Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
