    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Communications-Psychology-Business-Administration-Public-Health-_R00017429": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Communication/Psychology/Sociology/Social Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-05-22\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWee Kim Wee School of Communication and Information (WKWSCI) is looking for a candidate to join them as a Research Assistant who will work closely with the Director of the Centre for Healthy and Sustainable Cities (CHESS) and manage the running of the centre located at Wee Kim Wee School of Communication and Information. CHESS is an interdisciplinary research centre devoted to projects on health, risk and environmental issues from human-centred perspectives in the Asian context. As one of the research centres in COOL ASIA, CHESS draws upon theories and concepts from communication and information science, bringing into play the interaction of technology — new, emerging and future — with human behaviours. Key Responsibilities: Daily operational, administrative, and logistics duties related to project management, including financial operations, social media updates, and the organization of symposia, training workshops, coordinating student helpers; Help conduct interviews, quantitative and qualitative analyses, desk research, and write reports Help in writing grant proposals and reports Job Requirements: Graduated with a Bachelor degree in Communication/ Psychology/ Sociology/ Social Science Have relevant experience in academic research, especially in conducting online surveys Demonstrable intellectual excellence Maturity and capacity to begin an independent research career Desire and potential to develop as a future academic leader We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-time-Lecturer--School-of-Civil-and-Environmental-Engineering-_R00020729-1": {
      "title": "Part-time Lecturer (School of Civil and Environmental Engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-05-16\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nWe are looking for experienced part-time lecturers in following areas within the School of Civil and Environmental Engineering. Civil Engineering Graduate Programme International Construction Management Graduate Programme Maritime Studies Graduate Programme PhD Courses Candidates should have a proven track-record in the area that they are teaching. Responsibilities: Conduct lectures. Prepare and submit editable teaching materials to the School. Prepare, administer and grade continuous assessments and exams. Student consultation. Any other required duties, where applicable. Applicants should have extensive industry and/or academic experience, a passion for teaching and should preferably possess the following requirements: Requirements: Master’s degree or higher; candidates with strong relevant industry experience will be considered. At least 2-3 years of teaching experience at a tertiary level is preferred. Professional experience (min. 3 years) in the related field at managerial level. Demonstrates a profound knowledge of related course. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Mechanical-Engineering-Aerospace-Engineering-Applied-Physics-_R00020668": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Mechanical Engineering/Aerospace Engineering/Applied Physics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-05-08\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nYoung and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is ranked among the world’s top universities. NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science (CCDS) is a leading college that is known for its excellent curriculum, outstanding and impactful research, and world-renowned faculty. Today, we are ranked #2 for AI and Computer Science by US News Best Global Universities; and #8 for Data Science and AI by QS World University Ranking. A hot bed of cutting-edge technology and groundbreaking research, the College aims to groom the next generation of leaders, thinkers, and innovators to thrive in the digital age. Located in the heart of Asia, NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science is an ‘exciting place to learn and grow. We welcome you to join our community of faculty, students and alumni who are shaping the future of AI, Data Science and Computing. Cloud Application and Platform Group is a cutting-edge research group from CCDS. It is a leading research group in the area of Cloud Media Computing, Content Delivery Networks, Data Center architecture, and Big Data analytics. Mission of the Cloud Application and Platform Group is to conduct innovative and fundamental research in applications and platforms for cloud computing and to practice a learning-based framework for system prototyping and performance optimization, for large-scale networked computing systems. Vision of the lab is to incubate visionary technical leaders to drive future Information and Communication Technology (ICT) advances. The College of Computing & Data Science (CCDS) invites applications for the position of Research Associate.    Key Responsibilities: Develop new CFD solutions in partnership with our academic and technology partners; Providing CFD technical leadership to new research programs; Work closely with other team members to develop OpenFOAM methods, processes and workflows; Develop and implement mesh, solver and post-processing methodologies to improve the efficiency and effectiveness of our CFD tools and workflow; Support and optimise CFD tools including monitoring and resolving issues; Ensure that CFD simulations and analysis carried out within the department are aligned with the capability of the commercial tools; Conduct research into and analysis the energy usage of different scenarios; Write reports and mapping the total energy usage; Publish papers and support documentation. Job Requirements: Preferably Master in Mechanical Engineering, Aerospace Engineering, or Applied Physics from a recognized university; Strong organisational and project skills; Excellent team player and able to work effectively with other groups; Practical experience in OpenFOAM development and/or in C++ language development in a CFD environment; Good understanding of commercial CFD solvers (Fluent, 6Sigma, STAR-CCM+, etc.) Experience with energy modelling or coding platforms including SketchUp, EnergyPlus, OpenStudio, TRNSYS, and Python; Proven ability to work at a fast pace and to react rapidly to new information; F1 experience would be advantageous but not essential; Experience of Python, C++, and Unix shell scripting would be advantageous. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-time-Lecturer-in-Translation-and-Localisation_R00015722": {
      "title": "Part-time Lecturer in Translation and Localisation",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-05-08\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPart-time lecturer for Translation, Localisation, and Project management courses Master of Arts in Translation and Interpretation Programme  (MTI)  at NTU is seeking experienced part-time instructors who excel at teaching courses on translation, localisation, project and data management. A proven track record of practical experience in handling corporations and clients at multinational, regional and local levels, with the knowledge of applying cutting edge project management tools and software are preferred. The instructor’s responsibilities  include  designing the course syllabus, conducting lectures  and  student consultation, designing assignments, administering assessment and grading, and providing constructive feedback to support student learning. Requirements: Demonstrable experience in teaching and curriculum development in higher education. Candidates should have a master level of T&I (Translation and Interpreting) degree and/or postgraduate level degree of project  &  data management. Preference will be given to candidates who have strong industry experience in translation projects management. We are also looking for candidates who possess excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with a strong commitment to fostering a diverse and inclusive learning environment. The successful  candidate  is  expected to use both Chinese and English as the medium of instruction and to commence duty as soon as possible. Please click “APPLY” button to submit your application. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate-Research-Fellow--Power-Energy-Systems-and-Academic-_R00020628": {
      "title": "Research Associate/Research Fellow (Power/Energy Systems and Academic)",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-05-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research. With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 2,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 4th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2025 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee We are hiring a Research Associate/Research Fellow in electric power & energy systems to perform research in the area of modern power grids bordering on the topics like power electronics, energy storage, energy efficiency. The Research Associate/Research Fellow is also expected to support teaching activities as required by the school. We are looking for someone with experience in power engineering and a strong mathematical background. Key Responsibilities: Develop new methods for power systems control. Develop data-driven methods for application in power & energy systems Assist in preparation of teaching materials for electric power related courses Prepare report and conduct presentation at seminars. Assist the school in various teaching activities, including instructing or supervision of labs and tutorials. Job Requirements: PhD (Research Fellow), MEng/MSc (Research Associate) in Electrical Engineering, Computer Science, Statistics, or other related fields. Solid Mathematical skills. Experience in one of the programming language – Python, Matlab, Julia. Understanding of one or more of the following areas would be an advantage Optimization Dynamic systems Control theory Power electronics Signal processing Machine learning and data science (various subfields, including AI) Good written and oral communication skills. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Research-Fellow--Experimental-Quantum-Physics-_R00020592": {
      "title": "Senior Research Fellow (Experimental Quantum Physics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-05-02\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJoin Our Team at the School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore The School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences (SPMS) at NTU Singapore hosts research and education activities in two divisions: Division of Mathematical Sciences (MAS) and Division of Physics and Applied Physics (PAP). MAS covers diverse topics ranging from pure mathematics to the applications of mathematics in cryptography, computing, business, and finance. PAP covers many areas of fundamental and applied physics, including quantum information, condensed matter physics, biophysics, and photonics. Over the years, SPMS has attracted talented individuals from around the world and Singapore to join as scientific leaders and researchers. A Senior Research Fellow position is available under Quantum Technology with ultracold atoms lab in School of Physical and Mathematical sciences, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore. Key Responsibilities: Conduct research activities related to the Quantum project  Supervise a team of 6 to 9 researchers Train young researchers and students Coordinate technical and scientific efforts Job Requirements: The candidate must hold a PhD degree in Experimental Quantum Physics or a relevant discipline from a well-established university or institution. The candidate should also have at least 4 years of successful post-doctoral experiences in laser cooling of atoms or related research areas. The candidate must be highly motivated in research and must have proven experience in Quantum projects. The candidate should possess the ability to work both independently and collaboratively within a team. The College of Science seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Geometric-Data-Science-_R00020513": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Geometric Data Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-04-25\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJoin Our Team at the School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore The School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences (SPMS) at NTU Singapore hosts research and education activities in two divisions: Division of Mathematical Sciences (MAS) and Division of Physics and Applied Physics (PAP). MAS covers diverse topics ranging from pure mathematics to the applications of mathematics in cryptography, computing, business, and finance. PAP covers many areas of fundamental and applied physics, including quantum information, condensed matter physics, biophysics, and photonics. Over the years, SPMS has attracted talented individuals from around the world and Singapore to join as scientific leaders and researchers. Position Available: Research Associate in Geometric Data Science Join the laboratory of Dr Cyrus Mostajeran at the School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences. We are seeking a Research Associate to contribute to the research agenda of the project ‘Geometric Optimization and Design in Learning and Robotics'. Key Responsibilities: The successful applicant will be responsible for: Obtaining rigorous mathematical results at the interface of geometry, analysis, and data science Designing, implementing, and testing algorithms Engaging in scientific exchange with collaboration partners of the project Preparing reports, scientific papers, and presentations Project duration: 6 months Job Requirements: Master’s degree in Mathematics, Physics, Computer Science, or Engineering Advanced knowledge of one or more of the following areas: analysis, differential geometry, optimization, mechanics, biophysics, robotics, control theory Enthusiasm for applying advanced mathematical tools and techniques to applications including data science and robotics Good communication skills The College of Science seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Flow-Chemistry-_R00020427": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Flow Chemistry)",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-04-16\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Materials Science and Engineering (MSE) provides a vibrant and nurturing environment for staff and students to carry out inter-disciplinary research in key areas such as Computational Materials Science, Characterisation Materials Science, Defence Composite Materials, Functional Composite Materials, Energy, Nanomaterials, Low Dimensional Materials, Biomaterials Materials, Biological Materials, Bioinspired Materials and Sustainable Materials. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/mse/research . The Decarbonisation Programme “Singapore Max-Planck Alliance for the Sustainable Conversion of Biomass” is looking for a Postdoctoral Researcher in Chemical Engineering to optimize biomass extraction and for upscaling and improving flow processes. Key Responsibilities: Construction of a flexible flow platform to perform small-scale conversions Implementation of its automation and closed-loop optimization Maintenance of lab or equipment or supplies that include procurement and liaison with suppliers Assist or produce high quality reports and documents that consolidate research findings Contribute to the mentoring and guidance of junior researchers and students, fostering an environment of learning and innovation within the project team. Job Requirements: Doctoral degree in Chemical Engineering, Chemistry, or a related field Experience in python is required Experience in flow chemistry Experience in reactor design is beneficial Experience in process control and PAT Knowledge and interest in closed-loop optimization Experience with Computational Fluid Dynamics Experience with laboratory automation and flow platforms Capable of conducting independent research while effectively collaborating in a multidisciplinary environment. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--High-Temperature-Resistant---Miniaturized-Payload-Hardware-Design-_R00020360": {
      "title": "Research Associate (High Temperature-Resistant & Miniaturized Payload Hardware Design)",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-04-10\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCentre for Advanced Robotics Technology Innovation (CARTIN) are looking for a hardware-focused Research Associate to design and prototype a compact and heat-resistant multi-sensor payload. The system must withstand temperatures of 250°C for 10 minutes (without external cooling) while maintaining internal stability for embedded electronics. Key Responsibilities: Design compact mechanical housing to operate under 250°C ambient conditions. Ensure internal core temperature remains under 55°C during runtime. Select and integrate miniaturized components (compute, battery, sensors). Strip sensor casings and reassemble into a custom mount with thermal shielding. Perform heat simulation, thermal insulation, and shock-resistance design. Test hardware in specified sites and environments. Job Requirements: Bachelor or Master in Mechanical Engineering, Mechatronics, or similar. Strong experience in heat-resistant enclosure design and miniaturized hardware integration. Familiar with thermal simulation tools (ANSYS, SolidWorks, etc.). Experience with IP65/ IP67 standards, fanless computing, and embedded design. Knowledge of fire-fighting robot or harsh-environment robotic platforms is a plus. Join our team to build a compact and thermally protected SLAM sensor payload for extreme environments. The candidate will design hardware that survives 250°C conditions while maintaining internal electronics <55°C. Experience with high-temp materials, mechanical CAD, and embedded platform integration is essential. Ideal for Mechatronics/Mechanical engineers with strong prototyping skills. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturer-for-Introduction-to-Museum-Studies_R00020341": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer for Introduction to Museum Studies",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-04-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nSchool of Art, Design and Media Nanyang Technological University, Singapore Part-Time Lecturer for Introduction to Museum Studies   A Part-time Lecturer to teach an elective course – AP6203 From Colonial to Post Colonial Art: A Critical Survey commencing in August 2025, for the Master of Arts in Museum Studies and Curatorial Practices (MA MSCP) programme. The School of Art, Design and Media (ADM) at Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, invites qualified candidates to apply as Part-Time Lecturer for the Master of Arts (MA) in Museum Studies and Curatorial Practices programme. The Part-time Lecturer is expected to teach an elective course – From Colonial to Post Colonial Art: A Critical Survey. Please refer to the website for the detailed course content description for AP6104: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/adm/programmes/graduate-admissions/ma-in-museum-studies-and-curatorial-practices-(coursework)/courses#Content_C003_Col00 Successful candidates should have at least a Master’s degree in a relevant field with a track record of past teaching experience at Undergraduate and Master’s level. For more information on the course and its objectives, please email admcsep@ntu.edu.sg Further information about the University and the School can be viewed at the following websites: NTU      : www.ntu.edu.sg ADM     : www.ntu.edu.sg/adm Application Procedure Please login to the following webpage to submit your application :  https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers Closing date for applications: 5 May 2025. The successful candidate is expected to assume duty in August 2025. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Communication-Psychology-Sociology-Human-Computer-Interaction-Social-Science-_R00020303": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Communication/Psychology/Sociology/Human-Computer Interaction/Social Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-04-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWee Kim Wee School of Communication and Information (WKWSCI) is looking for a candidate to join them as a Research Fellow. The Research Fellow is tasked with supporting the planning and execution of the project on the “Intelligent Modelling for Decision-making in Critical Urban Systems (Descartes). Reporting directly to the Principal Investigator, the Research Assistant must facilitate key administrative and management duties, including but not limited to conducting literature searches and manuscript preparation by performing systematic reviews of relevant scholarly work and assist in writing research manuscripts. The Research Fellow plays a key role in experiment conceptualization, design and implementing by developing research protocols, design experiments (e.g., lab or online studies), recruit participants, and collect data. The Research Fellow is responsible for data analysis by analyzing experimental data using appropriate statistical tools (e.g., SPSS, R) and interpret findings; prepare materials for presentations at workshops and conferences and contribute to journal articles, conference proceedings, and other academic outputs. Key Responsibilities: Keeping track of expenditure and remaining budget in an organized manner, ensuring that the spend is optimized and on track with respect to goals set for the grant Liaising with external vendors to purchase necessary equipment/materials for research studies, including specialized equipment, software, and research participant incentives Lead the recruitment of participants for experiment sessions and focus groups Manage students and Project Officers in conducting literature reviews Plan the necessary logistics, for the administration of experiments and focus group sessions, such as scheduling, booking facilities, and preparing IRB documentation Participate in the data collection process for both qualitative (e.g. interviews, focus group sessions) and quantitative (e.g. experiments, surveys) studies Analyze data for various projects using tools such as SPSS, R, and/or Microsoft Excel Prepare presentations, as well as other research-related documents Draft conference and journal submissions based on research findings Job Requirements: PhD degree in Communication, Psychology, Sociology, Human-Computer Interaction, or a related social science discipline Good project management skills, with multi-tasking ability Academic writing skills required Demonstrated experience in designing, implementing, and analysing experiments (e.g., lab studies, online experiments) Proficiency in statistical software (e.g., SPSS, R) with strong quantitative analysis skills Ability to work both independently and collaboratively in a multicultural, interdisciplinary environment; excellent interpersonal and communication skills Prior involvement in research projects, evidence of publishing in peer-reviewed journals or presenting at conferences is desirable We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-time-Lecturer--English-Literature-_R00019942": {
      "title": "Part-time Lecturer (English Literature)",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-03-21\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe School of Humanities at NTU invites applications for part-time teaching of various literature modules. Candidates should have a track-record in teaching. Instructor will be responsible for leading lectures and seminars for three class hours per week in addition to syllabus planning, class preparation, course assessment and student consultations. Candidates who expect to receive their PhDs by the time of the appointment may also apply. Requirements: PhD degree in English Literature or related areas At least 1-2 years teaching experience at a tertiary level and excellent teaching evaluation. Only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Perovskites-_R00019991": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Perovskites)",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-03-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAt ERI@N, the Renewables & Low-Carbon Generation – Solar team focuses on cost-effective halide perovskite materials for solar energy conversion and light emitting application. The focus allows us to employ low energy intensive manufacturing processes, in which cost-effective and abundant starting materials are deposited via solution-processing techniques or vacuum evaporation techniques. We are looking for a focused and highly motivated individual to contribute to a dynamic and growing team. This team focuses on the fabrication of large-area perovskite devices with various functionalities. Key Responsibilities: Development of fabrication processes, material characterization and reliability testing capabilities for the perovskite devices Testing of new halide perovskite compositions Conceptualize and realize new device configurations with enhanced stability and reproducibility Design and test perovskite devices in various sizes Report writing and results presentation Regular maintaining of research and study records for possible publication in peer-review journals and conference proceedings. Work closely with internal colleagues, including postgrad students, as well as external collaborators in short-term and long-term research projects Job Requirements: PhD in Materials Science, Chemistry or related fields with in-depth knowledge of materials, device physics and processing Previous experience in the field of halide perovskites and large-area fabrication process (slot-die coating) is highly desired. Expertise in materials and device characterization techniques. Good skills in time management, experiment design and data analysis. Good English language skills (oral and written) for research purposes Good communication and interpersonal skills We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant--Robotics---Mechatronics-_R00019928": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Robotics / Mechatronics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-02-26\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering (MAE) is a robust, dynamic and multi-disciplinary international research community comprising of world-class scientists and bright students. MAE prides itself in its excellent research capabilities in areas including advanced manufacturing, aerospace, biomedical, energy, industrial engineering, maritime engineering, robotics, etc. The school is equipped with state-of-the-art research infrastructure, housing a comprehensive range of cluster laboratories, test bedding facilities, research centres/institutes and corporate laboratories. Cutting-edge research in MAE addresses the immediate needs of our industries and supports the nation’s long-term development strategies. In the new era of industrial 4.0 and sustainable living, MAE is rigorous in developing new competencies to support the growth and competitiveness of our engineering sector in the global landscape. MAE has grown to be leader in Engineering Research, ranking amongst the top engineering schools in the world. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/mae/research . Key Responsibilities: Assist research engineers and scientists for their experiments Assist to develop control system for insect-machine hybrid robot Write and prepare research papers, technical reports and presentations for project progress, and provide regular reports Reference: https://hirosatontu.wordpress.com/ Job Requirements: A Diploma Degree or Bachelor Degree in Science, Mechanical Engineering, Robotics, Electrical Engineering, Mechatronics, Control Engineering, Automation, or related field Oral and written communication skills, plus ability to read, comprehend, and explain engineering drawings and technical documents We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Quantum-physics-_R00019902": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Quantum physics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-02-26\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJoin Our Team at the School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore The School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences (SPMS) at NTU Singapore hosts research and education activities in two divisions: Division of Mathematical Sciences (MAS) and Division of Physics and Applied Physics (PAP). MAS covers diverse topics ranging from pure mathematics to the applications of mathematics in cryptography, computing, business, and finance. PAP covers many areas of fundamental and applied physics, including quantum information, condensed matter physics, biophysics, and photonics. Over the years, SPMS has attracted talented individuals from around the world and Singapore to join as scientific leaders and researchers. We are looking for a Research Fellow to be in charge of an experimental apparatus aiming to develop a quantum processor based on Neutral Atom Arrays. The role will focus on developing the experiment, take and analyze data, supervise undergrad and PhD students. Key Responsibilities: Develop a cold atom apparatus using state-of-the-art technologies Develop the necessary interface to drive a quantum processor Report on at least on a weekly basis on the progress to the principal investigator Supervise PhD and undergrad students Job Requirements: PhD degree in experimental physics either in quantum physics or in optics At least 1 years of relevant experiences in similar role Familiarity with laser systems, vacuum, atomic physics, photonics The School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Engineer-I---Research-Engineer-II--Computer-Science-Artificial-Intelligence-_R00019855": {
      "title": "Research Engineer I / Research Engineer II (Computer Science/Artificial Intelligence)",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-02-20\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Alibaba-NTU Global e-Sustainability CorpLab (ANGEL) represents a key collaboration between Alibaba Group and Nanyang Technological University (NTU). Supported by the Singapore RIE2025 Fund, ANGEL creates and deploys impactful green digital technologies for global sustainability. ANGEL’s mission aligns seamlessly with Singapore’s national objectives, such as the Singapore Green Plan 2030 and the Singapore Smart Nation Initiative. ANGEL’s work in developing sustainable and equitable digital solutions and promoting a sustainable and green lifestyle will contribute to a smaller carbon footprint. Its holistic approach will help to secure a brighter, more sustainable future for humanity ANGEL is looking for a motivated Research Engineer to develop PrimeNet. Key Responsibilities: Conducting cutting-edge research to develop new algorithms Exploring existing literature and staying up to date with advancements in the field Designing experiments to test hypotheses and validate models Translating research concepts into working prototypes Developing software, algorithms, or hardware systems for real-world applications Writing clean, efficient, and scalable Python code Collecting, preprocessing, and analyzing large datasets Job Requirements: Bachelor's or Master's degree in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, or a related field. Demonstrated experience in natural language processing, machine learning, and deep learning. Familiarity with deep learning frameworks like TensorFlow or PyTorch. Ability to analyze complex problems, identify patterns, and derive meaningful insights from data. Proficiency in Python for implementing NLP and Generative AI algorithms. Understanding of NLP concepts, machine learning algorithms, and their applications in text processing and generation. Capacity to address research challenges creatively and develop innovative solutions. Effective written and verbal communication skills for documenting research findings and presenting them to diverse audiences. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Research-Fellow--Low-temperature-electron-transport-measurement---Project-Officer--Experimental-Condensed-Matter-Physics-Laboratory-_R00018010-1": {
      "title": "Research Fellow/Senior Research Fellow (Low-temperature electron transport measurement)/ Project Officer (Experimental Condensed Matter Physics Laboratory)",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-02-14\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJoin Our Team at the School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore The School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences (SPMS) at NTU Singapore hosts research and education activities in two divisions: Division of Mathematical Sciences (MAS) and Division of Physics and Applied Physics (PAP). MAS covers diverse topics ranging from pure mathematics to the applications of mathematics in cryptography, computing, business, and finance. PAP covers many areas of fundamental and applied physics, including quantum information, condensed matter physics, biophysics, and photonics. Over the years, SPMS has attracted talented individuals from around the world and Singapore to join as scientific leaders and researchers. The Weber group at SPMS, NTU, has 3 positions available: (1 & 2) Research Fellow / Senior Research Fellow (Low-temperature Transport Measurement) We are seeking a highly motivated Research Fellow / Senior Research Fellow to lead experimental efforts on low-temperature transport measurement and 2D and topological materials, heterostructures and devices. Demonstrating capability, creativity and high-impact outcomes in low temperature experimental condensed matter physics will be a key requirement. The research fellow will be leading experimental work in an existing dilution refrigerator laboratory, equipped with a BlueFors LD250 cryostat equiooed with vectorized magnet, and GHz wiring. Other facility and protocols for crystal growth and device nanofabrication have been developed to support the Research Fellow’s / Senior Research Fellow’s work.  Key Responsibilities: Lead experimental work on low-temperature electronic measurement Help with procuring equipment and consumables Manage, maintain, and service laboratory and equipment Guidance/ Co-supervision of research students Writing of high-tier research publications Detailed Technical Requirements: Demonstrated track record in low-temperature electronic measurement (T = 4.2K and below), including cryogenics handling Experience with dilution refrigerators is strongly preferred Demonstrated know-how in servicing and maintaining a dilution refrigerator, especially with BlueFors systems will be a hiring advantage Further Job Requirements: PhD in experimental condensed matter physics (at least 5 years of experience required for SRF) Demonstrated track record of high-impact research achievements Demonstrated ability to publish high-tier research publications Excellent verbal and written communication skills (including scientific writing) Ability to work independently but also as part of a team ________________________________________________________________________ (2) Project Officer (Experimental Condensed Matter Physics Laboratory) We are seeking a highly organized and driven Project Officer to support laboratory management, technical operations such maintenance of laboratory equipment, as well as day-to-day organizational matters. Key Responsibilities: Operation and maintenance of cryogenic and vacuum lab equipment Overseeing organization matters such as purchases, stockkeeping, maintenance schedules Management of day-to-day operations and organization of scientific meetings  Job Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in physics, materials science, or electrical engineering Highly organized and structured mindset, proactive thinking Excellent verbal and written communication skills Ability to work independently but also as part of a team The College of Science seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Computer-Science---Engineering-Electronic-Engineering-Applied-Mathematics-Perception-Sciences-_R00019727": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Computer Science & Engineering/Electronic Engineering/Applied Mathematics/Perception Sciences)",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-02-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nYoung and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is ranked among the world’s top universities. NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science (CCDS) is a leading college that is known for its excellent curriculum, outstanding and impactful research, and world-renowned faculty. Today, we are ranked #2 for AI and Computer Science by US News Best Global Universities; and #8 for Data Science and AI by QS World University Ranking. A hot bed of cutting-edge technology and groundbreaking research, the College aims to groom the next generation of leaders, thinkers, and innovators to thrive in the digital age. Located in the heart of Asia, NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science is an ‘exciting place to learn and grow'. We welcome you to join our community of faculty, students and alumni who are shaping the future of AI, Data Science and Computing. The College of Computing & Data Science (CCDS) invites applications for the position of Research Fellow. Key Responsibilities: Responsible for performing intelligent signal, multimedia, muti-modal, and multi-task processing/computing, for building open databases of climate data, monitoring and mitigating climate change, and predicting climate change and effects of mitigation Submission of a comprehensive reports/IDs/Demos/papers summarizing/justifying the pioneer and innovative research performed Job Requirements: Possess a PhD degree in Computer Science (And Engineering), Electronic Engineering, Applied Mathematics, Perception Sciences, etc. Have good technical reading, writing and programming skills. Have good experience and track record for related R&D. High desire for technological exploration and achievement. Mastering of a programming language would be valued (e.g. Python, C, Matlab, …) Self-driven, highly motivated, with interest to work with other researchers and scientists (as a team player) to produce high-quality research. Excellent teamwork and verbal, written communication skills We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Project-Officer--Research-Project-Administration-_R00019698": {
      "title": "Project Officer (Research Project Administration)",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-02-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJoin Our Team at the School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore The School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences (SPMS) at NTU Singapore hosts research and education activities in two divisions: Division of Mathematical Sciences (MAS) and Division of Physics and Applied Physics (PAP). MAS covers diverse topics ranging from pure mathematics to the applications of mathematics in cryptography, computing, business, and finance. PAP covers many areas of fundamental and applied physics, including quantum information, condensed matter physics, biophysics, and photonics. Over the years, SPMS has attracted talented individuals from around the world and Singapore to join as scientific leaders and researchers. Join the laboratory of David Wilkowski at SPMS. We are seeking a Project Officer to contribute to a project focused on developing quantum processors at Nanyang Technological University. The incumbent will manage the administrative part of the project in close collaboration with the Principal Investigator, the other group members, and the various administrative offices of the university. Key Responsibilities: Execute finance, budgeting, manpower planning, grant administration, and policy interpretation to ensure smooth and efficient operations. Oversee procurement activities, including raising Purchase Requests (PR), Purchase Orders (PO), and Good Receipts (GR) to streamline purchasing operations. Plan and execute events such as industry and academic seminars, colloquia, and conferences, ensuring successful delivery and engagement. Manage logistics for local and international meetings and events, including travel arrangements, scheduling, and fulfilling event-specific requirements. Compile, analyze, and prepare reports and claims with detailed analytical insights to support decision-making processes. Maintain and update the website, ensuring it reflects current and accurate information while adhering to organizational standards. Job Requirements: Bachelor Degree in Business Administration, Project Management, or another related field. Minimum 2 years of relevant experience in research, academic, or administrative settings. Proficiency in Microsoft applications, Word, Excel, PowerPoint. Experience in SAP and Ariba is considered an added advantage. Abilities to work independently as well as teamwork The College of Science seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Biological-Physics-_R00019677": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Biological Physics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-01-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJoin Our Team at the School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore The School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences (SPMS) at NTU Singapore hosts research and education activities in two divisions: Division of Mathematical Sciences (MAS) and Division of Physics and Applied Physics (PAP). MAS covers diverse topics ranging from pure mathematics to the applications of mathematics in cryptography, computing, business, and finance. PAP covers many areas of fundamental and applied physics, including quantum information, condensed matter physics, biophysics, and photonics. Over the years, SPMS has attracted talented individuals from around the world and Singapore to join as scientific leaders and researchers. We are seeking two Research Fellows to contribute to a project focused on the collective motion of bacteria and mechanics of bacterial colonies and biofilms. It involves experiments, theory, and numerical simulations. One Research Fellow will focus on the experiments and the other theory and numerical simulations. Key Responsibilities: Design experimental systems and perform experimental measurements. Process experimental data analyze the results. Implement numerical calculations to simulate collective behaviors of bacteria. Build theoretical models to describe or explain the experimental or numerical results. Help organize the research lab. Help train other members of the lab, such as undergraduate students. Job Requirements: PhD (for Research Fellow and above equivalent) degree in biophysics, soft matter physics, mechanical engineering, chemical engineering, or related field. Good written and oral communication skills.  Proficiency in experimental techniques such as microscopy, microfluidics, or rheology OR molecular dynamics simulation or agent-based simulation. Competent in soft skills e.g. information visualization, oral presentation, etc. Entry level candidates are welcome to apply. Ability to work in a highly collaborative environment. The College of Science seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant--Communication--Psychology--Sociology--Social-Science--Information--Computer-Science-_R00016403": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Communication/ Psychology/ Sociology/ Social Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-01-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Wee Kim Wee School of Communication and Information (WKWSCI), together with the Earth Observatory of Singapore, is looking for a Research Associate to make an important contribution to the research project: “Climate Transformation Program (CTP): Cross Cutting Theme 1 – Sustainable Societies” funded by the MOE Tier 3C Grant. CTP aims to develop, inspire, and accelerate knowledge-based solutions and educate future leaders to establish the stable climate and environment necessary for resilient, just, and sustainable Southeast Asian societies. CTP will generate knowledge and innovation across disciplines including climate and Earth science, ecology, materials science, artificial intelligence, humanities, social sciences and the arts, finance, health, and engineering. It will also translate state-of-the-art scientific results into real world solutions for Singapore, and it will transfer these solutions to Southeast Asia (SEA) and beyond. As part of this programme, “Cross-cutting theme 1: Sustainable Societies”, this theme will leverage climate research in communication and virtual reality tools to shape public attitudes and behaviours towards climate change issues. The Research Associate will work directly with the PI of the Sustainable Societies theme, Professor Shirley Ho, based in the Wee Kim Wee School of Communication and Information at NTU. Key Responsibilities: To engage in conducting literature searches and manuscript preparation. To engage in VR app development and implementation. To engage in experiment conceptualization, design, and implementation. To conduct statistical analyses with experimental data.  To contribute to research publications and presentations. To write progress report and final research report. To engage in the dissemination of the results of the research with the support of and under the supervision of the Principal Investigator. To carry out administrative work associated with the program of research as necessary. Job Requirements: Master’s degree in communication, psychology, sociology, or a social science related discipline. Strong foundation in VR app development, experimental research and analytical skills (e.g., SPSS, MPLUS, or R). A team player in a project setting, also with ability to work independently in a multi-cultural team environment. Must demonstrate initiative and good interpersonal communication skills. Prior experience in VR app development and experimental research. An internationally recognized research track record as evidenced by journal publications and conference presentations. Interested applicants are invited to submit a cover letter, full CV and names and contact details of three referees in one document. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Project-Officer--Computer-Science-Electrical-Engineering-_R00019653": {
      "title": "Project Officer (Computer Science/Electrical Engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-01-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nYoung and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is ranked among the world’s top universities. NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science (CCDS) is a leading college that is known for its excellent curriculum, outstanding and impactful research, and world-renowned faculty. Today, we are ranked #2 for AI and Computer Science by US News Best Global Universities; and #8 for Data Science and AI by QS World University Ranking. A hot bed of cutting-edge technology and groundbreaking research, the College aims to groom the next generation of leaders, thinkers, and innovators to thrive in the digital age. Located in the heart of Asia, NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science is an ‘exciting place to learn and grow'. We welcome you to join our community of faculty, students and alumni who are shaping the future of AI, Data Science and Computing. The College of Computing & Data Science (CCDS) invites applications for the position of Project Officer.   Key Responsibilities: Research and develop novel ML-based methodologies and algorithms. Working closely with other Postdoc/RA/PhD students to discuss the ideas and implement the system. The research should lead to publications in top-tier international conferences and journals Job Requirements: Bachelor degree in Computer Science, Electrical Engineering or related disciplines Prior experience in NLP, and state-of-the-art ML techniques would be a plus; Good interpersonal communication and oral presentation skills Experienced in working in a team, with people of diverse skillsets and cultural background We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Scientist--Computer-Science--Electrical-Engineering-_R00019614": {
      "title": "Research Scientist (Computer Science/ Electrical Engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-01-22\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Alibaba-NTU Global e-Sustainability CorpLab (ANGEL) represents a key collaboration between Alibaba Group and Nanyang Technological University (NTU). Supported by the Singapore RIE2025 Fund, ANGEL creates and deploys impactful green digital technologies for global sustainability. ANGEL’s mission aligns seamlessly with Singapore’s national objectives, such as the Singapore Green Plan 2030 and the Singapore Smart Nation Initiative. ANGEL’s work in developing sustainable and equitable digital solutions and promoting a sustainable and green lifestyle will contribute to a smaller carbon footprint. Its holistic approach will help to secure a brighter, more sustainable future for humanity.  ANGEL is looking for a motivated Research Scientist to review the literature, define problem statements, formulate optimization problems, develop advanced AI algorithms, and implement solutions and tests for LAE optimal flight routing, improve battery usage, manage global and local air traffic, and conduct simulations of the proposed algorithms. Key Responsibilities: To survey the literature related to Low Altitude Economy (LAE) and energy consumption models To define problem statements to reduce energy consumption in LAE with multiple UAVs To formulate optimization problems and develop AI algorithms to reduce energy consumption, increase safety and reliability, and meet all LAE user demands To test and fine-tune the algorithms to achieve the best performance Job Requirements: Ph.D. in Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, or related disciplines Strong research experience Good track record of publications Good teamwork and collaboration skills Research background in data analytics and machine learning We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Psychology-_R00016038": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Psychology)",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-01-03\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCenter for Leadership and Cultural Intelligence (CLCI) at Nanyang Business School, is seeking a suitable candidate for the position of Research Associate. The Research Associate will be part of a dynamic team of researchers involved in spearheading high-impact research on leadership and cultural intelligence. In addition, this role offers great opportunities for acquiring research skills and capabilities. Key Responsibilities: Design and manage data-collection, including set-up and administration/coordination of surveys and field interviews Collate quantitative and qualitative survey data and managing the database Conduct literature review and data analyses Present information in both visual and written formats Job Requirements: Master’s Degree, preferably in Psychology Proficient in Microsoft Office (e.g. Word, Excel, Powerpoint) and other data visualization software (e.g., Tableau) Proficiency in statistical packages (e.g., R, SPSS) will be an advantage Detail-oriented, meticulous and able to work independently under time pressure Excellent interpersonal skills We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturer--Psychology-_R00019380": {
      "title": "Part Time Lecturer (Psychology)",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-12-22\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe School of Social Sciences invites applications for part-time lecturer (PTL). We are looking for PTL who will serve as primary instructor of core and elective courses in the Psychology major curriculum. Key Responsibilities: Preparation and delivery of lectures, tutorials, and discussion sections. Supervision and coordination of teaching assistants and tutors. Setting of assessment components and marking of examinations. Qualification and requirement: The successful candidate will hold a doctorate-level or a masters-level qualification in an appropriate Psychological field, be able to demonstrate effective teaching and training of undergraduate students.  Candidates with specializations in one or more of these fields are particularly welcome: Personality Psychology, I/O Psychology, Bio-psychology and Clinical Psychology. Evidence of excellence in teaching and/or clinical supervision is highly desirable. The successful candidate will be expected to contribute significantly to teaching and development of multiple courses at the undergraduate level, including introductory level survey-type courses, laboratory and methods courses, and seminar courses. Essential selection criteria: The attainment of a higher degree (PhD/DPhil/Masters) in Psychology or a related discipline Experience and interest in teaching undergraduate psychology students, with a strong and demonstrable commitment to the organization and delivery of teaching, particularly in one or more areas of Personality Psychology, I/O Psychology, Bio-psychology and/or Clinical Psychology Excellent communication and interpersonal skills relevant to teaching and pastoral care Willingness and ability to contribute to the overall objectives of the Programme and School, working collaboratively with others Desirable selection criteria: A developing track record of research (e.g. peer-reviewed publications and conference presentations) in Personality Psychology, I/O Psychology, Bio-psychology and/or Clinical Psychology Experience of academic administration For further information about the School, and Psychology, at NTU, please refer to the following website: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/sss/psychology To apply Interested applicants are invited to submit their applications by clicking the “Apply” button. The application should include the following: 1 page cover letter (include motivation, teaching experience, preferred course) CV (highlight teaching experience, if any) Student feedback on teaching (if available) Only shortlisted applicants will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Research-Fellow--Polymer-Upcycling-_R00019334": {
      "title": "Senior Research Fellow (Polymer Upcycling)",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-12-16\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Materials Science and Engineering (MSE) provides a vibrant and nurturing environment for staff and students to carry out inter-disciplinary research in key areas such as Computational Materials Science, Characterisation Materials Science, Defence Composite Materials, Functional Composite Materials, Energy, Nanomaterials, Low Dimensional Materials, Biomaterials Materials, Biological Materials, Bioinspired Materials and Sustainable Materials. Our research group focuses on research areas relevant to macromolecular and hybrid materials, including topics in the fields of polymer science and engineering, composite science, environmental science, and so on. Key job purpose is to d evelop green and scalable mechanical or chemical polymer upcycling technologies, particularly for polyurethane. Key Responsibilities: Develop green and scalable mechanical or chemical polymer upcycling technologies, particularly for polyurethane. Conduct research and development activities on polymer pre-treatment and mechanical/chemical upcycling, including formulation of problem statement, design and execution of lab-scale and pilot-scale experiments/operations, sample characterizations, data analysis, and so on. Engage and communicate with existing or future industrial and academic collaborators to advance the developed technologies from lab-scale verification to pilot implementation. Prepare technical reports, intellectual properties documents, safety documents, and academic publications Job Requirements: PhD degree in Materials Science, Polymer Science, Chemical Engineering, or fields related to polyurethane. At least 6-8 years graduate study or working experience in research and development on topics on polymer science, chemical engineering, and green technologies Proficiency in hands-on and characterization techniques such as TGA, DSC, FTIR, DMA, rheology, NMR, CHNS, XRD, XPS, engineering design and drawing etc. Able to exhibit leadership roles in handling and managing multi-disciplinary projects Experienced in preparation of academic and pilot-operation proposals Good team-player, good communication skill, problem solver, thinker and doer Good wet laboratory practice and familiar with considerations on laboratory safety Passionate in research and solving real-time environmental issues related to plastic upcycling Software skills relevant to process design, mass balance, cost analysis, and life-cycle-analysis are favorable Industrial experience in polymer upcycling and productization is favorable We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-time-Lecturer-in-Linguistics_R00019324": {
      "title": "Part-time Lecturer in Linguistics",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-12-13\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nNTU's Master of Arts in Linguistics is currently seeking experienced part-time lecturers for courses in linguistics that focus on three concentrations: Language and Cognition, Language and Society, and Language Structure. Candidates must have a proven track record teaching in at least one of these areas. The instructor’s responsibilities will include designing the course syllabus, assignments and assessments, conducting lectures and/or seminars, marking and grading, and providing student consultation, and constructive feedback to support student learning. Requirements: Candidates must have a master’s or PhD degree in linguistics or related fields. They should possess excellent communication skills and demonstrate excellence in teaching and curriculum development in higher education. Please note that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--AI-Law-_R00015991": {
      "title": "Research Associate (AI Law)",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-11-22\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Nanyang Business School (NBS) is recruiting a Legal Research Associate in the area of AI, data protection and data privacy law, technology law, health law and cybersecurity law and practice. Key Responsibilities: Assist in primary legal research on databases such as Lexis-Nexis, HeinOnline etc Collate research materials found, inclusive of preparing summaries of research materials which involves reading and drafting written summaries of regulatory materials, legal judgments, and secondary materials Formulation and development of data governance practices and frameworks Implementing empirical research Other research administrative tasks Job Requirements: Bachelor of Law degree or Juris Doctor from a good University, with experience in research and/or AI law and regulation and/or in data protection law Strong communication and interpersonal skills with leadership potentional Organised and meticulous Capable of following instructions meticulously Team player and able to work independently Solid understanding of technology is an advantage We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-time-lecturer_R00013875": {
      "title": "Part-time lecturer",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-11-13\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe School of Social Sciences, Sociology Programme is looking for Part-time Lecturers (PTL) who will be responsible for teaching undergraduate courses. We invite applications for part-time lecturers to teach courses in, but not limited to, the following areas: •  State and society •  Sociological methods •  Social policy •  Ethnicity, culture, and migration •  Southeast Asia and Singapore •  Global social change Key Responsibilities: •  Propose a new course or teach an existing course •  Conduct lectures or seminars •  Conduct tutorials and assessments for a course •  Conduct grading of course assessments/exam scripts. •  Other responsibilities related to undergraduate teaching. Qualification: 1.  At least a PhD Degree in social sciences 2.  At least 1-2 years teaching experience at a tertiary level with excellent teaching evaluation. Singaporeans and Singapore Permanent Residents are preferred. To apply Applicants are invited to submit their applications by clicking the “Apply” button. The application should include cover letter, detailed CV listing their teaching and industry experience as well as student feedback on teaching from previous institutions, if available). Only shortlisted applicants will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturer_R00018973": {
      "title": "Part Time Lecturer",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-11-07\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nYoung and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is ranked among the world’s top universities. College of Computing and Data Science (CCDS) is a leading school for higher learning that is known for its excellent curriculum, outstanding impactful research, and talented faculty. Today, we are ranked Top 10 for Computer Science in the latest US News and World Report Best Global Universities listing and NTU has been recognised as the top university for AI research and citation impact. CCDS serves a critical role in the university and society as we harness the power of digital technology and tech-enabled solutions to not only enhance the learning and research experience of our students and staff, but also to create innovative solutions for some of the grand challenges facing our world. The position is open for candidates working in all areas of computer science and engineering. However, we are particularly interested in candidates working at the frontiers of the following high priority areas: Design Thinking Project Management Mini Capstone Project (Foundation Stack) Responsibilities: Conduct lectures, tutorials and laboratory duties. Conduct coursework assessment, grade assignments/quizzes/tests/projects in accordance with the guidelines, criteria and rubrics given. Provide consultation to students. Carry out teaching related duties such as marks entry, invigilation. Set and mark exam papers. Requirements: You should possess at least a Master in related disciplines from a well-recognized university. You should possess excellent communication skills. You should have extensive industry experience. You should demonstrate tertiary-level teaching in the area of   Design Thinking and Project Management. Review of applications and shortlisting decision will be on an on-going basis until the positions are ﬁlled. Interested applicants are invited to submit their applications through the NTU career portal by clicking the “Apply” button. To facilitate the process, please submit the following documents if applicable. Full Curriculum Vitae Letters of Recommendation(s)a Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturer_R00018924": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-11-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe School of Social Sciences, invites applications for part-time lecturers (PTLs). We are looking for PTLs who can contribute to teaching (conducting tutorials and assessment) in our School on Ethics and Civics. Preference will be given to applicants who can teach the following topics: • Human rights, justice, and equality • Meritocracy • Political systems (Singapore, Southeast Asia) • Multiculturalism • Freedom of speech and responsibility • Gender and diversity Key Responsibilities: • Attend lectures (online). • Conduct tutorials and assessments for the assigned course. • Grade course assignments (including tests, quizzes, exam scripts). • Work closely with the course coordinator to handle students’ queries on course related matter. Qualification and requirement: • A degree in the social sciences, specialization in political science and sociology and good knowledge of Singapore will be an advantage. • Demonstrable ability to teach the proposed topics on Ethics and Civics at the undergraduate level will be an advantage. • Able to tutor/lecture during office hours. To apply Interested applicants are invited to submit their applications by clicking the “Apply” button. The application should include the following: • 1 page cover letter (include motivation, research and/or teaching experience on the course topics) • CV (highlight teaching experience, if any) • Student feedback on teaching (if available) Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Project-Officer--Materials-Science-Chemistry-Environmental-Engineering-Biology-_R00018830": {
      "title": "Project Officer (Materials Science/Chemistry/Environmental Engineering/Biology)",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-10-23\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Materials Science and Engineering is looking for a highly motivated candidate to join us as a Project Officer (PO). The PO will join an MOE funded project led by Prof Ng Kee Woei. The project aims to upcycle keratinous waste for the bioplastics development. The PO will be responsible to develop and optimize the formulation of keratin-based bioplastics, characterize the produced bioplastics and assess its biodegradation profile in soil. Key Responsibilities: Conduct thorough literature review and generate periodic updates Extract the keratin protein Formulate and optimize keratin-based bioplastics Characterize the keratin-based bioplastics properties (e.g. Mechanical strength, FTIR, SEM, degradability, permeability, water contact, etc.) Analyse and interpret research data Develop and optimize protocols Manage logistical issues and laboratory inventory. Participate in collaborative work within multidisciplinary team and external collaborators Assist the generation of periodic progress report as required by funding agency Job Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in Materials Science/Chemistry/Environmental Engineering/Biology or related fields Experience in polymers, biomaterials research and material characterization required (e.g. Mechanical strength, FTIR, SEM, degradability, permeability, water contact, etc) Experience in environmental science and engineering will be a bonus Good communication and writing skills Good coordination/project management skills Able to plan and execute experiments with minimal supervision Able to take initiative to improve processes and troubleshoot problems Able to organize well and adhere to deadlines We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-time-Lecturer-for-Translation-and-Localisation_R00018709": {
      "title": "Part-time Lecturer for Translation and Localisation",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-10-15\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nMaster of Arts in Translation and Interpretation Programme (MTI) at NTU is seeking experienced part-time instructors who excel at teaching courses on translation, localisation, project and data management. A proven track record of practical experience in handling corporations and clients at multinational, regional and local levels, with the knowledge of applying cutting edge project management tools and software are preferred. The instructor’s responsibilities include designing the course syllabus, conducting lectures and student consultation, designing assignments, administering assessment and grading, and providing constructive feedback to support student learning. Requirements: Demonstrable experience in teaching and curriculum development in higher education. Candidates should have a master level of T&I (Translation and Interpreting) degree and/or postgraduate level degree of project & data management. Preference will be given to candidates who have strong industry experience in translation projects management. We are also looking for candidates who possess excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with a strong commitment to fostering a diverse and inclusive learning environment. The successful candidate is expected to use both Chinese and English as the medium of instruction and to commence duty as soon as possible. Only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
