    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturer_R00011370": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-01-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Social Sciences invites applications for part-time lecturers (PTLs) who can contribute to teaching Singapore: Imagining the next 50 years.   Key Responsibilities: • Conduct lectures / tutorials in the related discipline (both face-to-face and online) • Handle administrative work concerning the grading of students • Give inputs regarding the course curriculum Qualification and requirement: • A least a Master’s Degree. • At least 2-3 years teaching experience at a tertiary level with excellent teaching evaluation. • Teaching experience in Singapore-related topics is preferred. To apply Interested applicants are invited to submit their applications by clicking the “Apply” button. The application should include the following: • Detailed CV listing teaching and industry experience • Student feedback on teaching from previous institutions, where applicable Only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturer_R00011229": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-01-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPart Time Teaching Positions Young and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University (NTU Singapore) is the fastest-rising university in the world’s Top 20 and ranked 11th globally. NTU is also placed 1st amongst the world’s best young universities. The School of Social Sciences at NTU offers a stimulating and multidisciplinary education and research in the social sciences, and is home to four major disciplines for undergraduate and postgraduate degrees (Economics, Psychology, Sociology and Public Policy and Global Affairs). Part-Time teaching position(s)  is available to cater to the short-term teaching needs of School of Social Sciences for the following: Subject Area: Principles in Economics International Finance               Job Responsibilities: Conduct lectures / tutorials in the related discipline (both face-to-face and online) Course Curriculum Planning and Coordination. Handle administrative work and examination matters concerning the grading of students Requirements: A least a Master’s Degree. At least 2-3 years teaching experience at a tertiary level with excellent teaching evaluation. Teaching experience in Microeconomics/Macroeconomics/Finance-related topics is preferred. It should include the reference  “Application for Part-time Teaching Position”  in the subject line with attached detailed CV listing teaching and industry experience, as well as student feedback on teaching from previous institutions, where applicable. Only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-time-Lecturer-in-Bahasa-Indonesia_R00010560": {
      "title": "Part-time Lecturer in Bahasa Indonesia",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-01-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nNTU invites applications for part-time teaching of the Bahasa Indonesia  language electives at the beginner and intermediate levels. Requirements: A postgraduate qualification, preferably in a humanities subject or relevant field. A degree in Bahasa Indonesia would be considered an advantage. Experience in teaching and learning, preferably at tertiary level. Skills and knowledge in IT and multi-media course development. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-time-Lecturer-in-Language-and-Communication-Centre_R00011043": {
      "title": "Part-time Lecturer in Language and Communication Centre",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-01-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nWe are seeking experienced candidates capable of teaching academic writing and communication skills. Instructors will be responsible for teaching 2-hour tutorials in addition to class preparation, assessing student assignments according to guidelines, being available for student consultations, working with curriculum writers on curriculum matters, and working with coordinators on administrative matters. Requirements: Master’s degree or higher in Linguistics, Education or Literature At least 2-3 years relevant teaching at a tertiary level   Only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-time-Lecturer-in-Malay_R00011408-1": {
      "title": "Part-time Lecturer in Malay",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-01-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nNTU invites applications for part-time teaching of the Malay  language electives at the beginner and intermediate levels. Requirements: Master’s degree in Malay language or equivalent. A native speaker with high proficiency of the Malay language. Effectively bilingual in both Malay and English Language. Knowledge in the application of IT in language teaching and experience with multimedia course materials Experienced in various genres of the Malay language. Only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-time-Lecturer-in-Publishing_R00010595": {
      "title": "Part‐time Lecturer in Publishing",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-01-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nNTU invites applications for part‐time teaching of various humanities related courses as one of our offerings in the Continuing Education program within the School of Humanities. Candidates should have a proven track‐record in teaching. Lecturers will be responsible for leading workshops and seminars for 12 hours in addition to syllabus planning, class preparation, marking for assessment and student consultation. We seek to fill several part‐time lecturer positions, subject to candidates with the following credentials: - MA/PhD degree or extensive industry experience  - Ability to teach at least one of the following: Practical Ethics Culture and history that are relevant to the Singapore context Digital humanities Environmental humanities Editing, Publishing, and Branding Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Project-Officer--Engineer--Algorithm-and-Operation-Researcher-_R00010743-1": {
      "title": "Project Officer (Engineer, Hardware Developer)",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-01-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering (MAE) invites applications for the position of Project Officer.  Key Responsibilities:  The Project Officer will j oin the team to develop insect-computer hybrid robots control system: Design and fabrication of wirelessly controlled sensor-backpack mounting on living insects to (i) electronically stimulate their neurons and muscles to navigate them on demands and (ii) report environmental conditions Develop firmware, algorithm, data structure and user interface for sensor-backpack remote control Integrate customized algorithm in insect computer hybrid robot operation and test the operation of sensor-backpack on living insect Technical write up and presentation Job Requirements: Degree in Mechatronics/ Robotics/ Electrical and Electronics/ Computer Engineering Experience in PCB design and fabrication Experience in C/C++ programming for embedded system Experience in real time operating system development Experience in wireless communication (BLE, Sub-Ghz, UWB, etc …) is advantageous Experience in C#, Java, JavaScript, Python is advantageous Knowledge and experience in insect anatomy and physiology is advantageous A team player and technically motivated to solve problems. Good interpersonal and communication skills. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Electrical---Electronic-Engineering-Mechatronics-Robotics-Engineering-Mechanical-Engineering-_R00011214-1": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Electrical & Electronic Engineering/Mechatronics/Robotics Engineering/Mechanical Engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-01-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering (MAE) invites applications for the position of Research Fellow. Key Responsibilities:  Work is related to development and demonstration of a prototype for Mobile robot combination coupling and decoupling device/platform. Excellent prototyping and problem solving skills. Capable of working independently and within a team, while supervising other Final year students working on their final year projects on related area. Can communicate and present technically complex issues to multidisciplinary/multinational teams (local and international) Job Requirements:  Ph.D degree in Electrical/Electronics/Robotics, mechanical or mechatronics engineering Experience in related area of cobot or related technologies (Plus). Familiar with control systems of cobot and robotic systems (Plus) Working knowledge of software (Python, C++, Matlab or similar). Practical and hands-on, active self-learner and able to pay close attention to technical details Proficiency in English and verbal communication, have strong work ethic and can work independently and comfortably in a multidisciplinary environment. Good working knowledge in ROS (Robot Operating System). We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--High-Frequency-Active-Circuit-Design-_R00010582-1": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (High Frequency Active Circuit Design)",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-01-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nA Research Fellow position is available in the Centre for Integrated Circuits and Systems, School of Electrical & Electronic Engineering, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore. Job Description: Support the research for the project titled:Terahertz Transmitter and Receiver Antennas for Wireless Communications. The project investigates the On-chip Hybrid Electronic and Photonics Transceiver design for high data-rate wireless communication at the sub-THz band. The CMOS/SiGe technologies will be used for the design of electronic circuits Work on the design and characterization of sub-THz electronic circuits (Oscillators, Mixers) Work closely with the Photonics team for hybrid integration of photonics devices Job Requirements: PhD degree in Electrical and Electronic Engineering and related study area Strong background in RFIC components design (mmWave will be advantageous) Good Experienced in EDA tools (Cadence, ADS) and EM modelling tools (HFSS, CST) RF characterization measurements Able to make active IC design of phased array antenna systems and on chip antenna including fabrication and characterization measurement Capable and broad experience in: (i) Active circuit design (ii) Work in group (iii) Post-fabrication measurement We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Research-Engineer-I--Computer-Science-_R00010614-1": {
      "title": "Senior Research Engineer I (Computer Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-01-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nA Senior Research Engineer I position is available in the Centre for Smart Platform Infrastructure Research on Integrative Technology (SPIRIT), Nanyang Technological University, Singapore. SPIRIT is a translational R&D institute funded by National Research Foundation and supported by Smart Nation Programme Office and GovTech, to develop the Smart Platform Infrastructure to enable applications in Video Analytics, Wireless Sensors Network and other areas required by Singapore as a Smart Nation. Through cutting-edge systems research, SPIRIT Centre aims to enable translational efforts in data science and analytics for solving public sector challenges through innovative solutions. Job Description: The Senior Research Engineer I will be responsible for the AI/NLP research and development in designing smart nation platforms. The key responsibilities include: Gather system requirements by defining and analyzing system problems Design and implement natural language processing (NLP) algorithms and models for semantic analysis, e.g., word embedding, named-entity recognition, coreference resolution and parsing, and ontology and knowledge graph constructions Application of NLP in knowledge and information retrieval, and relevancy ranking with spatiotemporal consideration Conduct “translational” research to apply the state-of-the-art solutions at scale for real world challenges Documentation and scientific reporting Job Requirements: PhD in computer science Some experience and research background in AI and NLP Passionate about NLP and AI related research, innovations and their applications Proficient in one or more programming languages (e.g., Python, C/C++, etc.) and research packages/modules Experience in large-scale text processing and analytics Good track records in publication We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Research-Engineer-I--Computer-Science-_R00010619-2": {
      "title": "Senior Research Engineer I (Computer Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-01-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nA Senior Research Engineer I position is available in the Centre for Smart Platform Infrastructure Research on Integrative Technology (SPIRIT), Nanyang Technological University, Singapore. SPIRIT is a translational R&D institute funded by National Research Foundation and supported by Smart Nation Programme Office and GovTech, to develop the Smart Platform Infrastructure to enable applications in Video Analytics, Wireless Sensors Network and other areas required by Singapore as a Smart Nation. Through cutting-edge systems research, SPIRIT Centre aims to enable translational efforts in data science and analytics for solving public sector challenges through innovative solutions. Job Description: The successful applicant will be responsible for the AI/NLP research and development in designing smart nation platforms. The key responsibilities include: Gather system requirements by defining and analyzing system problems Design and implement natural language processing (NLP) algorithms and models for semantic analysis, e.g., word embedding, named-entity recognition, coreference resolution and parsing, and ontology and knowledge graph constructions Application of NLP in knowledge and information retrieval, and relevancy ranking with spatiotemporal consideration Conduct “translational” research to apply the state-of-the-art solutions at scale for real world challenges Documentation and scientific reporting Job Requirements: PhD in computer science Some experience and research background in AI and NLP Passionate about NLP and AI related research, innovations and their applications Proficient in one or more programming languages (e.g., Python, C/C++, etc.) and research packages/modules Experience in large-scale text processing and analytics Good track records in publication We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturer---Public-Policy-and-Global-Affairs_R00008473": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer - Public Policy and Global Affairs",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-01-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe Public Policy and Global Affairs Programme, School of Social Sciences, invites applications for part-time lecturers (PTLs). We are looking for PTLs who can contribute to teaching (conducting seminars, lectures, tutorials and assessment) in our Programme, particularly in these areas: • Political Theory (including but not limited to the history of political thought, contemporary political theory, non-Western political theory, analytic political thought) • Public Policy or Public Administration (including but not limited to public policy and administration in Singapore and Asia, policy implementation, AI and governance, sustainability) • Environmental governance • Civil society • Gender and development • Ethics and Civics • Comparative politics Key Responsibilities: • Develop course materials and syllabus • Conduct seminars/lectures/tutorials • Develop assessments for the course • Grade course assignments (including tests, quizzes, exam scripts) • Invigilate the final examination. • Handle all student queries on course related matter • Work with the Head of Division to ensure smooth and timely course delivery Qualification and requirement: • A least a PhD in social sciences, specialisation in a political science subfield will be an advantage • Prior tutoring/lecturing experience will be an advantage • Able to teach and invigilate during office hours To apply Interested applicants should email their application to UG-PPGA@ntu.edu.sg. Application package (one file) should include the following: • 1 page cover letter (include motivation, teaching experience) • Sample syllabi of proposed course to be taught • CV (highlight teaching experience) • Student feedback on teaching (if available) Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturer--Public-Policy-and-Global-Affairs-_R00006003": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer (Public Policy and Global Affairs)",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-01-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe Public Policy and Global Affairs Programme, School of Social Sciences, invites applications for part-time lecturers (PTLs). We are looking for PTLs who can contribute to teaching (conducting tutorials and assessment) the core courses in the Programme, specifically: • Fundamentals of Politics • Politics of Singapore • Introduction to International Relations and Foreign Policy • Introduction to Political Theory • Introduction to Public Administration and Policy Key Responsibilities: • Attend lectures (to be discussed and agreed with course coordinator). • Conduct tutorials and assessments for the assigned course. • Grade course assignments (including tests, quizzes, exam scripts). • Invigilate the final examination. • Work closely with the course coordinator to handle students’ queries on course related matter. Qualification and requirement: • A least a Master Degree in social sciences, specialisation in a political science subfield will be an advantage. • Some prior tutoring/lecturing experience will be an advantage. • Able to tutor/lecture during office hours. To apply Interested applicants are invited to submit their applications by clicking the “Apply” button. The application should include the following: • 1 page cover letter (include motivation, teaching experience, preferred course) • CV (highlight teaching experience, if any) • Student feedback on teaching (if available) Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Lecturer_R00006159": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-01-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe School of Social Sciences, invites applications for part-time lecturers (PTLs). We are looking for PTLs who can contribute to teaching (conducting tutorials and assessment) in our School on Ethics and Civics. Preference will be given to applicants who can teach the following topics: • Human rights, justice, and equality • Meritocracy • Political systems (Singapore, Southeast Asia) • Multiculturalism • Freedom of speech and responsibility • Gender and diversity Key Responsibilities: • Attend lectures (online). • Conduct tutorials and assessments for the assigned course. • Grade course assignments (including tests, quizzes, exam scripts). • Work closely with the course coordinator to handle students’ queries on course related matter. Qualification and requirement: • A degree in the social sciences, specialization in political science and sociology and good knowledge of Singapore will be an advantage. • Demonstrable ability to teach the proposed topics on Ethics and Civics at the undergraduate level will be an advantage. • Able to tutor/lecture during office hours. To apply Interested applicants are invited to submit their applications by clicking the “Apply” button. The application should include the following: • 1 page cover letter (include motivation, research and/or teaching experience on the course topics) • CV (highlight teaching experience, if any) • Student feedback on teaching (if available) Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Part-Time-Lecturer-in-Screenwriting--Creative-Writing-_R00001319": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer in Screenwriting (Creative Writing)",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-01-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPart-time Lecturer in Screenwriting (Creative Writing) -School of Humanities We are seeking an experienced screenwriter capable of teaching HZ9205 Screenwriting as one of our offerings in Creative Writing within the School of Humanities. Candidates should have a proven track-record in writing and developing projects for the screen. Instructor will be responsible for leading workshops and seminars for three class hours per week in addition to syllabus planning, class preparation, marking for assessment and student consultation. Requirements: Master’s degree or higher At least 2-3 years teaching screenwriting at a tertiary level   For further information about the current Creative Writing Electives, please refer to the following website: http://www.soh.ntu.edu.sg/Programmes/english/undergraduate/Pages/Minorcreativewriting.aspx   Only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Part-Time-Tutors--Linguistics-and-Multilingual-Studies-_R00000625-1": {
      "title": "Part-Time Tutors (Linguistics and Multilingual Studies)",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-01-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nSchool of Humanities The Linguistics and Multilingual Studies (LMS) programme invites applications for part-time tutors. We are in particular looking for candidates who can teach the core courses in the Programme, namely, Introductory Linguistics, Phonetics and Phonology, Structure of English, Morphology and Syntax, Semantics and Pragmatics, Sociolinguistics, Bilingualism and Multilingualism. Criteria: Candidates must possess at least an Masters of Arts in Linguistics. Some prior tutoring experience will be an advantage. Able to tutor/lecture during office hours. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    }
  },
